2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1730
2 PLAC Enfield, Hartford, Connecticut , Colonial America
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} AKA Pryor
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT The original profile quoted from the Bullock Family Tree as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT "John Pryor was born on February 14, 1664, in Windsor Township, Hartford, Connecticut, to Humphrey Pryor (Houmfery Prior on the Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906 record) and Ann Osborne, the eldest of two sons born to
2 CONC  them. He married Mary Geer (Geares on the record) on April 15, 1686, in what was then Enfield, Hampshire County, Massachusetts, which is now in Hartford County, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT His name appear several times in John Chauncey Pease’s book History of Enfield Connecticut Volume III in the Early Deeds section. The earliest was dated December 17, 1711, and reads as follows: “John Pryor to his son Benjamin Jone
2 CONC s. (War. ) 10 acres in ‘ye field’ -Shubael Geers south, Great River west, John Pryor north, Country road east. Witnesses Thomas Jones, Mary Jones.” At that time, Benjamin Jones was his new son-in-law; Shubael Geer is his brother-i
2 CONC n-law; and John Pryor is his son. Because John had a son John who also had a son named John, it is sometimes hard to determine which John the deeds apply to. The latest record clearly of John Sr is dated September 22, 1727 and rea
2 CONC ds as follows: “Benjamin Jones Jun' to his father John Prier. (War.) 10 acres in South field-Shubael Gear south, Great River west, Benjamin Jones, formerly John Prier north, Country road east. 10 acres in the South field river div
2 CONC ision-Thomas Abby senr formerly north, Benjamin Jones, formerly John Prier south, Country road east, Great River west.” So we know that John was alive in the fall of 1727. There is one additional record which seems to be of John S
2 CONC r. that is dated December 28, 1730, which reads “John Pryor to his son Daniel Pryor. (War.) 1 1/2 acres on Buckhorn brook-John Bement decd south, uplands northwest. 5 acres-above meadow west.” From this we can assume John Pryor Sr
2 CONC  died after December 28, 1730. Some researchers believe it was in 1738 in Enfield. Unfortunately a death or burial record can not be found."
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Note: this writer adopted this orphaned profile while working on his daughter Ann. John Prior and his assumed father Humphrey (also an orphaned profile) have quite limited sources. Any additional good sources very welcome
2 CONC !
2 CONT
2 CONT John's daughter Ann Prior was born on 31 March 1690.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Prior-700
2 CONT
2 CONT John Prior (1664 - aft. 1730)
2 CONT Born 14 Feb 1664 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut 
2 CONT Died after 1730 after age 65 in Enfield, Hartford, Connecticut 
2 CONT
