1 NOTE GEDCOM line 69232 not recognizable or too long for MRIN 2118:
2 CONT   (SLGS) 2 STAT CLEARED
1 NOTE Benjamin Eggleston was born on 18 December 1653 at Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, the youngest of Bygod  Eggleston's eleven children.  Benjamin married Hannnah (Osborn) Shaddock on 6 March 1678 at Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut a
2 CONC nd died about November 1732 at East Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut. His will was probated on 16 December 1732.  Benjamin and Hannah were married by Captain Newberry.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Hannah was born on 18 December 1657 at Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut. She died on 17 August 1715. She had previously been married to Elias Shadduck / Shattuck.  She was the daughter of John Osborn, who died on 27 October 1686
2 CONC , and Ann Oldage.   Ann Oldage may have died on 28 August 1689.
2 CONT
2 CONT  The will of Benjamin Eggleston I (dated 16 December 1729):
2 CONT
2 CONT         I, Benjamin Eglestone of Windsor, do make and ordain this my last will and testament: Although I have given my  children portions according to my ability formerly, yet I think it wisdom to make this following small additio
2 CONC n to   prevent future trouble: Imprimis. I give unto my son-in-law, Samuel Osbond of Windsor, to complete his deceased wife's portion, 5 shillings. I give unto my daughter Marcy Miller 5 shillings. I give unto my daughter Sarah Bl
2 CONC iss 5 shillings. I give unto my daughter Dorothy West L5. I give unto my daughter Esther Osbond, of Enfield, 5 shillings.   i give unto my son Benjamin Eglestone the remainder of my goods and chattells whatsoever, who is obliged t
2 CONC o take care and honourably to maintain the testator as long as he liveth. And my son, Benjamin Eglestone I constitute my sole executor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin X Egleston, LS
2 CONT
2 CONT Witness: Thomas Stoughton
2 CONT Joseph Haraper, Robert Thompson
2 CONT Court Record, Page 78 -- 5 December, 1732: Will exhibited and proven.
2 CONT Invtory taken 24 November, 1732 by Thomas Stoughton and David Bissell.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Source: Genealogical Dictionary of New England Settlers
2 CONT
2 CONT Volume 4
2 CONT page 58
2 CONT Shadduck, or Chaddock, Elias, Windsor, m. Hannah, d. of John Osborn, had only ch. Hannah, wh. m. 14 Mar. 1692, Benjamin West, and d. 26 May 1676. His wid. m. 6 Mar. 1678, Benjamin Eggleston.
2 CONT
2 CONT Volume 3
2 CONT page 307
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Eggleston (son of Bigod Eggleston and Mary E. (Unknown) was born 18 Dec 1653 in Windsor, Hartford, CT, and died 24 Nov 1732 in Windsor, Hartford, CT633. He married Hannah Osborn on 6 Mar 1677/78 in Windsor, Hartford, CT, 
2 CONC daughter of John Osborn and Ann Oldage.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Notes for Benjamin Eggleston:
2 CONT Described in his father's will as "my stay & staff in my infirm old age". Per Bygod Eggleston: Englishman & Colonist and Some of His Descendants, by Dr. Rosalie Eggleston & Linda Eggleston McBroom, p. 123
2 CONT    Benjamin Eggleston was born on 18 December 1653 at Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, the youngest of Bygod  Eggleston's eleven children.  Benjamin married Hannnah (Osborn) Shaddock on 6 March 1678 at Windsor, Hartford, Connecticu
2 CONC t and died about November 1732 at East Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut. His will was probated on 16 December 1732.  Benjamin and Hannah were married by Captain Newberry.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Hannah was born on 18 December 1657 at Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut (Source:   The Descendants of John Porter, Volume II). She died on 17 August 1715. She had previously been married to Elias Shadduck / Shattuck.  She was th
2 CONC e daughter of John Osborn, who died on 27 October 1686, and Ann Oldage.   Ann Oldage may have died on 28 August 1689.
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Benjamin Eggleston I (dated 16 December 1729):
2 CONT
2 CONT         I, Benjamin Eglestone of Windsor, do make and ordain this my last will and testament: Although I have given my  children portions according to my ability formerly, yet I think it wisdom to make this following small additio
2 CONC n to   prevent future trouble: Imprimis. I give unto my son-in-law, Samuel Osbond of Windsor, to complete his deceased wife's portion, 5 shillings. I give unto my daughter Marcy Miller 5 shillings. I give unto my daughter Sarah Bl
2 CONC iss 5 shillings. I give unto my daughter Dorothy West L5. I give unto my daughter Esther Osbond, of Enfield, 5 shillings.   i give unto my son Benjamin Eglestone the remainder of my goods and chattells whatsoever, who is obliged t
2 CONC o take care and honourably to maintain the testator as long as he liveth. And my son, Benjamin Eglestone I constitute my sole executor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin X Egleston, LS
2 CONT
2 CONT Witness: Thomas Stoughton
2 CONT Joseph Haraper, Robert Thompson
2 CONT Court Record, Page 78 -- 5 December, 1732: Will exhibited and proven.
2 CONT Invtory taken 24 November, 1732 by Thomas Stoughton and David Bissell.
2 CONT     Source: Genealogical Dictionary of New England Settlers
2 CONT Volume 4, page 58
2 CONT Shadduck, or Chaddock, Elias, Windsor, m. Hannah, d. of John Osborn, had only ch. Hannah, wh. m. 14 Mar. 1692, Benjamin West, and d. 26 May 1676. His wid. m. 6 Mar. 1678, Benjamin Eggleston.
2 CONT The will of Benjamin Eggleston, I (dated 16 December 1729) reads as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT 		I, Benjamin Eglestone of Windsor, do make and ordain this my last will
2 CONT 		and testament:   Although I have given my children portions according to
2 CONT 		my ability formerly, yet I think it wisdom to make this following small
2 CONT 		addition to prevent future trouble:   Imprimis.   I give unto my son-in-
2 CONT 		law, Samuel Osbond of Windsor, to complete his deceased wife's portion,
2 CONT 		5 shillings.   I give unto my daughter Marcy Miller 5 shillings.   I
2 CONT 		give unto my daughter Sarah Bliss 5 shillings.   I give unto my daughter
2 CONT 		Dorothy West L5.   I give unto my daughter Esther Osbond, of Enfield, 5
2 CONT 		shillings.   i give unto my son Benjamin Eglestone the remainder of my
2 CONT 		goods and chattells whatsoever, who is obliged to take care and
2 CONT 		honourably to maintain the testator as long as he liveth.   And my son,
2 CONT 		Benjamin Eglestone I constitute my sole executor.
2 CONT 				Benjamin  X  Egleston, LS
2 CONT 	Witness:   Thomas Stoughton
2 CONT 	Joseph Haraper, Robert Thompson
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Benjamin Eggleston and Hannah Osborn:
2 CONT Marriage: 6 Mar 1677/78, Windsor, Hartford, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Benjamin Eggleston and Hannah Osborn are:
2 CONT i. Mary Eggleston, b. 2 Oct 1680, Windsor, Hartford, CT, d. Aft. 1732.
2 CONT ii. Sarah Eggleston, b. 20 Apr 1683, d. date unknown.
2 CONT iii. Abigail Eggleston, b. 11 Apr 1685, d. Bef. 16 Dec 1729.
2 CONT iv. +Benjamin Eggleston, b. 27 Mar 1687, Windsor, Hartford, CT, d. 30 Oct 1732.
2 CONT v. Dorothy Eggleston, b. 28 Feb 1688/89, d. Aft. 1729
2 CONT vi. Hester Eggleston, b. 10 Jul 1699, d. date unknown.
