2 CONT Disputed Mother
2 CONT
2 CONT Bigod Eggleston was assumed to have been the son of Juliana Harker, but this has been disproved.[29][3] It has been falsely assumed on the internet that the wife of Miles Harker was Dorothy Bigod (daughter of Francis), but this Do
2 CONC rothy Bigod married Roger Radcliffe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Possible daughter: Susannah EGGLESTON?
2 CONT
2 CONT It is suspected that Bigod actually had two daughters who married into the Denslow family. He could have easily had a daughter Susannah Eggleston born about 1625-1626, who married Henry Denslow about 1645 (their first known child 
2 CONC born in 1646). There is circumstantial evidence that she was an Eggleston, but probably the only way to prove it is through mitochondrial DNA testing. To read more about the circumstantial evidence, see the biography section of he
2 CONC r profile here: Susannah Eggleson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also found married 1630 in Hartford, Connecticut.
2 CONT His Given Name
2 CONT
2 CONT Several spellings have been found:
2 CONT Bigod,
2 CONT Begot,
2 CONT Bigot,
2 CONT Bagot,
2 CONT Begat,
2 CONT Bagott,
2 CONT Baggett,
2 CONT Beggatt,
2 CONT Beggat,
2 CONT Beget,
2 CONT Bigat,
2 CONT Biggott,
2 CONT Bygod,
2 CONT Bygood
2 CONT
2 CONT Bigod Eggleston ... his given name is variously reported as Bygood, Bigood, Bygod, Begat, Baggot, etc. There seems to be no consensus. The last name also varies considerably in England. We've chosen to standardize on "Bigod Eggles
2 CONC ton" just to simplify matters.
2 CONT LNAB
2 CONT
2 CONT A birth record is found, LNAB spelled Egelston, siblings LNAB spelled Egleston. Both or either attributable to an illiterate scribe. I propose we Note this in the Biography, also as a AKA so a search will find it, but use Egglesto
2 CONC n, which has descended to become the accepted spelling. Discussion welcome.[30]
2 CONT
