2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT BEGAT EGGLESTON, 1580-1674, was 50 at time of emigration, old for that day, but he lived nearly a half century longer, and raised a fine family in the new world. He probably came on the "Mary and John," although his name is not li
2 CONC sted. He settled in Dorchester with "Mary and John" passengers, and 5 years later was one of the founders of Windsor. He came from Exeter, Devonshire as did John Warham, the ship's minister. The Phelps family listed on this boat w
2 CONC ere also from Devonshire.
2 CONT In 1632, Begat married MARY TALCOTT from Colchester, Essex. (In 1632, on the "Hopewell," came from Essex, the RUGGLES, READS, DYERS; and BIGELOWS from Colchester (all are our ancestors including Mary Talcott). John Eliot, noted mi
2 CONC nister, came on this boat also from Essex.)
2 CONT The Talcott family had been prominent in England, tracing back to William the Conqueror. John Talcott, Mary's brother, became an early Governor in the new world.
2 CONT
