1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rebecca Wade, widow of John Owen, died 3 Dec 1711 in Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut Colony.  Her origins are not certain.  Not a known daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Wade/6000000007106489596?
2 CONC through=341991063100012941
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Wade-166
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca Wade married John Owen on October 3, 1650, in Windsor.[8][9][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca and John had 11 children, all born at Windsor. Each of these children were recorded multiple times and there are some discrepancies in the dates. Clues indicate the dates labeled '(MG)' were added in a group later.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Josiah, b. 8 Sept 1651[5][8][10] Removed to Simsbury[10]
2 CONT # John b. 5 Nov 1652; d. young[5][10]
2 CONT # John 2nd, b. 23 April 1654; d. 15 Jan 1670[5] d. 13 Jan 1670.[10]
2 CONT # Nathaniel, born 9 Aug 1656 (MG) (once)[5][8] or Aug 29, 1656 (twice)[8]; 9 Aug[10]
2 CONT # Daniel, born 28 Mar 1658[5][8][10] m. Mary Bissell[10]
2 CONT # Joseph, b. 23 Oct 1660[5][8][10] removed to Hebron.[10]
2 CONT # Mary, was born 5 Dec 1662[5][8]
2 CONT # Benjamin, was born 20 Sept 1664; d. 26 May 1665[5][8][10]
2 CONT # Rebecca was b. 28 March 1666;[5][8][10] m. Nathan Gillett of Windsor 30 June 1692.[8][10]
2 CONT # Obadiah, son of John was born 12 Dec 1667[5][8] or 12 Dec 1662 (MG)[8] 12 Dec 1667.[10]
2 CONT # Isaac. b. 27 May 1670[5][8][10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note, however, that the original Lucius Barnes Barbour typescript shows additional records for the death of a son John in 1665 (who would have been the John born in 1654) and the birth of a son John in Jan 1667 (who would have bee
2 CONC n the John who died in 1670). (See image attached to this profile).
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca's husband, John Owen, died February 18, 1698 Old Style[5][8] (which is February 18, 1699 New Style). Rebecca, his widow, died December 3, 1711.[5][8]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===disputed origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca WADE - d. Dec. 3, 1711, Windsor, CT. Possibly the daughter of Henry WADE and granddaughter of Richard WADE (b. about 1579, Dorestshire, England; d. CT) and Elizabeth (b. about 1574, England). Another source indicates she w
2 CONC as the daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Wade/6000000007106489596 Robert WADE], probably the brother of Henry. Robert WADE was living at Dorchester, MA in 1635, and moved to Hartford, CT in 1639, and to Norwich, CT i
2 CONC n 1660. Robert divorced his wife Joane, then living in England, on Aug. 12, 1657 after a fifteen year separation
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/g2g/327168/disputed-parents-rebecca-wade-wife-of-john-owen-connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Disputed Parents? Rebecca Wade wife of John Owen, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Yea or Nay? Parents of Rebecca (Wade) Owen m. to John Owen. They are listed on the profile as Robert Wade and Jemima Rebecca (Wade) Owen. Is a disconnect in order?
2 CONT
2 CONT Savage's Genealogical Dictionary suggests that the wife of John Owen, Rebecca Wade, was "perhaps d. of Robert of Hartford."[1] The Windsor Barbour Collection of Vital Records simply says John Owen married Rebecca Wade, Oct 3, 1650
2 CONC .[2] It does not suggest she was from Hartford. However, Robert was in the right place at the right time to be the father of Rebecca Wade, and Savage's "perhaps" should have lead to further research, not certainty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Savage's entry for Robert Wade mentions his 1657 divorce from Joane, but names no children.[3] If Savage had known of his children, he would have mentioned them. In 1929, an article on John and his family John Owen of Windsor, Con
2 CONC n., and some of his descendants by William Arthur Owen, makes no mention of Rebecca's parentage.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1941 Descendants of John Owen of Windsor, Connecticut (1622-1699), makes the leap from "perhaps" to "certainty" calling Owen's wife "Rebecca Wade of Hartford nearby. The bride was the daughter of Robert and Jemima Wade."[5] Th
2 CONC e author gives no source for this information. Did he make a slip of the pen calling the alleged mother Jemima? Robert had a wife Joane. He divorced Joane in 1657.[6  Clearly Robert did not have a wife Jemima.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition, the distribution of Robert Wade's estate makes no mention of a daughter Rebecca Owen.[7] It would appear he died intestate. He might have left Rebecca out of his will, but a court ordered distribution would include al
2 CONC l his children or their heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Savage:
2 CONT
2 CONT >OWEN, JOHN, Windsor, said to be b. 25 Dec. 1624, m. 3 Oct. 1650, Rebecca Wade, perhaps d. of Robert of Hartford, had Josias, b. 8 Sept. 1651; John, 5 Nov. 1652; d. soon; John, again, 23 Apr. 1654, d. at 16 yrs. ; Nathaniel, 9 Apr
2 CONC . 1656; Daniel, 28 Mar. 1658; Joseph, 23 Oct. 1660; Mary, 5 Dec. 1662; Benjamin, 20 Sept. 1664, d. soon; Rebecca, 28 Mar. 1666; Obadiah, 12 Dec. 1667; and Isaac, 27 May 1670; was freem. 1667, and rem. to Simsbury, and d. 1 Feb. 16
2 CONC 99. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
