2 CONT "Abel Wright married Dec 1, 1659, Martha kitcherel, daug of Samuel K. of Hartford, Conn, and had a family of 13 children (names, dates & spouses listed). He was a citizen of some note, both in the civil and military service of the
2 CONC  town. In 1685 he was elected to the General Court, and in May 1696, Deacon Burt and Lieut. Abel Wright were chosen to answer a petition of the people on the west side of the river asking to become a separate parish and procure a 
2 CONC minister of their own. In 1708, July 26th, Indians came upon the town and despoiled his family, scalping his wife, who died in consequence on the 19th of Oct. following. They also killed an infant of his son Henry, and captured hi
2 CONC s wife, who died soon after. But this venerable ancestor lived until 1725, for his tombstone record says: Lieut. Abel Wright died Oct 29th 1725, aged 94 years."
