2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.com/books?id=X6VPAAAAMAAJ&vq=Nancy%20durand&pg=PA324#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Amos Root, son of Joseph (2824), grandson of Thomas (2895), b. — 3, 1733, at Westfield, Mass. ;
2 CONT
2 CONT  m. (1) March 17, 1756, Abigail, dau. of Benj. and Abigail Sheldon. She d. Oct. 17, 1758. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. (2) Azubah Hubbard;
2 CONT
2 CONT  m. (3) . 
2 CONT
2 CONT His father, Ensign Joseph Root, made a codicil to his will, leaving ,£200 more to his son Amos, "provided he does not learn a trade." Probably he wished him to remain on a farm.* He rem. with his brother Eli to Pittsfield, Mass., 
2 CONC where he remained as late as 1 771, and from thence he rem. to a place then called Benson (now Pittsford), Vt.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children: (By first marriage.) (Born in Pittsfield, Mass.) 3095.
2 CONT
2 CONT  I. Amos, b. July 18, 1757, f. ; d. 1813, as. 56. 3096.
2 CONT
