1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Third wife of Deacon Joseph Hitchcock, of Brimfield
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of:
2 CONT # Sarah b. 3 Oct. 1751 md. John Thompson 
2 CONT # Elisha b. 20 Jan. 1753 md. Ursula Hitchcock 
2 CONT # Peter b. 1 Jul. 1754 md. Ruth Bliss 
2 CONT # Heli b. 8 Mar. 1756 md. Triphena Goodell 
2 CONT # Medad b. 24 Nov. 1757 md. Martha Stebbins 
2 CONT # Aaron b. 22 Jun. 1759 md. Mary Stebbins 
2 CONT # Ruth b. 2 Sep. 1761 md. Isaac Bliss Jr.  
2 CONT # Mary b. 7 Apr. 1763 md. Asahel Goodell 
2 CONT # Bathsheba b. 25 Dec. 1764 md. Vaniah Miller 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary, was the dau. of Henry and Elizabeth (Warriner) Burt, of Springfield, MA. Mary, married Noah Hitchcock, on 28 Nov 1738 in Springfield. Mary and Noah removed to Brimfield, MA, and had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Noah Hitchcock Jr. (1739-1826) Elijah Hitchcock (1741-1813) Mary Hitchcock (1743-1820) 
2 CONT
