1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for NEW HAMPSHIRE.
2 CONT [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A011299  DAR Ancestor #  A011299]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT 129th descendant of Thomas Bliss that came to American in 1635
2 CONT
2 CONT 129. 
2 CONT
2 CONT JONATHAN, jr., of Windsor, Conn., (son of Jonathan Bliss and Sarah  Eggleston, of East Windsor, Conn.,) was born at W., Jan. 4, 1712. On the  20th of January, 1740, he bought the right of Isaac Denslow " in the un-  divided lands 
2 CONC of Windsor ;" and in October, 1743, lot No. 123 was set off to  him; which shows a residence there after he arrived at man's estate. He  removed to Tolland, Conn., — which was originally set off from lands be-  longing to Windsor,
2 CONC  — where he was admitted as an elector, Jan. 28, 1751.  On the 20th of August, 1750, he bought one-half of a lot of 326 acres of  land in Tolland, and is described in the deed as " Jonathan Bliss, of Wind-  sor, in the County of H
2 CONC artford, and Colony of Connecticut." He sold this  on the 28th of January, 1752, when he removed to Gilsum, f N. H. He was  m. to Sybil Fox, who died at G., June 2, 1789. He d. April, 1799. Issue : 
2 CONT
2 CONT 347. *Jonathan, d. Oct. 14, 1799. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 348. *Levi. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 349. Sybil, b. about 1750, m. about 1771 Matthew Dwolf, (or Dolph.) Issue: 1. David, b. 
2 CONT
2 CONT March 11, 1772, m. Aug. 27, 1793, Sallv Borden. 2. Roxsa, b. Jan. 13, 1774. 3. Phi-  delle. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 350. *Abner, b. Nov. 29, 1752, d. May 29, 1812. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 351. *David, b. 1755, d. March 11, 1798. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 352. Anna, b. about 1757, m. Nov. 18, 1777, Stephen Bond, jr., of G. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 353. Thankful is said to have married a Mr. Bond. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/46825358/jonathan-bliss
