1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/46825097/sarah-kilbourn
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Bliss married in Windsor, CT Thomas Mugleston on 13 December 1733. On 2 September 1740, Sarah Mugleston petitioned the Court at Hartford for a divorce from Thomas Mugleston based on the fact he deserted her and their two chi
2 CONC ldren in 1736.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was identified in her father's will, dated 27 October 1737, as "Sarah Mugglestone, alias Sarah Bliss," suggesting she had returned to the use of her maiden name following Thomas Mugleston abandoning her and their children in 1
2 CONC 736. Sarah legally returned to the use of her maiden name following the divorce granted in September 1740, and using her maiden name, Sarah Bliss married in Litchfield, CT Jonathan Kilbourn on 17 September 1740.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Thomas and Sarah (Bliss) Mugleston
2 CONT *i. Mary Mugleston, m. Elisha Birge of Litchfield
2 CONT *ii. Lucy Mugleston, m. Daniel Beach of Litchfield
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Jonathan and Sarah (Bliss) Kilbourn
2 CONT *iii. Elijah, b. 17 Jan 1742/3, d. 27 Jan 1742/3
2 CONT *iv. Joseph, b. 5 Mar 1744/5
2 CONT *v. Lemiel
2 CONT *vi. Jehiel
