2 TITL Mary Corning and Bigget Eggleston Marriage
1 NOTE Biggett Eggleston was born on 12 March 1724 at Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut.  He married Mary Corning of Enfield, Hartford, Connecticut on 7 November 1743. He moved from Windsor Co. to Murrayfield, Hampshire County, Massachusett
2 CONC s and was on the valuation list there in 1768. The town of Murrayfield was re-named to Chester in 1783. About 1784 the family moved to Washington, Hampshire, Massachusetts. Washington is now part of Boston, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT      Source:   Town Records in the original handwriting says "First Book Windsor Births Marriages & Deaths 1638-1704" and later on "Windsor Town Book for the Recording of Births Marriages & Deaths July the 14th AnnoDom 1704 Dated 
2 CONC Sept 7 1720 by Timothy Loomis". On page 53, Bigget Eglestone of Windsor and Mary Corning of Enfield were married Novbr 7th A Dom 1745".
2 CONT
2 CONT Biggett Eggleston (son of Benjamin Eggleston and Mary Dibble) was born 17 Mar 1723/24 in Windsor, Hartford, CT, and died date unknown. He married Mary Corning on 7 Nov 1745 in CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Biggett Eggleston and Mary Corning:
2 CONT Marriage: 7 Nov 1745, CT.
2 CONT Biggett Eggleston was born on 12 March 1724 at Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut.
2 CONT He married Mary Corning of Enfield, Hartford, Connecticut on 7 November 1743. He moved from Windsor Ct. to Murrayfield, Hampshire County, Massachusetts and was on the valuation list there in 1768. The town of Murrayfield was re-na
2 CONC med to Chester in 1783. About 1784 the family moved to Washington, Hampshire, Massachusetts. Washington is now part of Boston, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Biggett Eggleston and Mary Corning are:
2 CONT Jehiel Eggleston, b. 17 Feb 1745/46, Windsor, Hartford, CT, d. 7 Nov 1790, Westfield, Hartford, CT.
