1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Removed Date Place and circa Death Date''' – Without sources to validate either one, it can be misleading to enter insupportable data. Yes, all the children listed below were born to Samuel and Sarah in Glastonb
2 CONC ury. However, as of 17 Dec 2022, I find no record proving a death place or date for Samuel. – (Ken Shelley)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A ''Tributaries'' write up and a ''Wikitree'' profile show excellent research about Samuel.''' While, ''Wikitree'' shows "1723" as Samuel's death year, ''Tributaries'' proves him being alive at least to the date posted in the d
2 CONC ata above. Both write-ups are linked to at the bottom. 
2 CONT ''Samuel's place of death and burial are unknown, but it's implausible to think the events occurred anywhere other than Connecticut.'' 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Marriage====
2 CONT >'''On page 103''' of ''U.S., New England Marriages Prior to 1700'', is shows the following: "Brooks, Samuel & Sarah __?__ b   1690; Simsbury". 
2 CONT >I think the chronicler entered "1690" meaning the year of marriage. However, did he mean this unknown Sarah was born was born or married in Simsbury? This question may find no answer in extant sources.
2 CONT >''' FYI:''' I live in a town that borders Simsbury. My wife works in Glastonbury.
2 CONT
