1 NOTE On May 26, 1674, he gave land in Fairfield to his dau. Priscilla wife of
2 CONT Cornelius Seeley; and it was recorded, 25 Nov 1678, that Thomas Bedient had
2 CONT land by gift from his father-in-law, Capt. Richard Osborn.
1 NOTE Colonial grant of 80 acres, May 1671, for service in Pequot War.
1 NOTE Sailed from London in 1634, Came to Hingham, Mass., 1635  , ; removed to
2 CONT Windsor, CT, with first settlers, and served in Pequot War 1637. He came to
2 CONT New Haven, 1639, and moved to Fairfield by 1652. He settled in Westchester, NY
2 CONT by 1682, and died there abt. 1685.
1 NOTE At New Haven, he signed the Fundamental Agreement, June 1639, and took the
2 CONT oath of allegiance, 1644; had three in his family, 1641; sold his property
2 CONT there in Apr and May 1652
