1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Find A Grave.com:  Matthew Osborne, II, son of Matthew Osborne I (Norse Ozbun) of England who immigrated to America in 1661 and settled in Pennsylvania for a few years before moving to Delaware where some of h
2 CONC is children were born.  Mathew Jr. married Isabella Dobson October 16,1723, in Duck Creek Monthly Meeting, Quaker Friends Church in Sussex County, Delaware. They then went south to Virginia before moving on to Centre, Rowan County
2 CONC , North Carolina, which was largely a Quaker settlement.  He owned a blacksmith shop and owned a shop that manufactured wood and steel articles and was a gun smith.
2 CONT
2 CONT Since Matthew and family had to walk about 18 miles to Monthly Meetings and were meeting in private homes, he and several friends felt that a church was needed for their little community.  Matthew along with four friends secured t
2 CONC itle to a tract of seven acres of land and were granted a Meeting for worship in 1757 and built their first meeting house in 1763.  The Monthly Meeting was established in 1772.  Since the location was half way between Cane Creek a
2 CONC nd New Garden it seemed only natural that the name of "Center" ("Centre") be chosen.  It was a log structure twenty feet square with a dirt floor and a rock fireplace and chimney in one end.  It was used until 1780 and a stone mar
2 CONC ker, erected at its site in 1928, carries an engraved picture of the building.  Among the recorded names of charter members of Centre Monthly Meeting Church are those of Mathew Osborne and son Thomas Osborne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mathew was buried in the Centre Friends Meeting Cemetery in Greensboro, Guilford County, North Carolina, and his headstone there reads as follows:  Mathew II Son of Mathew Osborne I (Norse Ozbun) of England Came From Penn to North
2 CONC  Carolina 1753, Died 1783, Wife, Isabell Dobson, died 1770.  The reverse side of the monument reads as follows:  Sons and Daughter of Matthew II:  Sarah - Wives of William - Rebecca Cox; Matthew - M. Reynolds; Samuel - Eliz. Lamb;
2 CONC  John - SA Bullard; Joseph - M. Angell; David - Ly. Davis; Daniel - Mar. Stout.  History Under Shaft.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella Dobson Osborne (1700 - 1770)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT William Osborne (1725 - 1768)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mathew Osborne (1729 - 1816)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Osborne (1734 - 1819)
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Osborne (1736 - 1807)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Osborne Frazier (1737 - 1784)
2 CONT
