2 DATE 29 SEP 1733
2 ADDR
3 CITY Windsor
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} >'''Nathaniel named no (''surviving'') son or daughter in his 1729 Will.'''
2 CONT >''Hartford, Connecticut Probate Records, 1729-1750'', Vol. 3 at [https://archive.org/details/digestofearlycon03manw/page/80/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.org].
2 CONT >'''The two attached person-profiles attached as children are not viably sourced.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From: Loomis, Elias, "Descendants of Joseph Loomis in America, and his antecedents in the Old world"; Berea, Ohio: Loomis, 1909.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Lt. Nathaniel; born 20 Mar 1656/57; died 29 Sep 1733 at age 76. married Elizabeth Ellsworth, daughter of Sgt. Josiah Ellsworth and Elizabeth Holcombe, 23 Dec 1680; He left a will on 26 May 1729.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Ellsworth on 23 DEC 1680 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut[1] "Nathaniel son of Nathaniel Loomys married Elizabeth Elfworth he 24 years .. she 23 years..." Matthew Grant Record, Early Windsor Records.
2 CONT
2 CONT It appears children did not survive him; none named in his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Estate 
2 CONT
2 CONT From “A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records: Hartford district, 1729-1750 edited by Charles William Manwaring. Page 80 - 81.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=g9QLAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA80&ots=3cMN2tsULb&dq=Lt.%20Nathaniel%2
2 CONC 0Loomis&pg=PA81#v=onepage&q&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT Loomis, Lt. Nathaniel, Windsor. Invt. £517-05-03. Taken 21 October, 1733, by William Wolcott, Hezekiah Porter and Samuel Bancroft. Will dated 26 May, 1729.
2 CONT
2 CONT *I, Nathaniel Loomis of Windsor, being now stricken in age, do make this my last will and testament: 
2 CONT *I give to my wife Elizabeth the use of the whole of my estate during widowhood, and 1-2 the moveables to be at her own dispose.
2 CONT *I give to my brother Daniel Loomis my meadow at Podunk, he paying my sister Mindwell Loomis £20. 
2 CONT * I give to my brother Hezekiah Loomis land I bought of Nathaniel Bissell, he paying to my brother's children, Jonathan and Ebenezer, £5 apiece.
2 CONT * I give to my brother Moses the homestead with the buildings, he paying to my brother Josiah Loomis £25 within two years after possession.
2 CONT * I give to Daniel Gillett, and, that part of the lott which I bought of Nathaniel Bissell west of the country road, he paying Hepzibah Loomis £30. 
2 CONT *The rest of my moveable estate not disposed of I give to be equally divided amongst my sisters and my wife's brothers and sisters living, and the children of those decd.
2 CONT * I make my wife Elizabeth, with Daniel Gillet, my executors. 
2 CONT *Witness: Richard Skinner, Nathan1el Loom1s, Ls.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/133356277/nathaniel-lomis
