1 NOTE Settled at Torrington, a little north of Dr. Elkanah Hodges (Orcutt). Stiles says he was married twice.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to: Stiles, Henry, History of Ancient Windsor, Vol. II:Pg. 437 and Deanna Bowman, Thomas Holcombe, Vol. I, pg. 37:   Abraham Loomis was born December 13, 1696.  He married Isabel Eggleston February 5, 1718. Isabel was bo
2 CONC rn January 25, 1697. Isabel was the daughter of Thomas Eggleston and Grace Hoskins. They rem. to Torrington, and was living there in 1761, where his wife and daughters Isabela and Jerusha joined the church on 17 July 1754.
2 CONT
2 CONT He rec'd £10 for hiring a man into the army in 1779. He was made freeman in 1777, and was one of the 136 Torrington Twp. patentees, 1732.
