2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Has errors!!
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogy of the Jones Family: ... the Descendants of Benajmin Jones who ...” By George Russell Jones [https://archive.org/details/genealogyofjones00jone/page/6/mode/2up Archive.Org]
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 sons
2 CONT
2 CONT (2.) BENJAMIN JONES, [the second, son of Benjamin Jones, the first and Hannah Spencer Jones, was born at Bedford, Conn., 1662. NO!] He married Elizabeth, his wife, the year 1684. 
2 CONT
2 CONT To this union six sons were born: 
2 CONT *Thomas Jones, born 1686; 
2 CONT *Ebenezer, born 1690, married Priscilla Smith, in 1713, settled in Somers, Conn.;
2 CONT * Eleazer, born April 12, 1693, married Mahetabel Gary, in 1719, also settled in Somers; 
2 CONT *Benjamin, third, born 1710, at Somers, Conn.; 
2 CONT *Levi, born 1716; 
2 CONT *Zebulon, born 1723. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The records show that a land grant was issued to Benjamin Jones, second, in the year 1686. He moved from Enfield to Somers, Conn., in 1706, and was the first settler in that vicinity, living on the lands during summer and moving b
2 CONC ack to town in the winter, and at other times when danger was apprehended, but did not make permanent home until 1713.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was the practice of Benjamin Jones to ride on horseback to his new settlement. It was deemed in those times very dangerous for a man to emigrate five or ten miles into the forest. If he exceeded that distance, his funeral sermo
2 CONC n surely would be preached. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1754, 92 years of age. [NO!]
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Somers, Conn., in Ye Olden Times, By Austin Chapman.
2 CONT
2 CONT * BENJAMIN JONES as he passed around 
2 CONT * Was the first to greet this noble town, 
2 CONT * For seven long years he lived alone, 
2 CONT * Then five neighbors from Enfield street 
2 CONT * Came to the place and there did meet. 
2 CONT * The venturesome man that owned the land 
2 CONT * Where all the emigrants first made stand 
2 CONT * Soon came twelve families more. 
2 CONT * Those numbers then made near a score, 
2 CONT * And from such numbers they formed a plan 
2 CONT * To establish a church, the first on the land.
