1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Omstead, Gideon (c. 1760-1797) came from the United States to Townsend Township, Norfolk County in 1793 and married Elizabeth Cooley. Includes four generations of descendants in Norfolk and Essex Counties, and in I
2 CONC owa and Oklahoma and elsewhere. Descendant surnames included: Warden, Swanton, Evans, Chapin, Nailor, Flynn, Turner, Limage, Casey, Dunn, Watson. Stephen Olmstead (1787-1854) came from Canaan, Columbia County, New York to Norfolk 
2 CONC County by 1817 and married widow Mary (Barber) Gilbert and settled in Middleton Township. Includes children and grandchildren in Norfolk County and in Michigan and elsewhere. Descendant surnames included: Snively, Thomson.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sites.google.com/site/longpointsettlers/settlers-o
2 CONT
2 CONT  FamilySearch Family Tree
2 CONT Birth:	Nov 3 1761 - Greenwich, Hampshire, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America
2 CONT Death:	1827 - Lyme Township, Huron, Ohio, United States
2 CONT Parents:	Gideon Cooley, Elisabeth Cooley (born Osborn)
2 CONT Spouses:	Israel Gideon Olmstead, Joshua Fairchild
2 CONT Children:	Jonas Olmstead, Pollie Olmstead, Israel Olmstead, Abigail Warner (born Olmstead), Jonathan Olmstead, Solomon Olmstead, Harvey Olmstead, and names of 7 more children
2 CONT Siblings:	Gideon Cooley, Jacob Cooley, Luther Cooley, Abigail Omsted (born Cooley), Mary Whiting (born Cooley), Charles Cooley, Keziah Cooley
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LHTD-8QT/elizabeth-cooley-1761-1827
2 CONT When Elizabeth Cooley was born on 3 November 1761, in Greenwich, Hampshire, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America, her father, Gideon Cooley, was 30 and her mother, Elisabeth Osborn, was 21. She married Israel Gideon 
2 CONC Olmstead about 1777, in Northampton, Hampshire, Massachusetts, United States. They were the parents of at least 5 sons and 3 daughters. She lived in Greenwich, Hampshire, Massachusetts, United States in 1761. She died in 1827, in 
2 CONC Lyme Township, Huron, Ohio, United States, at the age of 66, and was buried in Portland Township, Erie, Ohio, United States.
