1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Second Wife: Sarah Hale''' 
2 CONT After Elizabeth's death, Cummings married Sarah Hale of Springfield, Massachusetts, around 1757. 
2 CONT Their children are:
2 CONT
2 CONT Heman Pease: Born in 1757 in Enfield; he was a Revolutionary War patriot who later lived in Longmeadow and died there in 1828.
2 CONT
2 CONT David Pease: Born after 1757; he is identified as a half-brother to the children of Elizabeth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Most of these children were born in Enfield, Connecticut, before the family branch became more closely associated with East Longmeadow and Wilbraham, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Parentage
2 CONT She was the daughter of Thomas Hale and Thankful Jones. Her parents were early settlers of the Springfield and Enfield area.
