1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James was christened 21 Sept 1615 in New Malton, York, England[1] to Bigod Egglestonne.
2 CONT
2 CONT James and his father Begatt Eglstone were declared Freemen, 21 May 1657.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT James Eggleston served in the [Pequot War][3][4] and was granted 50 acres of land for his service.[5][6]
2 CONT
2 CONT James was involved in a few court actions:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Jeames Egleston, defendt in an Action of the Case dammages 39s.[7]
2 CONT 2. Jeames Egleston, ‘’In the Action betweene John Bissell plt Contra Jeames Egleston defendt the Courte findes for the defendt[8]
2 CONT James Eglstone sworne Counstable in Windzor for the yeare insuing. (1658)[9] James contributed to help the poor of Connecticut.[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Egleston, James, Windsor died on the 1st of December, 1679 as listed in his will. Invt. £275-16-06. Taken 24 December 1679, by Benjamin Newbery, Daniel Clarke, Jonathan Gillett, Mark Kelsey. Legatees: The Relict (his wife); John, 
2 CONC age 21 March next; Thomas 13, Ester 16, Nathaniel 13, Isaac 10, Abigail 8, Deborah 5, Hanna 3 years of age.[11] His date of death is listed as 2 December 1679 in Windsor town records.[12][13][14]
2 CONT
2 CONT James' wife was Hester Kelsey, daughter of William and Hester (Unknown) Kelsey, early settlers of Hartford. It is reported that she was the first English child born in Hartford. She became the wife of Jacques Eno and John Williams
2 CONC .[15]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James and Hester (Kelsey) Eggleston:[16]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. James
2 CONT 2. John
2 CONT 3. Thomas
2 CONT 4. Hester
2 CONT 5. Nathaniel
2 CONT 6. Isaac
2 CONT 7. Abigail
2 CONT 8. Deborah
2 CONT 9. Hannah
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Eggleston-272
2 CONT '''<nowiki>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</nowiki>'''
2 CONT '''James Eggleston (1617 - 1679)''', son of Bygod Eggleston and Mary Talcott, was born 1617 at Norwich, Norfolk, England, and died at the age of 62 on 1 December 1679 at Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut. He married '''Hester Kelsey 
2 CONC (1636 - 1720)''', daughter of William Kelsey. He emigrated from England to Boston, Massachusetts in March 1630 aboard the Mary and John. James Eggleston served in the Pequot Indian War. He became a freeman in 1637. He was named in
2 CONC  his father's will and in 1671 was granted 50 acres for military service.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children of James and Hester Eggleston==
2 CONT # James Eggleston (1 January 1656 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut - 29 December 1746 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut)
2 CONT # John Eggleston (27 March 1659 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut - 10 March 1731 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut)
2 CONT # Thomas Eggleston (27 July 1661 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut - 6 April 1732 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut)
2 CONT # Hester Eggleston (1 December 1663 Windsor, Connecticut - 1698 Enfield, Connecticut)
2 CONT # Nathaniel Eggleston, (15 August 1666 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut - date unknown, Westfield, Massachusetts)
2 CONT # Isaac Eggleston (27 February 1669 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut - 30 January 1753 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut)
2 CONT # Abigail Eggleston (1 September 1671 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut - 30 January 1753 Enfield, Hartford, Connecticut)
2 CONT # Deborah Eggleston (1 May 1674 Windsor or Wintonbury, Hartford, Connecticut - date unknown)
2 CONT # Hannah Eggleston (19 December 1676 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut - 28 January 1761 Lebanon, Connecticut)
2 CONT # Joseph Eggleston (1677 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut - 5 September 1767 Stonington, New London, Connecticut)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT *Bygod Eggleston and Mary Talcott had two sons named James. This is the second, who was born several years after the first died in infancy. Both were sons of MARY TALCOTT.
2 CONT * James Eggleston's wife, Hester Kelsey, was also called Esther. He only had one wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notable Descendants==
2 CONT James Eggleston was the great-great-great-grandfather of abolitionist John Brown.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
