2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/CONYERS1.htm#Catherine This URL shows an outstanding Conyers family tree with the Conyers mother of Dorothy Bigod recorded on the lineages. It states that Dorothy married first, Roger Radcliffe. They h
2 CONC ad children probably by about 1546-7. Dorothy Radcliffe (2) was one of them and then it states that she (2) was the one who married Miles Harker having children by about 1563, Margaret Harker born circa 1565, plus Elizabeth bc1563
2 CONC  d Dec.1637. Dorothy's step-son Ralph bc1560 d Oct.1637 with other step-siblings like Richard bc1553 are known from her husband's first wife. These are mistakenly listed with Dorothy Radcliffe (1) but if Dorothy Radcliffe's (2) na
2 CONC me is clicked, it is seen that (2) married Miles Harker by 1563 and would be the mother of the last two Harker children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Quote from Tudorplace.com.ar/CONYERS, the link given above:
2 CONT
2 CONT  "DOROTHY RADCLIFFE Father: ROGER RADCLIFFE of Tunstall
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Dorothy BIGOD
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Miles HARKER"
2 CONT
2 CONT  Roger Radcliffe and Dorothy had a son also named Francis Radcliffe born about 1548. This son was said to be the last Radcliffe to live at Mulgrave Castle, near Whitby, Yorkshire.This leaves room then for Dorothy Bigod to have Rad
2 CONC cliffe children before 1550. So there were two Dorothy's descending from Catherine and Francis Bigod: Dorothy Radcliffe (1) and the next generation, Dorothy Radcliffe (2) who married Miles Harker and in 1581 Robert Lamb. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Margaret and Dorothy Harker: By Rosalie Eggleston, Ph.D., and Linda Eggleston McBroom: "Richard Harker's will also shows that the Dorothy named in Miles Harker's will was not his first wife and not the mother of Richard 
2 CONC who calls her his mother-in-law, meaning stepmother. After the death of Miles, Dorothy Harker married Robert Lamb on 13 August 1581. These facts make the theory about Dorothy Bigod look very absurd. " (authors are pointing out the
2 CONC  impossibility that Dorothy Bigod (Radcliffe) (1) could have married Miles Harker and then Robert Lamb well after she died.) However the next generation Dorothy Radcliffe (2) bc1546, which the authors have admitted did exist, woul
2 CONC d be the Dorothy who married Miles and Mr. Lamb.
2 CONT
2 CONT Miles Harker married the second time to Dorothy Radcliffe (2). His first children before 1563 were all born to his first wife. They were: Richard c1553, Isabel 1554, George 1555, Thomas 1556, Agnes 1558, and Ralph b1559 died 1637.
2 CONC  Dorothy(2) bore Miles one more son named Radolphi in1561 and then at least two daughters: Elizabeth Nicholson c1563-1637 and Margaret Eggleston c1565 d before 1603. Then she had more children by another marriage after 1574 and Mi
2 CONC les died. Second marriage was in 1581 to Robert Lamb..
