1 NOTE The Eggleston family name appears in old records with a variety of spellings, including: Egleston, Eggelston, Egelston, Eggliston, Egliston, and several others.
2 CONT The original will in the Latin of James Eggleston, as well as the parish and the baptismal font at All Saint's Parish in  Settrington, Yorkshire, England where their son Bygod was baptized, are still standing and in use today.
2 CONT James and Margaret Harker had four children between 1586 and 1595, including Bygod Eggleston.
2 CONT In his marriage to Juliana Frear, they had four children between1603 and 1611.My 8th Great Grandfather James (Jacobus) Eggleston probably born in 1552 at Settrington, Yorkshire, England. He was buried on 30 March 1613 at Settringt
2 CONC on in the All Saint's Parish churchyard. He married twice. He probably first married Margaret Harker. They had four children between 1586 and 1595. Margaret was the daughter of Miles Harker. James also married Juliana Frear. They 
2 CONC had four children between 1603 and 1611. She was the daughter of John Frear. Juliana Frear married William Bainton on 15 June 1614. She was buried on 8 January 1636 or 1637, just a week after she wrote her will. It was probated in
2 CONC  February 1637 or 1638. William Bainton's will was dated 4 December 1632.
2 CONT James (Jacobus) Eggleston was probably born in 1552 at Settrington, England. He was buried on 30 March 1613 at Settrington (?). He married twice.
2 CONT He probablly first married Margaret Harker. They had four children between 1586 and 1595. Margaret was the daughter of Miles HARKER. To read the will of Miles HARKER go to the paper titled, "HARKER".
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Eggleston and Margaret Harker:
2 CONT 	i. Bygod Eggleston was baptized on 20 February 1586 / 1587.
2 CONT 	ii. Dorothy Eggleston was baptized about 1589. She married a Barwicke, and she was living at Norwich when her stepmother, Juliana Frear died in 1636 /1637.
2 CONT 	iii. Elizabeth Eggleston was baptized on 8 October 1592.
2 CONT 	iv. Jane Eggleston was baptized on 2 Nov 1595. She married Samuel Clarke at St. Peter Mancroft, Norwich, in November 1632. She was living at Norwich when her stepmother, Juliana FREAR died.
2 CONT James also married Juliana Frear. They had four children between 1603 and 1611. She was the daughter of John Frear.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juliana Frear married William Bainton on 15 June 1614. She was buried on 8 January 1636 / 1637, just a week after she wrote her will. It was probated in February 1637 / 1638.
2 CONT (See "Frear" to read her entire will). William Bainton's will was dated 4 December 1632.
2 CONT Children of James Eggleston and Juliana Frear:   (notice a gap of nearly eight years)
2 CONT 	v. James Eggleston Jr. was baptized on 19 June 1603.
2 CONT 	vi. John Eggleston was baptized on 6 April 1606.
2 CONT 	vii. Margaret Eggleston was baptized on 28 February 1608. She married John AVISON on 27 July 1635. She married Roger Thorpe on 20 May 1639.
2 CONT 	viii. Alice Eggleston was baptized about 1611. She married a BURNBY.
