2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Disputed origins
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Denslow-45
2 CONT
2 CONT >Anderson discusses other children reported by different authors, saying that Stiles includes sons Henry and John (but ignores the daughters); Anderson says that these two boys are certainly not Nicholas', but are possibly nephews
2 CONC  or more distant kinsmen. Anderson also mentions that Roberts identifies a Nicholas Denslow, who married in 1634 in Netherbury, as a son of this Nicholas. He never came to New England, and Anderson says there is no reason to belie
2 CONC ve he is a son of Nicholas Denslow of Windsor (this profile).[2] Savage reports that Nicholas and wife Elizabeth had no sons; only two daughters, Joan and Temperance.[13]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:John_Denslow_%282%29
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 6/7/1655 at Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut to Mary Eggleston
2 CONT
2 CONT MARY, 2nd known child of Bigod Eggleston by his 2nd wife, was born say 1636. She married at Windsor 7 June 1655 John Denslow. (He was not son of NICHOLAS DENSLOW.) 
