2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Pettibone-17 WikiTree Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 12 2016, 1:37:59 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sarah was born in 1667. She is the daughter of John Pettibone and Sarah Eggleston. She passed away in 1748.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Birth 24 SEP 1667 Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT 
2 CONT     Death 3 APR 1748 Windsor, Hartford Co, CT 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah and John Mills settled in West Simsbury (now called Canton) when they were married. They had five children in the first six years of their marriage, of whom two, Joseph and Benjamin, were twins. A family history of the Mills
2 CONC  family tells that the twins were carried seven miles to be baptized, their mother riding on horseback while their father and a friend carried a basket containing the two infants. [Mills, The Mills Family, 8] Since it was the cust
2 CONC om to have infants baptized as soon after they were a week old as possible, this hilly seven mile journey probably took place in December of a Connecticut winter.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Mills died 11 Mar 1698, when only about thirty years old. At the time of his death he held the position of constable, entrusted with collecting the County rates. A constable's duties included being captain of the watch, or ch
2 CONC ief of police, of the town in which he lived. He was the embodiment of the law. In fact, for many years, in the Colony of Connecticut the appointment of a constable by the court was considered a valid incorporation of a town, whic
2 CONC h town became thenceforth liable for taxation and entitled to representation. On 6 July 1699, Sarah (Pettibone) Mills married a second time. Her second husband, John Humphrey, was a son of Sergeant John and Hannah (Griffin) Humphr
2 CONC ey and grandson of Michael and Priscilla (Grant) Humphrey and John and Anna (Bancroft) Griffin, all of whom were earliest settlers of Simsbury [Stiles, Ancient Windsor 2:416]. It was John Humphrey, Jr.’s, ﬁrst marriage, but he alr
2 CONC eady had a home on his farm in Simsbury, and Sarah and her family moved there when she and John were married. (See John Humphrey's biography for further details. Sources 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of John Mills — married 4 Nov 1690 (to 11 Mar 1698) in Simsbury, Hartford, Connecticut map icon
2 CONT Wife of John Humphrey — married 6 Jul 1699 in Simsbury, Hartford, Connecticut Colony
2 CONT
