1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph Pettibone was born 11 MAR 1688/89 in Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT, and died 14 SEP 1762 in Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT. He was the son of John Pettibone and Sarah Eggleston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 
2 CONT #Thanks Shepard BEF 1715, daughter of Abraham Shepard and Judith Sills. She was born 30 JUN 1683 in Concord MA, and died 2 NOV 1724 in Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT.  Widow of the second Daniel Adams.
2 CONT #Hannah Large 11 MAY 1726 in Simsbury CT, daughter of Simon Large and Hannah Long. She died 16 APR 1758 in Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Thankful (Shepard) Adams and Joseph Pettibone are:
2 CONT * i.	Joseph Pettibone was born 26 FEB 1713/14.
2 CONT * ii.	Mary Pettibone was born 28 JUL 1718.
2 CONT * iii.	Bathsheba Pettibone was born 25 APR 1721
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hannah Large and Joseph Pettibone are:
2 CONT
2 CONT * i.	Abel Pettibone was born 17 DEC 1727.
2 CONT * ii.	Hannah Pettibone was born 29 OCT 1730.
2 CONT * iii.	Timothy Pettibone was born 29 DEC 1734.
2 CONT * iv.	Joseph Pettibone was born 13 DEC 1736, and died 28 MAY 1737.
2 CONT * v. Dudley Pettibone was born 3 AUG 1742
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Joseph Pettibone was abstracted in The Connecticut Nutmegger, vol. 39 (2006), p. 278. He names daughter Bathsheba Grimes and granddaughters Mary, Basheba, and Thanks Canada. This tells us that Mary was likely older tha
2 CONC n Bathsheba and Thanks, that Robert Kanada and his daughter Eleanor were apparently dead by 11 Aug. 1762, when the will was written, and that Bathsheba had remarried by that date.
2 CONT
2 CONT Named in his father’s Will:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pettibone’s will, dated 2 December 1707, and a codicil dated 1 November 1711, are ﬁled in the Connecticut State Library, as is an inventory of his estate, taken 22 July 1713. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >”... I give to my son Joseph Pettebone the other half of my house and homested and the land adjacent, the other half of my Nod Meadow lot, and the other moiety of my lot upon Second Brook. ...”
2 CONT
