1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Anne Pettibone Holcomb=
2 CONT * BIRTH 11 Mar 1679 Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 12 May 1753 (aged 74) East Granby, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL East Granby Cemetery, East Granby, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * Latitude: 41.94163, Longitude: -72.72618
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 33361772 photo added by Curt Miller
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT Anne (Pettibone) Holcomb was the wife of Ensign John Holcomb, who is also buried in this cemetery. She died at age 73. John was born at Simsbury, Hartford, Ct.  He died 11 JUL 1744 in Simsbury Hartford Ct.  John's Father was Natha
2 CONC niel Holcomb b: 4 NOV 1648 in Windsor Ct. and mother was Mary Bliss b: 23 SEP 1651.  Anne Pettibone married John on 9 MAR 1706 in Simsbury Hartford Ct.  They had 8 children (Ann, Dinah, John, Hester, Moses, Asahel, Martha, and Sar
2 CONC ah) of Anne Pettibone Holcomb (including 2 deceased) are listed in her will that follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Last Will & Testement==
2 CONT In ye name of God amen, I Ane Holcomb in ye County of Hartford being now by ye providence of God very sick and weak as to boddey but of a sound mind and memory at ____ sent Blessed Be God for ye same yet knowing ye it is appointed
2 CONC  for all mankind once to Die. I do therefore make and ordain this my Last will and testament in manner and form as followeth and first I resign my Soul to God ye Giver thereof and my bodey I give to be buried with a decent Christi
2 CONC an burial at ye discretion of my Executors and as to ye good things of this Life that God in his good providence hath blest mewith I do dispose of ye same as followeth viz.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the payment my funeral charges and all my just debts and dues I hereby give and bequeath to my son, John, my cane and a pare of tongs ye before mentioned cane to be his during his life after his decease to return to Asahel h
2 CONC is brother and to his son Asahel forever.
2 CONT And to the heirs of my son Moses deceased I do give five shillings to be paid out of my estate and to ye heirs of my daughter Ane deceased I do give five shillings.
2 CONT
2 CONT And to my daughter Dinah I do give my Bible and riding hood.
2 CONT And to Sarah my daughter I do give my short cloke.
2 CONT And to my four Daughters now surviving namely, Dinah, Ester, Martha & Sarah I do give all the rest of my estate to be divided in equal proportions between them.
2 CONT And I do hearby appoint my son John and Joseph Phelps Jr. to be my Executors to this my Last will and testament as witness my hand signed seal and delivered and published as my Last will and testament April 21st 1753. Signed with 
2 CONC her mark Ane Holcomb.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inscription'''
2 CONT Here Lies
2 CONT ye Body of
2 CONT Mrs Anna ye
2 CONT Wife of Mr
2 CONT John Holcomb
2 CONT She Died may
2 CONT ye 12 1753
2 CONT in the 74th Year
2 CONT of her age.
2 CONT
