1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Evidence needed to support as the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Andrews/6000000184876103834, daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Francis-Andrews-of-Hartford-Fairfield/6000000000658142798?
2 CONC through=6000000184876103834
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Disputed Origins 
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Andrus''' Gibbs
2 CONT * BIRTH	1635 - Exeter, City of Exeter, Devon, England
2 CONT * DEATH	13 Jan 1696 (aged 60–61) Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL	Spring Grove Cemetery, Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA 
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID	152717633 · View Source
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/152717633/elizabeth-gibbs
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Andrews, daughter of Francis Andrews and Anna, was mentioned in the 1662 will of her father.[1] She was born perhaps in Hartford, about 1643 based on baptism of brother in 1646. Jacobus has no further records.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Gibbs-847
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile is part of the Gibbs Name Study.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob was the son and eldest child of Giles Gibbs and Kathern Carwithe - he was baptized on 28 March 1629/30 at St. Sidwell, Exeter, England.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT An island in the Windsor Rivulet, at a place the Indians called Matumpsech, opposite the point called 'Indian Neck', was deeded to Jacob Gibbs 26 May 1670 by the Indian owner, Sepanquet, son of Sassohegan.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Andrus/Androus/Andrews 4 Dec 1657 - their children were:[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Mary, - born April 21 Apr 1659
2 CONT # Abigail, - born 7 Jan 1661/2
2 CONT # Jacob, born 1 Dec 1664. Died an infant.
2 CONT # Jacob, Jr., born 22 Jun 1666. First wife, Elizabeth, Second wife, Abigail Osband.
2 CONT # Sarah, born 23 Feb1668/9. Married Samuel Bronson.
2 CONT # Elizabeth, born 1 Apr 1670. Died an infant.
2 CONT # Elizabeth, born 13 Sep 1672.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob died 1 Mar 1708/9 at Windsor, Connecticut. "[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Gibbs-847
2 CONT # Rasmussen, James A. The Gibbs Family of Windsor CT, The American Genealogist (The American Genealogist, Barrington, RI, 1985), page 33. View with NEHGS membership.
2 CONT # Some Early Records and Documents of and Relating to the Town of Windsor, Connecticut, 1639-1703 (The Connecticut Historical Society, Hartford, 1930) Page 43-4.
2 CONT # Connecticut: Vital Records (The Barbour Collection), 1630-1870 (Online Database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2011.) From original typescripts, Lucius Barnes Barbour Collection, 1928. Volume:
2 CONC  Windsor, Page: 112. [Original: 2:236][1]
2 CONT # Anderson, Robert Charles. The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633 (New England Historic Genealogical Society, Boston, 1995), page 578. View with NEHGS Membership.
2 CONT # CT Marriages, pre-1870 (Barbour Collection)
2 CONT # CT Death & Burials Index
2 CONT # CT Wills & Probate Records
