1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Patriot DAR ancestor # A022915
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo, REF.: <http://www.geni.com/people/Lieutenant-Thomas-Catlin/6000000026976658558>
2 CONT
2 CONT REVOLUTIONARY WAR VETERAN:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Catlin was a Second Lieutenant in the Litchfield Co. commanded by Captain Abraham Bradley, which formed a part of six battalions (Second Battalion, Wadsworth's Brigade, Fifth Company), ordered by The General Assembly in Jun
2 CONC e 1776, to be raised to march to New York to join the Continental Army. On September 4th, following, he was taken prisoner by the British Troops on New York Island, and confined eleven days in close jail. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Finally on December 25th, 1776, he with two-hundred and twenty-five others was put on board the Glasgow at New York, to be carried to Connecticut for exchange. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1777, Thomas Catlin was voted one of a committee to purchase and provide clothing to the Continental Army, from Litchfield Co., Connecticut. In 1780 Thomas Catlin of Litchfield was appointed one of the inspectors of rations for
2 CONC  the army.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Connecticut in the Revolution, pg. 395
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref. Sons of the Revolution Annual, 1895 and 1896 page 295:
2 CONT
2 CONT "...THOMAS CATLIN (1737-1829, of Litchfield, Connecticut who was appointed by the General Assembly, in June, 1776, 2d Lieutenant of the 5th company, under Captain Abraham Bradley, in the regiment of Colonel Fisher Gay, which was a
2 CONC ssigned to the brigade commanded by General Wadsworth, composed of six battalions raised to reinforce Washington around New York.  He served at the Brooklyn front and in the battle of Long Island, and was taken prisoner in the ret
2 CONC reat from New York, September 15, 1776. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT A Guide to the Oliver Wolcott, Sr. Papers at the Connecticut Historical Society: 1	5	Vol. I Letters to and from Oliver Wolcott; Oliver Wolcott's commission as brigadier general; deposition of Lt. Thomas Catlin (prisoner of war). J
2 CONC anuary - May, 1777 (10 items)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Photo and info ref.:  < https://findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=16419021 >, Lieut Thomas Catlin, East Cemetery, Litchfield, Litchfield County, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT REVOLUTIONARY WAR VETERAN:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Catlin was a Second Lieutenant in the Litchfield Co. commanded by Capitan Abraham Bradley, which formed a part of six battalions (Second Batallion, Wadsworth's Brigade, Fifth Company), ordered by The General Assembly in Jun
2 CONC e 1776, to be raised to march to New York to join the Continental Army. On September 4th, following, he was taken prisoner by the British Troups on New York Island, and confined eleven days in close jail.
2 CONT
2 CONT Finally on December 25th, 1776, he with two-hundred and twenty-five others was put on board the Glasgow at New York, to be carried to Connecticut for exchange.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1777, Thomas Catlin was voted one of a committee to purchase and provide clothing to the Continental Army, from Litchfield Co., Connecticut. In 1780 Thomas Catlin of Litchfield was appointed one of the inspectors of rations for
2 CONC  the army.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Connecticut in the Revolution, pg. 395
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was the son of Thomas Catlin and Abigail Bissell. He married Avis Buell on December 25, 1763 in Litchfield Co., CT. They had six children, Thomas 3rd, Truman, Abel (Dr.), Levi, Avis, and Ann Catlin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth: 	Jun. 18, 1737 Litchfield County Connecticut, USA Death: 	Dec. 9, 1829 Litchfield County Connecticut, USA
2 CONT
