1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In his earlier life, he made several trips to sea as a whaleman.  While a resident of Litchfield, CT, he lived between the present addresses of Maj. David Marsh and Gen. Buel (On the west side of the street about a
2 CONC  mile and a half north of the court house)  During the revolution, he entered the British Army as Quarter Master; and subsequently served as Lieutenant of Artillery.  In 1780, he moved to Castleton, VT.  He lived here until 1798, 
2 CONC then emigrated to Canada.  He was a tanner and currier, and farmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT His Children were James, Abel, Eli, Hiram, Sarah, Mary, Roxana, and Ruth. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Son of James Kilborn Sr. and Sarah Bissell.  In early life he went to sea on several voyages as a whalesman. During the American Revolution he entered the British Army as a Quarter Master and subsequently served as Lieutenant of A
2 CONC rtillery. About 1780 he moved his family to Castleton, Vermont and resided there until about 1798 when he moved to eastern Ontario. By this time he was a widower. He was a tanner and currier, and farmer.
