2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/11436130/levi-jones
2 CONT
2 CONT Levi Jones BIRTH	1717 DEATH	23 May 1766 (aged 48–49) BURIAL	 Ancient Burying Ground Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA MEMORIAL ID	11436130 · View Source SHARE  SAVE TOSUGGEST EDITS MEMORIAL PHOTOS 3 FLOWERS 2 Levi Jones 
2 CONC was killed by the blowing up of the schoolhouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the news of the repeal of the Stamp Act reached Hartford, a great celebration was planned. Many men of the town were in the schoolhouse, preparing fireworks. Gunpowder for two companies of militia had been delivered to the sc
2 CONC hool house at the rate of one pound per soldier. Some was spilled when it was delivered, and some boys of the town (being in high spirits and meaning no harm) lit the spilled powder on the ground. This powder ignited and led a pat
2 CONC h to the schoolhouse which was blown up. Levi Jones died in the explosion, although many others were injured.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Cooke, daughter of Aaron Cooke and Hannah Wadsworth. Elizabeth married Hezekiah Marsh after Levi's Death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elizabeth & Levi: 1. Abigail bpt. Dec. 31. 1749 2. Mille died Nov. 15, 1759 bur Center Church Graveyard 3. Julius m. Elizabeth Dickinson 4. Hannah b. Dec. 5, 1758 m. William Hooker. ...from Families of Old Hartford
2 CONT
