1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT THE JOHN WILLIAMS FAMILY of Westfield, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 1 JOHN WILLIAMS (mar. Mary Buckley)
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 2 NATHANIEL WILLIAMS (mar. Mary Owen)
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 3 REBECCA WILLIAMS (mar. Jedediah Dewey II)
2 CONT
2 CONT NATHANIEL WILLIAMS Generation 2
2 CONT
2 CONT NATHANIEL WILLIAMS was born on 25 October 1647 at Windsor, Connecticut. He married MARY OWEN, who joined the Westfield church on 5 April 1713. Nathaniel was a farmer on Union Street in Westfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Abigail Williams, born at Westfield on 23 March 1684.
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. REBECCA WILLIAMS, born at Westfield on 27 September 1685. She married Jedediah Dewey II.
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Elizabeth Williams, born at Westfield on 22 September 1687; mar. 9 July 1717 at Westfield, Isaac Lyman of Lebanon.
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. John Williams, born at Westfield on 3 November 1689; died 28 September 1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. Nathaniel Williams II, born at Westfield on 25 August 1692.
2 CONT
2 CONT    6. Abigail Williams, born at Westfield on 15 September 1693; mar. Thomas Dewey.
2 CONT
2 CONT    7. Mary Williams, born at Windsor, Connecticut, on 28 September 1695.
2 CONT
2 CONT    8. Zebedee Williams, born at Windsor on 7 January 1697/98.
2 CONT
2 CONT    9. John Williams, born at Windsor on 16 April 1699.
2 CONT
2 CONT   10. Keziah Williams, born at Westfield on 11 December 1701; mar. John Hogins on January 25th, 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT   11. Naomi Williams, born at Westfield on 26 January 1703/04; mar. William Drake on January 22nd, 1731.
2 CONT
2 CONT   12. Orpha Williams, born at Westfield on 23 December 1706; mar. Japhet Bush in 1727. 
2 CONT
2 CONT REBECCA WILLIAMS Generation 3
2 CONT
2 CONT REBECCA WILLIAMS was born at Westfield on 27 September 1685. She married JEDEDIAH DEWEY II on the 17th of June 1703. They had nine children.
2 CONT
2 CONT PRIMARY REFERENCES
2 CONT
2 CONT Dewey, Louis M. [Williams]. Genealogical Notes. Copied as project of the National Youth Administration (1937) pp. 15-16.
2 CONT
