1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Hester (Esther) Hosford, wife of (1) Joseph Phelps and (2) Samuel Kent===  
2 CONT
2 CONT Hester Hosford was the daughter of John Hosford & Phillury Thrall.  Hester was born on 27 May 1664 in Windsor, CT.  She died on 18 Jan 1760 in Suffield, CT.   She married Samuel Kent, son of Samuel "The Immigrant" Kent and Frances
2 CONC  Woodall, on 1 May 1700, Suffield, CT.   She was his third wife.   She was the widow of Joseph Phelps who died in 1695.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hester Hosford outlived both her husbands and died at age 95 in Suffield, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Samuel Kent:
2 CONT # Martha Kent, b. 8 Feb 1702/03, Suffield, CT.
2 CONT #  Twin - Daniel Kent, b. 10 Jul 1704, Suffield, CT; m. Hannah Steel.
2 CONT # Twin  - Mary Kent, b. 10 Jul 1704, Suffield, CT.
2 CONT # Benjamin Kent, b. ca. 1706, Suffield, CT; m. (1) Apphia Ruggles; m. (2) widow Love Ensign.
2 CONT # Mary Kent, b. ca. 1708, Suffield, CT; m. Samuel Granger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Joseph Phelps seem to be Hester (Esther) Kent (husband was step-brother, Samuel Kent), Abigail Marshall (husband Samuel Marshall), Daniel Phelps (died as an infant), and Benoni Phelps.  Need primary sources for these
2 CONC  children.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Source=
2 CONT # http://www.suffieldhistoricalsociety.org/families/kent.htm - Reference Documents: 12, 13, 95, 164, 177, 187
2 CONT
2 CONT Esther was admitted to full communion, lst Cong. Ch, Suffield by Rev. Ebenezer Devotion on 27 Apr 1735 by letter of recommendation from church at Westfield, MA.
