2 CONT Page 59
2 CONT
2 CONT 112 Samuel Clark (Samuel 3, Samuel 2, Daniel 1), born Dec. 15, 1720; died June 14, 1807; married (1) Nov. 30, 1748, Eunice Lyman, daughter of Joseph and Abigail (Lewis) Lyman, born May 30, 1728, and died April 23, 1785; (2) Mary M
2 CONC inot, who died Oct. 31, 1816. Hartford, Conn., and Northampton, Mass., and Hatfield, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT 231 i '''Joseph''', born Oct. 8, 1749; died Dec. 18, 1828; married (1) Anna Barnard; (2) Lydia Cook.
2 CONT
2 CONT 232 ii Richard, born Nov. 7, 1751 ; killed at Ticonderoga Sept. 11, 1776.
2 CONT
2 CONT 233 iii Thomas, born Nov. 13, 1753; died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT 234 iv Susannah, born Feb. 7, 1756; died Feb. 15, 1806.
2 CONT
2 CONT 235 v Samuel, born July 2, 1758; died July 10, 1847, married (1) Jerusha Phillips; (2) Lucretia Sheldon.
2 CONT
2 CONT 236 vi Thomas, born April 2, 1761 ; died Jan. 25, 1840; married Lucinda Birge.
2 CONT
2 CONT 237 vii Mercy, born Nov. 26, 1763; married Edward Yeamons.
2 CONT
2 CONT 238 viii Eunice, born July 20, 1766; died May 8, 1843; married Ebenezer Parsons.
2 CONT
2 CONT 239 ix Henry, born Jan. 5, 1768-9; married Polly Pitt.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Stiles' Windsor, Appendix, Miss Anna B. Clarke, Northampton.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 84
2 CONT
2 CONT 231 '''Joseph Clark''' (Samuel 4, Samuel 3, Samuel 2, Daniel 1), born Oct. 8, 1749; died Dec. 18, 1828; married  (1) Anna Barnard; (2) Lydia Cook, who died Aug. 13, 181 5. Northampton, Mass. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 435 i Anna Laura, child of first wife, died in infancy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 436 ii Anna Laura, born July 4, 1788; died Aug. 15, 1 86 1 ; unmarried. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 437 iii Joseph Hawley, born March 30, 1790; died Nov. 22, 1825 ; married Nancy Gardner. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 438 iv George Miller, born Dec. 1, 1792; died March 22, 1826; married Parthenia Dunkin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 439 v Elizabeth Owen, born Dec. 28, 1799; died Sept. 27, 1863; married Oct. 16, 1830, Dr. Samuel Shaw. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 440 vi Frederick Watson, born July 29, 1804; died June 20, 1883; married Feb. 14, 1837, Lucinda Boleyn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 441 vii Francis Ellis, born April 3, 1807; died Sept. 8, 1809. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Cook was the daughter of Capt. Joseph Cook and Lydia Miller. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Stiles' Windsor Appendix; Miss Anna Clark of Northampton.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/clarkgenealogyso00walt#page/60/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT * Title: Antiquities, historicals and graduates of Northampton 
2 CONT * Author: Solomon Clark
2 CONT * Title: Antiquities, historicals and graduates of Northampton
2 CONT * Publisher: Northampton, Mass. : Steam Press of Gazette Print. Co.
2 CONT * Contributor: UMass Amherst Libraries
2 CONT * Format: txt
2 CONT * Size: 227 kb
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 20
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Joseph Clarke''' here named, the oldest of the preceding Capt. Samuers nine children, born 1749, was adopted and educated by Major Joseph Hawley, married Anna Barnard about 1775, by whom he had one child, a daughter; the mother
2 CONC  died at its birth. After living a widower twelve years, viz. : on the homestead at the lower end of Pleasant street on the left, he married Lydia Cook, daughter of Capt. Joseph, by whom he had six children. Anna Laura Clarke, who
2 CONC  died unmarried, 1861, aged seventy- three; Elizabeth Owen, who died 1863, wife of Samuel Shaw, M. D., of Plainfield; Frederick W. Clark, on Pleasant street, nearly opposite his father's. Also, other children, who deceased many ye
2 CONC ars ago. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.ebooksread.com/authors-eng/solomon-clark/antiquities-historicals-and-graduates-of-northampton-ral/page-13-antiquities-historicals-and-graduates-of-northampton-ral.shtml
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://beta.worldcat.org/archivegrid/record.php?id=225178568
2 CONT
2 CONT Residents of Northampton, Mass. Joseph O. Clarke was son of Samuel and Eunice (Lyman) Clarke; spent much time of his childhood in the home of Major Joseph Hawley and his wife Mary Lyman Hawley; harness/saddle maker and resident at
2 CONC  Bridge and Hawley streets; in 1775 m. Anne Barnard (d. 1776), leaving female child who died soon thereafter; in 1778 remarried Lydia Cook (d. 1815) and had 7, possibly 9 children. Anne Laura Clarke was the eldest child of Joseph 
2 CONC and Lydia Clarke and became guardian of the younger children. She attended Mrs. Royce's School at Hartford, Conn., and then taught at Fishkill Landing, N.Y.; became a public lecturer, one of the first female lecturers in the U.S.,
2 CONC  and traveled about the East Coast speaking on subjects of historical and geographical interest. Lectured in New York, N.Y., Petersburg, Va., and then settled in Northampton in 1825, also lecturing, 1836-1844 in various other loca
2 CONC tions.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.worldcat.org/title/papers-of-joseph-o-clarke-and-anne-laura-clarke-1773-1832/oclc/225178568
2 CONT
