1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Notes
2 CONT # '''There's zero evidence for a death place or date.''' Some websites merely suppose a date or place for death without providing a validly sourced rationale.
2 CONT # '''While there's no birth record in FamilySearch or AmericanAncestors repositories,''' [https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Caleb_Case_%281%29 WeRelate.org] sourced the familial connection:
2 CONT ## Case, Samuel, Symsbury, in Manwaring, Charles W. ''A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records''. (Hartford, Conn.: R. S. Peck & Co., 1904-06) 2:484-85 @[https://archive.org/details/digestofearlycon02manw/page/484/mode/2u
2 CONC p Archive.org]
2 CONT ### "… '''2 November, 1725-6: Caleb Case, a minor, 14 years of age''', chose his brother Samuel Case of Simsbury to be his guardian. Recog., £50. Arriam Case, a minor, 17 years of age, and Benjamin Case, 15 years of age, chose the
2 CONC ir brother Samuel Case to be their guardian. Recog., £100."
