1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Elizabeth Case''' was the eldest child of John Case and Sarah Spencer.
2 CONT
2 CONT She lived in Windsor, Connecticut until the spring of 1669, when her family moved to nearby Massacoe (now Simsbury), settling in the Weatogue section.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married Joseph Lewis of Simsbury in 1674. They had three children, likely all born in Simsbury:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Elizabeth Lewis, b. 20 March 1675; m. _____ Smith
2 CONT # Joseph Lewis, b. 15 March 1676/7; settled in Waterbury, Connecticut
2 CONT # John Lewis, b. 8 January 1680/1; m. Abigail Bacon
2 CONT
2 CONT Following Joseph death in 1680, Elizabeth married John Tuller in 1684. In 1690, they had a farm on the south border of Simsbury, to the east of the Farmington River. John was one of the founders of the church on 10 November 1697.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth had six children with John, all born in Simsbury:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sarah Tuller, b. 4 August 1685
2 CONT # William Tuller, b. 10 June 1687
2 CONT # Samuel Tuller, b. 1689
2 CONT # Mary Tuller, b. 27 November 1692
2 CONT # Jacob Tuller, b. 22 May 1694
2 CONT # Mabel Tuller, b. 22 February 1699
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth died suddenly on 9 October 1718. Per the local Simsbury records, "[s]he was well and died in about six hours' time."
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Goodwin, Nathaniel. ''First Settlers of Connecticut and Massachusetts''. New Orleans, Louisiana: L. Graham & Son, 1899, p. [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/48156/images/SettlersCTMA-002834-275 275-276].
2 CONT * "John Tuller (abt. 1652 - bef. 1742)." ''WikiTree'', revision of 27 January 2021. < [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Tuller-18 link] > Accessed 22 March 2022.
2 CONT * Kennan, Thomas Lathrop. ''Genealogy of the Kennan Family''. Milwaukee, Wisconsin: Cannon Printing Co., 1907, p. [https://books.google.com/books?id=1ixWAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA82#v=onepage&q&f=false 82].
2 CONT * Prichard, Sarah Johnson. ''The Town and City of Waterbury, Connecticut'', p. 84.
2 CONT * Torry, Clarence A. ''New England Marriages Prior to 1700''. Baltimore, Maryland: Genealogical Publishing Co., 2004, p. [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/3824/images/gpc_newenglandmarriages-0774 758].
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/46229278/elizabeth-tuller
