2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/b7/02/dc/76/53444846e191d555/connecticut_original.jpg?hash=2b269d47cf664ce3256e2242d9f4cd53e2e5f5a2b7fff953df136ea5a660c10b.1794815999
2 FORM jpg
2 _PRIM Y
1 NOTE Born in Simsbury, CT went to Long Island, about 1700 to Cohansey,NJ. (not sure if this applies to Mary Case, William Alderman, or hisson Thomas)
1 NOTE WIFE NOTES:-
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Mary Case was the daughter of John Case and Sarah Spencer. Sarah Spencer was the daughter of Honorable William Spencer. William Spencer's wife was Agnes Tucker. William Spencer's father was Gerrard Spencer (christened i
2 CONC n 1576 in England). Gerrard Spencer came to America in 1632 bringing his 5 sons, which included William Spencer. Gerrard was the son of Michael Spencer. Michael Spencer's father was John Spencer, born in 1568 (was in Stratford, En
2 CONC gland in 1576) and was married to Ann Gerrard. She was the daughter of Sir William Gerrard, the Lord Mayor of London in 1555. William Spencer returned to England in 1633 and brought back his wife Agnes Tucker on the ship Marie and
2 CONC  John. He was a member of the First House of Representatives in 1634 and served until 1638. The will of Mary Hillyer, of Simsbury, Connecticut, dated 12 Aug 1725. She left to her 3 sons, William Alderman, Jr., John Alderman, and J
2 CONC oseph Alderman my lands. The first is a piece of pine land on the west side of the river given me by my father John Case, the other is 5 acres of marsh land lying under West Mountain, all of my moveable estate except my wearing ap
2 CONC parel I give to my daughter Elizabeth Hillyer. I appoint my son John Alderman as my executor. Inventory taken shows £23 11s and 7p, the reason Thomas Alderman was not mentioned was because he died in 1715 (THE ALDERMANS IN AMERICA
2 CONC ).
2 CONT SPOUSE-PARENTS: Publication of Genealogy Unlimited Society, Inc., 2511 Churchill Drive, Valdosta, Georgia 316022547, Information in Volume III Number 2 June 1987 provided by Lillian McRee, 2511 Churchill Drive, Valdosta, Georgia 3
2 CONC 1602.
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY-SPOUSE-PARENTS-CHILDREN: William Alderman Parker, THE ALDERMANS IN AMERICA, Published by William A. Parker in 1957, reprinted by Edwards and Broughton Company, North Carolina, 1977. (Ellen Payne Odom Genealogy Library, M
2 CONC oultrie, Georgia)
