3 STAE Massachusetts
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Baptism: 07 APR 1616 Digswell, Hertfordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT "Martha, second wife of Anthony Dorchester, and previously wife of Samuel Kitcherell, died Dec. 17, 1662, at Springfield, Mass., having had issue by each husband. That her maiden name was Chapman is proved by a record in the Winth
2 CONC rop Papers as follows: Martha Dorchester, wife of Anthony of Springfield; living 15 Sept. 1659. Nathaniel and Johana Reskue [Ruscoe] did appear & declare that sd Martha before marriage was Martha Chapman, born Digswell, co. Herts,
2 CONC  and came over with the sister of Major Hezekiah Haines. This information was found by the late Col. Charles Edward Banks in volume 19 of the manuscript Winthrop Papers at the Massachusetts Historical Society rooms and is publishe
2 CONC d by the kind permission of Mr. Allyn Bailey Forbes, Librarian of the Society."[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha married twice.
2 CONT
2 CONT # She married in 1643 at Hartford, CT, as her 1st, and as his 2nd, to Samuel Kitcherel.[11]
2 CONT # She married on Jan 2, 1650 at Hartford, CT, as her 2nd, to Anthony Dorchester.[10][12]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Martha and Samuel Kitcherel (all born at Hartford, CT):
2 CONT
2 CONT # Samuel Kitcherel,
2 CONT # Martha Kitcherel, d 19 Oct 1708 scalped by Indians; m Dec 1, 1659 to Abel Wright (d Oct 19, 1725 aged 94 years).[11]
2 CONT # Hannah Kitcherel,
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She married second Anthony DORCHESTER on 2 Jan 1650/1 at Hartford County, CT;[2][6][7] children (surname DORCHESTER):[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Benjamin - b. 1651
2 CONT # Sarah - b. 1653
2 CONT # Hester - b. 1656; d. 1662
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
