1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Source: SOME DESCENDANTS OF THOMAS MORLEY By Herbert S. Horley of Newton Center, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Morley, also spelled Morlow, Marlow, and Mario, in different records, whose parentage and ancestry are uncertain, was married 8 Dec. 1681, by John Pynchon of Springfield, Mass., to Martha Wright, born 29 Nov. 1662, died at 
2 CONC Glastonbury, Conn., where her estate was inventoried 2 Jan. 1741, daughter of Lieut. Abel and Martha(Kitcherel, of Hartford) of Springfield. In 1686 he was granted land at Pochasic, now a part of Westfield, Mass., to which he subs
2 CONC equently added by purchase, and was admitted to the church in Westfield 18 Nov. 1702. His wife and daughter Martha were baptized at the church 10 June 1683. Thomas died at Glastonbury, Conn., in Jan. 1712, leaving a will mentionin
2 CONC g wife and children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, born at Westfield :
2 CONT # Martha,s b. 7 Sept. 1682; d. 22 Feb. 1763; m. 13 Jan. 1704, William Loomis ; had ten children.
2 CONT # Thomas, b. 14 Sept. 1684. ill. Mary, b. 30 Oct. 1686.
2 CONT # Abel, b. 18 Jan. 1689.
2 CONT # Thankful, b. 28 Feb. 1693. 
2 CONT # Mercy, b. 14 Nov.. 1695. 
2 CONT # John, b. 12 Mar. 1699; lived at Glastonbury; Inventory of his estate, dated 1 Nov. 1767, In Hartford probate records. 
2 CONT # Ebenezer b. 22 Mar. 1701.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Ebenezer* Morley (Thomat1), born at Westfield 22 Mar. 1701,
2 CONT
2 CONT died at Glastonbury, his will being made 16 Sept. 1747, and proved 26 Jan. 1748. He married at Glastonbury, 17 Feb. 1725-6, SuSanna (pellet, of Concord, Mass.) Wickham, widow of John. Children, born at Glastonbury :
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Mabtha,' b. 16 Oct. 1726.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Susanna, b. 24 June 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Prudence, b. 12 Oct. 1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT It. John, b. 19 July 1736; m. Abigail ; killed in the war at the
2 CONT
2 CONT taking of Savannah, Not. 1762.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Timothy" Morley (Thomas,* Thomas*) was born at Glastonbury 15
2 CONT
2 CONT Feb. 1726. He married at Glastonbury, 25 Apr. 1751, Maby 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wood, daughter of Dyer of Hartford. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, born at Glastonbury : 
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Elizabeth,' b. 14 Mar. 1752.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Maby, b. 1 June 1753; d. same day.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Maby, b. 23 Apr. 1754. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It. Timothy, b. 27 June 1766. 
2 CONT
2 CONT T. George, b. 10 Not. 1766. 
2 CONT
2 CONT vi. Thomas, b. 26 Mar. 1758. 
2 CONT
2 CONT vil. Ezkkiel, b. 15 Aug. 1759. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Till. Pbudkncb, b. 27 Jan. 1761.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ix. Jebusha, b. 18 June 1762.
2 CONT
2 CONT x. Daniel, b. 2 Dec. 1763.
2 CONT
2 CONT xl. Christiana, b. 2 Jane 1766.
2 CONT
2 CONT xll. Ruth, b. 16 Not., d. 20 Not. 1766.
2 CONT
2 CONT xili. Elijah, b. 4 Jan. 1768.
2 CONT
2 CONT X!t. Samuel, b. 30 Apr. 1769.
2 CONT
2 CONT Xt. Moses, b. 25 May 1771.
2 CONT
2 CONT xrl. Ruth, b. 23 Aug. 1772.
2 CONT
2 CONT xvii. Aaron, b. 22 June 1774.
2 CONT
2 CONT xviil. Enos, b. 29 Sept. 1779.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Abel' Morley (Abel,1 Thomat1), born at Glastonbury 22 Feb. 1721-2,
2 CONT
2 CONT died at Feeding Hills, 31 Dec. 1759, where he was a member of the church. He married, intention recorded 17 Mar. 1753, Mabt Miller, of Somers, Conn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, born at Feeding Hills and recorded at Springfield :
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Mabt,' b. 5 Aug. 1754; m. Thompson Philips.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Abel, b. 4 July 1756.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. David, b. 3 Mar. 1760.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Thomas' Morley (Abel,* Thomas1), born at Glastonbury 6 Mar.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1723-4, married at Westfield, 15 Nov. 1753, Sarah Phelps, 
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter of Isaac, 3d. He probably married secondly at Feeding 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hills, 29 Sept. 1779, Sarah Church of Westfield, who died at 
2 CONT
2 CONT Brutus, N. Y., 20 Sept. 1795. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, recorded at Westfield : 
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Sarah,' b. 16 June 1766.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Mindwell, b. 4 Jan. 1759.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. John, b. 16 Feb. 1761.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. Thomas, b. 20 Mar. 1766 ; d. at Brutus, N. Y., 2 Mar. 1813.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Isaac' Morley (Abel,3 Thomas1), born at Glastonbury 22 Mar.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1728-9, married first at Springfield, 8 May 1755, Hannah Miller, born 1 June 1733, daughter of Ichabod and' Hannah ; and married secondly Ruth - , whose will was dated 20 Mar. 1799. Children by first wife, recorded at Springfield 
2 CONC :
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Hannah,* b. 30 Dec. 1766.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Esther, b. 16 Apr. 1757 ; d. 14 Apr. 1772.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Dorcas, b. 16 Oct. 1768. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Iv. Sabbah, b. 17 July 1760. 
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Isaac, b. 6 Feb. 1762. 
2 CONT
2 CONT vi. Asahkl, b. 10 Oct. 1768. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Til. Sibkl, b. 1 Dec. 1766. 
2 CONT
2 CONT vlU. Huldah, b. 10 Sept. 1767. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ix. Eunice, b. 20 July 1769. 
2 CONT
2 CONT x. Obediah, b. 30 Nov. 1778. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. William* Morley (Abel,'' Thomas1), born at Glastonbury 3 Sept.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1731, married at Westfield, 15 Nov. 1753 (at the same time with 
2 CONT
2 CONT his brother Thomas), Jerusha Miller, daughter of Ichabod and 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah, and born 19 Mar. 1734-5, according to the record of T. 
2 CONT
2 CONT B. Warren of Springfield, or daughter of Samuel of Barkhamsted, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Conn., according to the record of Prof. E. W. Morley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, recorded at Springfield : 
2 CONT
2 CONT I. DERRICK,4 b. 18 Sept. 1766.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. William, b. 7 or 14 Aug. 1767 (at Westfleld). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ill. Jerusha, b. 7 Nov. 1769. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Iv. Abner, b. 8 Oct. 1761. 
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Lucy, b, 14 May 1764. 
2 CONT
2 CONT vl. Thankful, b. 1 Mar. 1766. 
2 CONT
2 CONT vi i . K i I.ik >kn , b. 4 Sept. 1767. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Till. Ruth, b. 1 Nov. 1769. 
2 CONT
2 CONT }\. Israel, b. 9 Apr. 1771. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Gideon* Morley (Abel* Thomas1), baptized at Westfield 9 Nov. 1738, died 24 Aug. 1818. He married, 28 June 1764, Mart Miller, born 14 Feb. 1742, died 4 Sept 1814 (gravestone), daughter of Moses and Elizabeth. . Children, born a
2 CONC t Feeding Hills and recorded at Springfield :
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Walter,' b. 17 Apr. 1766.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Mart, b. 14 Sept. 1766; d. 27 Oct. 1769.
2 CONT
2 CONT ill. Dosha (baptized Theodosia), b. 10 Jan. 1769.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. Mary, b. 11 Nov. 1770.
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Roderick, b. 22 Mar. 1773; d. 1777.
2 CONT
2 CONT vl. Anne, b. 5 May 1776; d. 1777.
2 CONT
2 CONT vii. Roderick, b. 11 Oct. 1778.
2 CONT
2 CONT viii. Nancy, m. 20 Oct. 1808, David Burbank.
2 CONT
2 CONT be. Asms, bapt. 12 Sept. 1784.
2 CONT
2 CONT Understand Thomas' town of Glastonbury by reading:
2 CONT
2 CONT Glastenbury for Two Hundred Years: A Centennial Discourse, May 18th, A. D. 1853 By Alonzo Bowen 
2 CONT
2 CONT Available on Google Books.
2 CONT
2 CONT This site:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/a/h/r/Richard-A-Ahrens/PDFGENEO1.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT shows a line from this Thomas back to Randulf de Charun in the 12th century, but I do not trust the immediate link back from this Thomas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is another guess:
2 CONT
2 CONT I have his parents being Marmaduke and Mary (Brewer). This was information I 
2 CONT
2 CONT had received years ago from a Mr. Campbell. Marmaduke was born 1633 in 
2 CONT
2 CONT Batesbord, Lincoln, England. No information on Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marmaduke's parents are listed as Thomas and Mary (Dolman). Same source. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas being born ca 1608 in Holme, Lincoln, England, died 1662, Nary born 
2 CONT
2 CONT ca 1611, died 1670, daughter of Marmaduke Dolman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas' parents being Edmund Morley Jr. and Phillipa Bower. Edmund born 1575 
2 CONT
2 CONT in Holme. Phillipa born ca 1583, died 1622.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund's parents being Edmund Sr. and Margaret (Hopkinson) Edmund born 1531 
2 CONT
2 CONT in England, Margaret born 1535 in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund's parents being William and Eleanor (Skipworth). William born 1507 in 
2 CONT
2 CONT Holme. No further information on Eleanor.
2 CONT
2 CONT William's parents being John and Lacon Morley. John born in 1487 in Holme. 
2 CONT
2 CONT NFI on Lacon.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's parents being Henry and Isabelle/Elizabeth Morley. Henry born in 1461.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry's parent being Thomas. Thomas born in 1435.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas' parent being William born in 1408 and the name also being spelled as: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Morlow, Marlow, Marlo
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Immigrated to Connecticut, where he married Martha Wright of MA
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''EDIT on 4/11/2014:  This note is attached to the Thomas Morrell born in England in 1662, who is one of the children mentioned in this excerpt.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The below is excerpted from "The ancestry of Daniel Morrell of Hartford" which can be read on-line at:  [http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7097855M/The_ancestry_of_Daniel_Morrell_of_Hartford]
2 CONT
2 CONT THOMAS MORRELL 
2 CONT
2 CONT FOUNDER OF THE FAMILY IN AMERICA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died at Newtown about 1704 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married in England  HANNAH (surname not known) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 THOMAS Born in England about 1662 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 SAMUEL " " " " 1664 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 JOSEPH " " Newtown 1667 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 JONATHAN " " about 1670 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 WILLIAM 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 SARAH 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 ABAGAIL Baptized (adult) October 31 1711 
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE The second generation of Thomas and Hannah Morrell is quite  fully established and verified in the Newtown Records. Owing to the absence of  churches and church records, the third generation cannot be well defined. Some  twen
2 CONC ty-rive names are known who must have been grandchildren of Thomas, the  founder but only about ten can be, assuredly, placed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT But little is positively known of the life of Thomas  Morrell prior to his advent at Newtown, but it is almost  certain that he was born in England. Following the  English occupation of New Amsterdam in 1664 and its  change of nam
2 CONC e to New York, there was a great influx  of English immigration and a reasonable assumption is  that Thomas and Hannah with their two sons were  among those who arrived in the autumn of 1665. He  is described in a deed as being a 
2 CONC carpenter, but all his  efforts seem to have been devoted to clearing his land  and farming. Besides the numerous grants he was pur-  chaser of several tracts and a number of deeds of sale  were executed by him. The date of his de
2 CONC ath is estab-  lished by deeds of his oldest son to the others in division  of his estate. One of these deeds alludes to a will,  naming sons Thomas and Samuel as executors; a dili-  gent search has been made for this will but it 
2 CONC has  nowhere been found. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.genealogyofnewengland.com/f_3cd.htm#10
2 CONT
