1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Martin Ashley was a soldier in the French and Indian War and was in Capt Hobbs' successful expedition from Northfield against the Indians twelve miles from Fort Dummer, 6/24 - 6/26/1748.  
2 CONT
2 CONT After the war he lived in Westfield, MA, Suffield, CT, and was a resident of Deerfield, MA in 1769.  He later returned to Walpole, NH. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a patriot in the Revolution, enlisting as surgeon on 6/28/1777 at the "second alarm" to reinforce the garrison at Ticonderoga.   He served during the remainder of the Saratoga campaign , which resulted in Burgoyne's surrend
2 CONC er.  
2 CONT
