1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Martin Ashley fought in the battle of Bennington during the Revolutionary War.   He left the service after 3 months (in 1776) and returned to his home in Walpole, NH where he was school collector in 1787.  He joine
2 CONC d the Congregational Church in 1788 and moved to Shrewsbury, VT in 1789 where he farmed for the remainder of his life.  There is a large pond in Shrewsbury known as Ashley's pond.
