2 CONT Mr Root military commission of adjutant of the New York state forces in the county of Columbia He was for a time associated with his brothers in the leather business and was one of the agents of the Van Rensselaer estate He made m
2 CONC any warm friends who often referred with admiration to his dignified courteous and gentlemanly demeanor and his eminently social qualities He was frank witty and intelligent and very fond of solid reading giving the Bible a promin
2 CONC ent place in his study He was also wholly temperate drinking nothing stronger than water which was a remarkable record in his day especially as he was prominent in political circles in Albany In 1 796 he was appointed one of the p
2 CONC residential electors by the legislature of New York in the interest of the federal party for the nomination of John Adams The Berkshire Star thus notices his death In the character of Mr Root was associated every quality that is a
2 CONC miable Possessing a mind naturally strong and intelligent he commanded the love and esteem of all who knew him 
