1 OCCU American Revolutionary War Soldier & Farmer, Town Assessor, Treasurer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for MASSACHUSETTS.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A055606  DAR Ancestor # A055606]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was married THREE times. He had children by each marriage.  Please use caution when merging and make sure the children are with the correct mother.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth: 	Aug. 25, 1719 Brimfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * Death: 	May 7, 1788 Brimfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * Burial: Brimfield Cemetery Brimfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT son of Nathaniel & Abigail (Lombard) Hitchcock
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the first white child born in Brimfield, two years after settlement. He was town assessor two years, treasurer five years, and selectman for four years. He was also a deacon of The Church. He was in his Majesty's service un
2 CONC der Capt. Tristam and he received from the town of Brimfield, Aug. 16, 1779 7 Pounds for service in their army.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married three times.  He married  (1) 11 Jan. 1741 Abigail King (2) 29 Aug. 1744 Patience Stebbins and (3) 11 Dec. 1750 Mary Burt. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Abigail King:
2 CONT # Joseph b. 28 Apr. 1742 md. Hannah Livermore
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Patience Stebbins :
2 CONT # Obed b. 7 Aug. 1745 md. Mary Dunham
2 CONT # Nathaniel b. 21 Aug. 1746 md. Ruth
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Mary Burt:
2 CONT # Sarah b. 3 Oct. 1751 md. John Thompson 
2 CONT # Elisha b. 20 Jan. 1753 md. Ursula Hitchcock 
2 CONT # Peter b. 1 Jul. 1754 md. Ruth Bliss 
2 CONT # Heli b. 8 Mar. 1756 md. Triphena Goodell 
2 CONT # Medad b. 24 Nov. 1757 md. Martha Stebbins 
2 CONT # Aaron b. 22 Jun. 1759 md. Mary Stebbins 
2 CONT # Ruth b. 2 Sep. 1761 md. Isaac Bliss Jr.  
2 CONT # Mary b. 7 Apr. 1763 md. Asahel Goodell 
2 CONT # Bathsheba b. 25 Dec. 1764 md. Vaniah Miller 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=126131131 Find A Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Created by: James Bianco
2 CONT * Record added: Mar 09, 2014 
2 CONT * Find A Grave Memorial# 126131131
2 CONT
2 CONT * Deacon Joseph Nathaniel Hitchcock
2 CONT * Birth: 	August 25, 1719
2 CONT * Springfield, Hamden Co., Massachusetts, United States
2 CONT * Death: 	May 7, 1788 (68)
2 CONT * Springfield, Hamden Co., Massachusetts, United States
2 CONT * Immediate Family: 	
2 CONT
2 CONT -- Son of Nathaniel Hitchcock and Abigail LOMBARD -- Husband of Mary BURT -- Father of Obed Hitchcock; Nathaniel Hitchcock; Peter Hitchcock and Heli Hitchcock -- Brother of Noah Hitchcock
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Joseph Hitchcock (1719-88) received seven pounds for services in the Continental Army, 1779. He was born and died in Brimfield, Mass. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution Volume 57
2 CONT
2 CONT page 143
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Fannie Burch Mehlin. & her sister applied for DAR numbers.  Here is Fannie's.
2 CONT
2 CONT DAR ID Number: 56412 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Steele County, Minn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Charles J. Mehlin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendant of Deacon Joseph Hitchcock, of Massachusetts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of I. W. Burch and Emily J. Bliss, his wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Granddaughter of Luther Bliss and Fanny Hawkins, his wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gr-granddaughter of Isaac Bliss and Ruth Hitchcock, his wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gr-gr-granddaughter of Joseph Hitchcock and Mary Burt, his 3rd wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Hitchcock (1719-88) received seven pounds for services in the Continental Army, 1779. He was born and died in Brimfield, Mass. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Laighton Hitchcock Bardwell.
2 CONT
2 CONT DAR ID Number: 158689 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Brookfield, Mass. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Frank D. Bardwell. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendant of Joseph Hitchcock, as follows: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Newton E. Hitchcock (1835-84) m. 1868 Annie Tighe (1849-1905). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Sylvester Hitchcock (1806-55) m. 1832 Lucy Lamberton (d. 1882). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Artemus Hitchcock (1781-1866) m. 1806 Abigail Brooks (d. 1865). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Nathaniel Hitchcock (1746-1816) m. Ruth Hitchcock (d. 1803). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Joseph Hitchcock m. 2d 1744 Patience Stebbins (d. 1750) (parents of Nathaniel). 
2 CONT
2 CONT [p.204] Joseph Hitchcock (1719-88) served as private in the Massachusetts troops. He was born and died in Brimfield, Mass. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The bookon "History of the Hitchcock Family",  says Joseph Hitchcock b 25 Aug 1719 was the first white child born in Brimfield, two years after its settlement.  He was town assessor of Brimfield 2 years, treasurer 5 years, and sel
2 CONC ectman 4 years.  A deacon of the church.  He was in his Majesty King George's service under Capt. Tristam and received on 16 Aug 1779 from Brimfield 7 pounds for service in the army.  His will dated 21 Apr 1788 gave all his proper
2 CONC ty to his wife Mary and son Medad and one shilling each to the rest of the children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Josephs father Nathaniel Hitchcock b 28 Aug 1777 Springfield, MA, was a weaver and the 1st settler of Brimfield in 1714.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Betsey's brother Samuel - says he m 27 19 Feb 1800 Azubah Blashfield in Brimfield and migrated to Homer, NY, in 1800; was a shoemaker and inventor of peg-shoes and all of his sons were either shoemakers or dealers.
2 CONT
