1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/121702273/peter_hitchcock
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT 1st buried in Homer Village Cemetery
2 CONT
2 CONT From the "History of the town of Homer" on the Cortland County, NY web site:
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel B. Hitchcock came to the town at an early day. His father, Peter Hitchcock, who long resided with his son, was elected one of the deacons of the first church of Homer upon its organization. Mr. Hitchcock settled first upon 
2 CONC the land recently owned by David Hannum, near the summit of the hill; his brother-in-law, John Bement, also settled near him. These two men erected a tannery, but how long they continued the business we have been unable to learn. 
2 CONC They were both practical boot and shoe makers, and subsequently moved to the village, where Mr. Hitchcock carried on the latter business in a building owned by Mr. Bowen, on Main street. It is stated on good authority that Hitchco
2 CONC ck & Bement obtained from the government the first patent for securing the soles of boots and shoes to the uppers with wooden pegs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Hitchcock is seen on Cortlandville, Cortland Co, New York Census from 1810-1860, however, it is Peters' Grandson, son of Samuel HItchcock, Peter Hitchcock seen on the later census.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
