1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  A Thomas was Probated in Salem 1680. Father of Thomas b 1629?? [Salem Town Record Vol 1]. In this volume is also a John West. brother of the Thomas's? [This is my independent research but may match previous work].
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Henry West were brothers and lived in Salem as early as 1658. Thomas was a planter." (The History of Salem, MA by Sidney Perley v2, p. 304) He was living in 1701.
2 CONT
2 CONT Changeable but For consideration below Thomas and Dorothy Thomas 1590's Son Thomas 1629 Grandson John 1667
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on the above I'm going to say Thomas and Henry were born in Cuckfield, Sussex  Not Wrentham. Father being Thomas. LDS Births and Baptism records (not submitter guess's). Show Henry 10 May 1627 and Thomas 1629, Cuckfield. The
2 CONC se birth dates are more in line with the marriage dates than previous birth date. One problem with the old dates; He would not be old enough to receive land grants in 1640 unless that was their father or some unrelated Thomas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There are several possible fathers for Thomas. Check the Sources area for these [EP] There are two possible grandfathers for Thomas b 1629. Thomas #1 buried in Cuckfield (Hodshouse,(Not on a map) possibly (a manor) property) 21 Ju
2 CONC l 1636)) or Thomas #2 13 Oct 1638. So not a permanent immigrant if he came at all. Following notes are another researchers
2 CONT
2 CONT Came in the Mary and John 1634--had grant of land 1640 (Savage's General Dictionary of 1st Settlers of New England)
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1st married 11 Oct. 1658 Phebe Waters (b. 1634 d. 16 Apr 1674 Salem MA)
2 CONT * 2nd married 14 Oct 1674 Mary Tenney Died 12 May 1732 [M J Tenney 1904
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT #  Samuel b. 23 Mar 1659/60
2 CONT # Joseph b. 23 Sept 1663
2 CONT # Benjamin b. 1 Oct 1665 "living in the Southward" in 1701 (from Middleton CT Land records.) married 14 Mar 1691/2 Hannah  d. 11 Dec 1733 Middleton CT
2 CONT # John b. 9 Sep 1667
2 CONT # Mary b. 31 January 1675/6 
2 CONT # Elizabeth bpt 1 July 1677
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT #  "I have a family tree from my grandmother's line of Wests beginning with Thomas and Phebe West in 1634. There are some sources given and I know it was compiled around 1947 by Ray D. West in Menominee MI with assistance from my 
2 CONC mother's cousin Edna West Herrman of Camden NY and others. I also know there are errors in it just in my immediate family. My book traces Benjamin the 3rd son. Sorry. Guess that's why it says "Thomas West 1634 and a few Descendant
2 CONC s" on the front cover. (http://boards.ancestry.com/surnames.west/5958.1.1.2.1.1/mb.ashx)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # [http://archive.org/stream/pioneersofmassac00pope#page/487/mode/1up The pioneers of Massachusetts, a descriptive list, drawn from records of the colonies, towns and churches and other contemporaneous documents. By Charles Henry 
2 CONC Pope ...Published 1900 by C.H. Pope in Boston . ]. Page 487.   Note in Pope's Pioneers Henry is reported to be (about) 59 in 1686 making him born in 1629 (or 1628)
2 CONT # see timeline tab for additional source citations.
2 CONT
