1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John West, son of Thomas and Phebe, was born 9: 7 m: 1667. (Sept 9 1667) at Salem, Massachusetts.[1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT John West, and Mary Webster, both of Bradford were married at Salem, Mar. 25, 1696.[3][4] The marriage was also recorded in the Bradford town records.
2 CONT
2 CONT John, died in Bradford Feb. 6, 1740.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Will dated 12 April 1739, April 20 1741 makes bequests to wife, Mary; sons: John (eldest), Isaac and Thomas; daughters: Mary Heath, Sarah West, Rebecca Grey, Bethiah Poor; son-in-law Thomas Coverly. Inventory £320.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children born in Bradford, Massachusetts[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary, d. John and Mary, born Jan. 12, 1696-7.
2 CONT Hannah, d. John and Mary, born July 6, 1699; died July 26, 1699.
2 CONT Sarah, d. John and Mary, born June 28, 170–. [bp. June 30, 1700. CR1]
2 CONT Abigail, d. John and Mary, born Feb. 18, 1703.
2 CONT Rebeckah, d. John and Mary, born June 20, 1706.
2 CONT Bethiah, d. John and Mary, born Apr. 19, 1709.
2 CONT John, s. John and Mary, born Dec. 6, 1711.
2 CONT Isaac, s. John and Mary, born Jan. 31, 1714-15.
2 CONT Thomas, s. John and Mary, born Aug. 10, 1717.
2 CONT Joanna, d. John and Mary, born ––– ––, 1721.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/West-3921
2 CONT
2 CONT John West (1667 - aft. 1740)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===John West===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 9 Sep 1667 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts, New England
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Thomas West and Phebe (Waters) West
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Samuel West, Joseph West, Benjamin West, Mary West [half], Elizabeth (West) Colby [half], Ebenezer West [half], Deliverance West [half], Sarah West [half], William West [half] and Phebe (West) Eastman [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Webster) West — married 25 Mar 1696 in Salem, Essex, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Mary West, Hannah West, Sarah West, Abigail West, Rebecca (West) Gray, Bethia (West) Poor, John West, Isaac West and Joanna West
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after 6 Feb 1740 after age 72 in Bradford, Essex, Massachusetts, New England
2 CONT
