1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Special Note:'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT This Samuel Bliss was born 1624 in England, not 1647 in  This is the Son of Thomas  the other Samuel was the son of Nathaniel Bliss, of Springfield they are not that same person.  This profile has and was being confused with this 
2 CONC  [https://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Bliss/6000000003198295091 Samuel Bliss]
2 CONT
2 CONT He is the Uncle of the other Samuel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth 1624  Posted by lorinorri 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death 1720
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT According to an article by Tom Bliss, Bliss Magazine, Vol 2,No 20 Dec. 2007, Samuel Bliss, son of Thomas and Margaret [Hulins] Bliss, was baptised 04 February 1638 at St. Mary de Crypt Church in Gloucester, England.  
2 CONT
2 CONT What the writer guessed was that Thomas Bliss Sr. came to Massachusettts in 1638 with some of his older children (probably Thomas and Anne from his first marriage), but his 2nd wife Margaret stayed in England with the baby Samuel 
2 CONC and her other children after father was taken ill. When the rest of Thomas' family arrived in New England was not cited in the article.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT According to Springfield records, Samuel arrived Springfield 1646, resided there 74 years and died in Springfield 1720.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Thomas Bliss(e) Mother Margaret Bliss(e) FAG 111672507
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Bliss Born 1624 died 1720
2 CONT
2 CONT Age 96
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage November 10, 1665 Mary LEONARD Father John Leonard Mother Sarah . died Died January 1, 1724
2 CONT
2 CONT He received several grants of land from the town,--at Freshwater Brook and on the north side of Agawam River, at Ackanunset, at the latter place 35 acres. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Selectman in 1685, '92, and '99. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel and Mary 
2 CONT
2 CONT c1 Hannah b. December 20, 1666 m1 John HALEY m2 Simon SMITH
2 CONT
2 CONT c2 Thomas b. February 8, 1668 m. Hannah CADWELL
2 CONT
2 CONT c3 Mary b. August 14, 1670  m. Philip SMITH
2 CONT
2 CONT c4 Jonathan b. February 5, 1672  m. Sarah EGGLESTON
2 CONT
2 CONT c5 Martha b. June 1, 1674  Samuel ELY
2 CONT
2 CONT c6 Sarah b. September 10, 1677  m. George WEBSTER
2 CONT
2 CONT c7 Experience  b. April 1, 1679 d. April 7, 1679
2 CONT
2 CONT c8 Mercy b. July 18, 1680  m. John ELY
2 CONT
2 CONT c9 Ebenezer b. July 29, 1683 m. Mary GAYLORD
2 CONT
2 CONT c10 Margaret b. September 11, 1684  m. Samuel COLTON
2 CONT
2 CONT c11 Esther b. April 2, 1688  m. Henry CHAPIN
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=111672672 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 11 2016, 23:57:08 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/75710042/person/34388059004 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 13 2018, 21:48:28 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 14th descendant of Thomas Bliss that came to America in 1635 
2 CONT
2 CONT SAMUEL, of Springfield, Mass., — called in the records " Samuel Bliss,  sen., 11 — (son of Thomas and Margaret Bliss, of Hartford, Conn.,) was born  in England in 1624, removed to America with his father in 1635, and mar-  ried No
2 CONC v. 10, 1664-5, to Mary, daughter of John and Sarah [Heath] Leon-  ard, of Springfield. She was born Sept. 14, 1647, and died 1724. He died  March 23, 1720, aged ninety-six years. Issue : 
2 CONT
2 CONT 45. Hannah, b. Dec. 20, 1666. John Haley, of Hadley, Mass., m. for his second wife, Hannah, 
2 CONT
2 CONT dau. of Samuel Bliss, and d. about 1688. She" afterwards m. May 1, 1689, Simeon Smith. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 46. *Thomas, b. Feb. 8, 1668, d. Nov. 10, 1733.- 
2 CONT
2 CONT 47. Mart, b. Aug. 4, 1670, m. in 1687 Philip Smith, and d. Dec. 23, 1707, at East Hartford, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Conn. He was a son of Lieut. Philip Smith and Rebecca Foot* of Hadley, Mass., was  b. about 1665, and d. Jan. 25, 1725. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 48. *Jonathan, b. Jan. 5, 1672, d. about 1740. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 49. Martha, b. June 1, 1674, m. Nov. 10, 1697, Samuel Ely. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 50. Sarah, b. Sept. 10, 1677. She was probably the Sarah Bliss who m. Dec. 13, 1695, George 
2 CONT
2 CONT Webster (b. Nov. 7, 1670) son of Thos. Webster and Abigail Alexander, and removed  to Lebanon, Conn., about 1705. Her cousin Sarah, daughter of Lawrence Bliss, is  supposed to have m. March 9, 1687, Samuel Smith, of Hadley, Mass. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 51. Experience, b. April 1, 1679, d. April 7, 1697. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 52. Merct, b. July 18, 1680, m. Dec. 30, 1703, John Ely. He was the fourth son of Samuel 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ely, of West Springfield, was b. in Springfield in 1678 and d. in 1758. Issue: John,  Reuben, Abner, Caleb, Noah, Mercy, (who m. Luke Bliss,) and Rachel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 53. *Ebenezer, b. July 29, 1683, d. Sept. 7, 1717. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 54. Margaret, b. Sept. 11, 16S4, m. Jan. 16, 1707, to Samuel Colton, of Longmead w, Mass., 
2 CONT
2 CONT (b. Jan. 17, 1679;) she d. Jan. 19, 1736. A daughter (Margaret) m. Jose a Frost of  Newcastle, and afterwards, 1792, Judge Ichabod Rollins, of Somersworth, _4. H. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 55. Esther, b. April 2, 1688, m. May 10, 1716, Henry Chapin, of Chicopee, Mass. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT According to Springfield records, Samuel arrived Springfield 1646, resided there 74 years and died in Springfield 1720.
