1 NOTE Oliver was a soldier in the War of 1812. It is indicated that his son, Oliver, Jr. was born in Connecticut, so he left Maine, stayed in Connecticut for awhile before going on to Ohio.  Oliver Eggleston, Sr. was born possibly 1769 
2 CONC at Murrayfield, Massachusetts and died probably in Ohio. He was a soldier in the War of 1812. Oliver Eggleston, Sr. went to Portage County, Ohio in 1812. Oliver Eggleston, Sr. married Cynthia Skinner on 22 November 1787 at Washing
2 CONC ton, Hampshire County, Massachusetts. Washington is now part of Boston, Massachusetts.  His son, Oliver Eggleston, Jr., was born in Connecticut, indicating the family left Massachusetts and was in Connecticut a very short time bef
2 CONC ore going to Ohio.
2 CONT Oliver Eggleston, Sr. was born possibly 1769 at Murrayfield, Massachusetts and died probably in Ohio. He was a soldier in the War of 1812. Oliver Eggleston, Sr. went to Portage County, Ohio in 1812. Oliver Eggleston, Sr. married C
2 CONC ynthia Skinner on 22 November 1787 at Washington, Hampshire County, Massachusetts. Washington is now part of Boston, Massachusetts.  His son, Oliver Eggleston, Jr., was born in Connecticut, indicating the family left Massachusetts
2 CONC  and was in Connecticut a very short time before going to Ohio.
2 CONT Oliver Eggleston, Sr. (son of Biggett EGGLESTON and Mary CORNING) was born ca. 1769 in Middlefield, Hampshire, MA, and died 1850 in Mantua, Portage, OH. He married Synthia Skinner on 19 Nov 1787 in Washington, MA, daughter of Samu
2 CONC el Skinner and Chloe Fuller.
2 CONT Oliver Eggleston, Sr. was possibly born in 1769 at Murrayfield, Massachusetts. The town of Murrayfield was re-named to Chester in 1783. He may have been buried in Ohio. He fought in the War of 1812.
2 CONT He married Cynthia Skinner on 22 November 1787 at Washington, Hampshire County, Massachusetts. Washington is now part of Boston, Massachusetts.
2 CONT They had the following seven children: Marriage: 19 November 1787, Washington, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Oliver Eggleston, Sr. and Synthia SKINNER are:
2 CONT Melinda Eggleston, d. date unknown, Mantua, Portage, OH.
2 CONT Milo Eggleston, d. date unknown.
2 CONT Zalmon Eggleston, b. Bet. 1794 - 1802, MA, d. date unknown.
