1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Implausible Marriage RE Elizabeth Brooks and Patrick Rice.====
2 CONT * Patrick's profile shows his birth and death in Winchester. VA. Elizabeth was born in Glastonbury, CT. '''The 400 mile chasm between Winchester, VA and Glastonbury, CT''' is tough to believe in an era when there were no paved roa
2 CONC ds and no automobiles.
2 CONT * A convincing narrative source must be found that convincingly reveals how and when Patrick met Elizabeth. Barring any finding and posting of that source to this profile, the relationship should be deemed spurious.
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''Name:''' Elizabeth Brooks
2 CONT >'''Daughter of:''' Samuel Brooks and Sarah
2 CONT >'''Birth Date:''' 24 Jan 1711
2 CONT >'''Birthplace:''' Glastonbury, Hartford, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America
2 CONT >"Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906", database, ''FamilySearch''; Samuel Brooks in entry for Elizabeth Brooks, 1711. – https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F7WX-85F
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-380213-1-6800/elizabeth-rice-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-c0cf1cec7fd2a18517ba01598f886675&mrid=5cba4bb756d2c2fd2e3f4dc5528c445f MyHeritage Family T
2 CONC rees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 13 2016, 13:43:26 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Rice (Brooks) could not have been the wife of both Johnathan Brooks, III and Patrick Rice, as these men had children in overlapping years with their Elizabeth Brooks.  It appears that the maiden name of Jonathan Brooks w
2 CONC ife was Harris.
