2 CONT
2 CONT >====Book
2 CONT >'''Stiles, Henry Reed. 1891.''' ''The History and Genealogies of Ancient Windsor, Connecticut; Including East Windsor, South Windsor, Bloomfield, Windsor Locks, and Ellington.'', Vol. 2. Hartford, Connecticut: Case, Lockwood & Br
2 CONC ainard. [https://archive.org/details/historygenealogi02stil/page/162/mode/1up?view=theater '''Archive.org''']:—
2 CONT >"Letters of administration were granted to the widow and son Richard, 12 Apl., 1725. Inv. exhib. 13 Apl., 1725). — Hartford County Probate Rec. He contributed with his sister (probably Abigail) 1s 3d to the Conn. Fund for Relief 
2 CONC of Poor of other Colonies, 1676. Children (b. W.):
2 CONT >1. Nathaniel. 1). 6 Apl., 1689. FAM. 5.
2 CONT >2. Sarah, b. 10 Feb., 1690.
2 CONT >3. Ebenezer. b. June, 1692.
2 CONT >4. Daniel, b. 9 Jan., 1693.
2 CONT >5. Lydia, b. 13 Mch., 1697: d. unm’d al Tolland, Conn., 1747; adm. Gr. 3 Nov., 1747.—Htfd. Co. Prob.
2 CONT >6. Mary. b. 10 Jan., 1700/1; m. Gilbert (mentioned in distribution of sister Lydia’s will).
2 CONT >7. Richard, b. 30 Aug., 1703. FAM. 6.
2 CONT >8. Abigail, b. 12 Jan.. 1705/6: m. —— Yeomans (mentioned in distribution of sister Lydia's will)
2 CONT >9. Elizabeth, b. 3 Oct., 1707; m. 18 June 1728, Joseph (s. Joseph and Mary Loomis) BARBER Jr., b. 28 Jan., 1708/9.
2 CONT >10. Jemima, b. 23 Sept., 1709. (Hinman erroneously calls this Jeremiah.)
2 CONT >11. Benjamin, b. 26 Mar., 1711.
2 CONT >12. Joseph, b. 1 Apl., 1713. FAM 7.
2 CONT >13. Aaron, b. 22 Apl. 1715; as a minor, æ about 14, made the choice of John Cook, Jr. to be his guardian, 3 Mar., 1730.
2 CONT
