1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Josiah Grant, son of John Grant & Mary Hull. 
2 CONT m. 1) Sarah Cooke (d. of John Cooke & Sarah Fiske) d. July 30, 1713. 3 ch. 
2 CONT m. 2) Sarah Cook (d. of Nathaniel Cook & Lydia) d. Feb. 28, 1777. 8 ch. 
2 CONT Josiah's wives, the two Sarah Cooks, were first cousins
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The birth of the first wife, Sarah  Cook, daughter of John Cook 1st and Sarah Fiske is unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah and Sarah Fiske Cook had three children,
2 CONT #  Josiah Grant Jr. 22 Jan 1711;
2 CONT # Sarah Grant 11 Mar 1712; 
2 CONT # Mary Grant 20 July 1713. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah then married Sarah Cook (cousin of first wife), daughter of Nathaniel Cook Jr. and Lydia. They had 
2 CONT # John, 17 May 1715; 
2 CONT # Increase 13 Feb 1717; 
2 CONT # Elijah 22 Jun 1719; 
2 CONT # Hulda, 25 May 1721; 
2 CONT # Ebenezer, 2 Mar 1724; 
2 CONT # Jerusha, 1 Jan 1726; 
2 CONT # Elijah, 28 Apr 1728; 
2 CONT # Anne Grant, 30 May 1730. 
2 CONT
2 CONT See Grant Family by Hastings, page 5; Town of Litchfield records by George C. Woodruff; Histories of Ancient Windsor.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Sarah (Cook) Grant (1691-1777)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cook-5205 : accessed 01 June 2024).
