1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Benjamin Woodworth===
2 CONT * Born about 1656 in  in Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts
2 CONT * died on 22 Apr 1729 in Lebanon, CT
2 CONT * Son of Walter Woodworth and Unknown (Unknown) Woodworth
2 CONT * Husband of Deborah  — married before 1678 [location unknown]
2 CONT * Husband of Hannah [(Damon?)] Woodworth — married before 1689 in Scituate, Plymouth Colony, Massachusetts 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family===
2 CONT
2 CONT Ca 1680 Benjamin first married Deborah.16 (name seen as Benjamin]
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT * 1. Elizabeth Woodworth (ca 1682-18 Jun 1713)
2 CONT * 2. Deborah Woodworth (ca 1682-)
2 CONT * 3. Mary Woodworth (ca 1683-10 Jul 1725)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ca 1689 Benjamin second married Hannah in Scituate, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT * i. Benjamin Woodworth (ca 1689-22 Apr 1747)
2 CONT * ii. Ichabod Woodworth (12 Mar 1691-26 Nov 1768)
2 CONT * iii. Ebenezer Woodworth (12 Mar 1691-1784)
2 CONT * iv. Hannah Woodworth (ca 1693-)
2 CONT * v. Ruth Woodworth (1695-)
2 CONT * vi. Amos Woodworth (ca 1697-)
2 CONT * vii. Ezekiel Woodworth (1699-20 Jul 1745)
2 CONT * viii. Judith Woodworth (ca 1701-)
2 CONT * ix. Margaret Woodworth (1703-1750)
2 CONT * x. Caleb Woodworth (22 May 1704-30 May 1780)
2 CONT * xi. Priscilla Woodworth (ca 1706-)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr03/rr03_483.html#P3345
2 CONT
2 CONT There is some confusion about Benjamin. According to some, he was a soldier in King Philip’s war and lost his life. In fact, he had moved to Little Compton, RI, and later to Lebanon, CT. Perhaps there was another Benjamin who died
2 CONC  in the war.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1703 Benjamin bought for 250 pounds from Philip Smith a large tract of land in Lebanon, Ct. where many of the Scituate people settled. He moved soon after to Lebanon with his family; was admitted inhabitant Dec. 22, 1704. In de
2 CONC eds of lands at Lebanon he is described as Benjamin Woodworth of Little Compton, RI.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Behan's The Woodworth Family of America, page 21
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 23rd day of June 1692, Benjamin sold his land at Scituate, his second wife Hannah signing the deed with him, and he removed to Little Compton, Bristol Co., Mass. Bay, where his brother Isaac had preceded him. In 1703, Benja
2 CONC min removed again to Lebanon and bought a large tract of land from Phillip Smith on 25 February 1703, and was admitted as inhabitant of the town on 22 December 1704. His farm was situated in the northeast part of the town, and on 
2 CONC account of its remoteness from the church, he with others, petitioned in 1714 for a new church. In 1716 this new church was formed called Lebanon North Parish; later the town of Columbia. In Lebanon land records (2:469) we find: “
2 CONC Moses Woodworth of Norwich sold to Benjamin Woodworth of Lebanon five acres in Little Compton, Bristol Co., Colony of Mass. Bay, land being one-third of a 15 acre tract which was originally Walter Woodworth’s.” Benjamin deeded lan
2 CONC d to his eldest son Benjamin in December 1712; to sons Ichabod and Ebenezer 13 February 1717/8; to son Amos 6 May 1720; to son Ezekiel who was “to care for his honored father and mother” 6 May 1723; to youngest son Caleb 21 Januar
2 CONC y 1726/7. On 4 November 1714, Benjamin is said to have received land for service rendered in King Phillip's War. It is believed this account may have become confused with a Benjamin Woodward who was killed in that war.
2 CONT Benjamin’s will was 21 Jan 1726 and proved 3 Jul 1728. Benjamin Woodworth was born about 1649 in Scituate. He married first Deborah (Perhaps Benjamin) she died between 1683 and 1688). He married second Hannah (perhaps Damon).[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1898 Woodworth book, Benjamin is said to be a son of Walter Woodworth (b. 1645), who is in turn listed as a son of Walter (d. 1685), the immigrant ancestor. In the preface to the 1898 book, the author confesses suspicions t
2 CONC hat Benjamin is not a son of Walter Jr. Modern compilations agree, and in fact Walter Jr. probably did not exist.
2 CONT
2 CONT In some sources Benjamin Woodworth is said to have been killed in King Phillip's War (1675-76) in Lebanon, Connecticut. In fact, however, Benjamin was alive when his father wrote his will. In 1714, Benjamin is recorded as receivin
2 CONC g land for services in that war. The Woodworth newsletter believes the soldier who was killed was another man, perhaps named Benjamin Woodward.
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin and Hannah sold their land in Scituate June 23, 1692, and moved to Little Compton, Rhode Island, where his brother Isaac lived. On February 25, 1703, they bought land in Lebanon, Connecticut, and Benjamin was admitted as 
2 CONC an inhabitant there December 22, 1704.
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin deeded land to his sons as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT to Benjamin December 1712, to Ichabod and Ebenezer, February 13, 1717-8, to Amos, May 6, 1720, to Ezekiel (who was to care for his parents), May 6, 1723, to Caleb, January 21, 1726-7. Benjamin's will was dated January 21, 1726-7 a
2 CONC t Lebanon and proved July 3, 1729 (the 1901 book says June 20, 1728). Hoppe's book says he died April 22, 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Little Compton Familes book says he was born about 1638, married to Deborah in 1659, and was killed in King Philip's War. The 1901 book by E. B. Woodworth says he was born in 1638 and died April 22, 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Hoppe book indicates that Benjamin and Hannah are ancestors of the Bush presidential family.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Woodworth-308
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Woodworth
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 6 Aug 1648 in Scituate, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Walter Woodworth and Unknown (Unknown) Woodworth
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Thomas Woodworth, Sarah (Woodworth) Mann, Joseph Woodworth, Elizabeth (Woodworth) Stedson, Mary (Woodworth) Simmons, Martha (Woodworth) Damon, Isaac Woodworth, Mehitabel Woodworth and	Abigail (Woodworth) Jackson
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Deborah (Unknown) Woodworth — married 1678 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Hannah (Damon) May — married before 1689 in Scituate, Plymouth County, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Elizabeth (Woodworth) Southworth, Deborah (Woodworth) Sprague, Mary (Woodworth) Sprague, Benjamin Woodworth, Ichabod Woodworth, Ebenezer Woodworth, Ruth (Woodworth) Owen, Ezekiel Woodworth, Margaret (Woodworth) Owen, Jud
2 CONC ith (Woodworth) Newcomb, Caleb Woodworth and Priscilla (Woodworth) Fuller
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 22 Apr 1728 in Lebanon, New London County, Connecticut Colony
2 CONT
