1 NOTE Benjamin Woodworth was born about 1649 in Scituate, Plymouth Co.,
2 CONT Massachusetts. He died 22 Apr 1728 in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut.
2 CONT m. (1) by about 1680 Deborah _____ ("Deborah the wife [and] Elizabeth [and]
2 CONT Deborah the children of Beniamin Woddward" were bp. at Scituate on 16 July
2 CONT 1682 [NEHGR 57:319]); m. (2) by 1691 Hannah _____ (on 24 June 1691 "Benjamin
2 CONT Woodworth and Hannah Woodworth his wife" acknowledged a deed in which
2 CONT Benjamin sold the land he had inherited from his father [PLR 3:11]).
2 CONT Above SOURCE: Excerpt from The Great Migration
2 CONT On the 23rd day of June 1692, Benjamin sold his land at Scituate, his second
2 CONT wife Hannah signing the deed with him, and he removed to Little Compton,
2 CONT Bristol Co., Mass. Bay, where his brother Isaac had preceded him.
2 CONT In 1703, Benjamin removed again to Lebanon and bought a large tract of land
2 CONT from Phillip Smith on 25 February 1703, and was admitted as inhabitant of
2 CONT the town on 22 December 1704. His farm was situated in the northeast part of
2 CONT the town, and on account of its remoteness from the church, he with others,
2 CONT petitioned in 1714 for a new church. In 1716 this new church was formed
2 CONT called Lebanon North Parish; later the town of Columbia.
2 CONT In Lebanon land records [2:469] we find: "Moses Woodworth of Norwich sold to
2 CONT Benjamin Woodworth of Lebanon five acres in Little Compton, Bristol Co.,
2 CONT Colony of Mass. Bay, land being one-third of a 15 acre tract which was
2 CONT originally Walter Woodworth's.
2 CONT Benjamin deeded land to his eldest son Benjamin in December 1712; to sons
2 CONT Ichabod and Ebenezer 13 February 1717/8; to son Amos 6 May 1720; to son
2 CONT Ezekiel who was "to care for his honored father and mother" 6 May 1723; to
2 CONT youngest son Caleb 21 January 1726/7.
2 CONT On 4 November 1714, Benjamin is said to have received land for service
2 CONT rendered in King Phillip's War. It is believed this account may have become
2 CONT confused with a Benjamin Woodward who was killed in that war.
2 CONT Children mentioned in Benjamin's Will, but not recorded in Lebanon or Little
2 CONT Compton [Genealogical & Family History of the State-of Connecticut, 1911, p.
2 CONT 885].
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin's Will is dated Lebanon 21 January 1726; proved 3 July 1728:
2 CONT : "In the name of God amen ye 21st day of January 1726/7. I, Benjamin
2 CONT Woodworth of Lebanon in ye County of Wendham and Colony of Connecticut in
2 CONT New England being very sick and weake in body but of perfect mind and memory
2 CONT thanks be given unto God therefore calling to mind ye mortality of my body
2 CONT and knowing that it is appinted for all men once to dey, do make and ordain
2 CONT this my last will and testament. That is to say princeaply and first of all
2 CONT I give and recomend my soul in to ye hands of God that gave it and my body I
2 CONT recomend to ye earth to be beuried in decent Christian Beuril at ye
2 CONT discretion of my executor - nothing doubting but that at ye generall
2 CONT resurrection I shall receve ye same again by ye mighty power of God - and as
2 CONT touching such worldly estate where with it had pleased God to bless me -
2 CONT with in this life I give demise and dispose of ye same in ye following maner
2 CONT and form: Imp - I give and bequeath to my well beloved and eldest son
2 CONT Benjamin Woodworth twenty acres of my common right that is laid out joyning
2 CONT to his land that I gave formerly given to him to be first laide out to him
2 CONT begining at ye highway ye wholl wedth as it is laide out and bounded on
2 CONT record and run so far by and ajoyning to his former land so far as to make
2 CONT twenty acres -
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath unto my sons Benjamin, Ichabod and Ebenezer
2 CONT Woodworths all ye remaining part of my common right of land that is laide
2 CONT out ajoyning to that twenty acres above sd given to Benjamin - to be equaly
2 CONT devided to my three sons Benjamin, Ichabod and Ebenezer they paying so much
2 CONT to my daughters as ye sd land shall be aprised at to be paide with in five
2 CONT years after my decease -and in case that my three sons Benjamin Ichabod and
2 CONT Ebenezer do not so cause to take ye sd lands and pay so much: to be devided
2 CONT amongst my daughters heare after named that ye ad lands shall be equaly
2 CONT devided amongst them my daughter.
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath unto my son Amos Woodworth 33 acres and two 3ds of
2 CONT an acre of land ajoyning to that lot of land on Chusnut Hill that I have
2 CONT formarly given to him he paying twenty pounds to my daughters with in five
2 CONT years after my deceas and in case he shall refuse to pay ye twenty pounds
2 CONT within the five years as afore sd that then ye sd 33 acres and two 3ds of an
2 CONT acre of land to be equaly devided amongst them -
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath unto my sons Ezekiell and Caleb Woodworths all
2 CONT thos two tracts or persals of land that I purchased of Capt. Joseph Marsh
2 CONT ajoyning to ye farm where my now dweling hows now stands to be equaly
2 CONT devided between them they paying all my just debts and in case they shall
2 CONT refuse to pay all my debts that then ye sd persels of land shall be sold to
2 CONT pay my just debts.
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath unto my beloved daughters heare named to wit
2 CONT Debrough Sprauge and Hanah Walar and Ruth Owen and Judeth Newcomb and
2 CONT Margret Owen and Precillah Fuller all my moveable estate that I shall dye
2 CONT seizd of except chains
2 CONT cart irons plough irons that my sons now have and one great chain that I use
2 CONT to take up ye mill that I give to my sons Ezekiel and Caleb. With ye mill
2 CONT and my Iron Harrow, I give to be used amongst all my sons so long as it
2 CONT shall last - all my moveables estate both within doars and without as ye
2 CONT stock and ye priece of my common lands laide out and not laide out and ye 20
2 CONT that my son Amos is to pay that is to say all but only what I have heare
2 CONT except to be equally devided amongst my above sd daughters only I give to ye
2 CONT children of Elezebeth Southard Deced - and ye children of Mary Sprauge
2 CONT Decd - ye heirs of thare own bodyes begoten amongst them half so much as to
2 CONT each of my daughtars above named -
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my children both sons and daughters heare named
2 CONT in this my last will and testament all my right of land or aney estate that
2 CONT of right dos belong to me at or within the bounds of Seconet in ye provence
2 CONT of Masachuse Bay and County of Bristoll they all being at equal charge in
2 CONT recovering ye same other wise ye charge to be payde out of ye part in
2 CONT proportion: and I do heareby likewise make and ordain my son Benjamin
2 CONT Woodworth my sole executor of this my last will and testament - heareby I do
2 CONT utterly disalow revoack and disanull all and every other and former
2 CONT testaments wills legasies and bequests and executors by me in any ways
2 CONT before named willed and bequeathed ratiefieing and confirmeng this and no
2 CONT other to be my last will and testament. In witness whereof I have heare unto
2 CONT set my hand and seall the day and year first above mentioned."
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Woodworth (Seall)
2 CONT Signed sealled published pronounced and declared by ye sd Benjamin Woodworth
2 CONT as his last Will and Testement in presents of us ye subscribars: Thomas
2 CONT Root, Nathaniel Dewey and John Woodward.
2 CONT SOURCE: Marvin "Woody" Woodworth 5/12/2005
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin married (1) Deborah Benjamin ?? before 1680.
2 CONT Last name uncertain.
2 CONT Information on this marriage came from the files of Jim and Karen Woodworth.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin also married (2) * Hannah Damon, daughter of John Damon and Martha
2 CONT Howland. Hannah was born 2 Dec 1672 in Scituate, Plymouth Co.,
2 CONT Massachusetts. She died 5 Aug 1741 in Hingham, Plymouth Co., Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT [email received from Woodworth Group member 03 Oct 2009. Varies from other sources.]
