3 CITY Goshen
3 STAE CT
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Williams-23375
2 CONT
2 CONT Deborah Williams' birth date and parentage are uncertain, but most plausibly she was the daughter of Benajah Williams and Deborah (Parke) Williams and was born about 1739-40. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Deborah Williams married John Owen in Salisbury, Connecticut on March 4, 1762.[1] Deborah and John had the following children in Salisbury:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Althea, b. October 17, 1762[2]
2 CONT # Asenath, b. July 12, 1764[2]
2 CONT # Chloe, b. August 12, 1766[2]
2 CONT # Elizabeth, b. August 6, 1768[2][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1771, John Owen moved to Poultney, Vermont.[2] Ralph Dornfeld Owen, in “Descendants of John Owen of Windsor, Connecticut (1622-1699)”, says that John may have had two wives, so it is possible that Deborah did not survive to mov
2 CONC e to Poultney. John (and possibly Deborah) may have had six more children in Poultney:[9]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Isaac, b. 1770-1774
2 CONT # Ethan, b. 1775-1780
2 CONT # Luther, b. 1782
2 CONT # Lucy (twin), b. 1785
2 CONT # Louisa (twin), b. 1785
2 CONT # Cynthia[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Given that Deborah would probably have been 45-46 at the time of the births of the later children in Poultney, it is perhaps unlikely that she was the mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1789, John Owen moved further north to Milton, Vermont.[2] Again, it is unknown if Deborah survived to accompany him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deborah Owen's date of death is unknown. Depending on when she died, she may have died in Salisbury, Connecticut or Poultney or Milton, Vermont.[2]
