1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Charles de Wolfe===
2 CONT * Born: 18 Sep 1673 - Glastonbury, Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT * Died: 5 Dec 1731 - Middletown, Mdlsx, Connecticut
2 CONT * Buried:  - Middletown, Middlesex, Conn
2 CONT * Father: Edward (Nathan) DeWolf (1646-1712)
2 CONT * Mother: Alice (Rebecca) Tinker (1650-      )
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT # 1694 - Glastonbury, Hartford, Connecticut to Prudence Beckwith (1676-1737), daughter of Matthew ll Beckwith & Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT A merchant, kept a general store, amassed considerable property Lived in Glastonbury, CT
2 CONT Esther thinks he married Prudence Beckwith, dau Matthew Jr and Elizabeth, in Glastonbury, CT
2 CONT
2 CONT There is disagreement as to who ws his wife; Prudence White or Prudence Beckwith. The matter would seem to be settled by a deed, in Lyme, where Prudence is referred to as daughter of Matthew Beckwith and wife of Charles DeWolf. Ap
2 CONC parently one of the genealogical resources on the family has it wrong.
2 CONT
2 CONT "In Lyme, vessels were built which went out to many markets, chiefly to the West Indies,and brought back cargoes to its wharves. Probably by these means Charles De Wolf made his 'venture' to the island of Guadaloupe." (Perry) 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Charles married Prudence  and their son Charles (2nd) was born in Lyme in 1695. He was the oldest of 10 children and the ancestor of the Guadeloupe and Bristol, Rhode Island  branches of the DeWolf family ... (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
