2 TITL Charles DeWolf Jr
1 NOTE Charles de Wolf emigrated to Guadeloupe, the French West Indies as a millwright and probably trader, in early manhood, where he married Margaret Potter on March 31, 1717.  He probably lived in Guadeloupe all his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT He carried on a business trade with the West Indies, & went to Guadaloupe to facilitate this trade. In accordance with the French pronounciation he was called D'OLF. He adopted this form spelling it DOLPH. His descendants in Glast
2 CONC onbury have spelled it that way ever since.
