1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Osborne_(Keeper_of_the_Privy_Purse)_
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Osborne, citizen and Grocer of London (died 1544), and his wife Elizabeth (née Coke), of Tyle or Tyled Hall, Latchingdon, Essex.  Son of Richard Osborne died in 1471.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT *1st son: John Osborne, Gentleman, who had 3 sons and 3 daughters including Elizabeth, who married first Richard Bettenson of London, and secondly Archer Breame, of Halstead, Essex.
2 CONT *2nd son: Peter Osborne, Esquire, married Anne, daughter of Dr. John Blythe and his wife Alice Cheke (sister of Sir John Cheke). They had eleven sons and eleven daughters
2 CONT *Anne (m 1) Edward Bowland 2) Edward Saxby)
2 CONT *1st wife of William Lane
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Pedigree 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Pedigree of the Osborn family is as follows,—with these brief notices :—
2 CONT
2 CONT *Peter Osborn, of Purleigh, Essex; ob. 1442.
2 CONT **Richard Osborn, ob. 1471.
2 CONT ***'''Richard Osborn, Tyld Hall, Essex; ob. 1544'''.
2 CONT ****Peter Osborn, Lord Treasurer s Remembrancer of the Exchequer, and Privy Purse; Ed. VI. Imprisoned in Queen Mary's reign. In great esteem with Lord Burleigh, and a High Commissioner for Ecclesiastical Affairs, active and zealou
2 CONC s in the Reformation; ob. 1592.
2 CONT *****Sir John Osborn, Kt„ Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer, married Dorothea, daughter of Sir John Danvers, and sister of Dan vers, Earl of Danby; ob. 1623.
