1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Cheek
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''Sir Thomas Cheeke1
2 CONT *M, #67959
2 CONT *Last Edited=14 Aug 2011
2 CONT *''''''     Sir Thomas Cheeke married, secondly, Essex Rich, daughter of Robert Rich, 1st Earl of Warwick and Lady Penelope Devereux.2
2 CONT *''''''     He lived at Pirgo, Essex, England.3 He was also known as Sir Thomas Cheke.2 
2 CONT *''''''Children of Sir Thomas Cheeke and Essex Rich
2 CONT **1.Anne Cheeke+1
2 CONT **2.Essex Cheeke+4 d. 28 Sep 1658
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume I, page 25. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage.
2 CONT *2.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 233. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *3.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume XI, page 332.
2 CONT *4.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2585. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p6796.htm#i67959
2 CONT *___________
2 CONT *''''''Essex RICH
2 CONT *Father: Robert RICH (1° E. Warwick)
2 CONT *Mother: Penelope DEVEREUX (B. Rich)
2 CONT *Married 1: Daniel FINCH
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Mary FINCH
2 CONT *''''''Married 2: Thomas CHEEKE 
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **2. Anne CHEEKE
2 CONT **3. Essex CHEEKE (m. Edward Montague, 2° E. Manchester)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/RICH.htm#Essex RICH1
2 CONT *_______________
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Rich, 3rd Earl of Warwick (28 June 1611 – 29 May 1659 in London), was the son of Robert Rich, 2nd Earl of Warwick and Frances Hatton. His only son, also Robert, predeceased him by 15 months dying of consumption . The earldo
2 CONC m passed to the 3rd Earl's brother Charles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Warwick married Lady Anne Cavendish, the daughter of William Cavendish, 2nd Earl of Devonshire, on 9 April 1632 at Battersea, Surrey. Their child, was the Earl's only son, Robert.
2 CONT *Robert married Frances Cromwell, daughter of Oliver Cromwell in 1657 but he died of consumption within three months of the marriage on 16 February 1658 (1657/1658), leaving no children and his widow remarried Sir John Russell, 3r
2 CONC d Baronet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Rich married secondly Anne Cheeke, daughter of ''''''Sir Thomas Cheeke and Essex Rich''''''. Their children were:
2 CONT *Anne who married Thomas Barrington of Barrington Hall Essex, heir of Sir John Barrington, 3rd Baronet.
2 CONT *Mary who married Sir Henry St. John, 1st Viscount St. John on 11 December 1673 and died in 1678, giving birth to their only son, Henry, Viscount Bolingbroke.
2 CONT *Essex Rich, who married Daniel Finch, 2nd Earl of Nottingham on 16 June 1674.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Rich is buried in Felsted, Essex.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT *http://thepeerage.com/p1309.htm#i13083
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Rich,_3rd_Earl_of_Warwick 
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *''''''Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900, Volume 48
2 CONT *Rich, Robert (1587-1658)   by Charles Harding Firth
2 CONT *RICH, ROBERT, second Earl of Warwick (1587–1658), .....
2 CONT *Warwick's eldest son, Robert, baron Rich, of Leighs, Essex, joined the king at York, but never bore arms; and the fine imposed upon him by parliament was remitted at his father's petition. He married twice: first, Anne, daughter 
2 CONC of William Cavendish, earl of Devonshire; secondly, Anne, daughter of ''''''Sir Thomas Cheke''''''. He died on 30 May 1659, leaving only three daughters (Cal. of Committee for Compounding, p. 1729; Autobiography of Mary, Countess 
2 CONC of Warwick, p. 27). .....
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Rich,_Robert_(1587-1658)_(DNB00)
2 CONT *_____________
