1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>PEYTON, Sir Thomas, 2nd Bt.</strong> (1613-84), of Knowlton, Kent. - b. 18 Aug. 1613, 1st s. of Sir Samuel Peyton, 1st Bt., of Knowlton by Mary, da. and coh. of Sir Roger Aston of Cranford, Mdx., master of the wardrobe to
2 CONC  James I. m. (1) 21 May 1636, Elizabeth (d. 10 Sept. 1642), da. of Sir Peter Osborne of Chicksands Priory, Beds., 3da.; (2) lic. 18 Jan. 1648, Cecilia (d. 26 Oct. 1661), da. of Sir John Clerke of Ford Place, Wrotham, Kent, wid. of
2 CONC  Sir William Swan of Hoopes, Southfleet, Kent, 1s. d.v.p. 1da.; (3) 2 Mar. 1667, Jane (d.1672), da. of Sir William Monins, 1st Bt. of Waldershare, Kent, wid. of Sir Timothy Thornhill of Olantighe, Kent, of one Mathews, and of Fran
2 CONC cis Swift, s.p. suc. fa. 27 Sept. 1623.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Offices Held ===
2 CONT Commr. of sewers, Kent 1639, array 1642, dep. lt. 1642-3, July 1660-d., j.p. July 1660-d., commr. for oyer and terminer, Home circuit July 1660, assessment, Kent Aug. 1660-80, col. of militia Oct. 1660-81; commr. for sewers, E. Ke
2 CONC nt Sept. 1660, Rother marshes Oct. 1660, corporations, Kent 1662-3, loyal and indigent officers 1662; sub-commr. of prizes, Dover 1665-7; commr. for recusants, Kent 1675."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1660-1690/member/peyton-sir-thomas-1613-84 The History of Parliament: the House of Commons 1660-1690], ed. B.D. Henning, 1983
2 CONT
