2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Jehiel Stewart (Sr) is mentioned in pages 492 & 493; Pgs. 495 & 498 of History of Sullivan Co. by Cathy L Connor, 2011. Page 492 & 3 contain a short informative piece of his moving to Sullivan Co. "Facts" taken from this history a
2 CONC re: At the end of the Revolutionary War Jehiel (& his brother Luther) were still residing in Middletown, Conn. In 1788 he took his family & moved into the wilderness..to Ulster Co. NY. The journey took about 2 weeks as he had to s
2 CONC lash his way through the wilderness with his axe. His goods were moved on "ox sleds." One incident was mentioned of the journey.  His littledaughter Lydia wandered off 1 evening in which Jehiel & his sister-in-law "Aunt Rachel" sp
2 CONC ent the night looking for her,fearing the worst as they could hear wolves. However she was found in the morning, she had slept by an old log. After settling in Sullivan Co. (Along with brother Luther) He first built a temporary sh
2 CONC elter then proceeded to clear the land, & build a home & mill. Another fact mentioned that he (along with other first residents) settled on the choicest land in the area & paid 75c per acre.story, as evidenced by the fact that Jeh
2 CONC iel is still found on the 1790 Census in Ulster Co. NY. In fact, Sullivan Co. was not created until 1808 from part of Ulster Co. NY. So it is very likely that Jehiel did not move from Ulster to Sullivan Co. & that he simply remain
2 CONC ed in the locality & that he resided on a portion that became part of Sullivan Co. NY at that time.
