2 CONT "Josiah Loomis Jr. was born March 11, 1708 at Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut to Josiah and Elizabeth Kelsey Loomis.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Abigail Bacon April 26, 1732 at Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut and they had ten children: Elizabeth, Abigail, Josiah III, Andrew, Michael, Abijah, Sarah, Daniel, Benajah and Rachel.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Simsbury, the family moved to Egremont, Berkshire County, Massachusetts before 1750.
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah was a member of the Episcopalian Church at Great Barrington in 1770.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to our family records, late in life, after the death of his wife, he moved to New York. About or after 1800, we show he died in Ancram, Columbia County, New York where we presume he was buried".
2 CONT
2 CONT Thank you for taking care of this. John E. Sherman #47749330: email October 31, 2015.
2 CONT
2 CONT August 14, 2016, S. Hamilton Clemow, member #48510600 suggested he was born 3/11/1709 in Windsor, Hartford, CT and died in 1800 in Egremont, Berkshire, MA
