1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT This biography is a rough draft. It was auto-generated by a GEDCOM import and needs to be edited.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:
2 CONT Date: 16 AUG 1733
2 CONT Place: Stafford, Connecticut[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT User ID: 5AEC037C904D014CB4FE283C7F799E58F358
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband: John Blodgett
2 CONT Wife: Irene Robinson
2 CONT Child: Irene Blodgett
2 CONT Marriage:
2 CONT Date: 4 DEC 1755[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Blodgett-219
2 CONT
2 CONT John Blodgett (1733 - 1813)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===John Blodgett===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 16 Aug 1733 in Stafford, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Daniel Blodgett and Deborah (Ellsworth) Blodgett
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Patience Blodgett, Daniel Blodgett, Nathan Blodgett, Seth Blodgett, Benjamin Blodgett and Samuel Blodgett
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Irene (Robinson) Blodgett — married 4 Dec 1755 in Tolland County, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Huldah (Blodgett) Warner, Irene (Blodgett) Buell and John Blodgett
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 10 Apr 1813 at age 79 in Claremont, Sullivan, New Hampshire, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 24 Nov 2020 | Created 6 Feb 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT WikiTree profile Blodgett-219 created through the import of meland2012.ged on Feb 6, 2012 by Greg Meland. See the Changes page for the details of edits by Greg and others.
2 CONT Source: S1 Abbreviation: The Descendents of Thomas Buell Title: The Descendents of Thomas Buell Author: Harlow Dunham Curtis Publication: Nathan Deloss Buell, Portland, Oregon
2 CONT ↑ Source: #S1
2 CONT ↑ Source: #S1
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Capt. John Blodgett, son of Lieut. Daniel and Deborah Ellsworth, was born at Stafford, Conn. on Aug. 16, 1733. He m. on Dec. 4, 1755 at Stafford, Irene Robinson, dau. of Benjamin Robinson and Jerusha Bingham of Windham, Conn. John
2 CONC 's younger brother Daniel was the husband of his wife Irene's younger sister, Lydia Robinson. At least twelve children were born of record at Stafford before the family finally settled at Claremont, NH. However, the family, or at 
2 CONC least some of the children, stopped on the way for brief residences at Amherst, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gravestone Inscription: Died Capt. John Blodget April 10, 1813 in the 80th year of his age. The memory of the just is blessed.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the day John died she was 79 years old, and Aetatis (i.e., Æ, "Aged," in the XX year of his Age) 80.
2 CONT
2 CONT source:  http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=45245206
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Capt. John Blodgett, son of Lieut. Daniel and Deborah Ellsworth, born in Stafford, Conn. Aug. 16, 1733. He m. on Dec. 4, 1755 in Stafford, Irene Robinson, dau. of Benjamin Robinson and Jerusha Bingham of Windham, Conn. John's youn
2 CONC ger brother Daniel was the husband of his wife Irene's younger sister, Lydia Robinson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Revolutionary War, John served in Capt. John Sherman's company, Col. Gideon Burt's regiment. June 16, 1782, served four days against insurgents at Springfield, and Northampton, Mass. (vol. 2, p. 196.)
2 CONT
2 CONT At least twelve children were born of record in Stafford before the family finally settled in Claremont, NH. However, the family, or at least some of the children, stopped on the way for brief residences in Amherst, Mass.:
2 CONT
2 CONT • i. Huldah Blodgett, b. Sept. 15, 1756; m. Sgt. (later called Capt.) Thomas Warner at the 1st Congregational Chh. of Stafford, Conn. Oct. 12, 1778. Their daughter Boadicia Warner was the wife of Levi Alden of Claremont, NH, a des
2 CONC cendant of Hon. John Alden of the Mayflower and Plymouth Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT • ii. Elizabeth Blodgett, b. May 29, 1758; no further record known.
2 CONT
2 CONT • iii. Irene Blodgett, b. Jan. 31, 1760; m. Thomas Buell at Stafford, Conn. Jan. 27, 1780.
2 CONT
2 CONT • iv. John Blodgett, Jr., b. Feb. 3, 1762; m. Lois Dickinson at Amherst, Mass. Apr. 5, 1788; they briefly resided in Claremont, NH before settling in Randolph, VT.
2 CONT
2 CONT • v. Darius Blodgett, b. Nov. 27, 1763; d. in infancy Mar. 5, 1764.
2 CONT
2 CONT • vi. Jesse Blodgett, b. Feb. 11, 1765; no further record known.
2 CONT
2 CONT • vii. Luke Blodgett, b. Feb. 20, 1768; m. 1) Martha Dickinson in Amherst, Mass. Apr. 8, 1789, who died in Claremont, NH in 1792; m. 2) Sarah Bangs in Claremont, NH on Jan. 30, 1794. Both died in Claremont in the 1850s.
2 CONT
2 CONT • viii. Samuel Blodgett, b. Dec. 29, 1770; m. Charity Alden at Claremont. NH where they both died in 1853 and 1862, respectively.
2 CONT
2 CONT • ix. Nathan Blodgett, b. June 23, 1773; no further record known.
2 CONT
2 CONT • x. Rosamond Blodgett, possibly the dau. b. at Stafford, Conn. Mar. 3, 1775; m. Walter Ainsworth in Claremont, NH Apr. 20, 1795.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two additional children were born of record int Stafford: twins Martha and Mary in 1768 who apparently died young.  However, the printed vital records and several genealogies of this Blodgett family do not match.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1792 at Claremont, NH Capt. John Blodgett recorded his cattle mark. He d. at Claremont on Apr. 10, 1813, Æ. 80. His widow died two days later on Apr. 12, 1813, also Æ. 80.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edited 7/22/2017 Inscription: Died Capt. John Blodget April 10, 1813 in the 80th year of his age. "The memory of the just is blessed."
2 CONT
2 CONT On the day John died he was 79 years old, and Ætatis suæ (i.e., Æ, "Aged," in the XX year of his Age) 80.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=45245206 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 12 2017, 1:22:31 UTC''
