2 CONT * Samuel "was commissioned April 27, 1759, Third Lieutenant in his Majesty's service at No. 4 (Charlestown, N.H.), by Gov. Pownall of the province of Mass. Bay. During the Revolutionary war he was for some time commissary at Charl
2 CONC estown, a point of concentration for the American troops under Gen. Stark. He was also high sheriff of the county and held at different times various local offices of honor and trust. Though small of stature he was energetic and b
2 CONC rave...He was a farmer at Charlestown, N.H. and quite wealthy."
