2 NOTE also known as the Ebenezer Grant House, 1653 Main St., South Windsor, CT.  Original site of the home of Samuel Grant, son of Matthew, the immigrant.  Inherited by Matthew's grandson, Ebenezer, who remodeled it in 1757. The homeste
3 CONC ad "represents the highest social condition of a prosperous merchant farmer of that period."  It was reproduced in Life Magazine as a "fine example of colonial architecture."  Standing in front, Phil Baker, Matthew's 9th great gra
3 CONC ndson.
