1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Jones/6000000014884418775
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (North) Jones migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1621-1640).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Mary North==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth:	Before Oct 4 1612 - Olney, Buckinghamshire, England
2 CONT * Death:	Feb 4 1682 - Gloucester, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Parents:	Richard North, Joan Bartram
2 CONT * Husband:	Thomas Jones
2 CONT
2 CONT Circa 1638 in Salisbury, Massachusetts, America.  Mary North married Thomas Jones. Her married name was Mary Jones (North). Mary North was an heir in the will of Richard North in 1649 in Salem, Massachusetts, America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary North made a will on 28 January 1681/82 in Gloucester, Essex, Massachusetts, America. She bequeathed to her three daughters one shilling each with the balance of her estate to her son, Benjamin.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 4 February 1681/82 in Gloucester, Massachusetts, America.1
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/North-171
2 CONT
2 CONT [Category:Puritan Great Migration]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT On July 24, 1669 "I, Thomas Jones, of Gloster, formerly of Cape Ann,have received of Ursula North, of Salisbury, Norfolk Co., widow and executrix, a lagasie given unto Mary, my wife, by her father Richard North of Salisbury, decd.
2 CONC " The receipt was acknowledged, April 29, 1673,before Salisbury Court, ye 2d. session. Ursula was the step mother ofMary.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Birth ===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Baptized:''' 4 October 1612 at Olney, Buckinghamshire, England.TAG 1993 vol. 68 no. 2 (April 1993): 65-70.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriage and Children  ===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Married:''' Thomas Jones on 4 Feb 1640 at Salisbury, Essex, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Torrey's New England Marriages gives:<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT JONES, Thomas (1598-1671) &Mary [NORTH]; ca 1637; Gloucester/Manchester {citing: Salisbury 218, 266; Jones (,4) 3; EIHC 42:150; Ferrin-Preston 67; Essex Ant. 11:174}
2 CONT
2 CONT Clarence A. Torrey, compiler, ''New England Marriages Prior to 1700'' (CD version) (Boston, MA: NEHGS, 2001)
2 CONT
2 CONT #Mary (Jones) Winsley.
2 CONT #Susanna North (Jones) Jackson.
2 CONT #Thomas Jones III.
2 CONT #Mary Jones.
2 CONT #North Jones.
2 CONT #Nathaniel Jones.
2 CONT #Ruth (Jones) Howard.
2 CONT #Samuel Jones.
2 CONT #Ephraim Jones.
2 CONT #Benjamin Jones.
2 CONT #Remember Jones.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death ===
2 CONT 4 February 1681/2 in Gloucester, Massachuestts. :"Jones, Mary, 4:12 m:1681."
2 CONT
2 CONT Topsfield Historical Society, compiler, Vital Records of Gloucester, Massachusetts to The End Of The Year 1849 (Topsfield, MA: The Topsfield Historical Society, 1917), Vol. 3:184.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # Greene, David L. The English Origin of Richard(1) North And His Daughter, Susanna(2) (North) Martin, Executed for Witchcraft in 1692. American Genealogist (D.L. Jacobus). (Apr 1993), 68:70. Mary (North) bp. Olney, Buckinghamshir
2 CONC e. 4 Oct. 1612, d. Gloucester, Mass., 4 Feb. 1681/2.
2 CONT # Gloucester, Essex, Massachusetts, United States. Vital Records of Gloucester, Massachusetts, to the End of the Year 1849. (Salem, Massachusetts.: Essex Institute, 1917), 3:184. Jones, Mary, [died] 4:12 m:1681 [February 4, 1681/8
2 CONC 2].
2 CONT # Jones (Thomas), in Pitman, H. Minot (Harold Minot); Donald Lines Jacobus; and G. Andrews Moriarty. Comstock - Thomas ancestry of Richard Wilmot Comstock. (Bronxville, New York: H.M. Pitman, 1964), 157. Mary Jones of Gloucester d
2 CONC ying intestate, Benjamin Jones, her son, presented an inventory of her estate and was appointed Administrator in March 1682. A cow was due to Thomas Howard from his mother. [Essex County Court Records, vol. 8, pp. 290, 371.]
2 CONT #The American Genealogist, vol. 68 no. 2 (April 1993): 65-70.  ''The English Origin of Richard North  and his daughter Susanna   (North) Martin executed for Witchcraft in 1692, David L. Greene. [http://tinyurl.com/yajzpmaf America
2 CONC nAncestors.org ($) LINK]
