2 TITL Flag of Buckinghamshire
2 NOTE https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_of_Buckinghamshire
3 CONT
3 CONT The flag of Buckinghamshire is the flag of the historic county of Buckinghamshire in England. It has been in use for centuries and flew from County Hall in Aylesbury. The flag was registered with the Flag Institute on 20 May 2011.
3 CONT
3 CONT Flag design
3 CONT This is the traditional flag of Buckinghamshire which features a chained swan (The Bohun swan) on a bicolour of red and black, taken from the arms of Bucks. The swan emblem dates back to Anglo-Saxon times, when Buckinghamshire was
3 CONC  known for breeding swans for the king. The Bucks swan appears on the arms of some of the historic towns in Buckinghamshire, such as Aylesbury, Buckingham, Chesham, Marlow and High Wycombe.
3 CONT
3 CONT The Pantone colours for the flag are:[1]
3 CONT
3 CONT Red 186
3 CONT Black
3 CONT White
3 CONT References
3 CONT  "UK Flag Registry: Buckinghamshire".
3 CONT External links
3 CONT Flag Institute registration particulars
3 CONT British County Flags site
2 NOTE https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Buckinghamshire.svg
3 CONT
3 CONT ©	The copyright holder of this file, The Flag Institute, allows anyone to use it for any purpose, provided that the copyright holder is properly attributed. Redistribution, derivative work, commercial use, and all other use is per
3 CONC mitted.
3 CONT Attribution: The Flag Institute
