1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Phebe Wildes
2 CONT * Birth:	1653 - Topsfield, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Death:	Apr 8 1723 - Gloucester, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Parents:	John Wildes, Priscilla Gould
2 CONT * Husband:	Timothy Day, Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:	
2 CONT * Anthony Day, Benjamin Day, Ebenezer Day, Elizabeth Day, John Day, Jonathan Day, Joseph Day, Priscilla Day, Susannah Day, Timothy Day
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT * Accused of witchcraft in 1692, spent time in the Ipswich jail because of it.  Signed [http://salem.lib.virginia.edu/texts/tei/BoySal3R?term=&div_id=d1e23800&chapter_id=BoySal3-n3.167&name=dowmeh "Petition of Ten Prisoners at Ips
2 CONC wich"] as "wife of T[h]imothy Day.". The article [http://www2.iath.virginia.edu/saxon-salem/servlet/SaxonServlet?source=salem/texts/bios.xml&style=salem/xsl/dynaxml.xsl&chunk.id=b44&clear-stylesheet-cache=yes "The Geography and Ge
2 CONC nealogy of Gloucester Witchcraft" Written by Jedediah Drolet (copyright, 2005)] discusses the Gloucester group of accused witches.
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT Phoebe2 Wildes (John1 Wild) was born 1653 in Topsfield, Massachusetts, and died 08 Apr 1723. She
2 CONT married Timothy Day 24 Jul 1679 in GLOUCESTER, MA, son of Anthony Day and Susannah Matchett.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Phoebe Wildes:
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband's receipt for her legacy from her grandfather Gould's estate is as follows:-- "This Massachusetts sartefi to houm it Massachusetts consern that I Timothy Day have reseued the full and iust sum of my wife house name  wa
2 CONC s Phoebe Wylds part of ye wish in riten bond of my unkel John Gould." In 1692 she was accused of witchcraft and was taken to Ipswich gaol where she remained until September 24, of the same year, when she was released on bonds for 
2 CONC her reappearance, together with Mary Rowe and Widow Rachel Vinson. These three Gloucester witches were accused of bewitching the sister of Lieut. Stephens, and the story is also related that when the three women were crossing Ipsw
2 CONC ich bridge on their way to the gaol, an old woman who met them was immediately thrown into convulsions. The fact that she was taken to Ipswich instead of to Salem, where the trials were being held, may have saved her life, for the
2 CONC re were so many victims in Salem that all others were forgotten.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died April 8, 1723, aged seventy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Timothy Day:
2 CONT
2 CONT [New.ged]
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy Day, son of Anthony and Susannah Day of Gloucester, lived on the westerly side of the Squam River. He was a member of the First Church of Gloucester. In 1730, he deeded his Gloucester property to his son John for care and 
2 CONC affection in his old age.[Cook.GED]
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Timothy Day and Phoebe Wildes:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Marriage 1: 24 Jul 1679, GLOUCESTER, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Phoebe Wildes and Timothy Day are:
2 CONT * + 30 i. Timothy3 Day, born 19 Jan 1678/79 in OR 1680 TOPSFIELD, Massachusetts; died 16 Sep 1757.
2 CONT * 31 ii. John Day, born 21 Jan 1680/81; died 22 Jan 1680/81.
2 CONT * + 32 iii. Anthony Day, born 20 Dec 1681; died 12 Jan 1711/12.
2 CONT * + 33 iv. John Day, born 01 Feb 1683/84 in GLOUCESTER, Massachusetts; died 1747 in Gloucester,
2 CONT * + 34 v. Jonathan Day, born 08 Nov 1685; died in Before 1732.
2 CONT * + 35 vi. Susannah Day, born 11 Apr 1688; died 19 Jun 1720.
2 CONT * 36 vii. Priscilla Day, born 25 May 1689; died 08 Jun 1689.
2 CONT * 37 viii. Elizabeth Day, born 23 May 1690; died 23 May 1690 in born alive but died shortly after.
2 CONT * 38 ix. Benjamin Day, born 05 Dec 1695; died 23 Jul 1697.
2 CONT * + 39 x. Ebenezer Day, born 14 Nov 1697.
2 CONT * + 40 xi. Joseph Day. (No dates) m. Patience __.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Priscilla Gould died date unknown. She married John sr Wildes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Priscilla Gould and John sr Wildes are: 
2 CONT i.	+'''Phoebe Wildes''', b. 1653, Topsfield Ma., d. April 08, 1723.
2 CONT
