1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Seen as wife of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Vinson/6000000002946576280 without evidence. She was “Rachel Cook” on her marriage record with Elisha Kibbe.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Rachel Cook 
2 CONT * BIRTH 25 Sep 1645
2 CONT * DEATH 10 Sep 1740 (aged 94)
2 CONT * BURIAL Burial Details Unknown 
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 38252652  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.jtbullock.com/Tree/EdKibbe.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachell Cooke was born on September 25, 1645, in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts to Henry Cooke and Judith Birdsall. She married Elisha Kibbe there on December 12, 1667: 
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000221986346821&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT They had at least seven children, the first four were born in Salem, the younger ones were born in Enfield, Hartford County, Connecticut — 
2 CONT
2 CONT #John on February 1, 1667/8;
2 CONT # ancestor Edward; 
2 CONT #Elisha on March 28, 1673, who died at 15 years old about the middle of August, 1688;
2 CONT # James on December 27, 1675; 
2 CONT #Mary in 1679;
2 CONT # Isaac on March 21, 1683, the first to be born in Enfield; and 
2 CONT # Rachel on April 17, 1688. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Potter-Richardson Memorial states that there was another son named Thomas, who probably died in infancy, but there isn’t documentation as to when and where he was born. He may have been born during the move to Enfield, or he m
2 CONC ay not be their child at all.
2 CONT
2 CONT Researchers say that Rachell Cooke Kibbe died in Enfield on September or December 10, 1740, a bit more than five years after her husband’s death, but this researcher has not found a death record for her in the Enfield records. It 
2 CONC is not known where she is buried, but she is probably buried with her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==References==
