1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Omsted-10
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses was born in 1782. He was the son of Gideon Omstead and Abigail Cooley. He passed away in 1837.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses married Catherine Risch (or Rust or Rush) about 1805 in Ontario, Canada. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1820, Moses and his family were in Oakland, Michigan Territory. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT The history of Branch County, Michigan, tells that the first inhabitant of the Town of Bethel was Eleazer Snow in the spring of 1830. In the fall of 1831, he sold his claim along with the improvements to Moses Olmstead, who had be
2 CONC en a resident of Oakland County, Michigan. He came with his wife [Catharine], his sons, Moses Jr., Philip, Gideon, and Lyman – and his daughters, Abby, Eliza, and Hannah. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT >They moved into the log hut built by Snow, and built another hut of rails, covered with hay, in which the men found a lodging place while the women occupied the log hut. In this manner the first winter was passed, and then a larg
2 CONC er and more convenient house was built for the accommodation of the family. Moses Olmstead was a thorough-going man, resolute and energetic, and carried these qualities into his farming operations. By reason of this he rapidly bro
2 CONC ught his farm into splendid condition, and his stock was always noted for the sleek and well-fed look that characterized it. He erected the first frame building in the township. It was a large and commodious barn, built in 1834-35
2 CONC . He was prominently connected with the work of organizing the town, but died soon after the first town meeting, in the spring or summer of 1837. His wife died about a year later.
2 CONT The history goes on to explain that of his children, Gideon died about two or three years after the family settled and was probably the first death of a white person in the town. Lyman Olmstead married Sarah Ann Cummings and died 
2 CONC in the town in October 1864. Moses Olmstead Jr. died in Missouri in 1872. Philip Olmstead moved to Utah. The three daughter all died in Bethel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses died April 13, 1837 in Bethel, Michigan. His Last Will is online in Michigan Probate Records. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LBG3-XQZ/moses-omstead-1782-1837
2 CONT
2 CONT When Moses Omstead was born on 12 March 1782, in Pittsford, Rutland, Vermont, United States, his father, Gideon Omsted, was 24 and his mother, Abigail Cooley, was 15. He married Catherine Risch in 1805, in Ontario, Canada. They we
2 CONC re the parents of at least 4 sons and 8 daughters. He died on 13 April 1837, in Bethel, Branch, Michigan, United States, at the age of 55.
2 CONT
