1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Pease, borrn about 1607 (aged 27 on 30 Apr 1634), son of Robert Pease of Great Baddow, Essex. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >''Alternate birth date:  born in 1589 in Great Baddow, Essex, England,1 was christened on 28 Oct 1589 of Ipswich, Suffolk, Eng,1 Ancestral File Number: 8KLR-VX.''
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 27 Oct 1644 in Salem, MA at age 55. 
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: First generation of the Pease family in America Part 1 of 2 1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Pease, son of Robert and Margaret (King) Pease, one of the immigrant ancestors of the Pease family in America; bpt. Oct 28, 1589 in Great Baddow, county Essex, England; d. Oct 27, 1644 in Salem, MA;
2 CONT
2 CONT M. (1) Lydia, (possibly Lydia West). She probably died before he made the journey to America. This marriage to Lydia West is not proven, and is not mentioned in the early Pease genealogies. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://minerdescent.com/2010/08/25/robert-pease-jr-great-baddow/
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Pease Jr – Great Baddow
2 CONT Posted on August 25, 2010 by markeminer
2 CONT Robert PEASE Jr. – Great Baddow(1589 – 1644)  was Alex’s 11th Great Grandfather twice, through his son Robert and his son John.  He was  two of 4,096 in this generation of the Miner line.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Pease – Coat of Arms
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Pease was baptized in 28 Oct 1589 in Great Baddow, Essex, England.  His parents were Robert PEASE and Margaret KING.  He married Lydia WEST in England.  After Lydia died, he married Marie [__?__] also in England.   He came 
2 CONC to New England in the ship Francis, John CUTTING [our ancestor], master, sailing from Ipswich, England the last of Apr 1634. The ship landed at Boston without the loss of a single passenger. Robert was accompanied by his brother J
2 CONC ohn, his eldest son Robert, a Miss Clark, aged fifteen, who was the daughter of a fellow passenger, and a Miss Greene, aged fifteen, perhaps a servant.  His wife Marie and other family members probably came on a later ship.   Robe
2 CONC rt died on 27 Oct 1644 in Salem, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia West  probably died before he made the journey to America. This marriage to Lydia West is not proven, and is not mentioned in the early Pease genealogies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert’s second wife, Marie, whose possible maiden name was Rodans, and the other children arrived in New England on a later ship. Marie, which is French for Mary, may have been born in Great Baddow, and her parents were probably 
2 CONC Protestant refugees from France.  She has also been called Marie Browning, Marie Warren and Marie French. After Robert Pease died, Marie married Richard Haines of Beverly, Mass. taking the three other children with her.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Pease Probate 1644 Source: A genealogical and historical record of the descendants of John Pease, Senior by Rev. David Pease and Austin Pease 1869
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert's baptism is not recorded in St. Mary's. He came to New England in the ship Francis, John Cutting, master, sailing from Ipswich, England the last of Apr 1634. The ship landed at Boston, MA without the loss of a single passe
2 CONC nger. Robert was accompanied by his brother John, his eldest son Robert, a Miss Clark, aged fifteen, who was the daughter of a fellow passenger, and a Miss Greene, aged fifteen, perhaps a servant. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Pease disappeared from records from the time he landed at Boston until three years later in Salem, MA, where in Jan 1637, he and his brother John had grants of land, Robert receiving ten acres. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Pease, widow and mother of Robert and John, also emigrated to America, and died Sep 01, 1644 in Salem. In her will dated Sep 01, 1642, proved Jan 01, 1645, she mentions a grandchild, John, son of Robert. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Robert and Lydia Pease, born and baptized in Great Baddow, Essex, England: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.1 Robert bpt. Apr 1630 d.  
2 CONT * 1.2 John bpt. Feb 11, 1632 d. Jul 08, 1689 Enfield, CT 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert's second wife, Marie, whose possible maiden id was Rodans, and the other children arrived in New England on a later ship. Marie, which is French for Mary, may have been born in Great Baddow, and her parents were probably Pr
2 CONC otestant refugees from France. Robert Pease and Marie were admitted to the Salem Church Oct 01, 1643, and two weeks later, three of their children were baptized there. Marie, widow of Robert Pease was administratix, and the invent
2 CONC ory of his estate was filed Aug 27, 1644. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Robert and Marie Pease baptized in Salem, MA: 
2 CONT * 1.3 Nathaniel b. 1634 d. 
2 CONT * 1.4 Sarah b. 1642 d. 
2 CONT * 1.5 Mary b. Aug 15,1643 d. ca. 1683 Salem, MA 
2 CONT
2 CONT There may have been another son of Robert and Lydia or Marie, Isaac Pease, born and baptized in England, who did not have a family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After Robert Pease died, Marie m. (2) Richard Haines of Beverly, MA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married Lydia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children from this marriage were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * + 11 M    i. Robert PEASE was christened in Apr 1630 in Great Baddow, Essex, England 2 and died after 1717. 
2 CONT * + 12 M    ii. John PEASE was christened in Feb 1631 in Great Baddow, Essex, England 2 and died on 8 Jul 1689 in Enfield, Hartford Co., CT at age 58. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Came from Ipswich, England in April 1634 aboard the ship Frances. Settled in Salem, MA.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT He was baptized October 28, 1589 in Great Baddow, Essex, England. Robert immigrated from Ipswitch to Salem, New England aboard the ship Francis in 1634. He was accompanied by his brother John and eldest son, Robert. His wife and o
2 CONC ther members of the family including his son John and his mother Margaret probably came in a later ship the same year. Robert Pease is supposed to have been the son of Robert and Margaret Pease of Great Baddow, Essex county, Engla
2 CONC nd. He received a grant of land at Salem, Mass., in 1637 and resided there until his death. His mother joined the First Salem Church in 1639. Robert joined it in 1643 and three of his children were baptized at that time. There is 
2 CONC no record as to when his wife died; she was alive at the time of his death according to his will. His mother died in 1644. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
