2 CONC e on-line]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT November 1634: Sailed with his brother John on the ship Francis from Ipswich arrivinb at Boston late in 1634
2 CONT
2 CONT 1637, Salem: mentioned as having land in the early Salem Town Record. "Robert Pease and his Brother"
2 CONT
2 CONT 1643: Joined the church at Salem. At which time three of his children were baptized.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died before his mother, his estate inventoried 3 Nov 1644 and the widow Marie appointed administrator. Widow Mare remarried Richard Haines of Beverly, MA taking the three other children with her.
2 CONT
