1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Pease, son of Robert and Margaret (King) Pease, one of the immigrant ancestors of the Pease family in America; bpt. Oct 28, 1589 in Great Baddow, county Essex, England; d. Oct 27, 1644 in Salem, MA;
2 CONT
2 CONT M. (1) Lydia, (possibly '''Lydia West'''). She probably died before he made the journey to America. This marriage to Lydia West is not proven, and is not mentioned in the early Pease genealogies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Robert and Lydia Pease, born and baptized in Great Baddow, Essex, England:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.1 Robert bpt. Apr 1630 d.
2 CONT * 1.2 John bpt. Feb 11, 1632 d. Jul 08, 1689 Enfield, CT
2 CONT
2 CONT There may have been another son of Robert and Lydia or Marie, Isaac Pease, born and baptized in England, who did not have a family.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources 
2 CONT *[https://www.ancestry.com/interactive/2496/42521_b158316-00531/37924?backurl=https%3a%2f%2fsearch.ancestry.com%2fcgi-bin%2fsse.dll%3fdb%3dgreatmigration%26gsfn%3dRobert%26gsln%3dPease%26hc%3d50%26new%3d1%26rank%3d1%26redir%3dfals
2 CONC e%26uidh%3dyd5&ssrc=&backlabel=ReturnRecord#?imageId=42521_b158316-00532 link] to Robert Pease in The Great Migration Begins 
