1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rufus Pease
2 CONT BIRTH	17 May 1756
2 CONT Enfield, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT DEATH	7 Apr 1801 (aged 44), Enfield, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	Enfield Street Cemetery, Enfield, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA  Show Map
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID  25612988, Photos by Sue
2 CONT
2 CONT [Rufus Pease "was born May 17, 1757, [to Isaac and Rachel (Hall) Pease], in Enfield, where all his life was spent in the cultivation of his extensive property and where he died in 1801. Ruth Cooley, who became his wife in 1782, bo
2 CONC re him the following children: (1) Rufus, born in 1783, married Bathsheba Pease, was a farmer and shoemaker in Tolland, and died Jan. 7, 1854. (2) Alpheus, who married Lois Dwight, was born in 1785 and followed farming in Enfield,
2 CONC  where he died. (3) Enos, born in 1786, married Lucy Adams, of Stafford, Conn., was a farmer and lived in Enfield during his earlier years, but later removed to Somers, where he died. (4) Ruth, born in 1789, married Thomas Pease, 
2 CONC a farmer of Ellington, but later of Enfield, where they both died. (5) Dorothy, born in 1790, married William Hills, a farmer and hunter in Enfield, where they died. (6) Cooley [born in Enfield on Nov. 8, 1822], the father of Salm
2 CONC on F. ... (7) Augustus, born in 1794, married Maria Knight, and was a farmer in Enfield." [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT In Memory of 
2 CONT Mr. Rufus Pease
2 CONT who Died April 
2 CONT 7th 1801 in the 44th
2 CONT year of his Age.
2 CONT
2 CONT All you advans'd in years
2 CONT you healthy and robust,
2 CONT you are totering around the grave,
2 CONT And soon must turn to dust.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse
2 CONT Ruth Cooley Pease 1756–1828 (m. 1783)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT Rufus Pease 1783–1854
2 CONT Alpheus Pease 1785–1860
2 CONT Ruth Pease 1789–1845
2 CONT Cooley Pease 1792–1853
2 CONT Augustus Pease 1794 – unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT [1] https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/25612988/rufus-pease
