1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikitree.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Pease formerly Farrington
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 2 Sep 1744 in Somers, Tolland, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Abner Pease — married 25 Jan 1763 in Somers, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Abner Pease, Daniel Pease, John Pease, James Pease, Samuel Pease, Sally (Pease) Hayes and Sybil (Pease) Powers
2 CONT
2 CONT Died about 1822
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 17 Nov 2017 | Created 5 Jan 2017
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT 122. CAPT. ABNER PEASE,5 (Isaac,4 Isaac,3 John,2 Robert,1) third son of ISAAC and AMY (FRENCH) PEASE, was born at Enfield, 1733; married Elizabeth Farrington, January, 1763. [Somers Town Records.] He married, second, Lovisa Allen.
2 CONC  It appears he first settled in Somers, Ct., but subsequently removed to the eastern part of the State of New York. He held the office of deputy sheriff, in what was the county of Albany, in 1777, and came near losing his life in 
2 CONC the discharge of his duty, while apprehending riotous Tories. He joined the Shakers, which congregated near New Lebanon, N. Y., in 1780; and died in that connection at his residence in Stephentown, N. Y., in 1784, of small pox, ag
2 CONC ed about 51 years.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ A Genealogical and Historical Record of the Descendants of John Pease, Sen., Last of Enfield, Conn., Compiled by Rev. David Pease, and Austin S. Pease, as Associate Editor (1869). See generally:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F7WN-W68 : 3 December 2014), Elizabeth Farrington, 07 Oct 1744; citing ; FHL microfilm unknown. "Connecticut Births 
2 CONC and Christenings, 1649-1906," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F74D-N86 : 3 December 2014), Elizabeth in entry for Abner Pease, 24 Apr 1763; citing ; FHL microfilm unknown. A Genealogical and Histori
2 CONC cal Record of the Descendants of John Pease, Sen., Last of Enfield, Conn., Compiled by Rev. David Pease, and Austin S. Pease, as Associate Editor (1869).
2 CONT
