1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Burial record:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/17836825/elizabeth-allyn
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Booth Allyn
2 CONT BIRTH 19 Aug 1705 Enfield, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT DEATH 10 Sep 1751 (aged 46) East Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT BURIAL Town Street Cemetery, East Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID 17836825
2 CONT Info by F.A.G. #47028054
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was the daughter of Zachariah Booth (1666-1741) and Mary Harmon. Sergeant Zachariah Booth was a prominent man in the Enfiled life of his day. His name occurs often in the town records in connection with various offices o
2 CONC f trust; when the first bank was organized he was one of the trustees; he was Constable in 1692, and Selectman several times. He was the third Town Clerk, serving from 1723-1729; was Sergeant of the train band, and Deputy in 1731 
2 CONC and 1732. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was the wife of Samuel Allen (1702-1771) and they married on 27 Jan 1728 in Enfield, Hartford, CT. They had nine known children: Samuel, Elizabeth, Abel, Tabithy, Love, Peletiah, Zachariah, Sarah and Amasa "Amzi", Sr.  E
2 CONC lizabeth's husband Samuel and his brother Joseph engaged in the manufacture of tar and pitch, and also operated a farm in East Windsor, CT.  His farm was later known as the "Landlord Allen Farm" and was situated on the old stage r
2 CONC oad from Springfield to Hartford, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT The family name is sometimes spelled Allyn - which has created confusion in records and documentation. Some of the children of Samuel and Elizabeth spell the name Allen. Will try to include links where possible with alternate spel
2 CONC lings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inscription'''
2 CONT wife of Samuel Allyn - died in the ? year of her age
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Zechariah Booth 1669–1741
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Samuel Allyn 1701–1771
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Robert Booth 1692–1714
2 CONT John Booth 1697–1778
2 CONT Sarah Booth Pease 1703–1792
2 CONT Jemima Booth Pease 1708–1772
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''' 9x
2 CONT Elizabeth Allyn Mather 1724–1791
2 CONT Samuel Allen 1731–1759
2 CONT Abel Allen 1733–1808 m. Elizabeth Sophia Chapin in 1756 in Enfield, CT.
2 CONT Tabithy Allen Chapin ____-1790 m.  Abner Chapin in 1781.
2 CONT Love Allyn
2 CONT Peletiah Allyn
2 CONT Zachariah Allyn 1742–1831
2 CONT Sarah Allen Pasco 1746–4/20/1825 m. Jonah Pasco
2 CONT Amasa "Amizi" Allen Sr. 1750–1820 m. Alie Lord in 1780 at East Windsor, CT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Descendant Details==
2 CONT Son Amasa married Alie Lord in 1780 in East Windsor, CT.  He served in the Rev War and enlisted on 21 Apr 1777 in Col Parvin's Regt at Enfield.  He later transferred to Col Van Schaich's NY Regt.  He served until April 1780.  Amas
2 CONC a was honorably discharged and engaged in the battles of Princeton, Trenton, and Monmouth, CT.  Amasa and Alice eventually settled in Pavillon, Genesse, New York. Amasa's name was Amizi in some records.  He was known as the younge
2 CONC st child of Samuel and Elizabeth (Booth) Allen. Burial in Maplewood Cemetery in Genessee Co. NY.  Amasa and Alice eventually settled in Pavillon, Genesse County, New York. Amasa's name was aka Amizi in some records. He was the you
2 CONC ngest child of Samuel and Elizabeth (Booth) Allen. Burial in Maplewood Cem in Genessee Co. NY.
2 CONT
