1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Warriner-56
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Warriner (1682 - 1737)
2 CONT Born 4 Mar 1682 in Springfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts Bay Colony 
2 CONT Died 5 Feb 1737 at age 54 in Springfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts Bay Colony 
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of James Warriner and Elizabeth (Baldwin) Warriner
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Samuel Warriner, James Warriner II, Elizabeth (Warriner) Burt, William (Warringer) Warriner, Hannah (Warriner) Graves, Joseph Warriner, Samuel Warriner, Mary Warringer, Sarah (Warriner) Thomas [half], Jonathan Warriner 
2 CONC [half], Benjamin Warriner [half] and David Warriner [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Joanna (Dickinson) Warriner — married 8 Jan 1700 in Springfield, Hampshire, Province of Massachusetts Bay map icon at age 17
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Ebenezer Warriner, Joanna Warriner, Mary (Warriner) Cadwell, Abigail (Warriner) Pease, Joanna (Warriner) Brooks, Elizabeth (Warriner) Stebbins, Martha Warriner, Rachel (Warriner) Bliss, Ebenezer Warriner and Hezekiah War
2 CONC riner
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Warriner was born on 4 March 1682 in Springfield, Hampden, Massachusetts. His parents were Deacon James Warriner (1640 - 1727) and Elizabeth (Baldwin) Warriner (1645 - 1687).[1].[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT His siblings were...
2 CONT
2 CONT * Samuel Warriner (1666 - )
2 CONT * James Warriner II (1668 - ~1735)
2 CONT * Elizabeth (Warriner) Burt (1670 - >1711)
2 CONT * William Warringer (1672 - 1738)
2 CONT * Hannah (Warriner) Graves (1674 - 1711)
2 CONT * Joseph Warriner (1677 - )
2 CONT * Samuel Warriner (1678 - 1713)
2 CONT * Mary Warringer (1685 - )
2 CONT * Sarah (Warriner) Thomas (1690 - >1728)
2 CONT * Benjamin Warriner (1698 - 1764)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer filed intentions to marry Joanna (Dickinson) Warriner (1684-) on 21 December 1700, and they were married on 8 January 1701 in Springfield, Hampden, Massachusetts.[3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were...
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ebenezer Warriner (1701 - 1713)
2 CONT * Joanna Warriner (1703 - 1709)
2 CONT * Mary Warriner (1703 - ~1791)
2 CONT * Abigail (Warriner) Pease (1705 - 1763)
2 CONT * Joanna (Warriner) Brooks (1711 - 1756)
2 CONT * Elizabeth (Warriner) Stebbins (1713 - 1805)
2 CONT * Martha Warriner (1716 - 1742)
2 CONT * Rachel (Warriner) Bliss (1717 - 1795)
2 CONT * Ebenezer Warriner (1719 - 1813)
2 CONT * Hezekiah Warriner (1724 - 1785).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer died on 5 February 1737 in Springfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts Bay, British Colonial America.[5] He is buried in the Springfield Cemetery in Springfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts.[6]
