1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for CONNECTICUT with the rank of SERGEANT.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A071567   DAR Ancestor #: A071567]	
2 CONT
2 CONT Served with the Connecticut Troops enlisting in May, 1775. Served as a Private for seven months in Capt. Hezekiah Parsons' Company, which took part in the seige of Boston. Served as a Sargeant on tours in 1777, 1778, and 1781, in 
2 CONC all at least seven months, a part of the time under Capt. Amasa Loomis, Col. Samuel B Webb's Regt
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Connecticut Men in the War of the Revolution; Lists and Returns of Connecticut Men in the Revolution, 1775-1783.
