3 CITY Wethersfield
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 MAR 1793
2 ADDR
3 CITY Granville
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Find a Grave contributor:
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/64661387/abigail-rose
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Hale Rose had 14 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born
2 CONT Died 1793
2 CONT Age 103 yrs
2 CONT COD
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail had been blind for 15 years. Her memory remained strong until closer to her death. She settled with her husband, Jonathan who was born 1679 (Scotland) in East Granville,Ma about 1741.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan was a Deacon in the Congregational Church. He burned to death when their home caught fire in Oct 1767.
2 CONT
2 CONT Together Jonathan and Abigail had 14 children, 7 lived to a very old age. Her seven children all had families.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1790, her 100th birthday, a meeting was called of her family. A sermon was given and her family enumerated. In 1790 her had 110 grandchildren, over 300 great-grandchildren and over 40 family members of the 5th generation. She h
2 CONC ad 450 LIVING descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT A new house was erected to replace the family home that claimed her husband on the same plot. Abigail lived in this home and in 1859 two of her grandchildren lived their "golden years" like their grandmother in the same home.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 15 children were, 8 sons, 7 daughters
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 JONATHAN ROSE, JR (II)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 18 Feb 1707/08, Wethersfield, Hartford, CT
2 CONT d. Aft. 1790, prob Granville, Hampshire, MA
2 CONT married (1) MARY GILMAN
2 CONT Born Abt. 1707
2 CONT Died 1750;
2 CONT Mary, had two children from a previous marriage,They 5 children of their own
2 CONT Married (2) LYDIA UNKNOWN
2 CONT Died 10 Mar 1763.
2 CONT They had 5 children
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 DAVID ROSE
2 CONT Born 13 Sep 1709, Wethersfield, Hartford, CT
2 CONT Died Bet. 1790 - 1793
2 CONT David was the one who started the family migration from to Bedford, MA (Granville) David Rose left Durham and secured 100 acres in Granville, built a cabin, started clearing land, and moved his family to Granville. He then purchas
2 CONC ed 1500 acres more in 1741. (26 families left Durham for Granville) David was a deacon, a tithingman, and served the town in many ways. In 1790 he left the Congregational Church and started a Baptist Church in his home, which late
2 CONC r became the first Baptist Church in Granville.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 DOROTHY ROSE
2 CONT Born 20 Jun 1711, Wethersfield, Hartford, CT
2 CONT Died 1746, Granville, Hampshire, MA
2 CONT Married 22 Nov 1732, Guilford, Connecticut, as his 3rd wife
2 CONT DR EBENEZER SEWARD
2 CONT Born 1703. Notes for DR EBENEZER SEWARD: marriages. The Father Caleb Seward of Guilford
2 CONT Mother Lydia Bushnell(daughter of William Bushnell of Saybrook)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 DAMARIS ROSE (1)
2 CONT Born 30 Jul 1713, Wethersfield, Hartford, CT
2 CONT Died 09 Jun 1714, Wethersfield, Hartford, CT'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 ABIGAIL ROSE
2 CONT Born Abt. 1715, Durham, Middlesex, CT
2 CONT Died 10 Sep 1768
2 CONT Married
2 CONT BENJAMIN PEASE
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 DANIEL ROSE
2 CONT Born 12 Jan 1716/17, Durham, Middlesex, CT
2 CONT Died 20 Jun 1790, Granville, Hampshire, MA
2 CONT ACHSAH BALL
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 ELISHA ROSE (1)
2 CONT Born 08 Feb 1718/19, Durham, Middlesex, CT
2 CONT Died 01 Mar 1718/19, Durham, Middlesex, CT'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 JOHN ROSE
2 CONT Born 18 Feb 1719/20, Durham, Middlesex, CT
2 CONT Died 1788, Granville, Hampshire, MA
2 CONT Married (1) RUTH HOLCOMB
2 CONT Married (2) KEZIAH GOSS
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 DAMARIS ROSE
2 CONT Born Bef. Mar 1721/22, Durham, Middlesex, CT
2 CONT Died 03 May 1807, Wethersfield, CT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT OLIVER TREAT
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 JUSTICE ROSE
2 CONT Born 22 Mar 1723/24, Durham, Middlesex, CT
2 CONT Died 25 Sep 1781, Granville, Hampshire, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 ELIZABETH ROSE
2 CONT Born 20 Feb 1725/26, Enfield, Hartford, CT
2 CONT Died 22 Oct 1786, Granville, Hampshire, MA
2 CONT Married 22 Apr 1762, Granville,Hampshire, MA
2 CONT AARON SPELMAN
2 CONT Born 22 Jan 1732/33
2 CONT Died 18 Oct 1821, Granville,Hampshire, MA
2 CONT The book, Spelman Genealogy, observes: the marriage of Aaron Spelman caused some odd
2 CONT relationships. His first wife was Elizabeth Rose, sister to Justice Rose. At the death of Elizabeth, he married the widow of Justus, Deborah Barlow. His brother, Stephen, who was several years younger than Aaron, had married Debor
2 CONC ah Rose, the daughter of Justus and Deborah. Thus Aaron and his second wife were, by marriage, at one the uncle and aunt, the step-father and mother, and the brother and sister-in-law of Stephen and his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT 12 ELISHA ROSE
2 CONT Born Jun 1728, Enfield, Hartford, CT
2 CONT Died 10 Dec 1814, Granville, Hampton, MA
2 CONT Married (1)Bef. 1752, Granville,Hampshire, MA
2 CONT ABIGAIL UNKNOWN
2 CONT Born Abt. 1730
2 CONT Died 1775, Granfield,Hampshire, MA
2 CONT Married (2)17 Apr 1777, Wintonbury Parish, CT
2 CONT SYBIL GRISWOLD
2 CONT Born 17 Apr 1742, Windsor,Hartf ord, CT
2 CONT Died 14 Aug 1829, Granville,Hampshire, MA
2 CONT Buried in West Cemetery, Granville CentreElishu was a private in the Revolutionary War, under Capt.
2 CONT Cooley Co, Col John Mosley, Hampshire Co. Served 4 days, then served 24 days under Capt. Aaron Coe's Co.
2 CONT 14 Children
2 CONT 1-Dorothy
2 CONT 2-Amos b 1756 Mar 6 Granville, MA
2 CONT 3-Elisha
2 CONT 4-Phineas
2 CONT 5-Abigail
