2 CONT Jonathan Rose, who was burned to death at the age of one hundred and three, had three sons, — Sharon, Daniel, and Timothy. The latter served as a soldier in the Revolutionary war,yand after the close of the war earned some distinc
2 CONC tion by con-
2 CONT ducting a colony" of settlers from Granville, Mass., to Granville, Ohio, where he became one of the judiciary, and died in 1815.
2 CONT Sharon had a large family, consisting of Giles, Sharon, Jr., Peter, Oliver, Dwyer, Mercy, Ruth, and Abigail. The descendants of Jonathan Rose now living in Granville are Isaac, Justus, Patrick, Salem P., Jephtha, James, Emerson,an
2 CONC d Miles.
