1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/108812909/daniel-kingsbury
2 CONT
2 CONT Ens Daniel Kingsbury VVeteran
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT 20 Sep 1749
2 CONT Bolton, Tolland County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT Death
2 CONT 1810 (aged 60–61)
2 CONT Rushford, Allegany County, New York, USA
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT First Burying Ground Cemetery
2 CONT Rushford, Allegany County, New York, USA
2 CONT Memorial ID
2 CONT 108812909 · View Source
2 CONT Memorial
2 CONT Photos 1
2 CONT Flowers 1
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sponsor this memorial with an exclusive premium layout and no ads.
2 CONT Sponsor this page
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel was the son of John Kingsbury(1710-1780) & his wife Abigail Phelps- bissell(1709-1782)
2 CONT
2 CONT He married on 12/2/1751 in Enfield, Hartland County, Connecticut to Rose Pease, daughter of Benjamin Pease & his wife Abigail Rose of Enfield, Massachusetts. He lived in Enfield on land that his father gave him. He was a Sargent o
2 CONC f the company started in Enfield for the Lexington Alarm under Major Nathaniel Terry. He was appointed Ensign in the 2nd Battalion of State Troops 11/1776 & he also served in Rhode Island under General Wooster in 1777.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their Children were:
2 CONT 1. Lucy Kingsbury(1772-)b. Enfield,CT
2 CONT 2. Daniel Kingsbury(1773-1842)
2 CONT 3. George Kingsbury(1775-) "
2 CONT 4. Isaac Kingsbury(1777-) Hartland, CT
2 CONT 5. Benjamin Kingsbury(1779-1850) Sandisfield, Berkshie Co, MA
2 CONT 6. John Kingsbury(1782-1850) "
2 CONT 7. Abigail Kingsbury(1785-) "
2 CONT 8. Eunice Kingsbury(1786-) "
2 CONT 9. William Kingsbury(1788-1789)born & died @ Sandisfield, Ma
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT 1. Connecticut Men in the Revolution
2 CONT 2. Rushford & Rushford People by Helen J White Gilbert
2 CONT 3. Genealogy of the Descendents of Henry Kingsbury of Ipswich, Massachusetts by, pgs. 258-259
2 CONT 4. The Sprague Project by Richard Weber
2 CONT
2 CONT I believe that Ensign Daniel Kingsbury may have died in Cherry Valley, but there is NO gravestone to mark his place of burial, as so many unmarked graves in the Cherry Valley Area( Roseboom), NY & that his son John Kingsbury suppo
2 CONC seably was also buried in Cherry Valley, NY
