1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT == Biography: Lydia (Abbott) Chandler ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Abbott was born on March 31, 1675, in Andover, Essex County, Massachusetts, to the foundational colonial family of '''George Abbott, Jr.''' and '''Sarah Farnum'''. Her birth is explicitly recorded in the Andover vital books 
2 CONC under the variant entry *"(ABBOT) Lydia, d. George and Sarah, Mar. 31, 1675."*
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia married into the neighboring Chandler family and spent her early adult life in Andover. In 1723, she and her husband joined a coordinated multi-family migration inland to the newly developing frontier town of Enfield (then w
2 CONC ithin the disputed borders of Massachusetts, later annexed into Hartford County, Connecticut). Lydia lived out the remainder of her life in Enfield, dying there on March 11, 1739, at the age of 63. She is buried at the Enfield Str
2 CONC eet Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Through her son, Deacon Daniel Chandler, Sr., Lydia is a direct maternal ancestor of Rutherford Birchard Hayes, the 19th President of the United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage and Family ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia married '''Henry Chandler''' on November 28, 1695, in Andover, as recorded in the town's marriage register: *"(ABBOTT) Lydia, and Henry Chandler, Nov. 28, 1695."* Henry was born on May 28, 1667, to Captain Thomas Chandler an
2 CONC d Hannah Brewer. He was an influential surveyor and landowner who purchased extensive acreage in Enfield prior to their relocation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia and Henry were the parents of thirteen children, all born in Andover before the family's westward migration:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Deacon Henry Chandler, Jr.''' (1696–1756) m. '''Hannah Foster'''.
2 CONT * '''Samuel Chandler''' (1698–1781) m. '''Hepzibah Colt'''.
2 CONT * '''Lydia Chandler''' (1699–1760) m. '''John Booth'''.
2 CONT * '''Deacon Daniel Chandler, Sr.''' (1701–1785) m. '''Sarah Keep'''. (Great-great-grandparents of President Rutherford B. Hayes).
2 CONT * '''Nehemiah Chandler, I''' (1703–1756) m. '''Mary Allen'''.
2 CONT * '''Abigail Chandler''' (1705–1772) m. '''John Rumrill'''.
2 CONT * '''Sarah Chandler''' (1707–1777) m. '''Joseph Booth'''.
2 CONT * '''Deborah Chandler''' (1709–1769) m. '''Ebenezer Colton'''.
2 CONT * '''Hannah Chandler''' (1712–c. 1745) m. '''Ezekiel Pease'''.
2 CONT * '''Mary Chandler''' (1713–1789) m. '''Timothy Pease'''.
2 CONT * '''Isaac Chandler''' (1717–1787) m. '''Abigail Hale'''.
2 CONT * '''Mehitable Chandler''' (1719–1720); died in infancy in Andover.
2 CONT * '''Mehitable Chandler''' (1721–c. 1723); died young around the time of the family's move to Enfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Forensic Note: The "Two Henries" Identity Firewall ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Curators handling this lineage must enforce a distinct firewall regarding Lydia's husband, Henry Chandler:
2 CONT
2 CONT === The "Widower" Inscription Error ===
2 CONT Some modern transcriptions or index summaries misinterpret the 1695 marriage record by inserting "widr." next to Henry's name. Primary archival audits confirm that Henry Chandler was *not* a widower in 1695; this was his first and
2 CONC  only marriage. The onomastic confusion stems from secondary compilers conflating him with his uncle or contemporary cousins of the same name within the Thomas and William Chandler lines of Essex County. Lydia Abbott was the sole 
2 CONC mother of all his children.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Immediate Family and Kinship Group ==
2 CONT
2 CONT === Parents ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Father: '''George Abbott, Jr.''' (1627–1689)
2 CONT * Mother: '''Sarah (Farnum) Ingalls''' (c. 1638–1728)
2 CONT
2 CONT === Spouse ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Henry Chandler''' (1667–1737)
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Vital Records of Andover, Massachusetts, to the End of the Year 1849'''. Vol. 1 (Births), p. 13: Records the birth of Lydia.
2 CONT * '''Vital Records of Andover, Massachusetts, to the End of the Year 1849'''. Vol. 2 (Marriages and Deaths), p. 25: Records the marriage of Lydia Abbott and Henry Chandler.
2 CONT * '''Allen, John Kermott'''. ''The Henry Chandler Family of Enfield, Connecticut'' (1905). Details the 1723 migration from Andover to Enfield and maps the complete household inventory.
2 CONT * '''Abbott, Lemuel Abijah'''. ''Descendants of George Abbott, of Rowley, Mass.'' (1906). Traces Lydia's structural position as a sibling in the George Jr. branch.
2 CONT * '''Gary, Boyd'''. ''Ancestry of Rutherford B. Hayes'' (Open-source presidential pedigree studies). Verifies the lineage down through Daniel Chandler and the Keep alliance to the Birchard-Hayes family.
2 CONT *Her descendants include President of U.S. Rutherford Birchard Hayes.
2 CONT *https://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Essex/Andover/aBirthsA.shtml "(ABBOT (Abbet, Abbett, Abbott, Abbut, Abbutt, Abett)) Lydia, d. George and Sarah, Mar. 31, 1675."
2 CONT *https://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Essex/Andover/aMarriagesA.shtml "(ABBOTT (Abbet, Abbett, Abbot)) Lydia, and Henry Chandler, widr., Nov. 28, 1695."
