1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Stone:  Here lyes Buried the Body of Mrs. Sarah Booth who died April __ AD 1784 in the 76 year of her age.
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT One Branch of the Booth Family..., page 140 details the vital info for him, his wife and their children. [https://books.google.com/books?id=r781AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA138&lpg=PA138&dq=simeon+booth+%26+rebecca+frost&source=bl&ots=LzIgjOLKhC
2 CONC &sig=ACfU3U2HV_gCnL5HAKL9lvEZzidBJoMdfw&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwi68YH6vb7hAhUkiOAKHbFBByoQ6AEwCHoECAkQAQ#v=onepage&q=simeon%20booth%20%26%20rebecca%20frost&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph4 Booth, b. April 10, 1710, in Enfield. d. Nov. 9, 1784, in Enfield, m. Sarah4 Chandler, Jany. 29, 1736, in Enfield. b. July 9, 1707, in Andover. d. April 16, 1777, in Enfield. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Booth received from his father, soon after his marriage, thirteen acres of land for his home lot, eighty-one acres in or near Freshwater Meadows, and fifty-six acres near Kibbe's "sprong." He was Constable in 1736.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT * I. Joseph, b. Oct. 17, 1736. 
2 CONT *II. Sarah, b. and d. May 14, 1738. 
2 CONT *III. Isaac, b. March 9, 1739. d. Jany. 13, 1798.     m. Deborah Hurlbnt (Obadiah, William), June 5, 1765.      b. Feb. 13, 1741. d. Jany. 3, 183o.    He went to Union, Ct., soon after his marriage. 
2 CONT *IV. Samuel, b. Aug. 28, 174o. d. Jany. 14, 1778. m. Elizabeth Phelps (Ezekiel3, Joseph4, Joseph3, Joseph9, William'), May 29, 1766. b. Sept. 17, 1744- d.   They lived in Simsbury. 
2 CONT *V. Zachariah, b. March 29, 1742. d. Jany. 18, 1819.  m. Susannah Chapin6, March 8, 1792. b. Aug. 21, 1764. d. They lived in Enfield. 
2 CONT *VI. Sarah, b. Dec. 1, 1743. d. July 27, 18oo, in E. Windsor. m. Samuel' Allen (Joseph*, Samuel3, John2, Samuel'). b. June 8, 1736, in E. Windsor. d. Oct. 1o, 1816, in B. Windsor. he m. first, Elizabeth Wells (Lamson3, Joshua2, Jo
2 CONC shua'). b. June 5, 174o. d. May n, 1778. he m. third, Lucy Alden (Rev. Noah), widow of Darius Markham, Dec. 6, 1801.. b. July 2, 1749, in Longmeadow. d. Feby. 3, 1837, in East Windsor. Samuel Allen lived in that part of East Winds
2 CONC or called Scantic.
2 CONT *VII. Henry, b. Nov. 17, 1745. d. March 1, 1792. m. Dorothy Fish (Jonathan), Nov. 2, 1768. b. March 2o, 1744. d. Oct. 17, 1834. she m. second, Elijah Burt (Davids David3, Nathaniel2, Henry1). Oct. 31, 1793. b. Oct. 3, 1742. d. Apr
2 CONC il 5, 1820. Henry Booth lived in Windsor.
2 CONT *VIII. David, b. July 22, 1747. d. Sept. 14, 1747. 
2 CONT * IX. Mehitable, b. March 6, 1749. d. Sept. 21, 1823. 
2 CONT --------------------
