1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Spencer-5938
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikitree contributers:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of David Pease — married 29 Jan 1783 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of James Lusk — married 1805
2 CONT
2 CONT Jerusha, the daughter of Janathan and Jerusha (Jones) Spencer was born April 3, 1764. David Pease, the youngest son of Dea. Cummings and Sarah (Hale) Pease, was born at Enfield, April 6, 1760; He married Jerusha Spencer, of Somers
2 CONC , CT., January 29, 1783,[1] and they settled first in East Windsor, but not long after removed to Simsbury, CT., and afterward to Enfield, his native town, where for a time he practiced medicine. His last residence was New Shoreha
2 CONC m, RI. He died, November, 1803, aged 44 years. He did military duty in the Revolution; was on Long Island at the time of our defeat there; he was then 16 years old; David was also in a battle at White Plain. Near the close of the 
2 CONC Revolutionary War he commenced his study of medicine with Dr. Asa Hamilton, of Somers, CT. David died in November of 1803 and his widow married 2nd James Lusk, of Enfield, on July 7, 1805. She died there, February 21, 1815, aged 5
2 CONC 1 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ "Connecticut, Vital Records, Prior to 1850," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QPSC-N4DW : 21 September 2019), Jerusha Spencer, ; citing Marriage, , Compiled by Lucius A. and Lucius B. Barbour, hous
2 CONC ed at State Library, Hartford, Connecticut; FHL microfilm 008143425. Pease, David & Austin S. A Genealogical and Historical Record of the Descendants of John Pease, Sen., Last of Enfield, Conn. (Samuel Bowles & Company, Springfiel
2 CONC d Mass., 1869). Page 51. Flora S Clark, Descendants of Obediah Spencer Son of Thomas Spencer of Hartford, Connecticut, Spencer Historical & Genealogical Society, Inc, Elkins Park, PA 1987 Find A Grave: Memorial #26650623
