1 NOTE James Eggleston and Margaret Harker (Margaret is probable).
2 CONT
2 CONT     The Eggleston family name appears in old records with a variety of spellings, icluding: Eggleston, Egleston, Eggelston, Egelston, Eggliston, Egliston, Eagleston, Egglestone, Eglestone, Eccleston, Eccelston, Ecclestone and prob
2 CONC ably a few dozen others. Despite the various spellings, most of us Egglestons are from the same rooster. Most North Americans are descended from James' son, Bygod Eggleston (also known as Bagot, Baggot, Bigod, or Bigot) Eggleston 
2 CONC who came from England with three sons on the ship "Mary & John" in 1630 to Dorchester, Massachusetts and eventually settled in what is now Windsor, Connecticut. We northern Egglestons are very fortunate in that, thanks to a couple
2 CONC  of scoundrels, Settrington Manor, Yorkshire, was the object of one of the most extensive surveys of an English manor ever to be ordered by the Queen and done and the Manor rolls and survey have been microfilmed. The original Will
2 CONC  in the Latin of James Eggleston, as well as the parish and the baptismal font at All Saint's Parish in Settrington, Yorkshire, England where my 7th Great Grandfather Bygod Eggleston was baptized, are still standing and in use tod
2 CONC ay.
2 CONT       James Eggleston, born Abt. 1560 in or near, Settrington, Yorshire, England; died 1613 in Settrington, Yorkshire, England. He married . Margaret Harker.
2 CONT
2 CONT        Margaret Harker, born Abt. 1562 in or near, Settrington, Yorshire, England; died Abt. 1600 in Settrington, Yorkshire, England. She was the daughter of  Miles Harker.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Eggleston and Margaret Harker are:
2 CONT     i. Begat Eggleston, born Bef. February 20, 1585/86 in Settrington, Yorkshire, England; died September 01, 1674 in Windsor, Connecticut; married (2) Sarah Talcott Abt. 1634 in Windsor, Connecticut.
2 CONT    ii.   Dorothy Eggleston.
2 CONT    iii.   Elizabeth Eggleston.
2 CONT    iv.   Jane Eggleston.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Eggleston and Juliana Freer are:
2 CONT    i.   James Eggleston, born Bef. June 19, 1603 in Settrington, England; died Aft. January 01, 1636/37.
2 CONT    ii.   John Eggleston, born Bef. April 06, 1606 in Settrington, England.
2 CONT    iii.   Margaret Eggleston.
2 CONT    iv.   Alice Eggleston.
1 NOTE     From Ancestral File (TM), data as of 5 JAN 1998.
