1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT === Birth ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Miller was born April 1, 1668 in Middletown, Colony of Connecticut.  He was the son of [[Miller-5222|Thomas Miller]] and [[Nettleton-21|Sarah Nettleton]]. [[#Bacon|Bacon]]: Page  61& 99
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel was married to [[Eggleston-281|Mary Eggleston]] July 26, 1702 in Middletown, Colony of Connecticut. Together, they had five children.[[#Bacon|Bacon]]: Page 61
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Miller died April 11, 1738 in Middletown, Colony of Connecticut. [[#Bacon|Bacon]]: Page 61
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT *Jacobus, Donald Lines. "The Nettletons in America", ''[[Space:The Connecticut Quarterly|The Connecticut Quarterly]]'' (Hartford, Conn., 1908) Vol. 11, Pt. 2, [https://archive.org/stream/connecticutmagazv11p2hart#page/492 Page 492
2 CONC ]
2 CONT *Bacon, Reginald. ''Early Families of Middletown, Connecticut'' (Variety Arts Press, 2012) Vol. 1: 1650 - 1654. pp.5, 61-63, 99.
2 CONT * [http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~ctsmfsd/MillerInDepth.pdf A Compilation of The Society of Middletown First Settlers Descendants]: accessed 12 Apr 2014.
