1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Abigail (Pettibone) Phelps Strong''' was born on April 22, 1706 and died on October 16, 1787 at age 80. She was first married to Lt. David Phelps. They are the parents of '''David, Elisha, and Noah Phelps'''. Sh
2 CONC e married second '''Deacon David Strong'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks to Jack Shackles for supplying the following information about Abigail...
2 CONT
2 CONT A memorial plaque to '''Abigail Pettibone Phelps Strong''' is located in the Hop Meadow Cemetery, Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut. It is dedicated by the Abigail Phelps Chapter, Daughters of the American Revolution, on thei
2 CONC r 110th anniversary. It is an honor worthy of posting here.
2 CONT
2 CONT The plaque notes that Abigail and Lt. David Phelps are the parents of '''David, Elisha, and Noah Phelps'''. Their sons were distinguished officers who served in the American Revolution. The sons are buried in Hop Meadow Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT The plaque also notes that Abigail is buried with her second husband, Deacon David Stong, in Bolton, Tolland County, Connecticut. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===Abigail Pettibone 
2 CONT *Born 22 Apr 1706 in Simsbury, Ct 
2 CONT *Died 16 Oct 1787 in Simsbury, Ct.
2 CONT *Daughter of John Pettibone Jr and Mary (Bissell) Pettibone
2 CONT *Sister of John Pettibone, Mary Pettibone, John Pettibone, Samuel Pettibone, Catherine Pettibone and Sarah (Pettibone) Phelps
2 CONT *Wife of David Phelps — married 25 Apr 1731 in Simsbury, Ct
2 CONT *Wife of David Strong — married 1 Jan 1772 (to 1787) in Simsbury, Ct
2 CONT *Mother of David Phelps, David Phelps, Abigail (Phelps) Case, Elisha Phelps, Noah Phelps, Rachel (Phelps) Humphrey, Ruth (Phelps) Case, Sarah (Phelps) Hayden, Susannah (Phelps) Nash and Lois (Phelps) Hayden
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Pettibone-129
