1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT 12 May 1726 Simsbury, Hartford, Connecticut, British Colonial America
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT ===Birth===Joseph Mills was born 23 Dec 1694 in Simsbury Township, Hartford County, Connecticut. His parents were John and Sarah Mills. <ref>"Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906," database, FamilySearch (https://familys
2 CONC earch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F745-HLW : accessed 8 July 2015), Joseph Mils, 23 Dec 1694; citing ; FHL microfilm unknown.</ref><ref>Brown, Abiel, [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhist00browiala Genealogical history, with short 
2 CONC sketches and family records, of the early settlers of West Simsbury, now Canton, Conn.], p. 92-93 within biography of John Mills, Press of Case, Tiffany, and Company, Hartford,1856; Reprinted, N. Y. 1899.</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===At the age of thirty years (1724) he married Hannah  Adams, aged fifteen years, who was born 1709. She died September 1776, aged 67. They had sons and four daughters, all of whom married and had children.<ref>Brown, 
2 CONC Abiel, [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhist00browiala Genealogical history, with short sketches and family records, of the early settlers of West Simsbury, now Canton, Conn.], p. 92-93 within biography of John Mills, Pres
2 CONC s of Case, Tiffany, and Company, Hartford,1856; Reprinted, N. Y. 1899.</ref> Nine sons and at least one son-in-law served in the American Revolution. All were active in their churches and six sons were deacons. Four sons were amon
2 CONC g the founders of Norfolk, Connecticut. {{Citation needed}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Residence===Joseph Mills lived in Meadow Plain, Old Parish, and moved to West Simsbury, in 1742 or 1743. <ref>Brown, Abiel, [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhist00browiala Genealogical history, with short sketches and f
2 CONC amily records, of the early settlers of West Simsbury, now Canton, Conn.], p. 92-93 within biography of John Mills, Press of Case, Tiffany, and Company, Hartford,1856; Reprinted, N. Y. 1899.</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===Joseph Mills died April 19th, 1783, aged 89 years. <ref>Brown, Abiel, [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhist00browiala Genealogical history, with short sketches and family records, of the early settlers of West S
2 CONC imsbury, now Canton, Conn.], p. 92-93 within biography of John Mills, Press of Case, Tiffany, and Company, Hartford,1856; Reprinted, N. Y. 1899.</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT <References/>
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:* Pettibone Registry, page 33, see [[Sharp-661 | K. Pontius]]. Phelps, ''The Phelps Family in America.'' 
