1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''SARAH MILLS''' (JOHN5, SIMON4, SIMON3, JOHN2, EDWARD1) was born November 05, 1696 in Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut and died November 11, 1797 in Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut.  She married thre
2 CONC e times:  
2 CONT * She married (1) '''SAMUEL TULLER''' January 06, 1713/14, son of JOHN TULLER and ELIZABETH CASE.  He was born 1689 in Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut, and died January 13, 1719/20 in Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut.
2 CONC  [n.b. one of these dates may not be correct.]
2 CONT * She married (2) '''FRANCIS GARRETT''' March 19, 1729/30 in Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut.  He was born 1674 in Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut, and died June 24, 1731 in Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut. 
2 CONT * She married (3) '''JOSEPH WOODFORD''' February 14, 1743/44. He was born 1677 in Farmington, Hartford County, Connecticut, and died February 27, 1760 in Avon, Hartford County, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah's second husband, '''Major John Garrett''', born in West Simsbury, Connecticut, Colony, in 1727, was the oldest son and third child of '''Francis Garrett''', and his wife, '''Sarah (Mills) Tuller''', born 1696, died 1797, in
2 CONC  her 101st year. Sarah was the daughter of John Mills, of West Simsbury, and the widow of Samuel Tuller, whom she married in 1715. She married 2d, Francis Garrett in 1722, and after his death in 1731 she married 3d, 1745, Captain 
2 CONC Joseph Woodford, who was born 1676 and died January 1760. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sarah was the daughter of John and Sarah Pettibone Mills.  She married:
2 CONT # '''Samuel Tuller''' Jan 6, 1714 in Simsbury, Hartford, Connecticut Colony. He passed on Jan. 13, 1720 at Simsbury.
2 CONT # '''Francis Garrett''' March 19, 1723 in Simsbury, Hartford, Connecticut Colony. He passed June 24, 1731 at Simsbury.
2 CONT # '''William Roberts''' March 12, 1735. He passed Jan. 4, 1761 at Simsbury.
2 CONT # '''Joseph Woodford II''' Feb. 14, 1744 Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut Colony. He passed on Feb. 2, 1760 at Avon.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sarah Mills Woodford BIRTH	5 Nov 1696 Hartford County, Connecticut, USA DEATH	8 Nov 1797 (aged 101) Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA BURIAL	Cremated, Other, Specifically: Burial place not known at this time.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/137560298/sarah-woodford
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Photo	 Joseph Tuller 1718–1798
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo	 Isaac Tuller 1720–1806
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo	 Susanna Garrett Woodford 1725–1805
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT According to my grandmother's notes she and her children (John, Francis Jr., Sarah and Susannah and another child expected) were mentioned in her husband's will (Francis Garrett). She was the widow of Samuel Tuller who died in 171
2 CONC 9 when she married Garrett.and later  married Joseph Woodford of Farmington, Conn on Feb 14, 11774-5
2 CONT She lived to be 101 years old
2 CONT My grandmother's references:
2 CONT Genealogical Sketches of Early Settlers of West Simsbury, Conn. by Abel Brown 1856 p. 91, 92
2 CONT Simsbury, Conn. Records p. 14, 20,26,27,95
2 CONT Genealogies of Ancient Windsor, Conn. (Stiles) p. 707
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT married 14 Feb 1744 in Simsbury, Hartford, Connecticut Colony
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Woodford-118
