1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John was born in 1701. He is the son of John Humphrey and Sarah Pettibone. He was a twin of his sister Hannah. He passed away in 1760. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Humphrey, Jr. was very active in Simsbury affairs. From 1735 until 1760 he was justice of the peace in Simsbury, serving concurrently as a representative to the General Assembly of the Colony during the years 1733-54 and agai
2 CONC n in 1757; and for a few years was town clerk of Simsbury, as his father had been before him. In 1758-60 he was Justice Judge of Hartford County Court [Humphreys, 123].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Read, daughter of Dr. Jacob Reade and Elizabeth Law, was born ca. 1703; aged 13 in 1716; m. in SImsbury, 15 June 1721, John Humphrey b. 17 March 1700, d. in 1760 in New Haven, son of John Humphrey.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Humphreys Family in America" (New York, 1883) page 23 wrong calls her the daughter of Josiah and Hannah (Amsdale) Read of Windsor."
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT from [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=118843532 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 12 2016, 1:52:36 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT John Humphrey, 3rd, Esqr., twin of Hannah and eldest s. of Dea. John Humphrey, Jr. and Sarah Pettibone, b. of record Mar. 17, 1700/1 at Simsbury, Conn. He d. Nov. 2, 1760 at New Haven, Conn.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the "The Humphreys Family in America" (1883), John was buried near the grave of John Dixwell, one of the regicide Judges who participated in the death warrant for King Charles, I of England and subsequently hid in Con
2 CONC n. under the alias of James Davids. Dixwell's stone and memorial are in the New Haven Center Church's cemetery just behind the Church enclosed by a fence. Franklin Bowditch Dexter's 1882 "Inscriptions on Tombstones in New Haven Er
2 CONC ected Prior to 1800" includes Dixwell's memorial, but not one for John Humphrey. It is assumed John Humphrey either never had a gravestone or by 1882 it was not discernable.
2 CONT
2 CONT His death entry in the Simsbury, Conn. records states:
2 CONT
2 CONT • John Humphrey, Esqr. Departed this Life the 2nd day of November, 1760, at New Haven, in the 61st year of his age. He has been Capt. of a military Company in this Town, an assistant Judge in the County Court, and a Representative
2 CONC  to ye Gen'l. Assembly.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
