1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Thankful Shepard
2 CONT * Birth:	June 30 1683 - Concord, MA
2 CONT * Death:	Nov 2 1724 - Simsbury, Hartford, CT
2 CONT * Parents:	Abraham Shepard, Judith Sill 
2 CONT * Husband:	1) Daniel Adams 2) Joseph Pettibone
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=REG&db=stuw&id=I01364
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks Shepard (Abraham Shepard2, Ralph Shepard1) was born 30 JUN 1683 in Concord MA, and died 2 NOV 1724 in Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 
2 CONT #Daniel Adams BET 1702 AND 1703, son of Daniel Adams and Mary Phelps. He was born ABT 1678 in Windsor CT?, and died 10 JAN 1712/13 in Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT. 
2 CONT #Joseph Pettibone BEF 1715, son of John Pettibone and Sarah Eggleston. He was born 11 MAR 1688/89 in Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT, and died 14 SEP 1762 in Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT.  He survived her and married 2nd, on 11 MAY 1726 
2 CONC in Simsbury CT, to Hannah Large.
2 CONT  	  Children of Thanks Shepard and Daniel Adams are:
2 CONT *  i.	Daniel Adams was born ABT 1705 in Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT?, and died 21 MAY 1779 in Simsbury CT.
2 CONT *   ii.	Thanks Adams was born ABT 1703 in Simsbury, Hartford Co, CT. She married William Wilcoxson ,Jr. 2 MAY 1723 in Simsbury CT. He was born 22 APR 1702 in Simsbury, Hartford Co, Connecticut, and died 27 DEC 1772.
2 CONT *    iii.	Abraham Adams was born 16 AUG 1707. He married Elizabeth Humphrey 29 DEC 1731 in Simsbury CT.
2 CONT *  iv.	Hannah Adams was born 22 OCT 1709. She married Joseph Mills.
2 CONT *   v.	James Adams was born JUN 1712, and died 22 MAY 1787 in Tinmouth VT. He married Sarah Callender 8 DEC 1736 in Sheffield
2 CONT
2 CONT 	 Children of Thankful (Shepard) Adams and Joseph Pettibone are:
2 CONT *  i.	Joseph Pettibone was born 26 FEB 1713/14.
2 CONT *   ii.	Mary Pettibone was born 28 JUL 1718.
2 CONT *  iii.	Bathsheba Pettibone was born 25 APR 1721
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT >The will of Joseph Pettibone was abstracted in The Connecticut Nutmegger, vol. 39 (2006), p. 278. He names daughter Bathsheba Grimes and granddaughters Mary, Basheba, and Thanks Canada. This tells us that Mary was likely older th
2 CONC an Bathsheba and Thanks, that Robert Kanada and his daughter Eleanor were apparently dead by 11 Aug. 1762, when the will was written, and that Bathsheba had remarried by that date.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=115181870
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=stuw&id=I01364 cites 
2 CONT *Title: Adams Family Ancestors and Descendants of Parmentio Adams (1747-1809) Author: Gerald J. Parsons Repository:  Note: I have a copy Media: Manuscript
2 CONT *Title: The Shepard Families Of New England, volume I, Ralph Shepard Of Dedham Author: compiled by Gerald Faulkner Shepard, edited by Donald Lines Jacobus Publication: The New Haven Colony Historical Society New Haven, Connecticut
2 CONC  1971 Repository:  Note: I have pages copied for me by Gerald Parsons 1/02 Media: Book Page: 14
2 CONT *https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=46396787&id=I19885
2 CONT *story of Ancient Windsor Vol II Title: Genealogies and Biographies of Ancient WindsorPage: pg 562
2 CONT
