3 STAE Connecticut
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 6 AUG 1789
2 ADDR
3 CITY Simsbury
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bathsheba Pettibone was born 25 APR 1721 in Simsbury, Hartford, Connecticut. She was the daughter of Joseph Pettibone and Thanks Shepard. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 
2 CONT #Robert Kanady 15 OCT 1739. 
2 CONT #Benjamin Grimes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT #Mary Kennedy 
2 CONT #Bathsheba Kanady 
2 CONT #Thankful Kanady 
2 CONT #Eleanor Kanady
2 CONT #Benjamin Grimes
2 CONT # Mary Grimes 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Joseph Pettibone (1762) was abstracted in The Connecticut Nutmegger, vol. 39 (2006), p. 278. He names daughter Bathsheba Grimes and granddaughters Mary, Basheba, and Thanks Canada. This tells us that Mary was likely ol
2 CONC der than Bathsheba and Thanks, that Robert Kanada and his daughter Eleanor were apparently dead by 11 Aug. 1762, when the will was written, and that Bathsheba had remarried by that date.
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Grimes, appears to be the man of this name who served among the Connecticut troops at the Siege of Havana in 1762. Between combat and disease, his company lost more than 50% dead. Benjamin Grimes, the soldier, was dischar
2 CONC ged 8 December 1762. Benjamin, husband of Bathsheba was dead months later, 5 April 1763, when Bathsheba Grimes and Abel Pettibone were named administrators of his estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bathsheba, "wife of Benjamin Grimes," joined the Simsbury church before 1777 [Barbour Index 3:224] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *Chicago: Brown, Pettibone & Kelly, 1885.  pg 16 Notes 3, 19.  Bathsheba Pettibone.  Robert Kennedy and Benjamin Grimes. https://www.familysearch.org/library/books/records/item/346311-redirection
2 CONT *https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=dcmillett&id=I10635
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Pettibone-142 cites 
2 CONT * Simsbury, Connecticut, births, marriages and deaths. By Simsbury, Conn.  page 117 [https://books.google.com/books?id=7esnAQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA117&dq=bathsheba%20kanady&pg=PA117#v=onepage&q=bathsheba%20kanady&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * Families of Early Hartford, Connecticut. By Lucius Barnes Barbour.  Page 397 [https://books.google.com/books?id=WJ_XiLoXvLkC&lpg=PA397&dq=bathsheba%20grimes&pg=PA397#v=onepage&q=bathsheba%20grimes&f=true GoogleBooks]
