1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Stephen, was the son of Aaron and Olive (Osborn) Powers of Greenwich, MA.  Stephen married Elizabeth Hinds on 7 Jun 1787 in Greenwich.  Stephen and Elizabeth resided in Greenwich and had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Powers (1788-1856) Stephen Powers Jr. (1790-1860) Francis Powers (1792-1862) Rhoda Hinds Powers (1798-1866) Jason Powers (1805-1883) Rufus Powers (1811-1882)
2 CONT
2 CONT Although he was a farmer, Stephen enlisted for 3 years in the Continental Army during the Revolution. He served in Col Patterson's Brigade in Capt Dix's Co. which was a component of the 3rd Massachusetts Regiment.  In 1818 Stephen
2 CONC  applied for and received, a Revolutionary War pension in the amount of $8 per month.
