1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Joseph Kilbourne 
2 CONT * Gender:	Male 
2 CONT * Birth:	circa 1674  Wethersfield, Hartford County, Connecticut Colony
2 CONT * Death:	August 19, 1744 (66-74)  Litchfield, New Haven County, Connecticut Colony
2 CONT * Son of Sgt. John Kilbourne and Sarah (Bronson) Kilbourne 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1) Dorothy Butler abt 1674 - 1709 m. 4 Jun 1696
2 CONT
2 CONT Their Children 
2 CONT *Dorothy Kilbourne 1697 -
2 CONT *Joseph Kilbourne, Captain1700 - 1756
2 CONT *Jonathan Kilbourne 1703/4 - abt 1777
2 CONT * James Kilbourne 1707 - 1762
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 2)   Esther Gibbs m. 29 Jun 1710
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children 
2 CONT *Benjamin Kilborn 1711 - 1711/2
2 CONT *Esther Kilborn 1713 -
2 CONT *Elizabeth Kilbourn 1716 -
2 CONT *Mary Kilborn 1719/20 -
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations 
2 CONT *↑ Kilbourne, Payne Kenyon. The History and Antiquities of the Name and Family of Kilbourn. (New Haven: Durrie & Peck, 1856), page 61. 'JOSEPH, was born in Wethersfield about the year 1672, and was married to Dorathy, daughter of 
2 CONC Deac. Samuel Butler, June 4, 1696, by Capt. John Chester, Commissioner.'
2 CONT *↑ Kilbourne, Payne Kenyon. The History and Antiquities of the Name and Family of Kilbourn. (New Haven: Durrie & Peck, 1856), page 64. His will 'was proved before the Court in 1744, which renders it probable that Joseph Kilborn di
2 CONC ed in that year.'
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Links
2 CONT * https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Joseph_Kilbourne_%282%29
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT 63. Joseph KILBOURNE (John8, Thomas7, John6, John KYLBORNE5, John4, William3, Richard2, Richard1)87. Born circa 1672 in Wethersfield, Hartford Co., Connecticut. Joseph died in 1744.87 29 Vol. 2, p. 681, Vol. 3, p. 994 30 pp. 27-9,
2 CONC  34
2 CONT * His Will, probated in 1737, Glastonbury, Connecticut 25 Vol. 13, p. 91, Vol. 18 p. 226
2 CONT * moved to Litchfield, Connecticut 1721
2 CONT
2 CONT “Joseph was born in about 1672 in Wethersfield, Connecticut. On June 4, 1696 he married for his first wife Dorothy, daughter of Deacon Samuel Butler. She died August 19, 1709, leaving four children. Joseph Kilbourn was one of the 
2 CONC first settlers of Litchfield, Connecticut, of which town he was admitted an inhabitant on December 12, 1721. The next year he was chosen a selectman. He also served as lister, moderator of town meetings and sealer of weights and m
2 CONC easures. He owned considerable land and apparently was prosperous. His home lot was the site afterward known as the "county house corner," and here afterward were born Mrs. Harriet Beecher Stowe, Rev. Henry Ward Beecher, and other
2 CONC  members of Dr. Beecher's family. Joseph Kilbourn's will was proved before the court in 1744 ---” - Douglas Chaffey On 4 June 1696 Joseph first married Dorothy BUTLER87, daughter of Deacon Samuel BUTLER (1639-31 December 1692) & E
2 CONC lizabeth OLMSTEAD (20 November 1642-12 October 1681), in Wethersfield, Hartford, Connecticut.87 by John Chester. Dorothy died on 19 August 1709.87 29 Vol. 2, p. 681, Vol. 3, p. 994 30 pp. 27-9, 34 25 Vol. 13, p. 91, Vol. 18 p. 226
2 CONC  They had the following children: 209i. Dorothy KILBOURNE (17 April 1697-) 210ii. Capt. Joseph KILBOURNE (9 July 1700-1756) 211iii. Jonathan KILBOURNE (17 March 1703-? ) 212iv. James KILBOURNE (13 April 1707-9 March 1762) On 29 Ju
2 CONC ne 1710 Joseph second married Esther GIBBS87, daughter of Jacob GIBBS. 29 Vol. 2, p. 681, Vol. 3, p. 994 30 pp. 27-9, 34
