2 CONT ====Peter Blinn's Will
2 CONT * '''Manwaring, Charles William, ed. 1904.''' ''A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records.'' 1723 to 1729. Hartford, Connecticut, USA: R.S. Peck & Company. Available at: [https://archive.org/details/adigestearlycon01manwgo
2 CONC og/page/468/mode/1up?q= '''Archive.org''']:—
2 CONT ** Name: Peter Blinn
2 CONT ** Location: Wethersfield
2 CONT ** Date of Will: 2 Mar 1724-1725
2 CONT *** '''Invt. £79-00-01.''' Taken 18 March, 1724-5, by David Goodrich, William Warner and Richard Montague. 
2 CONT *** I, Peter Blinn of Wethersfield, having arrived at the age of 84 years, do make this my last will and testament: 
2 CONT *** Item. I give to my beloved wife 1-3 part of all my moveable estate, except my wearing apparrell, my silver-headed cane and joyner tooles. 
2 CONT *** Item. I give to my beloved son Peter all my wearing apparrell and all my joyners tooles, besides £18 he hath already received of me, as may appear in the 71st page of my Book of Accompt. 
2 CONT *** Item. I give to my son James Blin 5 shillings. I give to my son William Blinn 1 shilling. I give to my daughter Mary Hurlbut 5 shillings.''' I give to Daniel Blinn, my grandson, son to my son Daniel Blinn''', 5 shillings. I gi
2 CONC ve to my son Jonathan Blinn 1 shilling. I give to my son Deliverance Blinn 1 shilling. Item. I give to my daughter Margaret Belding, after all my just debts are paid and the severall legacies before mentioned, 2-3 of my moveable e
2 CONC state, except my silver-headed cane, which I give to my grandson George Blinn, son of Deliverance Blinn. And I make my son Deliverance Blinn sole executor. Witness: David Goodrich, David Williams, Christopher Graham. Peter Blinn, 
2 CONC ls. 
2 CONT *** Court Record, Page 82--4 May, 1725: Will now exhibited and proven. 
2 CONT *** Page 88-89--6 July, 1725: Mary Blynn, widow, her 1-3 part set out by Joshua Robbins, John Russell and Richard Montague (per order of Court).
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Wikitree
2 CONT * Wikitree [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Blinn-3#_note-7 Peter Blinn (abt. 1641 - 1724)] states the following extra information about Peter's son Daniel and grandson Daniel drawn from 'The New England Historical & Genealogical Re
2 CONC gister, 1847-2011'', Vol. 143:—
2 CONT ** "Daniel was a mariner. He died intestate; admin given to his widow 5 Dec 1720. One child Daneil, b 9 Oct 1709; mentioned as grandson in Peter1 Blinn's will at Westhersfield in 1724/5; probably the Daniel Blin whose will dated 2
2 CONC 3 Sep 1742, Bath..., Beaufort County, North Carolina; named wife Mourning Blin." 
2 CONT * '''Wikitree''' gives no reason for providing Mary as an alternate name of Daniel's wife. No source supports it.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Find a Grave®: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/231045036/daniel-harris-blinn Daniel Harris Blinn]:—
2 CONT * ''' NOTE:''' The Find a Grave volunteer curator is misguided.
2 CONT ** '''Where Daniel died is unknown as of 31 Jan 2024.''' He is '''''Not''''' included along with other family members in the book, [https://archive.org/details/wethersfieldinsc00till/page/n45/mode/2up ''Wethersfield Inscriptions''
2 CONC ]. 
2 CONT ** '''A wide search for any Daniel Blinn or Blyn''' in Massachusetts and Connecticut failed to yield death information. – 31 Jan 2024.
2 CONT ** '''Daniel was not given a middle name.''' '''''No Source''''' supports it. Middle names were rarely if ever given to any British Colonial Americans.
