1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====NOTES
2 CONT * '''Her first husband should be this https://www.geni.com/people/William-Clark/6000000092757171834?through=6000000009689124107 .''' Another https://www.geni.com/people/William-Clark/6000000027277203120?through=6000000010467962837
2 CONC  is an incomplete duplicate. Whether to detach the latter or merge it with the first is something I'm not familiar with doing. – (Ken Shelley, 1 Feb 2024)
2 CONT *  '''Apart from the marriage record provided by Torrey, no other prized source shows her second married surname as "Belden." The Belding family''' was and remains a prominent one Hartford County. There was/is also Belden family i
2 CONC n CT with an entirely different lineage. '''So be aware;''' some chroniclers conflated Beldinsg and Beldens;
2 CONT * '''As of 1 Feb 2024, there is No primary source for death.''' The previous entry was 31 Mar 1774 in Wethersfield. No legitimate secondary sourcing proves it. There are books showing the date now entered, but the quoted-matter do
2 CONC es not state where Margaret died or was buried. 
2 CONT ** '''Margaret may have died in Wethersfield's south-bordering of Rocky Hill.''' There's a death record in "Connecticut, U.S., Church Record Abstracts, 1630-1920" (''See'' [https://www.ancestry.com/discoveryui-content/view/215076:
2 CONC 3032?tid=174604283&pid=132555794282&hid=1037193142124 Ancestry.com]) showing her husband's death there. '''However''', Rocky Hill is probably the town where the family attended church. Daniel's Will was drafted in Wethersfield. Da
2 CONC niel refers to himsellf as "of Wethersfield." A copy Daniel's his handwritten Will is posted in Sources.
2 CONT * '''Margaret does Not appear''' as "Margaret Belding" in Tillotson's [https://archive.org/details/wethersfieldinsc00till/page/20/mode/1up?view=theater ''Wethersfield inscriptions''],... or Blinn. 
2 CONT ** '''Neither is there buried in Wethersfield a Margaret''' [https://archive.org/details/wethersfieldinsc00till/page/n91/mode/1up?view=theater&q=Clark Clark] '''''nor''''' [https://archive.org/details/wethersfieldinsc00till/page/3
2 CONC 9/mode/1up?view=theater&q=Belden Belden].
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Marriage to William Clark
2 CONT * '''Torrey, Clarence Almon. (1985) 2004.''' ''New England Marriages Prior to 1700''. Edited by Elizabeth P. Bentley and Gary Boyd Roberts. Baltimore, Maryland, USA: Genealogical Publishing Company. Available at: [https://www.goog
2 CONC le.com/books/edition/_/mOgK8dM9qqUC?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=%22Clark,%20William%20(1673/4-1708)%20%26%20Margaret%22 '''Google Books''']:—
2 CONT ** “CLARK, William (1673/4–1708) & Margaret [BLINN[ (1684-), m/2 Daniel Belden[sic]; b. 1701?; Wethersfield, CT”
2 CONT *** '''Note:''' Since the couple '''''only had one''''' child in early 1706/7, Torrey's estimate of1701 for marriage is probably incorrect.
2 CONT *** '''As of 1 Feb 2024,''' [https://www.familysearch.org/search/record/results?count=20&q.anyDate.from=1701&q.anyDate.to=1706&q.anyPlace=Wethersfield%2C%20Hartford%2C%20Connecticut%20Colony%2C%20British%20Colonial%20America&q.fat
2 CONC herGivenName=WIlliam&q.fatherSurname=Clark&q.motherGivenName=Margaret&q.surname=Clark&c.birthLikePlace1=on&f.birthLikePlace0=10&c.birthLikePlace2=on&f.birthLikePlace1=10%2CConnecticut&f.birthLikePlace2=10%2CConnecticut%2CHartford 
2 CONC '''FamilySearch'''] shows the couple with only one child: '''Abigail''', born 4 Feb 1706 in Wethersfield. She died on 27 July 1752 in Glastonbury, Hartford, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America – wife of Richard Smith. (He
2 CONC r tombstone inscription says she died having lived "46 years 187 days".)
2 CONT
