2 CONT * '''PETER BLINN: LAST WILL AND TESTAMENT'''
2 CONT ** '''Manwaring, Charles William, ed. 1904.''' ''A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records.'' 1723 to 1729. Hartford, Connecticut, USA: R.S. Peck & Company. Available at: [https://archive.org/details/adigestearlycon01manwg
2 CONC oog/page/468/mode/1up?q= '''Archive.org''']:—
2 CONT *** Name: Peter Blinn
2 CONT *** Location: Wethersfield
2 CONT *** Date of Will: 2 Mar 1724-1725
2 CONT **** '''Invt.''' £79-00-01. Taken 18 March, 1724-5, by David Goodrich, William Warner and Richard Montague. 
2 CONT **** I, Peter Blinn of Wethersfield, having arrived at the age of 84 years, do make this my last will and testament: 
2 CONT **** Item. I give to my beloved wife 1-3 part of all my moveable estate, except my wearing apparrell, my silver-headed cane and joyner tooles. 
2 CONT **** Item. I give to my beloved son Peter all my wearing apparrell and all my joyners tooles, besides £18 he hath already received of me, as may appear in the 71st page of my Book of Accompt. 
2 CONT **** Item. I give to my son James Blin 5 shillings. I give to my son William Blinn 1 shilling. I give to my daughter Mary Hurlbut 5 shillings. I give to Daniel Blinn, my grandson, son to my son Daniel Blinn, 5 shillings. I give to
2 CONC  my son Jonathan Blinn 1 shilling. '''I give to my son Deliverance Blinn 1 shilling'''. Item. I give to my daughter Margaret Belding, after all my just debts are paid and the severall legacies before mentioned, 2-3 of my moveable 
2 CONC estate, except my silver-headed cane, which I give to my grandson George Blinn, '''son of Deliverance Blinn. And I make my son Deliverance Blinn sole executor'''. Witness: David Goodrich, David Williams, Christopher Graham. Peter 
2 CONC Blinn, ls. 
2 CONT **** Court Record, Page 82--4 May, 1725: Will now exhibited and proven. 
2 CONT **** Page 88-89--6 July, 1725: Mary Blynn, widow, her 1-3 part set out by Joshua Robbins, John Russell and Richard Montague (per order of Court).
2 CONT * '''DELIVERANCE: PROBATE::''' ''A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records''. Vol. 3. 1732 to 1737. Available at: [https://archive.org/details/digestofearlycon03manw/page/142/mode/1up?q=Deliverance&view=theater '''Archive.
2 CONC org''']:—
2 CONT ** Name: Deliverance Blynn
2 CONT ** Location: Wethersfield
2 CONT ** Date of Probate: 11 Dec 1736
2 CONT ** Invt. in Vol. XIII, Page 19-20 
2 CONT ** '''Invt.''' £1256-02-03. Taken 11 December, 1736, by Nathaniel Stilman, Hezekiah May and John Stilman. 
2 CONT ** '''Court Record, Page 53'''--4 January 1736-7: Adms. granted to Benjamin Stilman of Wethersfield. Recog., £800, with John Stilman. 
2 CONT ** '''Page 47 (Vol. XIII)''' April, 1739: George Blynn, a minor, 14 years of age, son of Deliverance Blynn, chose his uncle Nathaniel Stilman to be his guardian. Recog., £200.
