1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Elizur-Wright/6000000020457320460
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizur, son of Nathaniel (died 1727?), moved ca. 1740 when is father's estate was settled, to South Canaan, Ct in the far northwest of the state/colony and died there in 1787. His grave is in the Falls Village cemetery in S.Canaan
2 CONC  along with his second wife, Hannah (Dix?) Boardman and some of her children by an earlier marriage. Their son, Elizur II (1762-1845),(Yale 1781) moved to the "western reserve" (of CT) in Tallmadge, Ohio in 1810. Elizur III (1804-
2 CONC 85) (Yale 1824), the aboliltionist and life insurance reformer, returned East and lived his last years in Medford, Mass.
2 CONT --------------------
