1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ens. Samuel Wright and Mary Butler had the following children of record at Wethersfield:
2 CONT
2 CONT • iii. Hannah Wright, b. circa 1663-1664, d. Feb. 25, 1746/7 at Wethersfield, Æ 83 (g.s.); m. 1) June 8, 1683 at Wethersfield, Daniel Boardman, s. of Samuel Boardman and Mary Betts, b. Aug. 4, 1658 at Wethersfield. He d. testate a
2 CONC t Wethersfield Feb. 20, 1724/5, Æ 67. Twelve children of the family, ten who lived to maturity. Hannah m. 2) after May 1727 as his 2nd wife, James Treat, Jr., s. of Lieut. James Treat & Rebecca Latimer, b. Apr. 1, 1666 at Wethersf
2 CONC ield. He d. testate Feb. 18, 1742/3, Æ 76 (g.s.). There were no children by this second marriage. By his 1st wife Prudence Chester, James Treat had seven children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT • ii. Mary Wright, b. circa 1662 and living at the time of her father's Jan. 1689/90 will. Stile's (Ancient Wethersfield) erroneously claims the two husbands (Daniel Boardman and James Treat) of sister Hannah were Mary's husbands.
2 CONC  In context in the order in which Mary is named in her father's will: "I give to my son Samuel a small parcel of Money made up in a Bag marked S. W.; to my daughter Mary another parcel of Money marked M. F.; to my daughter Hannah 
2 CONC another parcel of Money marked H. B. [i.e., Hannah Boardman]." At his death, the Feb. 27, 1689/90 inventory of Mary's father includes "The children: 3 of them married; David Wright, almost 13 years of age." Mary was married by Jan
2 CONC uary 1689/90, but what was her married surname beginning with the letter "F," if in fact Manwaring transcribed it correctly?
2 CONT
