1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Daniel Boardman''' was born in Wethersfield, Connecticut, the son of Hannah (Wright) and Daniel Boardman of that town. He graduated Yale University in 1709. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On Nov 1, 1812 he married Jerusha Sherman in New Milford, daughter of (Mercy Wheeler?) and Deacon David Sherman of Stratford, CT. Daniel and Jerusha had several children, including one son, Sherman Boardman. In 1713 Mr. Daniel Boa
2 CONC rdman was given land and a house in New Milford on the condition that he become New Milford's "minister of the place" for 20 years. In 1716, the First Church of Christ (Congregational) was organized by eight men and five women wit
2 CONC h Reverend Daniel Boardman as pastor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Reverend Boardman died Aug 25, 1744 in New Milford. (See: Town of New Milford, CT http://www.newmilford.org/content/59/168.aspx 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also: History of the towns of New Milford and Bridgewater, Connecticut, 1803-1882. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Boardman genealogy, 1525-1895 : the English home and ancestry of Samuel Boreman, Wethersfield, Conn''., Thomas Boreman, Ipswich, Mass. by Goldthwaite, Charlotte (Publication date 1895).  Page 226.  < [https://archive.org/details
2 CONC /boardmangenealog00gold/page/226/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org] >
2 CONT
2 CONT 34. Rev. Daniel Bordman was twice married ; first, Feb. 26, 1716-17, to Hannah Wheeler of Milford, who bore him one daughter and died June 20, 1719. The record by his own hand in his Family Bible reads :
2 CONT
2 CONT * “My daughter Hannah was born, Jan. 12th day, about sunsetting Anno Christi 1717-8 (this was on the Lord’s day) and was baptized the Sabbath following, at New Milford.
2 CONT *My well-beloved, tender companion, and yoke-fellow departed this life, June 20, New Milford, Anno Christi 1719, on a Sabbath morning, at the break of day.”
2 CONT
2 CONT He married second, Nov. i, 1720, Mrs. Jerusha Seelye, born June. 1693, of Stratfield, now Bridgeport, the widow of Mr. Ebenezer Seelye, and one of the nine daughters of Dea. David Sherman of Stratford. His record in his family Bib
2 CONC le goes on as follows :
2 CONT
2 CONT * “ My daughter Penelope was born, Dec. 26, 1721, upon Tuesday, at the sunrising, at New Milford ; baptized the Lord’s day following.
2 CONT * “ My daughter Tamar was born March 26tb, 1723, on a Monday at or about midnight, baptized the next Sabbath following at New Milford.
2 CONT * “ My daughter Mercy was born, Feb. 9th day, at or about 8 o’clock at night, in the year 1725 ; baptized the next Sabbath following at New Milford.
2 CONT * “ My son Sherman was born, Aug. 2 day, at the break of the day Anno 1728, upon Friday ; baptized nth of August.
2 CONT * “ My daughter Jerusha was born May 4th, about 10 of the clock at night 1731 ; baptized the Sabbath following, the 9th day.
2 CONT * “ Ebenezer Seely e was born, Nov. 5, 1717, at Stratfield.”
2 CONT
2 CONT The last named was Mrs. Bordman’s only child by her first husband. He was brought up and educated by Mr. Bordman, and afterward settled in the adjoining town of Kent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Bordman* died of consumption, Aug. 25, 1744, aged 57. “ Mrs. Bordman, or Madam Bordman, as she was respectfully styled, was, on the death of her husband, left with a family of three unmarried daughters, and a son about sixteen
2 CONC  years of age ; but being a woman of uncommon firmness and mental energy, she, by the aid of her youthful son, so managed as to maintain herself and family in a manner respectable for those days, from the productions of the farm l
2 CONC eft by her hus- band, now her only support. She continued to occupy the house built for him when first settled (situated on the brow of the hill at the north end of the town street, with the homestead about it) for fourteen or fif
2 CONC teen years, and until her son, who had been previously married, had built a house on the principal farm about two and a half miles from the center of the vil- lage, to which, her daughters having all been previously married, she r
2 CONC emoved with him, and there resided in his fam- ily during the remainder of her life.” f She died Aug. 30, 1777, in the 85th year of her age.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Rev. Daniel through life spelt his name Bordman.
2 CONT *f Hon. David Sherman Boardman in “ Life of Mrs. Mary Anna Boardman.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Boardman genealogy, 1525-1895 : the English home and ancestry of Samuel Boreman, Wethersfield, Conn''., Thomas Boreman, Ipswich, Mass. by Goldthwaite, Charlotte (Publication date 1895).  Page 228. < [https://archive.org/details/
2 CONC boardmangenealog00gold/page/227/mode/1up?q=Sperry&view=theater Archive.Org] >
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000186609489847&size=large}}
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Manwaring, Charles W. A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records. (Hartford, Conn.: R. S. Peck & Co., 1904-06) 2:469. Will of "Daniel Boardman Wethersfield", dated 13 Feb 1724/5 mentions "Hannah, my beloved wife", "my son
2 CONC  Richard Boardman", "my son ''Daniel Boardman''", "my son Israel Boardman", "my son Timothy Boardman", "my son Joshua Boardman", "my son Benjamin Boardman", "my son Charles Boardman", "my daughter Mabel Nickolss", "my daughter Han
2 CONC nah Abbey", and "my daughter Martha Churchill".
2 CONT * Goldthwaite, Charlotte. Boardman Genealogy, 1525-1895: The English Home and Ancestry of Samuel Boreman, Wethersfield, Conn.; Thomas Boreman, Ipswich, Mass. : With Some Account of Their Descendants (Now Called Boardman) in Americ
2 CONC a. (Hartford, Conn.: William F. J. Boardman, 1895) page 224. 'Rev. Daniel Bordman ([son of] Daniel...), of New Milford, Conn., was born in Wethersfield July 12, 1687.'
2 CONT * Reference: [http://person.ancestry.com/tree/42722996/person/28671449511 Ancestry Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 9 2017, 18:20:35 UTC''
2 CONT * ''Boardman genealogy, 1525-1895 : the English home and ancestry of Samuel Boreman, Wethersfield, Conn''., Thomas Boreman, Ipswich, Mass. by Goldthwaite, Charlotte (Publication date 1895).  Page 224-228.  < [https://archive.org/d
2 CONC etails/boardmangenealog00gold/page/223/mode/1up?q=Sperry&view=theater Archive.Org] >
2 CONT * https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Daniel_Boardman_%289%29 
2 CONT * Connecticut, United States. The Barbour Collection of Connecticut Town Vital Records Wethersfield Vital Records:32 (typescript). 'BOARDMAN,BORDMAN,BORMAN,BOREMAN,... Daniell,s.Daniell & Hannah,b.July 12,1687'
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT =Rev Daniel Boardman=  
2 CONT * BIRTH 1686 Wethersfield, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 25 Sep 1744 (aged 57–58) New Milford, Litchfield County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Center Cemetery, New Milford, Litchfield County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 11571152
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Boardman was born in Wethersfield, Connecticut, the son of Hannah (Wright) and Daniel Boardman of that town. He graduated Yale University in 1709. He married Hannah Wheeler in 1716. She died in 1719. On Nov 1, 1720 he marri
2 CONC ed Jerusha Sherman in New Milford, daughter of Mercy Wheeler and Deacon David Sherman of Stratford, CT. Daniel and Jerusha had 4 daughters and one son. In 1713 Daniel Boardman was given land and a house in New Milford on the condi
2 CONC tion that he become New Milford's "minister of the place" for 20 years. In 1716, the First Church of Christ (Congregational) was organized by eight men and five women with Rev. Daniel Boardman as pastor and he died Aug 25, 1744 in
2 CONC  New Milford.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inscription'''
2 CONT Here lyes buried ye body of ye Rev. Mr. Daniel Boardman. Who departed this Life September 25th Anno Dom. 1744 Aged 58 Years.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gravesite Detail'''s
2 CONT In cover photo, marker of Jerusha (left) and Daniel Boardman (right). A third marker to right of his is marked "HB 1719" thought to be his first wife, Hannah (Wheeler) Boardman.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Daniel Boreman 1658–1724
2 CONT Hannah Wright Boardman-Treat 1663–1746
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouses'''
2 CONT unknown Boardman unknown–1719 (m. 1716)
2 CONT Jerusha Sherman Boardman 1693–1777 (m. 1720)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Lieut Richard Boardman 1684–1755
2 CONT Hannah Boardman Abbe 1693–1780
2 CONT Martha Boardman Churchill 1695–1780
2 CONT Israel Boardman 1697–1725
2 CONT Timothy Boardman 1700–1753
2 CONT Joshua Boardman 1702–1761
2 CONT Benjamin Boardman 1705–1788
2 CONT Charles Boardman 1707–1724
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Penelope Boardman Carrington 1721–1799
2 CONT Tamar Boardman Taylor 1723–1795
2 CONT Mercy Boardman Speary 1725–1795
2 CONT Sherman Boardman 1728–1814
2 CONT Jerusha Boardman Farrand 1731–1806
2 CONT
