1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 'Benjamin Bordman ([son of] Daniel...), of Sharon, Conn., was born in Wethersfield, March 10, 1705-6. ... The wife of Benjamin, whose family name is not given in Sharon records, was Deborah Goodrich [footnote: Debo
2 CONC rah was born, probably in Wethersfield, June 8, 1707, and was the oldest child of William Goodrich, ...] , as appears from a note in the family Bible of her great grandson, ... They were probably married about 1735, and she died i
2 CONC n Sharon, Sept. 17, 1755.'
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # Goldthwaite, Charlotte. Boardman Genealogy, 1525-1895: The English Home and Ancestry of Samuel Boreman, Wethersfield, Conn.; Thomas Boreman, Ipswich, Mass. : With Some Account of Their Descendants (Now Called Boardman) in Americ
2 CONC a. (Hartford, Conn.: William F. J. Boardman, 1895), pages 241-43.
2 CONT # IGI File: Benjamin Baordman is son of Daniel Boardman & Hannah Wright; He married (1) Deborah Goodrich who D: 17 sep 1755 at Sharon, Litchfield, Conn; He married (2) Mercy Gillett;
2 CONT # A Digest of the Early Conn. probate Records: 1729-1750: Nathaniel Gillett of Salisbury, son of Jacob Gillett chose his mother Mercy Boardman, wife of Benjamin Boardman guardian on 20 October 1765;
