2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lillie-54
2 CONT Hannah (Lillie) Daggett (1700 - 1783)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Daggett formerly Lillie aka Burnap
2 CONT Born 5 May 1700 in Reading, Middlesex, Massachusetts Baymap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Daughter of Samuel Lillie Sr. and Hannah (Boutwell) Lillie
2 CONT Sister of Samuel Bragg Lillie, John Lilley, Sarah (Lillie) Parker, Jonathan (Lilli) Lillie, Jonathan Lillie, Mary (Lilli) Gibbs, David Lilley and Elizabeth Lilli
2 CONT Wife of Ebenezer Burnap Sr — married 24 Dec 1719 (to 1723) in Wakefield, Reading, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay Colonymap
2 CONT Wife of Ebenezer Daggett — married 25 Nov 1731 in Reading, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay Colonymap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Mother of Hannah (Burnap) Sibley, Ebenezer Burnap Jr, Samuel Daggett, Hannah Daggett and Rebecca (Daggett) Rich
2 CONT Died 27 Aug 1783 at age 83 in Sutton, Worcester, Massachusetts, United Statesmap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONS
2 CONT Profile last modified 29 Jun 2022 | Created 25 May 2011
2 CONT This page has been accessed 604 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah was born in 1700 to Samuel and Hannah Lillie.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 24 December, 1719, Hannah married Ebenezer Burnap.[2] Together, they had two children: Hannah (b. 1721)[3] and Ebenezer (b. 1723).[4] Ebenezer Burnap passed away in 1723.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 25 November, 1731, Hannah married Ebenezer Daggett.[5] They had three children together: Samuel (b. 1732),[6] Hannah (b. 1736),[7] and Rebecca (b. 1739).[8] Ebenezer Daggett passed away in 1762.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah passed away in 1783.[9]
2 CONT
