1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''BAKER, Joseph 
2 CONT *Family:
2 CONT *'''Marriage: 7 JUL 1702
2 CONT *'''Spouse: POMEROY, Hannah 
2 CONT *'''b. 4 JUL 1682 Northampton, Hampshire, Mass.
2 CONT *'''Parents:
2 CONT *Father: POMEROY, Caleb 
2 CONT *Mother: BAKER, Hepzibah 
2 CONT *'''Children:
2 CONT **BAKER, Joseph 
2 CONT **BAKER, Samuel  b. 28 JUN 1705 Windsor, Hartford, CT.
2 CONT *From: http://www.genealogyofnewengland.com/f_485.htm#74 ___________________
2 CONT *'''Joseph Baker, Jr
2 CONT *Birth: 	Apr. 13, 1678  Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT *Death: 	Jan. 29, 1754  Tolland County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT *Son of Joseph & Hannah (Cook) Baker. '''Married (1) Hannah Pomeroy at Windsor, CT on July 8, 1702'''; married (2) Abigail Bissell.
2 CONT *Family links: 
2 CONT * Spouse:
2 CONT *  Abigail Bissell Baker (1681 - 1767)*
2 CONT * Children:
2 CONT **  Jacob Baker (1711 - 1742)*
2 CONT **  Daniel Baker (1717 - 1742)*
2 CONT **  Heman Baker (1719 - 1805)*
2 CONT **  Titus Baker (1722 - 1729)*
2 CONT *Inscription:
2 CONT *"In Memory of '''Mr. Joseph Baker''' who died Janurey 29th 1754 in ye 77th Year of his Age"
2 CONT * Burial:  South Yard Cemetery, Tolland, Tolland County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT *Find A Grave Memorial# 25341658
2 CONT *From: http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=25341658 __________________
2 CONT *'''New England families, genealogical and memorial: a record of the ..., Volume 2 edited by William Richard Cutter
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=1M8UAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA881&lpg=PA881#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.881
2 CONT *   ( XIX ) Caleb Pomeroy, son of Eltweed Pomeroy, the American immigrant, was baptized at Windsor, Connecticut, March 6, 1641. he married, March 8, 1665, Hepsibah Baker, who was born May 10, 1646, daughter of Jeffrey and Joan (Ro
2 CONC ckwell) Baker, of Windsor. He was one of the original settlers of Northampton, Massachusetts. He was admitted a freeman in 1663. he was a selectman of the town for several years. When the contribution for Harvard College was take 
2 CONC in the colonies, he contributed three pounds of flax. He was a soldier in King Philip's war and took part in the fight at Turner's Falls, May 19, 1676. he sold is farm in 1686 and moved to Southampton or Easthampton. he owned much
2 CONC  land and was a man of large influence. Pomeroy Mountain, Pomeroy Ford and Pomeroy Meadows took their names from him. Children, born at Northampton: Hepsibah, born July 27, 1666, died young; Samuel, mentioned below; Hepsibah, Janu
2 CONC ary 19, 1673; Ebenezer, March 14, 1774; Caleb, May 3, 1777; Eldad, December 6, 1679; '''Hannah, July 4, 1682'''; Mercy, September 20, 1684; Sarah, at Southampton, August 6, 1687.
2 CONT *   ( XX ) Samuel Pomeroy, son of Caleb Pomeroy, was born at Northampton, Massachusetts, May 29, 1669. He married (first 1690, Elizabeth French, of Rehoboth, Massachusetts, daughter of Joseph and Mary (Kingsley) French. He married
2 CONC  (second) December 7, 1703, Johanna Root, who was born .... etc. _____________________________
