2 CONC  AIS from microfilmed schedules of the U.S. Federal Decennial Census, territorial/state censuses, and/or census substitutes.  Records of Marriages and Births in the Town of Windsor, Connecticut, The New England Historical and Gene
2 CONC alogical Register: NEHGR Vol 5 (1851), page 63  S109: Stiles, Henry Reed The History and Genealogies of Ancient Windsor, Connecticut (Hartford, CT., Case, Lockwood & Brainard, 1891) vol II  Pettibone Registry, page 9, see K. Ponti
2 CONC us.  Connecticut Marriages, 1640-1939," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QLMW-DVXB : 17 March 2018), Samuel Bissell, Death 1697, Hartford, Hartford, Connecticut, United States; Connecticu
2 CONC t State Library, Hartford; FHL microfilm 1,316,427. 
