1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Removed birth data December 29, 1627 Southwold, Suffolk, England - no references.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''New England, The Great Migration and The Great Migration Begins, 1620-1635'' [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/2496/images/42521_b158319-00602?pId=59550 Ancestry.com]'''
2 CONT “i. HANNAH, b. say 1628; m. Windsor 30 November 1648 John Drake [WiLR 1:55; Grant 32 (day and year lost from record)].”
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Wikitree: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Moore-1414 Hannah (Moore) Drake (abt. 1627–1686)]'''
2 CONT '''Born''' about 1627 in England
2 CONT '''Wife of''' John Drake Jr. — married 30 Nov 1648 in Windsor, Hartford Co., Connecticut
2 CONT '''Died''' 16 Feb 1686 at about age 59 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of John Drake and Hannah Moore'''
2 CONT John b. 14 Sep 1649 
2 CONT Deacon Job b. 15 Jun 1651, d. 19 Apr 1733 
2 CONT Hannah b. 8 Aug 1653, d. 4 Aug 1694 
2 CONT Enoch b. 8 Dec 1655, d. 21 Aug 1698 
2 CONT Ruth (our line) b. 1 Dec 1657, d. 13 Nov 1731 
2 CONT Simon b. 28 Oct 1659, d. 21 Dec 1711 
2 CONT Lydia b. 26 Jan 1662, d. 7 May 1702 
2 CONT Elizabeth b. 22 Jul 1664 
2 CONT Mary b. 29 Jan 1666, d. 2 Dec 1728 
2 CONT Mindwell 10 Nov 1671, d. 1 Mar 1736 
2 CONT Capt. Joseph b. 26 Jun 1674, d. 14 Jan 1754 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Citations'''
2 CONT [S52] Henry R. Stiles History of Ancient Windsor II, Vol. II:Pg. 178/Family 3. 
2 CONT [S578] Frank B. Gay, John Drake, page 5. 
2 CONT [S578] Frank B. Gay, John Drake, Page 6. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is referred to as the "daughter of Deacon Moore".
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Hannah was the daughter of John Moore. She was born in England and came to Dorchester, Massachusetts with her father, two sisters and grandfather about 1630. This would indicate that her mother had died in England sometime prior t
2 CONC o 1630. The family came to Windsor, Connecticut, with the first settlers. There is a partial record in Windsor of her father's marriage to an Abigail in 1639, but daughters Hannah and Elizabeth are too old to have been born from t
2 CONC his marriage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah married John Drake in Windsor on November 30, 1648. John was the son of John & Lettice Shakespear Drake, born in Warwickshire, England. John & Hannah had 11 children. In January of 1670, Hannah, along with the wives of Nath
2 CONC aniel Loomis and Lieutenant Filer, had crossed the Connecticut River on a neighborly errand. On their way back across the river, their canoe was hit by an ice floe, and all three were cast into the freezing river. All three were m
2 CONC iraculously rescued by Nathaniel Bissell and an Indian, who were in another canoe on the river. The story of the rescue was written by Increase Mather, and titled "Remarkable Providences". Both John and Hannah died in Windsor, Han
2 CONC nah on February 16, 1686, John late in 1689. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Information for this biography from "The Descendants of John Drake of Windsor, Connecticut" by Frank Gay; Early Connecticut Probate Records; the Early Records of Windsor, Connecticut; "The Great Migration Begins" by Robert Anderso
2 CONC n and "History & genealogies of Ancient Windsor" by Stiles. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT Ancestry.com  Web: Netherlands, GenealogieOnline Trees Index, 1000-2015  Name: Ancestry.com Operations, Inc.; Location: Provo, UT, USA; Date: 2014;  @R10@
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT Edmund West, comp.  Family Data Collection - Deaths  Name: Ancestry.com Operations Inc; Location: Provo, UT, USA; Date: 2001;  @R1@
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
