2 CONT ===Daniel White (1698 - 1786)===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Daniel White
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 5 Sep 1698 in Hatfield, Hampshire, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Daniel White and Sarah (Bissell) White
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Sarah (White) Griswold, Thomas White, Joel White Esq. [half], Elisha White [half], Simeon White [half], Seth White [half], Lucy (White) Wolcott [half], Elizabeth White [half] and Oliver White [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Dickinson) White — married 7 Oct 1719 (to 8 Jul 1721) in Hadley, Hampshire, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Elizabeth White — married 19 Jan 1726 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Salmon White, Daniel White, Mary (White) Paine, Salmon White, Elihu White, Elizabeth (White) Murray and Hannah White
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 15 Dec 1786 in Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT White-4838 created 22 Jun 2011 | Last modified 20 May 2018
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel White was born in Hatfield, Massachusetts, on September 5, 1698, the son of Captain Daniel White and his first wife, Sarah Bissell. [1] [2] [3] [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT As a child, he had accompanied his father's family to Windsor, Connecticut, but he returned to Hatfield before 1719, where he became a farmer. On October 7, 1719, he married Mary Dickinson of Hatfield. The ceremony was officiated 
2 CONC by Colonel Partridge. They had one child, Salmon, on June 23, 1721, but the child died while still an infant. Two weeks later, on July 8, 1721, the child's mother also died, at the age of 22. [3] [5] [6] [7] [8] [9]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married second, Elizabeth White, his second cousin, and the daughter of Deacon John White, on January 19, 1726. The couple had six children: [3] [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel, born December 28, 1726; married Submit Morton.[10]
2 CONT Mary, born August 30, 1729; married Dr. Elijah Paine.[11]
2 CONT Salmon, baptized October 31, 1731; married Mary Wait.
2 CONT Elihu, baptized April 21, 1734; married Zeruiah Cole.
2 CONT Elizabeth, baptized September 5, 1726; married first, Gen. Seth Murray, second, Isaac Maltby.
2 CONT Hannah, baptized October 26, 1740. Probably died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1731, he and his family moved to Bolton, Connecticut, and remained there until 1742. In the spring of that year, they returned to Hatfield after purchasing the home of Elizabeth's father there. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Over the years, Daniel was quite active in the community affairs of both Hatfield and Bolton. He sat on important local committees and held jobs such as constable, town clerk, assessor and selectman. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Daniel White died in Hatfield on December 15, 1786, at the age of 88. He was buried in the Old Hadley Cemetery in Hadley, Massachusetts. [3] [4]
2 CONT
