2 CONT ----
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel White was born in Hatfield, Massachusetts on July 4, 1671 to Lieutenant Daniel and Sarah (Crow) White. [1] [2] [3] [4] [5] [6] [7] [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT He originally resided in Hatfield, but moved to Windsor, Connecticut in 1704 or 1705 where he pursued the business of trade. He was Windsor's School Commissioner from 1712 to 1713. [2] [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT In May, 1716, he became the fourth captain of the First Connecticut Troop, the oldest Company in the United States. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married three times, and had eleven children. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married first, Sarah Bissell. She was the mother of: Sarah (died as an infant), Sarah, Daniel and Thomas. [2] [9]
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, Sarah, passed away in 1703 at the age of 31.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married second, Ann Bissell on July 6, 1704. She was the mother of: Joel, Elisha and Simeon. [2] [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, Ann, passed away in 1709 at the age of 33. They had been married for less than 5 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married third, Elizabeth Bliss on April 25, 1710. She was the mother of: Seth, Lucy, Elizabeth, Pierce and Oliver. [2] [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Daniel White passed away in Windsor on June 22, 1726 at the age of 54. [2] [5] [10]
2 CONT -------
