1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rev. Thomas White, Pastor of First Church of Christ in Bolton. Died Feb. 22, 1763. Age 61.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Capt. Daniel White and Sarah Bissell.
2 CONT
2 CONT He graduated from Yale College in 1720. He then taught in the grammar school at Northampton and probably at the same time pursued his theological studies with the Rev Solomon Stoddard. The next year, he supplied the pulpit of the 
2 CONC First Church in Worcester, MA. In 1725, he accepted a call to the newly formed church in Bolton, and was ordained there October 26, 1725, and continued his work until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 17 June 1725, Martha Hunt of Northampton MA, daughter of Jonathan Hunt and Martha Williams.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: - The New England Historical and Genealogical Register, Volume 52; Volume 1898 - Vital Records of Bolton to 1854 and Vernon to 1852 - Memorials of Elder John White By Allyn Stanley Kellogg (1860)
