1 NOTE {geni:about_me} IV) Isaac, son of Samuel Catlin, was born in Hartford, Connecticut, November 11, 1712,
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1) (Elizabeth) Kilbourn; 2)Abigail (Ives) (second) a widow. 3) Desire Bradley, widow Tuttle 
2 CONT
2 CONT CATLIN, ISAAC, of Samuel; 
2 CONT
2 CONT m. Elizabeth Kilborn. Their children:
2 CONT #Elizabeth, b. ;m. Amos Barnes.
2 CONT #Elisha.
2 CONT #Isaac, b. Aug. 20, 1739.
2 CONT #Charles.
2 CONT #Irene.
2 CONT #Polly.
2 CONT #Ruth.
2 CONT #Sarah.
2 CONT
2 CONT m. Abigail  Ives ( a widow). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #  Bradley, b. Oct. 12, 1758. 
2 CONT #  Caroline, b. April 1, 1760. 
2 CONT #  Hannah, b. Oct. 14, 1762. 
2 CONT #  Samuel, b. Dec. 6, 1764. 
2 CONT #  Abigail, b. July 19, 1767. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Desire Bradley, widow of Eliphalet Tuttle.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is not clear whether the children born 1758 - 1767 were from 2nd or 3rd wife 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Catlin, son of Samuel & Elizabeth (Norton) Catlin, was born 11 Nov 1712 in Hartford, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served in the French & Indian Wars under Capt. Archibald McNeale in CT
2 CONT
2 CONT He married as his first wife Elizabeth Kilborn/Kilbourne, daughter of Joseph & Esther (Gibbs) Kilborn/Kilbourne, about 1738 at Hartford, CT - parents of Isaac II & Ruth
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Elizabeth he married Desire Bradley, daughter of William & Elizabeth (Chedsey) Bradley about 1757 in CT - their children were Bradley, Caroline, Hannah, Samuel & Abigail
2 CONT
