2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Deacon John Loomis, b. Co. Essex, England, 1622 D. Sep 1, 1688, 66 years of age Married Feb 3 1648-9 to Elizabeth Scott Elizabeth Scott B.1625 D. May 7 1696 Daughter of Thomas and Ann Scott who sailed from Ipswich England April 16
2 CONC 34 to Ipswich, Mass. and had with them Daughter Elizabeth age 9. They removed to Hartford Conn. John was admitted to the Windsor Church Oct. 11 1640 On May 3rd 1643 he had granted him from the Plantation 40 Acres of land. he resid
2 CONC ed in Farmington from 1652 to 1660  when he returned to Windsor, CT.  and was Deacon of the Church. He was deputy to the General Ct. In 1666 and 7 Also from 1675 to 1687. There is a monument which is preserved in the Windsor buryi
2 CONC ng ground. His will is preserved in the probate office at Hartford, and his name is signed John Loomys. All his children were born in Windsor Ct. except. 3rd, 4th, 5th, and 6th they were born in Farmington.
