2 FORM png
2 TITL Person Details for John Loomys, "Connecticut, Births and Christenings, 1649-1906" — FamilySearch.org
1 NOTE From Ancestral File (TM), data as of 5 JAN 1998.
1 NOTE From “A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England, Vol. 3,” by James Savage, p. 111: JOSEPH, son of John the first, Hannah, and Ann, born 10 Jan. 1678; Joseph, 13 Feb. 1681; Joseph, 28 Nov. 1682; Grace, 17 Mar. 
2 CONC 1685; Lydia, 15 Apr. 1686, who died at 16 years.; and Sarah, 8 Jan. 1693.
1 NOTE Resided Hatfield, Mass., then removed to Windsor abt 1683. His will, dated 1729, left his estate to his four children Esther, Sarah, Damaris, and John, but did not mention Abel.
2 CONT
2 CONT From "A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England., James Savage, Vol. III, p. 114:  LOOMIS, JOHN, Hatfield, s. prob. of Joseph the second, by w. Mary had John, b. 19 Oct. 1670, d. soon; John, again, 1676; and M
2 CONC ary, 1677; liv. at H. until 1683 or later, and rem. to Windsor. There Stiles gives him sec. w. 30 Aug. 1705,Esther , d. of the first Cornelius Gillett, I presume, and ch. John, 12 Feb. 1707; Esther, 13 Sep. 1708; Sarah, 26 Sep 171
2 CONC 0, Damaris, 1 Dec 1712; John, 21 Sept. 1713; and Abel, 3 Aug. 1716.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records (Online database: NewEnglandAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2006), (A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records, by Charles W. Manwaring, R. S. Peck
2 CONC  & Co. Printers, Hartford, CT, 1904.), Volume 3, Page 79:
2 CONT
2 CONT                         Page 241-2.
2 CONT         Loomis, John, Windsor. Invt. £342-06-06. Taken 1st December, 1732, by Joseph Newbery and Joshua Loomis. Will dated 18 June, 1729.
2 CONT         I, John Loomis, of the Town of Windsor, do make this my last will and testament: I give to Esther, my wife, the improvement of 1-2 of my land within fence, and also my woodland, as she think fitt, during the term she shall
2 CONC  continue my widow. If she shall marry, then she shall have the 1-3 of sd. lands with the use of 1-2 of my dwelling house during life. I give to my sd. wife Esther the 1-4 part of my household stuff and goods. I give to my son Joh
2 CONC n a double portion of my estate with my three daughters, and to be disposed of as in manner followeth, viz., that he the sd. John shall have all my lands after my decease, he paying the legacies to each of my daughters, to Esther,
2 CONC  to Sarah and to Damaras, if any there be to pay, so much as to make each of them to have half so much as his double portion. And he shall have three years time to pay out to them the sd. Esther, Sarah and Damarus their portion. A
2 CONC nd also that they shall have each of them their equal part in moveables belonging to my estate. I make and ordain my son John sole executor to this my last will.
2 CONT Witness: Simon Wolcott,                        JOHN LOOMIS, LS.
2 CONT Isaac Loomis, Nathaniel Loomis.
2 CONT
2 CONT         Codicil, dated 20 June, 1729: That he only gave to his three daughters to each of them a single share in his estate, in his moveable estate and his lands on which his house standeth, that is, the meadow and upland to the T
2 CONC hree Miles. And I do give unto my son John all my lands in Windsor, laid out or in time to come may be laid out as a property to me or to my estate, and also all the right or property in any other town or place whatsoever.
2 CONT Witness: Thomas Skiner,                        JOHN LOOMIS, LS.
2 CONT Nathaniel Loomis, Isaac Loomis.
2 CONT
2 CONT         Court Record, Page 78-28 November, 1732: Will and invt. exhibited, accepted and ordered to be kept on file.
1 NOTE Batch #: 7329613, Sheet #: 60, Source Call #: 822321 Merged General Note: Batch #: 8101450, Sheet #: 32, Source Call #: 1260820 Batch #: 7329613, Sheet #: 60, Source Call #: 822321
1 NOTE Batch #: 7329613, Sheet #: 63, Source Call #: 822321
1 NOTE Resided in Lebanon, Conn., for some time.
2 CONT
2 CONT From "A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England, Vol. 3,"  by James Savage, p.112:  JOHN, Windsor, eldest s. of the first John, had Mary, b. 20 Mar. 1672; Elizabeth 31 Dec. 1677; Deborah, 1680; Zechariah, Nov.
2 CONC  1681; Ezekiel, Oct. 1683; Ephraim, Nov. 1685, d. young; Rebecca, Dec. 1687; and Ruth, 28 Jan. 1690; beside John, 28 Mar. 1692. He was deac. and m. 1696, Sarah, wid. of Isaac Warner.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: "The Descendants of Joseph Loomis in America," by Elias Loomis,
2 CONT 1909, p. 129: 21. DEAC. JOHN LOOMIS, b. Windsor Conn., Nov. 9, 1649; m. 1st, (???); m. 2nd, Dec 30, 1696, Sarah (Boltwood) Warner. d. July 14, 1726, widow of Isaac Warner. He was deac. of the church and d. Aug. 31, 1715. 9 ch'n.: 
2 CONC 111. REBECCA, b. Dec. 1687; m. Dec. 10, 1713, Josiah, b. Mch. 10, 1678, son of Samuel and Mary (Norton) Rockwell, (See Tuttle Gen., p. 678). Lebanon, Conn. Ch'n: 1. Rebecca, 2. Ruth, 3. Josiah, 4. Ezra, 5. Waitstill, 6. Eunice."
2 CONT Nathanale Porter
