2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Benjamin Bissell''' was the son of John III Bissell & Sarah: Benjamin was born 22 Mar 1701 Windsor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Wattles was the daughter of William and Abigail Belcher Wattles. Mary married Benjamin BISSELL on 17 Jul 1728 in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Jerusha BISSELL was born in 1730 in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut
2 CONT *Joseph BISSELL on 2 Jul 1731 in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut. He died after 1824 in , Mahoning, Ohio.
2 CONT *Sarah BISSELL was born on 13 Oct 1734. Married Capt. Walter Hyde who was a Revolutionary War Patriot. Sarah Bissell and Capt Walter Hyde are buried in the same cemetery. Sarah died prematurely, so Capt Walter Hyde married Mary Wa
2 CONC ddles.
2 CONT *Betsy BISSELL was born on 1 May 1738 in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut. She died on 7 Aug 1830. 
2 CONT *Benjamin BISSELL was born on 23 Nov 1740 in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut. He died on 1 Nov 1760. 
2 CONT *Tertias BISSELL was born on 7 May 1748 in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT Proved 29 Aug 1758. Names wife Ann, son Joseph (executor), son Benjamin, and daughters Sarah, Bettey and Zerviah.[4]
2 CONT
