2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-313771301-1-502630/daniel-white-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-0c3a84058406f8ee88c171e63ba4e331&mrid=39f0eb772a6cd13e0482f1621c827ee4 MyHeritage Famil
2 CONC y Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 30 2016, 1:03:28 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Daniel White was born about 1638 in Cambridge, Massachusetts or Hartford, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Sarah Crow on 1 Nov 1661 in Hadley, Massachusetts. Sarah was 14 years and 8 months old at the time of her marriage. Their Children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah WHITE Born 15 Oct 1662 Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts, USA Died Aft 1723 Spouse 1 Thomas LOOMIS Married 31 Mar 1680 Hartford, Hartford County,Connecticut Spouse 2	John BISSELL Married 12 Nov 1689 Mary WHITE Born 1664 Hat
2 CONC field, Hampshire, Massachusetts, USA Died 05 Sep 1664 Mary Crow White Born 05 Aug 1665 Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts, USA Spouse 3	Noah WELLS Married Abt 1685 Spouse 1	Francis BERNARD Married Abt 1682 Spouse 2	John WHITE Marr
2 CONC ied Abt 1684 Elizabeth WHITE Born Between 13 Nov 1667 and 1668 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, Died 25 Feb 1736 Colchester, New London, Connecticut, USA Spouse Samuel LOOMIS Married 02 Jul 1688 Hatfield, Massachusetts Esther WHITE
2 CONC  Born 1675 Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts, USA Died Between Feb 1674 and 1675 Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts, USA Daniel WHITE, Jr.Born 04 Jul 1671 Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts, USA Died 22 Jun 1726 Windsor, Hartford
2 CONC , Connecticut, USA Spouse Sarah BISSELL spouse 2	Anna BISSELL Esther WHITE Born 1671 Died 07 Sep 1766 Spouse John ELLSWORTH Married 07 Dec 1696 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, USA Hannah WHITE Born 04 Jul 1674 Hatfield, Hampshire,
2 CONC  Massachusetts, USA Died in infancy John WHITE Born 16 Nov 1676 Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts, USA Died Aug 1677 Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts, USA Hannah WHITE Born Sep 1679 Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts, USA Spous
2 CONC e Nathaniel DICKINSON Mehitable WHITE Born Between 14 Mar 1682 and 1683 Hatfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts, USA Spouse Jeremiah BISSELL Married 18 Dec 1705 Daniel White's first land grant in Hatfield, Massachusetts is dated Jan 21
2 CONC  1660.[1] He became a farmer, and he was chosen constable in 1666.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lt. Daniel took the oath of allegiance 8 Feb 1668/1669 and made Freeman in 1690 . He was selectman in 1670. He occasionally held other offices and was often appointed on committees for attending to various town affairs which calle
2 CONC d for the exercise of discretion and sound judgment. He was also active in the Church. He was first mentioned as "Lieutenant" Daniel White on the records in 1692.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT "He died on 27 Jul 1713 in Hatfield, Massachusetts. By his will, dated 11 July 1713, he gave £ 4 to the church in Hatfield, and made his only surviving son, Daniel his executor. Prior to his death he had given a part of his land t
2 CONC o son Daniel, and to his daughter, Hannah, but he left a large estate for those times. The inventory amounted to £636, not including the homestead and some other property, which was appraised in 1719 after the death of his widow, 
2 CONC at nearly £ 300." [1] “Mrs. Sarah White died at Hatfield, June 26, 1719 aged 72. Her inventory shows the following list of articles in her wardrobe. She was not only well supplied, but seems to have been a little extravagant, for 
2 CONC that day, for one residing in a small town. 8 shifts; damask gown; silk girdle; linen gloves, muff, head linen, leather gloves, blue stockings, silk gloves, lustring hood, 8 handkerchiefs, fan, plain cloth coat, white waistcoat, d
2 CONC amask coat, painted serge coat, blue damask gown, streaked under coat, silk pranella gown, serge hood and bluefacing, 5 aprons…evaluated at $54.67”[1]
2 CONT Lt Damiel White was born about 1638 in Hartford CT. Married Sarah Crow 1 Nov 1661 in Hartford. Child: Elizabeth (White) Loomis.
