1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography of Mehitable (White) Bissell ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mehitable White''' was born on March 14, 1683, in Hatfield, Hampshire County, Massachusetts Bay. She passed away in 1772 in Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut. She was the daughter of '''Lieutenant Daniel White''' and '''Sar
2 CONC ah (Crow) White'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Spouse: Jeremiah Bissell ===
2 CONT Mehitable married '''Jeremiah Bissell''' on December 18, 1705, in either Hatfield, Massachusetts, or Windsor, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah was born on June 22 or 23, 1677, in Windsor, Connecticut. He was the son of '''John Bissell Jr.''' and '''Israel (Izrell) Mason'''. Jeremiah died in December 1755 in the Connecticut Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Children of Mehitable and Jeremiah ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Rachel Bissell'''
2 CONT * '''Mabel (Bissell) Willes'''
2 CONT * '''John Bissell''' (born circa 1706–1710)
2 CONT * '''Sarah (Bissell) Crane''' (married name)
2 CONT * '''Reverend Hezakiah Bissell'''
2 CONT * '''Jerijah Bissell'''
2 CONT * '''Samuel Bissell'''
2 CONT * '''PVT Israel Bissell, Sr.''' (born 1718, died 1776; married Hannah Sacket on November 27, 1744)
2 CONT * '''Jeremiah Bissell'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Mehitable White
2 CONT United States, Marriages from Newspapers on OldNews.com
2 CONT Text:	...married, second (name not Jeremiah Bissell, a son by the given). second wife, married Mehitable White, Dec. 18 or 19, 1705. Their daughter, Mabel Rissell, born Jan. 16, 1708, married Lamson...
2 CONT Marriage:	Circa 1705
2 CONT Husband:	Jeremiah Bissell
2 CONT Newspaper:	The Boston Transcript
2 CONT Publication:	Feb 24 1930 - Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts, United States
2 CONT Article summary:	A genealogical note on the marriage of Jeremiah Bissell and Mehitable White, and their daughter Mabel Rissell's marriage to Lamson Wells.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
