2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *  Kaye, Ruth Lincoln.  NEHGR (1969).  Vol. 123, page 114 - 117 . ''Dorothy, Unidentified Wife Of Edward Kellogg. ''  < [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB202/rd/11620/114/235587665 AmericanAncestors] >; ([https://www.geni.com/d
2 CONC ocuments/view?doc_id=6000000198565256856 document attached])
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Clark
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah’s first husband Ebenezer Hunt was born 6 Feb 1676 in Northampton, Hampshire, Mass. His parents were Jonathan Hunt (1637 – 1691) and Clemence Hosmer. Ebenezer died 23 Feb 1743 in Lebanon, New London, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah’s second husband Thomas Bissell was also her first cousin.  He was born  03 Dec 1683 in Windsor, Hartford, CT.  His parents were Thomas Bissell and Hester Strong.  His maternal grandparents were Elder John STRONG and Abigai
2 CONC l FORD. He first married 16 Feb 1710 to Martha Loomis.    Thomas died 11 Jun 1771 in East Windsor, Hartford, CT,
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hannah and Ebenezer
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Hannah Hunt b. 4 Oct 1699 Northampton, Hampshire, Mass.; d. 1769 New London, CT; m. 24 Jun 1731 Lebanon, New London, CT to Saxton Bailey (b. 1708 in Lebanon – d. 1743 in Lebanon)  His parents were Isaac Bailey (1681 – 1711) and
2 CONC  Mercy Saxton (1686 – 1759) Hannah and Saxton had at least one child:  Saxton (b, 1743)
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Stephen Hunt b. 24 Jul 1701 Lebanon New London, CT; d. 7 Apr 1784 Columbia, Tolland, CT; m. 18 Jun 1730 in Lebanon to Esther Janes (b. 1695 in Northampton, Hampshire, Mass. – d. 17 Feb 1779 in Lebanon) Her parents were Abel Ja
2 CONC nes (1644 – 1718) and Mary Judd (1658 – 1735). Stephen and Esther had nine children born between 1731 and 1749.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1758/59 – Stephen served in the French and Indian War.
