1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Haynes Graves resided at East Haddam up to 1768 when he moved to Shelburne, Massachusetts, and lived there until about 1783. He then moved to Salisbury, Connecticut. He was one of the town officers in Shelburne in 
2 CONC 1771. He bought 93 acres of land in Salisbury from Lemuel Wheeler for ,464 on  December 12, 1783. He held and conveyed various pieces of land in Salisbury, the last conveyance being dated February 14, 1816.
