2 CONT Robert Davis (abt. 1620 - bef. 1693)
2 CONT Born about 1620 [uncertain] in England  [uncertain]
2 CONT Died before 29 Jun 1693 before about age 73 in Barnstable, Barnstable, Province of Massachusetts Bay 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Davis aka Davies
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of [father unknown] and [mother unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Ann (Unknown) Davis — married about 1645 in Barnstable, Plymouth Colony  map icon
2 CONT Father of Deborah (Davis) Geer, Mary Davis, Andrew Davis, John Davis, Robert Davis II, Josiah Davis, Hannah (Davis) Dexter, Sarah (Davis) Young, Mercy (Davis) Mayo and Joseph Davis
2 CONT
2 CONT The Birth Date is a rough estimate. See the text for details.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Davis is currently protected by the Puritan Great Migration Project for reasons described in the narrative.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Caution: Not Identical to the Robert Davis, of Sudbury
2 CONT
2 CONT Another Robert Davis, of Sudbury, was born in 1609, immigrated in 1638 as a servant to Peter Noyes. He was with a Margaret Davis, who was possibly his sister and married to a wife, Bridget, and had daughters: Rebecca and Sarah.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Unknown Origin
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Davis was born about 1620, possibly in England. His birth date, place and parents are unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT The birth date shown here is an estimate, based on the birth date of his eldest child.
2 CONT
2 CONT The profiles for Ichabod Davis and Suzy Unknown have been disconnected as parents (no evidence and no source). Please do not replace these or any parents without appropriate evidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigration
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert emigrated by 1643, when he was among those "liable to bear arms,"[2] and settled in Barnstable, Massachusetts.[3] His ship and exact date of immigration are not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married by about 1645 (first child b Jan 1645[/6?]) to Ann Unknown. Because she did not mention all the children in her will, Otis assumes that Ann was a second wife.[1] If so, we have no information about an unknown first 
2 CONC wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT One source found shows the list of children born to each of his wives, both named Ann _______. However, it cites no sources, itself.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Davis' Children's Births:[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Deborah Davis, b Jan 1645[/6?]; m Thomas Gere of Enfield
2 CONT Mary Davis, b May 1648
2 CONT Andrew Davis, b May 1650
2 CONT John Davis, b 1 Mar 1652
2 CONT Robert Davis, b Aug 1654
2 CONT Josiah Davis, b Sep 1656; m 25 Jun 1679 Anne Taylor[2]
2 CONT Hannah Davis, b Sep 1658; m Unknown Dexter
2 CONT Sarah Davis, b Oct 1660; m Unknown Young
2 CONT Joseph Davis*
2 CONT Mercy/Marcy Davis;* m Unknown Young
2 CONT *Two of the children above were not recorded at Barnstable.[1] A son named Joseph was mentioned in both Robert and Ann's wills, but no son named John. The son named "John" in the Barnstable Vital Record is assumed to have died you
2 CONC ng. An alternate explanation is that the record may have been written Jos and was transcribed as Jo. Some propose Joseph was an eldest son born in England, and some propose he was a youngest son born in Barnstable, but not recorde
2 CONC d.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert's will mentioned "my two Daughters Sarah and marcy" and also "my Daughter mary." For this reason, we assume there were two different daughters named Marcy/Mercy and Mary. Ann mentioned only the one daughter, "Mercy Young." 
2 CONC This discrepancy is explained by making Ann a second wife, who only mentioned the younger children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Caution: a different Robert Davis, of Sudbury, had two daughters: Rebecca and Sarah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Will & Testament
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Davis of Barnstable made his will 14 April 1688.[6] His residence is not stated in the will, but he was "Late of Barnestable" when the inventory was sworn to. Bequests were as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT to wife Ann all my household goods of Iron and brass and pewter and wooden ware and Linnen and Beding except it be ye bed that my son Joseph Lyieth on which I... bequeath to him with ye Beding belonging to it"
2 CONT To my son Joseph Davis my Land that I bought of ye Indians Lying in ye Comon field
2 CONT I will to my Son Josiah Davis and do also confirm to him a parcel of Land and swamp within ye Comon field fence nere about two acres butting on Samuel Cobs Land on ye North side and on James Gorehams Land that was on ye east sid a
2 CONC nd butting westerly against my Improved Land and a parcel of Land that his house Stands up on of four Rod Squear lying on ye back side of his house and easter end faceing to ye highway not to come westerly about half a Rod of ye w
2 CONC est end of his house with what he formerly had
2 CONT To my son Joseph Davis all ye Rest of my Lands and ye housing Standing up on it... he paying to his mother twenty shillings a year in Corne at Currant prise if shee hath need of it and his mother to have ye use of ye dwelling ouse
2 CONC  during her Natural Life
2 CONT I do confirm to my Daughter Deborah Geere what she hath alredy had
2 CONT I do confirm to my two Daughters Sarah and marcy what they already had
2 CONT To my son Andrew Daves five shillings in currant pay
2 CONT To my Daughter mary five shillings in currant pay
2 CONT To my Daughter Hannah Dexter ten Shillings in currant pay
2 CONT To my Son Robert Davis five shillings in Currant pay
2 CONT after my Just debts be paid I do give all my Stock of Cattel and Swine to my wife and Son Joseph to be equally devided between them two Except my Sheep them I... bequeath to my wife
2 CONT my Loving wife Ann and my Son Joseph Davis to be my executors
2 CONT The will was signed by a mark. The witnesses were James Gorham and John Gorham.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 29 June 1693, both witnesses made oath to the will, before Barnabas Lothrop, Judge of Probate.
2 CONT
2 CONT [p. 82] An Invintory of ye Estate of Robert Davis deceased ye 9 day of April 1693: taken ye 29 day of June 1693 by James Gorham and Jabez Lumbert. The total amount as 75 pounds, 13s. The only real estate was "his house and Land" 3
2 CONC 0 pounds.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Davis vid Relict of Robirt Davis Late of Barnestable deceased and Joseph Daves Son of ye said deceased made oath to the inventory, before Barnabas Lothrop, Judge of Probate 29 June 1693.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT The will and inventory were recorded 3 July 1693 by Joseph Lothrop, Register.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert was born about 1608 to Ichabod and Suzy (unk) Davis in Benefield, Northamptonshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Ann Kingman [[1]]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann and Robert have ten children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Deborah b.1645/1646 Yarmouth
2 CONT Mary b. April 28th, 1648 Yarmouth
2 CONT Andrew b.1650 May, Barnstable
2 CONT John b. 1652, Barnstable
2 CONT Robert, Aug 1654, Barnstable
2 CONT Josiah, Sept 1656, Barnstable
2 CONT Hannah b Sept 1658 Barnstable
2 CONT Sarah, b.1660, Barnstable
2 CONT Joseph b. Barnstable
2 CONT Mercy b. Barnstable
2 CONT [[https://www.wikitree.com/photo/jpg/Davis-67574
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away in 1688 in Barnstable, Barnstable, Massachusetts
