1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The sixth child of Robert Davis (d 1692) was Josiah,2 born in September, 1656, further mentioned as follows, p. 223: “Josiah Davis and Ann Tayler married June 25, 1679.” “Their son Josiah, born in August, 1687.” Th
2 CONC e printed record includes also (p. 225). under “Josiah Davis and Mehitable, his wife,” “Their son Josiah was born 2 Aug. 1718.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Otis’s “Genealogical Notes of Barnstable Families” has this record: “Josiah3 Davis son . Iof Josiah,2 married July 10, 1712, Mehitable, daughter of Edward Taylor, of West Barnstable.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT I found this at this web site http://bigelowsociety.com/rod2005/davis05.htm:
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Josiah Davis, born September 1656, married Anne Taylor and died in 1710.
2 CONT
2 CONT I found this at this web site: https://archive.org/stream/cu31924028819212/cu31924028819212_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Josiah Davis' house is named in the laying out of the County road, in 1686, as next east of Samuel Cobb's, on the north side of the way. It stood a few feet east of the present dwelling house of Lot Easterbrook's, and was taken
2 CONC  down not many years ago. In his will, dated 21st April, 1709, and proved the 5th of October following, he names his nine children, all of whom were then living. To his sons John, Josiah, and Seth, he gave his  dwelling house, the
2 CONC  land he bought of James Gorham, the Common Field land, given him by his father, and one-half of the orchard lying before his door, on the south side of the road. To his sons Jonathan and Stephen, the other half of the orchard. He
2 CONC  names his daughters Hannah Cobb, and Ruth, Sarah and Anna unmarried. The legacies to his daughters he ordered to be paid out of the £53 he ventured in trading at sea, £30 in the hands of his son John, and £23 in the hands of Gers
2 CONC ham Cobb. His estate was apprised at over £500, corn being then worth 10 shillings a bushel, showing that there had been some depreciation in the currency since the death of his father. In the division of the common he was entitle
2 CONC d to 43 1-2 shares, a number above the average. He was a soldier in Capt. John Gorham's company in King Phillip's war in 1675, and one of the proprietors of Gorham-  town. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I found this web site here: http://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Barnstable/Barnstable/Images/Barnstable_04-222.gif
2 CONT
