1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From: THE GEER GENEALOGY, A Historical Record of George and Thomas Geer and Their Descendants in the United States From 1623 to 1923  pages 6 & 7
2 CONT
2 CONT But little is known about Jonathan Geere, the immediate ancestor of the family in England.  No record has been found of his baptism, or that of his sons, as the Parish Register of Heavitree does not begin early enough to contain t
2 CONC hese records, the earliest entry being dated 1653.  Nor has any record been found of his will, after a careful search for wills of testators of that name proved in the Prerogative Court of Canterbury.  Jonathan seems, nevertheless
2 CONC , to have been a man of considerable property, and it is possible that he did not live in Devonshire the later years of his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the best information available, Jonathan was born about 1580, and died prior to 1635, soon after the death of his wife.  He left two young sons, George and Thomas, under the guardianship of an uncle.
2 CONT
