1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Elizabeth Gibbs Jones=
2 CONT * BIRTH 1719
2 CONT * DEATH 28 Jun 1800 (aged 80–81)
2 CONT * BURIAL West Cemetery, Somers, Tolland County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 11473085  Photos by Sue, Contributor: Gene Zubrinsky, FASG (47226970), 9/3/2020
2 CONT
2 CONT Though not documented, Elizabeth Gibbs’s parentage is strongly attested by circumstantial evidence. Among the children of SAMUEL3 GIBBS (b. 16 April 1677, d. bet. 5 Oct. 1756 and 5 Sept. 1757) were sons Giles and Stephen, whose re
2 CONC spective forenames Elizabeth (Gibbs) Jones and her husband, Benjamin4 Jones (mem. 11473068, Benjamin Jones III), gave to two of their sons (James A. Rasmussen, “The Gibbs Family of Windsor CT, Part One,” _American Genealogist_ 61[
2 CONC 1985]:32–43, at 34–37; Somers Deeds, D:505–6). In 1726 SAMUEL3 GIBBS's namesake son, Samuel4 (b. 1704), bought a 50-acre parcel in Enfield’s East Precinct—incorporated as Somers in 1734—from Ebenezer3 Jones, uncle of Benjamin4 ([O
2 CONC ld] Hampshire Co., Mass., Deeds, D:616). In 1743 Samuel4 Gibbs was living in Windsor’s Ellington Parish (adjacent to Somers) and in 1749 bought additional land there; in 1751 he sold Ellington land to his namesake son, Samuel5 (b.
2 CONC  1729) (_American Genealogist_ 61:36–37, citing Windsor Deeds, 7:209, 8:180, 9:161, 162). 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1768 Samuel5 Gibbs bought 60 acres next to Benjamin4 Jones’s land in Somers and lived there until his death, in 1775 (Somers Deeds C:168–69 [see also D:131, 153, 393]; Somers Vital Records, Barbour Collection, 49; Stafford Dist
2 CONC rict Probate, file 869 and volume 2:24). One of the minor children Samuel5 Gibbs left was a daughter Azubah, aged 15 when she chose a guardian, in 1776 (_American Genealogist_ 61:37, citing Stafford District Probate File 884). In 
2 CONC 1770 a daughter was born to Benjamin4 and Elizabeth (Gibbs) Jones’s son Daniel5 (b. 1746[/7]) and his wife, Jemima (Webb), whom they named Azubah (Somers VR, Barbour, 63). 
2 CONT
2 CONT The foregoing facts lead to the inescapable conclusion that SAMUEL3 GIBBS (Samuel2, Giles1) and his wife, MARY (WINCHELL) (m. Windsor 4 March 1702/3 [VR, Barbour, 113]), were the parents of Elizabeth (Gibbs) Jones, among whose sib
2 CONC lings were Samuel4, Giles, and Stephen Gibbs and whose son Daniel5 Jones emulated his first cousin Samuel5 Gibbs in naming a daughter Azubah.
2 CONT
2 CONT wife of Benjamin, age 81 years
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Samuel Gibbs 1677–1757
2 CONT Mary Winchell Gibbs 1683 – unknown
2 CONT
