1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wife of Sam Gowdy.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Gowdy, eldest son of Samuel and Abial (Pease) Gowdy, born in Enfield, Connecticut, 10 June 1760, was married there 29 Jan. 1784, to Alice Gleason. He died 19 April 1840. The Muster Rolls and Pension Records show that Samuel
2 CONC  Gowdy, Jr., enlisted 10 July 1780, as a private in the Second Regiment of the Connecticut Line formation of 1777-1781. The Enfield Revolutionary army records show that on 13 Feb. 1783, an order was given to pay Samuel Gowdy, Jr. 
2 CONC for his services in the 'short levies' in the year 1780 in bills of the state £11 7s. 4d. Also in hard money for said services £0. 19s. 6d.
2 CONT After marriage moved to Middlefield, Connecticut. From there traveled overland by ox team to New York. Arrived in spring of 1802 together with one Martin and settled near Martinsburo.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memori
2 CONC al/61464711/alice-gowdy Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 20 2023, 23:08:41 UTC''
