1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Recorded as written:
2 CONT
2 CONT JOSEPH CHANDLER( Daniel, Henry, Thomas, William1) and Mary Chapin, Enfield, She was b. 24 Feb., 1744; d 1 Jan., 1828, in her 84th year; dau. of David Chapin of Enfield by his wife Thankful.
2 CONT
2 CONT > Joseph Chandler was one of those who Enlisted into the Continental Army, agreeable to a Vote of the Town of Enfield, Nov. 19, 1777, and he received of the town L12 for his expenses to march to West Point under the command of Cap
2 CONC t. R. Ablie, at the order of the Committee.
2 CONT
2 CONT > He was partially sun struck or heated in the army and was obliged to leave and get a substitute, which misfortune was the occasion of his mental derangement in after life. and the reason why he did not receive a pension for his 
2 CONC military services. A farmer; he died in Enfield l6 Sept., 1816, in his 85th year.
2 CONT
2 CONT >The children of Joseph and Mary (Chapin) Chandler were
2 CONT
2 CONT  *   i Mary, b. 18 Aug., 1766; m. 24 Nov., 1794, Truman Banister
2 CONT
2 CONT *  ii Sarah, b. 6 April, 1769; m.  28 June, 1787 Noah Coole,y of Enfield. Their daughter Hannah Cooley was b. 4 Nov, 1787. She married.
2 CONT
2 CONT  *  iii Joseph, b. 27 July, 1771; m first Lydia Hawkins; m. second, 4 March, 1825, Mary Hardy widow of - Butler
2 CONT
2 CONT *  iv Thomas, b. 29 July, 1775; m. 14 Feb 1796, Mary Steele
2 CONT
2 CONT *  v Mehitable, b. 18 Nov., 1777; m. 1795, Jonathan Taylor 
2 CONT
2 CONT *  vi Daniel, b. 17 Dec., 1780; m. 17 Aug., 1802, Clarissa Hale
2 CONT
2 CONT *  vii George, b. 10 Nov., 1781; m. first ,29 Nov., 1810, Catherine Bancroft of Granville, Mass; m. second, 14 Jan., 1845, Eunice Sacket 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''':Source: THE FAMILY OF WILLIAM AND ANNIS CHANDLER; WHO SETTLED IN ROXBURY, MASS 1637; by George Chandler; printed for the family on the press of George Hamilton of Worcester, Mass; 311 Main Street, 1883; Pg.174-175
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Links''': 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.com/books?id=h2JmAAAAMAAJ&dq=decendents%20of%20annis%20chandlers&pg=PA930&ci=293%2C190%2C639%2C257&source=bookclip#v=onepage&q=stephan%20chandler%20&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=g2473p&id=I22311
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.com/books?id=ja0yAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA1002&lpg=PA1002&dq=joseph+chandler+enfield+ct+continental+army&source=bl&ots=R6aXFZ0aRq&sig=ACfU3U2GEV07iPsGEgM_noYTNoC70aHH9w&hl=en&sa=X&v  pg. 1002
2 CONT
2 CONT Added by D. Glenn/2016
2 CONT
2 CONT I received a suggestion to remove the paragraph concerning his mental disability due to lack of sources. As I read George Chandler's biography, I take it that Joseph was denied a pension due to getting a stand in to complete his s
2 CONC ervice due to illness caused  by sun stroke. I am leaving this as written. It is often difficult to source on older profiles. I have found George Chandler's writing is often used  as a source by professional's, for their work on t
2 CONC he Chandler family. D. Glenn-2018
2 CONT
