1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  From The Chandler Family: The Descendants of William and Annis Chandler; Pg.504
2 CONT
2 CONT  MARY CHANDLER (Joseph, Daniel,  Henry, Thomas, William) and Truman Banister Wilbraham, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was b. 13 April, 1777; d. 29 Nov., 1844, son of Joseph and Statira Banister, of Springfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Mrs. Mary Banister, at the age of 94, was feeble in body, but had a clear mind and retentive memory of early transactions. She died 1804, aged 98, in Wilbraham.
2 CONT
2 CONT  The children of Mary and Truman Banister were:
2 CONT
2 CONT  i Sarah Banister, b. in Springfield 27 Feb., 1796; lived unm. with her sister Mrs. Whitcomb Gray in Wilbraham, and took care of her mother in her last days.
2 CONT
2 CONT  ii Alvan Banister, b. 22 Oct., 1797
2 CONT
2 CONT  iii Polly Banister, b. 30 Aug., 1799; m. Roderick Ashley of Springfield, boatman; assessor.
2 CONT
2 CONT  iv Sophia Banister, b. 7 April, 1801; d. 24 July, 1804 
2 CONT
2 CONT v Ruel Banister, b. in Springfield 16 July, 1804; resides at Colebrook, N.H.; m. Mary Butler, dau. of his uncle Joseph Chandler's second wife by her first husband
2 CONT
2 CONT  vi Sophia Banister, 2d; b. 9 May, 1808; m. Whitecomb Gray of Wilbraham; resides about half a mile west of the Academy.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Links:''' 
2 CONT
