1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Chandler Family: The Descendants of William and Annis Chandler 
2 CONT
2 CONT  JOSEPH CHANDLER (Joseph, Daniel, Henry, Thomas, William) and Lydia Hawkins, Colebrook, N.H. She was b. 18 Nov., 1768; d. 24 Feb., 1822, in Colebrook, leaving nine children; dau. of Joel Hawkins.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He m. second, Mary Chickering Hardy, widow of David Butler, formerly of Pelham, Mass. She died 1 Nov., 1849, in her 68th year.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was a shoemaker and had a farm, near the geographical centre of Colbrook, of about thirty acres. He was on the tax list there in 1806.
2 CONT
2 CONT  The children of Joseph Chandler were:
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1225 i Luther, b. in Enfield, Conn., 24 Oct., 1789; m. first, 20 Oct., 1809, Sally Stone; m. second, 1 Dec., 1847, Olive Brainard, widow of John Whittemore; m. third, 18G4 Sarah Dowse
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1226 ii Samuel, b. 8 Oct., 1791; m. first Hannah Chapin; m. second, in Albany, N.Y., June, 1818, Anne E. McKelsey
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1227 iii Joseph, b. 5 Dec., 1793; m. 19 Nov., 1824, at Frankfort, N.Y., Sophia Earl
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1228 iv Sarah, b. 12 April, 1796; d. 13 Jan., 1815; m. Marvin Clark of Enfield; no issue
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1229 v Lydia H., b. 29 Aug., 1798; m., in Colebrook, 13 Dec., 1816, Geo. W. Lucas, both of Colebrook
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1230 vi Elizabeth S., b. 29 Aug., 1798, twin of Lydia; m. 1 Jan., 1818, Francis Flanders, Esq. of Hereford, L.C.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1231 vii Rodolphus, b. 29 Oct.,1800; m. 7 Dec., 1822, Tabitha Wells
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1232 viii, Almira, b. 8 July, 1803; m. 18 Feb., 1824, Benjamin Whittemore of Dixville, N.H,
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1233 ix Mary, b. 22 Nov., 1806; m in Colebrook, 13 Nov., 1828, Joel W. Locke, both of Colebrook
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1234 x Sarah Adaline, b. 14 March, 1826; m. 27 Dec., 1845, John S. Chase
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Link''' : https://books.google.com/books?id=h2JmAAAAMAAJ&q=william+chandler#v=onepage&q=sally%20stone&f=false
2 CONT
