2 CONT
2 CONT 1709, March 22: "Att the same meeting the town by a voate gave liberty to mr. John Hamlin and Sarg't ffrancis Whitmore to build a warfe on the north side the crick upon their own charg for their own and the towns benefit for conve
2 CONC niancy of landing and laying of vessels, they exacting wharfage of none but of strangers."
2 CONT "The History of Middlesex County 1635-1885: Town and City OF Middletown" by Henry Whitmore; pp. 282-320; J. H. Beers and Company; New York City, New York; 1884
2 CONT and
2 CONT "Genealogies and Family History of the State of Connecticut" by William Richard Cutter; Historical Publishing Company; New York City, New York; 1911 (929.2 Connect/Cutter CSL) (974.6 C991 1997 LAPL) (974.0 CT/ Genealogy SCGS)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1748, April 4: The Last Will and Testament of Francis Wetmore was dated. "I, Francis Whitmore of Middletown, do make this my last will and testament: I give unto Mary, my well-beloved wife, the equal third part of all my personal 
2 CONC estate after my just debts and funeral charges are paid, and the improvement of the equal half of my dwelling house and cellar, and the use of 1-3 part of my barn and the 1-3 part of all my improved lands during her natural life. 
2 CONC I give to my grandson Francis Whitmore, the only son of my eldest son Francis Whitmore, Jr., decd., 7 acres of land which joyns Nathan Sayre's and Hamilton's land; and to the six daughters of my sd. son, namely, Sarah, Mary, Isabe
2 CONC l, Susannah, Zerviah and Abigail, to each the sum of £10. I give to my son Jacob Whitmore 15 acres of land joyning the Connecticut River, Harris's meadow, Lemuel Lee's land and Daniel Pryor's land; and half of the land I have in t
2 CONC he lott that did belong to John Boarn, adjoining a highway, Daniel Lucas's land, and on my own land; and 1-5 part of all that part of my Kent lott that lyes on the west of the highway by Samuel Brooks's. I give to my son Daniel Wh
2 CONC itmore that 6 acres of land that I bought of Samuel Hurlburt, and 4 acres adjoining Daniel Pryor's land. I give to my son Nathaniel Whitmore all that place where he now dwells, bounded west on a highway. I give to my son Ebenezer 
2 CONC Whitmore all the land adjoining to the land where his house stands, and all the land lying between 10 acres of land that I have given him by deed of gift. I give to my son Hezekiah Whitmore, and to his heirs and assigns forever, a
2 CONC ll my dwelling house and barn and the land on which they stand, bounded northerly on Daniel Pryor's land, west on a highway by sd. highway till it comes two lotts southward of the north fence of my son-in-law John Davis. I give to
2 CONC  my daughter Margery, the wife of John Davis, and to her heirs forever, all my land that lyes between the lands of Nathan Sayes and the land herein given to my son Hezekiah. I give to my daughter Elizabeth, the wife of Peter Morga
2 CONC n, and to her heirs and assigns forever, all that 25 acres of land which I bought of Zachariah Hubbard. And all the remaining part of all my personal estate (after my just debts and funeral charges and legacies are paid and 1-3 pa
2 CONC rt taken out for my wife) I give to my four daughters, Margery, Hannah, Elizabeth and Abigail, in equal parts. And I further give to my daughter Hannah £100 old tenor, to be paid by my son Hezekiah aforsd. I also give to my daught
2 CONC er Abigail £60 old tenor, to be paid her by my son Ebenezer. I appoint my two sons, Jacob Whitmore and Daniel Whitmore, executors.
2 CONT Francis Whitmore, L.S.
2 CONT Giles Hall, George Hubbard and William Rockwell
2 CONT "A Digest of Early Connecticut Probate Records: Hartford District" compiled by Charles William Manwaring; III:683; R. S. Peck & Company, Printers; Hartford, Connecticut; 1904 (974.6 CT/Probate SCGS) (Gen 974.6 M295 1904 LAPL)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1750, May 8: The inventory of the Estate of Francis Wetmore, Middletown. was taken by Jonathan Allyn and Timothy Bigelow and amounted to £685-19-05.
2 CONT "A Digest of Early Connecticut Probate Records: Hartford District" compiled by Charles William Manwaring; III:683; R. S. Peck & Company, Printers; Hartford, Connecticut; 1904 (974.6 CT/Probate SCGS) (Gen 974.6 M295 1904 LAPL)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1750, May 14: The Last Will and Testament of Francis Whitmore, late of Middletown, was now exhibited in Cout by Jacob and Daniel Whitmore, executors. Will Proven (Court Record; p. 130).
2 CONT "A Digest of Early Connecticut Probate Records: Hartford District" compiled by Charles William Manwaring; III:683; R. S. Peck & Company, Printers; Hartford, Connecticut; 1904 (974.6 CT/Probate SCGS) (Gen 974.6 M295 1904 LAPL)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Whitmore and Whittemore Families" by Rev. Charles N. Sinnett; Carthage, South Dakota
2 CONT
2 CONT "Record of the Descendants of Francis Whitmore of Cambridge, Massachusetts" by William Henry Whitmore; printed for private circulation by John Wilson and Son; Boston, Massachusetts; 1855 (929.2 W597W ACPL)
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Whitmore Genealogy: A Record of the Descendents of Francis Whitmore of Cambridge, Massachusetts, 1625-1685" by Jessie Whitmore Patten Purdy; Pengelly and Brothers, printers; Reading, Pennsylvania; 1907 (929.2 W597P ACPL)
2 CONT
2 CONT "A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England Showing Three Generations of those Who Came Before May 1692 on the Basis of the Farmer's Register" by James Savage; The Genealogical Publishing Company, Inc.; Baltimo
2 CONC re, Maryland; 1981 (929.274 S264 LAPL) (NE Sec. SR) (974.0 NEa SCGS)
2 CONT
2 CONT "John Whitmore/Wetmore of Hartford & Middletown, Connecticut" by Raeola Ford Cooke; privately published - 2060 11th Avenue East, Twin Falls, Idaho 83301; 1986
2 CONT
2 CONT "Vital Records of Cambridge, Massachusetts to the Year 1850" compiled by Thomas W. Baldwin; New England Historic and Genealogical Society; Boston, Massachusetts; 1915"A Digest of Early Connecticut Probate Records: Hartford Distric
2 CONC t" compiled by Charles William Manwaring; II:329; R. S. Peck & Company, Printers; Hartford, Connecticut; 1904 (974.6 CT/Probate SCGS) (Gen 974.6 M295 1904 LAPL) 
2 CONT
