2 CONT Name: William WARD Sex: M Birth: 29 OCT 1720 Death: 25 FEB 1786
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: 20 MAR 1786 Middletown, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference Number: 2263
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT     1767 he was appointed to Assembly Lieutant of 14th Company 6th Regiment. In 1771 he made Captain.
2 CONT     He freed two of his slaves named Venture & Cuff. He gave his wife a negro named Fannie. When Fannie turned 26 years old she was to be freed.
2 CONT
2 CONT     His father William Ward left him 99 Acres in Middlefield. Plus three slaves named Mingo, Venture & Phillis.
2 CONT
2 CONT     He settled in Middlefield alittle south of the Capt. Ward Spring in which was named after him. Later it was owned by Cornwell Coe.
2 CONT
2 CONT     In 1767 he was appointed assembly Lieut. in the 14th Company, 6th Regiment. In 1771 he made Captain.
2 CONT
