2 CONT Add another spouse & children ▼Facts and Events Name[1][2] 	Dr. Ebenezer Prout Alt Name 	Captain Ebenezer Prout Gender 	Male Birth[2][3] 	14 Mar 1656/57 	Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts, United States Baptism[4] 	15 Mar 1656/57 	Bo
2 CONC ston, Suffolk, Massachusetts, United States Marriage 	28 May 1678 	Concord, Middlesex, Massachusetts, United Statesto Elizabeth Wheeler Marriage 	bef 1690 	to Grace Sherman Death[5] 	27 Apr 1735 	Middletown, Middlesex, Connecticut
2 CONC , United States ▼References
2 CONT
2 CONT     ↑ Ebenezer Prout, in Savage, James. A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England: Showing Three Generations of Those Who Came Before May, 1692, on the Basis of Farmer's Register. (Boston: Little, Brown, and C
2 CONC o, 1860-1862), 3:490.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Prout, * Ebenezer, Concord, s. of Timothy, was capt. and rep. 1689 and 90, and clk. of the house, was freem. 1690, m. 1678, Elizabeth d. of capt. Timothy Wheeler, had Timothy. His w. d. at Charlestown, 11 Oct. 1683; and by sec
2 CONC . w. Grace at Watertown, had Eunice, bapt. 13 Apr. 1690; Mary, b. Apr. 1694, d. soon; John, 6 Nov. 1695, d. young; was town clk. selectman, rep. 1693.
2 CONT     ↑ 2.0 2.1 Jacobus, Donald Lines. The Family of Rev. John Sherman of Wethersfield, Milford and Branford, Conn., and Watertown, Mass. American Genealogist (D.L. Jacobus). (Jan 1944), 20:134.
2 CONT
2 CONT     (Capt.) Ebenezer Prout, b. at Boston, 14 Mar. 1656, d. at Middletown, Conn., 27 Apr. 1735, son of Capt. Timothy and Margaret (_____) Prout. He moved from Watertown to Concord, Maas., about 1696, and by 1711 to Wethersfield, Co
2 CONC nn., and some years later to Middletown. He was Deputy and Clerk of the House in 1689, and represented Watertown in 1693; Town Clerk in 1694. In May 1711, "Mr. Ebenezer Prout, now residing in Wethersfield, is by this Assembly allo
2 CONC wed to practice physick and surgery, within this Colony" [Col. Rec. of Conn., 5-228]. In 1715 he was proceeded against for illegally buying land of an Indian [ib., 5-538].
2 CONT     ↑ Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts, United States. Births, Baptisms, Marriages, and Deaths, 1630-1699 (A Report of the Record Commissioners). (Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts, United States: Rockwell and Churchill, City Printers,
2 CONC  1883), 56.
2 CONT
2 CONT     1656 … Ebenezer of Timothy & Mary Prout born 14th March.
2 CONT     ↑ Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts, United States. Births, Baptisms, Marriages, and Deaths, 1630-1699 (A Report of the Record Commissioners). (Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts, United States: Rockwell and Churchill, City Printers,
2 CONC  1883), 63.
2 CONT
2 CONT     1657 … Ebenezer of Timothy Proute (baptized First Church) 15 day 1 mo.
2 CONT     ↑ Middletown Vital Records [NEHGS], in Connecticut, United States. The Barbour Collection of Connecticut Town Vital Records, 353.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Prout, Ebenezer, Dr., d. Apr. 27, 1735 [1:44].
2 CONT
