2 CONT [[Category: Battles of Lexington and Concord]][[Category: Suffolk County Militia, Massachusetts Militia, American Revolution]]
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT {{Society Ancestor|society=DAR|ancestor= A042396}}{{1776 Sticker|rank=Sergeant |unit=Col. Ebenezer Thayer's Regiment of Militia, Massachusetts Militia, American Revolution}}
2 CONT Elijah was born in 1726. He was the son of [[French-5047|Thomas French]] and [[Owen-11798|Mary Owen]].  He passed away in 1800. 
2 CONT DAR lists service as Private with Captain Adams, Colonel Lincoln (Suffolk County Militia).  Lexington Alarm.  Then as Sergeant Captain SilasWild who served with Col. Ebenezer Thayer's Regiment of Militia, Massachusetts Militia, Am
2 CONC erican Revolution. 
2 CONT
