1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Daughters of American Revolution Ancestor #: A032279
2 CONT * Service:  VERMONT    Rank: PATRIOTIC SERVICE
2 CONT * Birth:  4-11-1714    WESTFIELD HAMPSHIRE CO MASSACHUSETTS
2 CONT * Death:  12-21-1778     BENNINGTON VERMONT
2 CONT * Service Source: JENNINGS, MEMORIALS OF A CENTURY, BENNINGTON, VT, P 85,86
2 CONT * Service Description: 1) PATRIOT PREACHER
2 CONT
2 CONT Info added per DAR's "Lineage Book of the Charter Members" by Mary S Lockwood and published 1895 stating:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Rev Jedediah Dewey, a recognized patriot and leader in helping to band together the men who successfully resisted the British and Hessians at the battle of Bennington."
2 CONT
2 CONT Monument Inscription: "In Memory of the Rev. M. JEDIDIAH DEWEY, First Pastor of the Church in Bennington, Who after A Laborious Life in the Gospel Ministry, Resign'd his Office in God's Temple For the Sublime Employment of Immorta
