2 CONT * '''Wikitree:''' [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Dewey-1440 Abner Dewey (1726 - abt. 1777)] 
2 CONT ** Death place showing at last update (5 Dec 2024) is impossible. 
2 CONT *** Hopkinton, NY and St. Lawrence County, NY were created in 1802.
2 CONT * '''WeRelate.org:''' [https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Abner_Dewey_(1) Abner Dewey]
2 CONT ** No evidence given for "Bennington, Vermont" or anything at all as of 5 Sep 2025. Considering potential of his being int the following military record (below), Abner may have died in or near Pittsfield, Berkshire, MA — where Wik
2 CONC itree places '''''some''''' births of children borne by Abner's wife. However, a book mentions "Abner Dewey" among others being among others in Poultney, Vermont on 12 September 1761:—
2 CONT *** "Then follow the named of the grantees on the back of the Charter" – "Abner Dewey" — Though he may have been in Poutney, about 90 miles north of Pittsfield, his presence in Poultney does not confirm that Poultney was his resid
2 CONC ence from 1761 until he died.
2 CONT **** "History of Poultney." In ''A History of the Town of Poultney, Vermont'', [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/22149/images/dvm_LocHist007745-00021-0?pId=13 Ancestry.com].
