1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Vital Notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Some children are named in Isaac's Last Will & Testament but do not have birth records.
2 CONT * '''Be Wary of "Find A Grave":''' Some persons have been tempted to accept data from this 	[https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/28050146/isaac-gillet '''Find A Grave page'''] simply because it shows a burial of a same-named man w
2 CONC ith a same given-named wife. '''''However''''', there is NO record proving that Isaac had a son named Roderick. Even if Isaac did, the assumptive Roderick must've died young—before Isaac's Will was dictated. '''Key Point:''' 
2 CONT * The only reason to explain burial in Southwick, MA is that is appear (without deeper study) that Isaac Jr. moved to Southwick and died there. However, evidence must be found that proves Isaac Jr.'s ''Simsbury-residing'' parents 
2 CONC chose to be buried in Southwick, MA. There also could be a mix-up on which Isaac Gillet was the father of Roderick.
2 CONT * A transcribed copy of the handwritten document is posted in Source. Whether the children without birth records were biological children of Isaac and Honora is not known. Isaac only refers to them as his sons and daughters.'' 
2 CONT * In Simsbury, Isaac dictated his will on 16 Apr 1780. The assumption that he died in Massachusetts was without sources merit and Simsbury now replaces it for death until as sure source proves otherwise. Simsbury was Isaac's long-
2 CONC time residence at the time of dictating his will. 
2 CONT * It is assumed that his death occurred closer to the date of the will being proved – nearly 4 years after dictating it.
2 CONT * Isaac's will was "proved and approved this 9thj day of October 1784 and to Lay on file as accomplished & recorded in the 2nd of Records of Wills."
2 CONT * One or two children in the sourced births posted below have not yet been added. — (Ken Shelley, 24 Dec 2022)
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''''Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906'', [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F74M-F4G FamilySearch]'''
