2 CONT Came from a family of substantial yeomen in Dorset. To Dorchester MA 1633. An original settler of Windsor. Deputy to the first General Court, a ruling elder of the church. Known for his piety, received a call to fill a vacancy in 
2 CONC a church in Springfield in 1653. But he was not university educated, and was a poor preacher, and was not a success as a minister. Returned to England (1654), and took aparish in Tiverton, Devon. (Source: Thistlethwaite, Dorset Pi
2 CONC lgrims) Jane Hosford, William's second wife, bequeathed a meadow to the church of Windsor, for the "use of a pastor or teacher as the church shall see most needful." In October 1692 the church petitioned the court for the right to
2 CONC  use the meadow, which was currently in the hands of some of John Hosford's heirs, who claimed his wife was still alive. The Court, however, claiming she was aged when she went to England nearly 40 years before and had not been he
2 CONC ard from for several years, declared that, unless the heirs could prove that she was alive, the land should go to the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT #1 Ye Horseforde booke Horsford-Hosford families in the United States of America. By Henry Hallock Hosford. This is the William Hosford that is the start of the book. 1. WILLIAM William Horsford was born in England and came with h
2 CONC is wife to Dorchester, Massachusetts Bay Colony, about 1630. He returned to England and died at Tiverton, Co. Devon, about 1660. His first wife, the mother of his children, died Aug. 20, 1641. He married, second, at Windsor, Conn.
2 CONC , Jane, a widow of Henry Fawkes (Fokes, Fookes, Fouks, etc.). Henry F. died in 1640. Jane followed her husband to England and died there after 1674. Born by about 1595, based on date of marriage. Died in England after 1655. Came f
2 CONC rom Beaminster, Dorset to Massachusetts Bay in 1633. First settled in Dorchester; moved to Windsor in 1635, Springfield in 1653. Returned to England permanently in 1654. Children of William and his first wife, perhaps Sara by name
2 CONC : 2 i. SARA ( -1647) 3 ii. ESTHER (?) 4 iii. JOHN (1636(?)-1683)
