2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Hester Horsford, daughter of William and Florence (Hayward) Horsford, was born in Beaminster, and baptized at St. Mary's, Beaminster, Dorsetshire, England on 17 October 1621.[1] [2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married first, Richard Samwiss (Samos, Samwais, Sammis, etc.) who died Jan. 4, 1654.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hester and Richard Samways[1] had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Sammis (or Samways) born 1643[4]
2 CONT Johanna Sammis/Samways born 1648[4]
2 CONT Mary Sammis/Samways, born 1650.[4]
2 CONT Richard Sammis (or Samways) died 4 Jan 1654.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Hester (Hosford) Sammis married 2nd John(?) Williams,[4] by 27 October 1674.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, second, John(?) Williams. The second marriage is inferred from a Connecticut court record dating October 27, 1674, reading in part as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT "We the underwritten; In behalf of ourselves and Joan and Mary, the daughters of Richard Samwais, having received this day of the Sect'y a bond, made to colony of Conn. of 60 pounds obligating ye grandfather Hosford or uncle John 
2 CONC Hosford or our father Williams," etc.
2 CONT Signed:
2 CONT John Samwais
2 CONT Richard Brush (or Beach)[4]
2 CONT Children of Hester and John Williams:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca Williams b. c 1652 (Married Mr. (?) Warriner)
2 CONT Hannah Williams b. c 1654 (Married Nathaniel Bancroft)
2 CONT Mary Williams b. c 1656 (Married John Gunn)
2 CONT Abigail Williams b. 31 May 1658 (Married Samuel Phelps)
2 CONT Abigail Williams b. c 1661, d. 16 Sep 1690 (Married Edward Griswald)
2 CONT Hester Horsford passed away after 1712 having been widowed by the passing of her second husband.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: The given name of Hester was sometimes mentioned as "Esther" in the previously unmerged biography (Horsford-116). All references to her have been updated to "Hester" in this profile.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is named Ester Williams in the probate records for her second husband John Williams in 1712.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Web Site: 1652: Mary or Mercy Hosford (12 Apr 1674 - 11 Jul 1753) http://www.idsonline.com/userweb/hurlburt/html/d0006/g0000008.htm
2 CONT Source: Smail, Mamie Ford, Email dated Tuesday, September 26, 2000 with extensive data on the descendants of William Hosford. Many sources cited. Text: Descendants of William Hosford Generation No. 1 WILLIAM1 HOSFORD was born Bet.
2 CONC  1590 - 1595 in Beaminister, Dorsetshire, England, and died Aft. 1666 in Tiverton, Devonshire, England. He married (1) Widow Jane Fowkes. He married (2) Florence Hayward January 21, 1619/20 in Beaminister, Dorsetshire , Eng.. She 
2 CONC was born Bef. April 14, 1594 in Beaminister , Dorsetshire , England, and died Bef. August 20, 1641 in Windsor , Hartford Co. , Ct. Notes for WILLIAM HOSFORD: On the list of Freemen Oaths was a William Horseford , while we know tha
2 CONC t spellings etc were made, I wonder if it was William Hosford that took that Oath on April 01, 1634 . Source ; Book , "The Cooley Genealogy " (Descendents of Ensign Benjamin Cooley )by Mortimer Elwyn Cooley , printed 1941 , by Tut
2 CONC tle Pub. Company Inc. , Rutalnd , Vt. , their source of Hosford Linage ; Savage Genealogical Dictionary of New England : -- Stiles , Genealogy of Ancient Windsor , Conn , Litchfield Genealogical Register , 1720-1800 ; New England 
2 CONC History & Genealogical Register , Vol . XXXIX , page 330 ; Vol. V, page 460 ; and Vital records of the Conn. State Library. WILLIAM HOSFORD1 , Immigrant in Dorchester, Mass., 1633; Freeman April 01, 1634, when his name was spelled
2 CONC  HORSEFORD. His name, along with Henry Wolcott, Esq. appears on the records of 1640 as "the first settlers of Windsor", five years after their removal from Dorchester (England). His first wife, whose name is unknown, d. Aug. 26, 1
2 CONC 641, Windsor, Conn; he married (2) Jane, widow of Henry Fowkes, and removed to Springfield, Mass., where he preached from Oct. 1652 to Oct. 1654. After several years he and his 2nd wife returned to England, where in 1656 he gave l
2 CONC and at Windsor, Conn. to his two children; his 2nd wife also gave land to the Church in Windsor, and to her husband's children. In 1671, Jane (Fowkes) Hosford was in Tiverton, Co. Devon, England. The place and date of her death an
2 CONC d that of her husband, William Hosford, are not known. (As written in the Cooley Genealogy Book.) We now know his 1st wife was Florence Hayward. OTHER Sources; " Ye Horseford Book -Horsford, Hosford Families in United States of Am
2 CONC erica" by Henry Hallock Hosford, printed in 1936, Kendall Green, Ma. LAND RECORDS, that appeared on town (Windsor ) records in 1640 shows WILLIAM HOSFORD's name as well as THOMAS BUCKLAND; HENRY WOLCOTT, Esq.; JOHN HILLYER; ETWELD
