2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Geni.com Samuel "Son of the Immigrant" Born 26 Oct 1661, Gloucester, MA; died 31 May 1740, Suffield, CT; son of Samuel Kent & Frances Woodall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1: Priscilla Hunter, married on 1Nov1683 in Suffield, CT; daughter of William Hunter & Priscilla Corish; born 2Mar1665 in Springfield, MA; died 7Mar 1694/95 in Suffield, CT. Children of Samuel Kent (1661) and Priscilla Hu
2 CONC nter:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Samuel Kent III, b. 8 Dec 1684, Suffield, CT; d. 20 Feb 1684/85, Suffield, CT.
2 CONT 2. Samuel Kent IV, b. 6 Dec 1685, Suffield, CT; m. Hester Phelps.
2 CONT 3. Thomas Kent, b. 3 Apr 1688, Suffield, CT; m. Phebe Winchell.
2 CONT 4. John Kent, b. 24 Aug 1690, Suffield, CT; d. young.
2 CONT 5. Josiah Kent, b. 24 Jan 1692, Suffield, CT; m. Esther Granger.
2 CONT 6. Priscilla Kent, b. 24 Feb 1694/95, Suffield, CT; m. Samuel Brown.
2 CONT Marriage 2: Martha Allen married on 28Jul1696 in Suffield, CT; daughter of Edward Allen & Sarah Kimball; born ca. 1671 in Ipswich, MA; died on 23Feb1697/98 in Suffield, CT. Children of Samuel Kent (1661) and Martha Allen:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Martha Kent, b. 16 Feb 1696/97, Suffield, CT; d. 24 Feb 1697/98, Suffield, CT.
2 CONT Marriage 3: Hester Hosford, married 1May1700 in Suffield, CT, ; daughter of John Hosford & Phillury Thrall; born 27May 1664 in Windsor, CT; died 18Jan1760 in Suffield, CT. Hester was the widow of Joseph Phelps, who died in 1695. C
2 CONC hildren of Samuel Kent (1661) and Hester Hosford:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Martha Kent, b. 8 Feb 1702/03, Suffield, CT.
2 CONT 2. Twin - Daniel Kent, b. 10 Jul 1704, Suffield, CT; m. Hannah Steel.
2 CONT 3. Twin - Mary Kent, b. 10 Jul 1704, Suffield, CT.
2 CONT 4. Benjamin Kent, b. ca. 1706, Suffield, CT; m. (1) Apphia Ruggles; m. (2) widow Love Ensign.
2 CONT 5. Mary Kent, b. ca. 1708, Suffield, CT; m. Samuel Granger.
2 CONT Samuel came with his family to Brookfield in 1668, and moved to Suffield in 1678 after Brookfield was destroyed by Indians.
2 CONT
2 CONT He became a member in full communion lst Cong. Church of Suffield under Rev. Ebenezer Devotion on 28Dec1718 having transferred by letter of recommendation from 1st church, Northampton, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel's son Samuel IV (1685-1763) married Esther Phelps in 1710. Ester was the daughter of his third wife from her previous marriage with Joseph Phelps, whose name was also Esther Phelps (widow). Samuel IV and Esther Phelps had c
2 CONC hildren: Silas b 1711, Amos b 1713, Dinah b 1717, Esther b 1719, Abigail b 1720, Joseph b ? d 1758
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas's estate passed probate. His will names five sons--Samuel, Thomas, Josiah, Daniel and Benjamin--and three daughters--Priscilla, Martha and Mary.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
