1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=123112989
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~steeles/Steele/d125.htm#P2024
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Joseph PHELPS''' was born on 27 Sep 1666 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT. (18656)  
2 CONT * He died on 30 Aug 1716 in Hebron, Tolland Co., CT. (18657)(18658) He had an estate probated on 26 Sep 1716 in Hartford, Hartford Co., CT. (18659)(18660)  
2 CONT * Parents: '''Timothy PHELPS''' and '''Mary GRISWOLD'''. 
2 CONT * He was married to '''Sarah HOSFORD''' on 18 Nov 1686 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT.(18661) (18662) * Children were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sarah PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Mary PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Joseph PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Abigail PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Capt. Edward PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Benoni PHELPS, 
2 CONT # John PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Abel PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Daniel PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Ichabod PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Jonathan PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Abigail PHELPS.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph set tled in W indsor, wh ere his c hildre n w ere all born. He owned a large amount of land in Hebron, and probably removed there late in life, about 1710, where some of his children were living. His will mentions his wife 
2 CONC Sarah, and 10 children: Joseph, Daniel, Edward, John, Abel, Ichabod, Jonathan, Mary, Sarah,and Abigail. Sarah was the daughter of John and Philbury (Thrall) Hosford. Her father was a man of large family and considerable property, 
2 CONC leaving her at his death 100 pounds.
2 CONT
2 CONT THE ANCESTRY OF RUTH PHELPS CASE. First Generation. The genealogy of the Phelps family has been taken from the compilation by Oliver. S. Phelps
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth:  Sep. 27, 1666 Windsor Hartford County Connecticut, USA  Death:  Aug. 30, 1716 Hebron Tolland County Connecticut, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph PHELPS [47] was the second son of Lt Timothy PHELPS [W24 in P&S]. He had 5 brothers and 6 sisters. Joseph was born on 27 Sep 1666 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Sarah HOSFORD, daughter of John THRALL and Phillury HOSFORD. She was born on 27 Sep 1666, the same day as her husband. Her father had a large family and considerable property, leaving her at his death 100 pounds. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Joseph PHELPS settled in Windsor. All of his children were born in Windsor. He owned a large amount of land in Hebron and probably remove there late in life, in about 1719, where some of his children were living. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children, all born in Windsor, Hartford Co., Connecticut: Sarah PHELPS 1687–1717
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary PHELPS Bissell Griswold 1689–1745
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph PHELPS II 1692–1761
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail PHELPS 1693–1774
2 CONT
2 CONT Benoni Phelps 1694–1709
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt Edward PHELPS 1698–1790
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah
2 CONT
2 CONT John (W165) PHELPS 1703–1768
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt Abel PHELPS 1705–1779
2 CONT
2 CONT Deac Daniel PHELPS 1707–1792 NTV
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt Ichabod PHELPS 1708–1794 NTV
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph's wife Sarah Hosford Phelps passed away on 9 Apr 1708 in Windsor, probably of childbirth complications after son Ichabod was born. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph remarried to Sarah GILLETT on 22 Feb 1709 in Windsor, Hartford Co., Connecticut. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph had two more children with his second wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan PHELPS 1711–
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail PHELPS 1714 - 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died 30, Aug 1716, aged 50 years. 
2 CONT
