2 CONT
2 CONT ◦RESEARCH_NOTES:
2 CONT  1. Mentioned in father's will and listing of father's children as follows per the book "The Phelps Family of America and their English Ancestors," comp. by Oliver Seymour Phelps of Portland, Oregon and Andrew T. Servin of Lenox, 
2 CONC Massachusetts, 1899, pp. 93-97:
2 CONT  "Hartford Probate Records. Vol. 9, p.p. 338. Last will and testament of Mr. Timothy Phelps of Windsor, in the County of Hartford and Colony of Connecticut in New England.
2 CONT  'I, Timothy Phelps of Windsor, in the town, county and colony aforesaid in New England, being very aged, and yet through the mercy of God retaining a good measure of that understanding and memory that he had been pleased to besto
2 CONC w upon me, do make and ordain this to be my last will and testament: First, I commit my soul to God in Jesus Christ my saviour and my body to the earth, to be decently entered. As for my estate Real and personal, my just Debts and
2 CONC  funeral expenses being deducted and paid by my Ex's, I will devise and bequeath as followeth.
2 CONT  Imprimis, I give, devise, and bequeath all my estate whatsoever, Both Real and personal, To my three sons William, Cornelius, and Samuell to have and to hold and Improve the same in trust for the use of my wife during her natural
2 CONC  life and after her decease my will is and I hereby do give and devise all my houseing and Lands with the appurtenances, to my sons Timothy Phelps, William Phelps, Cornelius Phelps, Samuel Phelps, Natl. Phelps and the heirs of Jos
2 CONC eph Phelps, in the Room of their father to be equally divided into Six Equal parts provided always; and it is my will that they pay and make up to their Sisters Sarah, Hannah, Ann and Martha, my daughters or to their heirs and to 
2 CONC the heirs of my daughter Abigail deceased fourty eight pounds as money apiece and my will is that what they have already received as entered upon my book shall be reckoned as part of said sum and if my said sons and the heirs of m
2 CONC y son Joseph shall pay their sisters and their heirs above mentioned in equal proportion except that the heirs of Joseph shall pay four pounds more then an equal proportion and my son Cornelius four pounds less then an equal propo
2 CONC rtion. And my will further is that my wife shall have the free disposal of all her wearing apparel at her decease and that my grandson Samuel Tiler shall have half of that bequeathed to the heirs of my Daughter Abigail if he livet
2 CONC h with me so long as I live or till he comes to the age of eighteen years and I do hereby nominate and appoint my living wife Mary to be my executrix and my three sons William, Cornelius and Sam'l to be my executors to this my las
2 CONC t will and testament.
2 CONT  In witness whereof that his is my last will and Testament I ye sd. Timothy Phelps have hereto put my hand and seal this Second day of March Anno Domini 1716 or 1717. Timothy (his X mark and a seal] Phelps... [Witnesses: John Mans
2 CONC field and Thomas Moore.]
2 CONT  And whereas I being aged and my wife so and not knowing how long it may please God to continue my life and not knowing what debts and charge may Arise before I leave this world my will is that my sons and my daughters & their hei
2 CONC rs shall pay their equal parts and shares of my debts and charges after my decease and my daughters Sarah Hannah, Ann & Martha & and the heirs of Abigail shall have fourty six pounds apiece with what they have already have to be p
2 CONC aid as money out of my estate after my decease by the charge as above mentioned I intend that if there be any extraordianry charge so that the improvement of my estate will not maintain me this addition of my will was made and pub
2 CONC lished this 2nd day of March 1716 or 1717. Timothy [his X mark and a seal] Phelps. Witnessess: John Mansfield and Thomas Moore.'
2 CONT  [There is another statement added 28 Sep 1719 wherein the two witnesses came before Matthew Allyn, Asst., to declare that they saw Timothy Phelps sign the document with a sound mind and memory.]
2 CONT  Children [listed in the book] (all born Windsor, CT.) were:
2 CONT  I. Timothy, b. 1 Nov, bp. 8th 1663, m. Martha Crow.
2 CONT  II. Joseph, b. 27 Sep 1666, m. Sarah Hosford.
2 CONT  III. William, b. 4 Feb 1669, m. 1st Abigail Mudge, 2nd Ruth Barber.
2 CONT  IV. Cornelius, b. 26 Apr 1671, m. Sarah Mansfield.
2 CONT  V. Mary, b. 14 Aug 1673, d. 23 May 1690, aged 17 yrs.
2 CONT  VI. Samuel, b. 29 Jan 1675, m. Abigail Eno.
2 CONT  VII. Nathaniel, b. 7, bp. 13 Jan 1677, m. 1st Hannah Bissell, 2nd Abigail Pinney.
2 CONT  VIII. Sarah, b. 27 Dec 1679, m. David Marshall of Hebron, Ct.
2 CONT  IX. Abigail, b. 3 Jun 1682, m. Samuel Filer.
2 CONT  X. Hannah, b. 2, bp. 16 Aug 1684, m. Thomas Phelps.
2 CONT  XI. Anne, b. 2 Oct 1686, m. David Porter.
2 CONT  XII. Martha, b. 12 Nov 1688, m. Corporal Samuel Holcomb."
2 CONT
2 CONT  2. The book "The Phelps Family of America and their English Ancestors," comp. by Oliver Seymour Phelps of Portland, Oregon and Andrew T. Servin of Lenox, Massachusetts, 1899, pp. 108-109:
2 CONT  "Joseph Phelps, b. Windsor, Ct., 27 Sep 1666, m. Sarah Hosford, 18 Nov 1686, dau. of John and Phillury (Thrall) Hosford, she b. Windsor, Ct., 27 Sept 1666, the same day as her husband. Her father was a man of large family and con
2 CONC siderable property, leaving her at his death 100 pounds. She died probably in Hebron. Mr. Phelps settled in Windsor, where his children were all born. He owned a large amount of land in Hebron, and probably removed there late in l
2 CONC ife, about 1710, where some of his children were living. He died 30 Aug 1716, aged fifty year. His will dated 23 Aug 1716, probated Hartford probate records, Vol. 9. He appoints his wife, Sarah, executrix, and mentions 10 children
2 CONC , Joseph, Daniel, Edward, John, Abel, Ichabod, Jonathan, Mary, Sarah and Abigail. Inventory of estate 2 Oct 1716, gives age of children, Edward about 18, John 16, Mary 13, Abel - , Ichabod 9. Samuel and William Phelps were appoint
2 CONC ed guardians, while the mother was appointed guardian for Jonathan and Abigail. Children b. Windsor, Conn.:
2 CONT  I. Sarah, b. 14 Aug 1687.
2 CONT  II. Mary. b. 8 Jun 1689, m. Matthew Griswold.
2 CONT  III. Joseph, b. 16 Mar 1692, m. Susannah Eno.
2 CONT  IV. Abigail, b. 15 Oct 1693, d. young.
2 CONT  V. Edward, b. 1697, m. Deborah Bissell.
2 CONT  VI. Benoni, b. 24 Jun 1699, not mentioned in father's will, probably d. young.
2 CONT  VII. John, b. 20 Sep 1703, m. Anna Hosford, 2nd Mindwell Hosford.
2 CONT  VIII. Abel, b. 19 Feb 1705, m. Jerusha ___, and (prob.) Mary Pinnack.
2 CONT  IX. Daniel, b. 28 Mar 1707, m. Sarah.
2 CONT  X. Ichabod, b. 3 Apr 1708, m. Martha Tillotson.
2 CONT  XI. Jonathan, b. 1710.
2 CONT  XII. Abigail, b. Dec. 1714."
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT : Joseph Phelps<ref name="TAG37"/>
2 CONT : Joseph Phelps was born 27 SEP 1666 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut.<ref name="NEHGR5">NEHGR Vol 5 (1851) page 230</ref>  It is not a typo that Joseph Phelps was born on the exact date of his wife's birthday - they were born on th
2 CONC e same day at Windsor, Connecticut. <ref name="PhelpsFam">''The Phelps Family of America and Their English Ancestors: with copies of wills, deeds, letters, and other interesting papers, coats of arms and valuable records'', by Phe
2 CONC lps and Servin, Vol 1 (1899), pages 108-109</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriages and Children ===: Joseph Phelps married Sarah Hosford 18 NOV 1686 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut<ref name="PhelpsFam"/><ref name="NEHGR5"/> All of his children were born at Windsor, Connecticut.<ref name="PhelpsFam"/
2 CONC >
2 CONT
2 CONT : Husband:  [[Phelps-728|Joseph Phelps]]
2 CONT : Wife:  [[Hosford-14|Sarah Hosford]] ::  Ten Children Named in his will:<ref name="PhelpsFam"/>
2 CONT #  Sarah, born 14 Aug 1687
2 CONT #  Mary, born 8 June 1689, m. Matthew Griswold
2 CONT # Joseph, born 16 Mar 1692, m. Susannah Eno
2 CONT # Edward, born 1697, m. Deborah Bissell
2 CONT #  John, born 20 Sept 1703, m. 1st Anna Hosford; 2nd Mindwell Hosford# Abel, born 19 Feb 1705, m. 1st Jerusha ___; 2nd probably Mary Pinnack
2 CONT # Daniel, born 28 Mar 1707, m. Sarah ___#  [[Phelps-735|Ichabod Phelps]], born 3 April 1708, m. Martha Tillotson :::   Not named in his will: :::   Abigail (first of the name) born 15 Oct 1693 - died young  :::   Benoni -  probabl
2 CONC y died young : Sarah (Hosford) Phelps died sometime between the birth of her last child, Ichabod, 3 April 1708, and the marriage of Joseph Phelps to his second wife 22 Jan 1709.<ref name="TAG37"/> : Joseph Phelps married second, a
2 CONC t Windsor, 22 Feb 1709/10, Sarah Gillett, born at Windsor 3 Jan 1673/4, daughter of Cornelius and Priscilla(Kelsey) Gillett.<ref name="TAG37"/> It was this second Sarah who wasthe widow of Joseph Phelps when he died in 1716.<ref n
2 CONC ame="TAG37"/> The older children were assigned to guardians Samuel and William Phelps, but their mother Sarah was appointed guardian for the two youngest, her own children.<ref name="PhelpsFam"/>
2 CONT
2 CONT #  Jonathan Phelps born 1710
2 CONT #  Abigail (second of the name) Phelps born Dec 1714
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death ===: Joseph Phelps died 30 AUG 1716, Windsor, Connecticut<ref name="TAG37">''Early Connecticut Items: Phelps, Hosford, Gillett, Case, Hillyer, Palmer'', by George E. McCracken, Ph.D., F.A.S.G., TAG Vol 37 (1961), pages 2
2 CONC 6-27</ref><ref name="NEHGR5"/>
2 CONT
