1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anne Sterling, dau. of William Sterling and Anne Nichols (widow of John Neale, and 3rd wife of William Sterling), was born Mar. 14, 1684 in Haverhill, Essex Co., Massachusetts. She was the only child of this marria
2 CONC ge. She married with SAMUEL WATERS, probably in Lyme, Conn., around 1702. There is no record of this marriage, and thus no proof that Anne, the wife of Samuel Waters, was in fact Anne Sterling. But thereis,in the Hoyt Genealogy, a
2 CONC  section that is called " The Journal of Aaron Haight" in which journal Aaron claimed that his wife is the granddaughter of Samuel Waters and her grandmother was Anne Sterling. There is also the fact that of one of Anne and Samuel
2 CONC 's grandchildren was named Sterling Waters, obviously a family name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: (known): Samuel (1719-1782) and Adam (1720-1804).
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne and Samuel moved from Lyme to Saybrook, Conn., before 1706, and their first three children were born there. By ate 1708, they bought land in Hebron, Conn. and were living there before 1710. All the rest of their children were
2 CONC  born in Hebron. Samuel died in Hebron in early 1743. There is no record of the death of Anne, but she was alive in July 1749, when she appeared in court in Colchester. There is no reason to believe she moved from Hebron, or that 
2 CONC she was not buried there after her death, but there is no gravestone in this cemetery for her, and no record of her burial there.
2 CONT
2 CONT *FInd a grave
