1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Mayflower Families Vol. 17 p. 86 provides that her LNAB is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Verde (1668 Lebanon, New London, Connecticut - 23 FEB 1709 Lebanon, New London, Connecticut). Names of parents have not been recovered.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Thomas Hunt Sr. about 1690[1][2][3].
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was born 23 Jan 1663 in Northampton, Hamshire, Massachusetts[4] the first child of Deacon Jonathan Hunt and his wife Clemence (Hosmer) Hunt.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is recorded as a church member in Lebanon, Connecticut 27 Nov 1700[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Include:
2 CONT
2 CONT Clemence Hunt b. 5 Feb 1690 Lebanon – 1760 m. Samuel Wadsworth 1665–1759
2 CONT Elizabeth Hunt (20 Oct 1692 Lebanon – 1770) married Silas Owen
2 CONT Mary Hunt b. 17 Nov 1694 Lebanon – 1764
2 CONT Thomas Hunt Jr 1697–1735
2 CONT Jonathan Hunt 1699–
2 CONT Anna Hunt 1702–1777
2 CONT Hannah Hunt 3 Oct 1702 Lebanon – 2 Apr 1781 married William Summer
2 CONT Gideon Hunt (1705 Lebanon – 26 Jun 1786 Lebanon) m. (1) Rebecka Ordway, (2) Abigail Clover
2 CONT Jonathan Hunt I (1708 Lebanon – 18 Aug 1788 Columbia County, New York) married Ruth Cushman
2 CONT Death[6]:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Hunt
2 CONT Death Date 23 Feb 1708/9
2 CONT Death Place Lebanon, Connecticut
2 CONT Spouse Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT
