2 CONT Clemence Hunt (5 Feb 1690 Lebanon Twp, New London, Connecticut[5] – 1760) m. Samuel Wadsworth 1665–1759
2 CONT Elizabeth Hunt, (20 Oct 1692 Lebanon Twp, New London, Connecticut[6] - ) apparently died young as another child named Elizabeth was born 18 Mar 1700.
2 CONT Mary Hunt (17 Nov 1694 Lebanon Twp, New London, Connecticut[7] – 1764)
2 CONT Thomas Hunt Jr (08 Apr 1697 Lebanon Twp, New London, Connecticut[8] –1735)
2 CONT Jonathan Hunt 1699–
2 CONT Elizabeth Hunt (18 Mar 1700 Lebanon Twp, New London, Connecticut[9] – 1770 ) married Silas Owen
2 CONT Anna Hunt 1702–1777
2 CONT Hannah Hunt (3 Oct 1702 Lebanon Twp, New London, Connecticut[10] – 2 Apr 1781) married William Summer
2 CONT Gideon Hunt (1705 Lebanon – 26 Jun 1786 Lebanon[11]) m. (1) Rebecka Ordway, (2) Abigail Clover
2 CONT Jonathan Hunt I (1708 Lebanon – 18 Aug 1788 Columbia County, New York) married Ruth Cushman
2 CONT His will was written on 2 August 1736, Thomas Hunt will found in State Library in Hartford, CT by Stephen & Kelly Sanwald, also on CS: Reel; #567, LDS # 0003904, data compiled by Mrs. Lindy Brunkhorst Olewine, genealogist, Lebanon
2 CONC  Historical Society on 5 Jan 2013.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died either 4 Apr or 19 Apr 1746 in Hebron, Connecticut at age 84[12]. Another source shows DOD for Thomas Hunt as 08 May 1746[13]
2 CONT
2 CONT DOD discrepancy: One Connecticut record list his death as 19 Apr 1746 while others shows 4 Apr 1746. FAG shows his death as 4 Apr 1746. The headstone is completely unreadable so that is no verification which date is correct. Hale 
2 CONC Headstone Inscriptions[14] also shows 4 Apr 1746.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: [15], Thomas Hunt, Andover Road Cemetery in Hebron, Tolland County, Connecticut, USA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate: Will probated 1 July 1746 Hebron, CT but became part of Colchester’s probate records. Thomas left the farm of 160 acres to son Jonathan and remainder to other children and grandchildren. He is buried in the Old Cemetery i
2 CONC n Hebron.
2 CONT
2 CONT
