2 CONC and, in Hartford in 1651, Northampton. Mass., 1666, Westfield 1668-9. He married three times. Dorothy Ford was daughter of Thomas Ford, Gentleman', and Dorothy his wife, of England, and one of the first and most prominent settlers
2 CONC  of Hartford. Mr. Phelps settled in Westfield, Mass., where he died 6 Oct., 1689, in his 40th year. His widow, Dorothy, m. for 2nd husband a Mr. Root.[2] Children, b. Westfield. Mass.:
