1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT WikiTree contributors, "Temperance (Denslow) Buckland (abt.1620-abt.1681)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Denslow-128 : accessed 15 August 2024).
2 CONT
2 CONT Temperance (Denslow) Buckland immigrated to New England as a child during the Puritan Great Migration (1621-1640).
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth and Migration
2 CONT
2 CONT Temperance Denslow was born by about 1620,  probably in England; daughter of Nicholas Denslow and his wife Elizabeth (surname unknown).
2 CONT
2 CONT The family migrated to New England in 1632, residing at Dorchester, then Windsor, Connecticut by 1636.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Temperance married Thomas Buckland by about 1638. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Timothy was born March 10, 1638; married Abigail Vore, daughter of Richard Vore, at Windsor on March 27, 1662.
2 CONT # Elizabeth was born February 21, 1640/1. She married (1st) Edward Adams at Windsor on May 25, 1660; and (2nd) James Miles aka "Mielles" by 1686.
2 CONT # Temperance was born November 27, 1642; married John Ponder at Hartford on June 26, 1668.
2 CONT # Mary was born October 2, 1644. She had the measles and was treated by John Winthrop Jr., but died at Windsor on December 13, 1657.
2 CONT # Nicholas was born February 21, 1646/7. He married (1st) Martha Wakefield at Windsor on April 14 or October 21, 1668; married (2nd) Elizabeth Drake at Windsor on March 3, 1685/6; married (3rd) Hannah (Smith) (Trumbull) Strong on 
2 CONC June 16, 1698. Hannah was the daughter of Hugh Smith of Rowley, and widow of J.oseph Trumbull and John Strong.
2 CONT # Sarah was born March 24, 1648/9. She married John Phelps by 1675.
2 CONT # Thomas was born February 2, 1650/1 (annotated "Dead"). He married Hannah Cook at Windsor on October 21,1675. She was the daughter of Nathaniel Cook.
2 CONT # Hannah was born September 18, 1654 (annotated "Dead"). She married Joshua Wells at Windsor on August 11, 1681.
2 CONT # Her husband, Thomas Buckland, died at Windsor on May 28, 1662. The inventory of the estate was taken June 20, 1662, and totaled L346, 12s, and 4d; of which L232 was real estate. He had divided his estate, giving generously to ea
2 CONC ch child, to leave his widow Temperance L118
2 CONT
2 CONT Temperance (Denslow) Buckland died at Windsor on July 26, 1681. In her will she bequeathed her house, homelot, orchard, two acres of pasture land, and six acres in the Great Meadow to her son Nicholas; her household goods went to 
2 CONC her youngest daughter Hannah.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Temperance died, there was a family dispute over the will of her husband Thomas Buckland with Timothy Buckland, Joshua Willes, James Mielles, and John Phelps, saying that it should have construed to mean that the widow recei
2 CONC ved the L118 only for her lifetime. On May 17, 1686, Nicholas Buckland responded, arguing that it would be contrary to law for the General Court to reconsider the case. On May 19, 1686 the court found in favor of Nicholas Buckland
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT #Unless otherwise cited, this biography is based on "Great Migration Begins" and "Great Migration." https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Denslow-128
2 CONT ## The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633, Volumes I-III. (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2010), (Originally Published as: New England Historic Genealogi
2 CONC cal Society. Robert Charles Anderson, The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633, Volumes I-III, 3 vols., 1995). Sketch of Nicholas Denslow. p. 528 to < [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/great-migra
2 CONC tion-begins-immigrants-to-ne-1620-1633-vols-i-iii/image?pageName=528&volumeId=12107&rId=23894887 AmericanAncestors] >
2 CONT ## Great Migration 1634-1635, A-B. (Online database. AmericanAncestors.org. New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2008.) Originally published as: The Great Migration, Immigrants to New England, 1634-1635, Volume 1, A-B, by Ro
2 CONC bert Charles Anderson, George F. Sanborn, Jr., and Melinde Lutz Sanborn. Boston: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1999. Sketch of Thomas Buckland. pp. 450 - 453.link for subscribers$
2 CONT # removed birth data of October 02, 1609 Of Allington, , Eng, Dorset, England, United Kingdom as unsourced.
