1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Buckland was born on February 2, 1650 in Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut Colony;[1][2] the son of Thomas Buckland and his wife Temperance (Denslow) Buckland. He married Hannah Cook at Windslow on Octob
2 CONC er 21, 1675 (daughter of Nathaniel Cook.)[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on May 28, 1676 in Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut, British Colonial America.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Buckland-2602
2 CONT
2 CONT Buckland-2602 created 6 Aug 2013 | Last modified 26 Jul 2021
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Thomas Buckland (1650 - 1676)===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Buckland
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 2 Feb 1650 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Thomas Buckland and Temperance (Denslow) Buckland
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Timothy Buckland, Elizabeth (Buckland) Miles, Temperance Buckland, Mary Buckland, Nicholas Buckland, Sarah (Buckland) Phelps and Hannah Buckland
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Hannah (Cook) Baker — married 21 Oct 1675 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT [children unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 28 May 1676 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F741-RWB : 7 January 2020), Thomas Buckland, 1650.
2 CONT ↑ Shields, Herb, Email dated Wednesday, November 20, 2002 with excerpts from "A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records, 1650 to 1663," "Connecticut Puritan Settlers, 1633-1845," and "First Settlers of the Colony."
2 CONT ↑ Great Migration 1634-1635, A-B. (Online database. AmericanAncestors.org. New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2008.) Originally published as: The Great Migration, Immigrants to New England, 1634-1635, Volume 1, A-B, by Rob
2 CONC ert Charles Anderson, George F. Sanborn, Jr., and Melinde Lutz Sanborn. Boston: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1999. Sketch of Thomas Buckland Sr.subscription needed
2 CONT ↑ Connecticut Vital Records, Prior to 1850, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QP3M-6QVZ : 21 September 2019), Thomas Buckland, ; citing Death, , Compiled by Lucius A. and Lucius B. Barbour, housed at State Libr
2 CONC ary, Hartford, Connecticut; FHL microfilm 008272223.
