1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Wikitree: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Gunn-13 Deborah (Gunn) Thrall (1641–1694)]
2 CONT * "Deborah Gunn Thrall is mentioned in Old Windsor records. Her father moved in 1665, to Westfield, Mass. and became active in the Westfield Parish.
2 CONT * "Thomas Gunn's daughters married and remained in Windsor. The oldest of the three children, Deborah, married Timothy Thrall on the 10th of November, 1659, and they had eleven children, two of whom died in infancy. The rest marri
2 CONC ed and they too remained in Windsor, or in nearby Simsbury. Upon his departure to Westfield, Thomas deeded property, including his home lot, to Timothy and Deborah. In later Windsor records their home is referred to as the Thrall 
2 CONC mansion house, so it may have been a substantial structure. Timothy was the only son of William Thrall, one of the founders of Windsor and a participant in the Pequot War. He died in June, 1697, and is said to have left “a good es
2 CONC tate.” Deborah died three years earlier, in January of 1694/95. She was only 53 years old."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/74978354/deborah-thrall
2 CONT
