3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Note: DANIEL CLARK of Colchester, Connecticut; b. 5th April, 1654; bapt. 10th April, 1654, in Windsor, Connecticut; after reaching manhood he located elsewhere but was temporarily in Hartford in 1675, where he had 
2 CONC a passage at arms with Mayor Treat and got fined for contempt of court which was remitted and peace restored on the joint petition of his father and Mayor Treat; he later lived in Hartford where he was a locksmith until 1710, when
2 CONC  he removed to Colchester, Connecticut, where he died before 1746; not as prominent as his father, yet his name frequently occurs in the Colonial records of Connecticut, and it is related that he served in one Indian [p.100] campa
2 CONC ign and was enlisted in the Louisburg Expedition ( The Louisbourg Expedition (1757) was a failed British attempt to capture the French Fortress of Louisbourg on Île Royale during the Seven Years' War.) just prior to his death; m. 
2 CONC in 1678, Hannah PRATT, dau. of Daniel and Hannah PRATT of Hartford; the former was a son of first John PRATT of Hartford and gd. son of Rev. William PRATT of Hertfordshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From "A CATALOGUE OF THE NAMES OF THE EARLY PURITAN SETTLERS OF THE COLONY CONNECTICUT"
2 CONT
2 CONT CLARK, DANIEL, Jun., son of Hon. Daniel Clark, of Windsor, at a meeting of the council in Hartford, March 10, 1675-6, was convicted for notorious, reproachful, contemptuous speeches, and threatening Mayor Treat; fined him £20, and
2 CONC  committed him to prison during the pleasure of the council. And at a meeting of the council, Jan. 2, 1676(7,) Capt. Daniel Clark appeared and requested "that his son's fine" might be remitted,and statedit would be a great encoura
2 CONC gement for him to settle " here," in the improvement of his trade and art, for the benefit of the country, &c. Mayor Treat also interceded for him, and stated Daniel's confession, reformation, &c. The council remitted the fine, ex
2 CONC pecting his return and settlement in attendance of his art and trade. (See Meeting of the Council, Jan. 2, 1676, and March 10,1675-6.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Daniel Clark was father of Daniel Clark, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Clark, Jr. was father of Nathaniel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Clarke was father of Nathaniel Clark Jr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Clark Jr. was father of Arunah .
2 CONT
2 CONT Arunah Clark was father of Willis G. Clark.
2 CONT
2 CONT Willis G. Clark was father of Volney B. Clark.
2 CONT
2 CONT Volney B. Clark was father of Willis R. Clark.
2 CONT
2 CONT Willis R. Clark was father of Robert H. Clark, who married Fanny Jean Berry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert H. Clark was father of Yvonne Charlotte Clark, who married Hughbert Blake-Thomas. Robert H. Clark was also step-father of Myrle (Eberle) Clark and Mable (Eberle) (Stuckey) Clark
2 CONT
2 CONT Hughbert and Yvonne (Clark) Blake-Thomas were parents of Hugh and David Blake-Thomas.
2 CONT ______________________________
2 CONT
