1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (III) Lieutenant Benjamin Lyman, fourth son of Ensign John and Dorcas (Plumb) Lyman, was born in Northampton, Massachusetts, August 10, 1674, and died there October 14, 1723. He was an enterprising and successful m
2 CONC an, and at the time of his death was owner of five hundred acres of land near Granville, Massachusetts. His estate free of debt was appraised at 1147 pounds. He also engaged in trade, and his sbop and goods were appraised at 198 p
2 CONC ounds. He was an extensive farmer and fatted cattle in the stall. He owned a negro slave named Nancy, who was appraised at 40 pounds. October 27, 1698, Lieutenant Benjamin Lyman married Thankful Pomeroy, daughter of Deacon Medad P
2 CONC omeroy, and granddaughter of Eltweld Pomeroy, who came from Devonshire. England, in 1630, and lived first in Dorchester. Massachusetts. then in Windsor, Connecticut, and still later in Northampton, Massachusetts, where he died in 
2 CONC 1673. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Lyman and Thankful Pomeroy had twelve children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. '''Joseph''', born August 22, 1699, died 1764; married Abigail Lewis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Benjamin, born December 19, 1701, died in infancy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Benjamin, born January 2, 1703; settled in Easthampton, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Aaron, born April 1, 1705; settled in Belchertown, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Eunice, born in May, 1707, died in June, 1720. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Hannah, born July 14, 1709, died in 1794; married Nathaniel Dwight, of Belchertown, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Caleb, born August 8, 1711, and lived in Boston; never married. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Susannah, born July 18, 1713; married Baxter, of Boston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. William, born December 12, 1715. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Daniel, born April 18, 1718; graduated from Yale College, in 1745; became a prominent lawyer and judge in New Haven. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. Elihu, born July 10, 1720; graduated from Yale College, 1745; afterward became an officer of the French army; never married. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 12. Medad, born March 20, 1722; was a tavern keeper in New Haven. Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliographic information:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Title	Genealogical and Personal Memoirs Relating to the Families of Boston and Eastern Massachusetts, Volume 2
2 CONT * Genealogical and Personal Memoirs Relating to the Families of Boston and Eastern Massachusetts, William Richard Cutter
2 CONT * Editor	William Richard Cutter
2 CONT * Publisher	Lewis historical Publishing Company, 1908
2 CONT * Original from	Harvard University
2 CONT * Digitized	Sep 20, 2006
2 CONT * http://books.google.com/books?id=kFoLBC2TwFYC&pg=PA726&lpg=PA726&dq=Joseph+Lyman+1699+%22Benjamin+Lyman%22+Thankful&source=bl&ots=7ZkuYvIFvL&sig=_x68GbYw7UxWIfD2J4fBW5ofzBU&hl=en&sa=X&ei=zSr_U92eH8SbjAKioIDgCg&ved=0CDsQ6AEwAw#v=
2 CONC onepage&q=Joseph%20Lyman%201699%20%22Benjamin%20Lyman%22%20Thankful&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 '''Joseph Lyman'''4, Benjamin3, John2, Richard1, 1699-1763, b. 1699; m. Abigail Lewis of Farmington, Ct., who was b. in 1701. He remained in Northampton where he d. March 30, 1763, thirteen years before the death of his wife on 
2 CONC whose tombstone are inscribed these words:
2 CONT
2 CONT The grave is that home of man Where dwells the multitude. Northampton, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, Fifth Generation: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 1 Eunice, b. May 30, 1723; m. Capt. Samuel Clark of Northampton.
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 2 Mercy, b. Sept. 7, 1729; m. Flon. Joseph Hawley, the patriot of the Revolution, who first uttered the sentiment, "We must fight," afterwards quoted by Patrick Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 3 Joseph, b. May 4, 1731.
2 CONT
2 CONT 17 4 Eleanor, b. May I8, 1732; d. in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 5 Elisha, b. June 22, 1734.
2 CONT
2 CONT 19 6 Eleanor, b. Sept. 24, 1737; m. Capt. Oliver Lyman, of Vt. Ch.6th Gen.:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Erastus, b. Feb. 9, 1761, who m. Abigail Bracket. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Mary, b., 1765; m. Lynde Lord, of Litchfield, Ct., Jan. 30, 1786. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Joseph, b. Oct. 22, 1767.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliographic information:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Title	Genealogy of the Lyman Family in Great Britain & America: The Ancestors & Descendants of Richard Lyman, from High Ongar in England, 1631
2 CONT * Author	Lyman Coleman
2 CONT * Publisher	J. Munsell, 1872
2 CONT * Original from	the University of Wisconsin - Madison
2 CONT * Digitized	Jun 13, 2007
2 CONT * Length	533 pages
2 CONT * Page 392
2 CONT * https://books.google.com/books?id=IR43AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA392&lpg=PA392&dq=Mercy+Lyman+1729&source=bl&ots=TISL-d_C2K&sig=cUrx4VhrC5cDTJAOYJMxkE4gndU&hl=en&sa=X&ei=IxrOVLasF5XgoATMooHwBw&ved=0CD4Q6AEwBw#v=onepage&q=Mercy%20Lyman%201729
2 CONC &f=false
