2 CONT
2 CONT '''LYMAN, JOSEPH''' Ancestor #: A072609 
2 CONT
2 CONT Service:  MASSACHUSETTS
2 CONT
2 CONT Rank: CAPTAIN
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 5-4-1731    NORTHAMPTON HAMPSHIRE CO MASSACHUSETTS
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 10-21-1804     NORTHAMPTON HAMPSHIRE CO MASSACHUSETTS
2 CONT
2 CONT Service Description:  1) COLS JONATHAN WARD,BENJ R WOODBRIDGE
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence 1) City: NORTHAMPTON - County: HAMPSHIRE CO - State: MASSACHUSETTS
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Number 1) Name MARY SHELDON  
2 CONT
2 CONT http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A072609
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Joseph Lyman4, Benjamin3, John2, Richard1, 1699-1763, b. 1699; m. Abigail Lewis of Farmington, Ct., who was b. in 1701. He remained in Northampton where he d. March 30, 1763, thirteen years before the death of his wife on whose 
2 CONC tombstone are inscribed these words:
2 CONT
2 CONT The grave is that home of man
2 CONT
2 CONT Where dwells the multitude.
2 CONT
2 CONT Northampton, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, Fifth Generation:
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 1 Eunice, b. May 30, 1723; m. Capt. Samuel Clark of Northampton.
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 2 Mercy, b. Sept. 7, 1729; m. Flon. Joseph Hawley, the patriot of the Revolution, who first uttered the sentiment, "We must fight," afterwards quoted by Patrick Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 3 '''Joseph''', b. May 4, 1731.
2 CONT
2 CONT 17 4 Eleanor, b. May I8, 1732; d. in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 5 Elisha, b. June 22, 1734.
2 CONT
2 CONT 19 6 Eleanor, b. Sept. 24, 1737; m. Capt. Oliver Lyman, of Vt. Ch.6th Gen.:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Erastus, b. Feb. 9, 1761, who m. Abigail Bracket.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Mary, b., 1765; m. Lynde Lord, of Litchfield, Ct., Jan. 30, 1786. (NOTE: Daughter of Joseph, above. -- Jessica German)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Joseph, b. Oct. 22, 1767.
2 CONT
