1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 2 Joseph Lyman4, Benjamin3, John2, Richard1, 1699-1763, b. 1699; m. Abigail Lewis of Farmington, Ct., who was b. in 1701. He remained in Northampton where he d. March 30, 1763, thirteen years before the death of hi
2 CONC s wife on whose tombstone are inscribed these words:
2 CONT
2 CONT The grave is that home of man Where dwells the multitude. Northampton, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, Fifth Generation:
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 1 Eunice, b. May 30, 1723; m. Capt. Samuel Clark of Northampton.
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 2 Mercy, b. Sept. 7, 1729; m. Flon. Joseph Hawley, the patriot of the Revolution, who first uttered the sentiment, "We must fight," afterwards quoted by Patrick Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 3 Joseph, b. May 4, 1731.
2 CONT
2 CONT 17 4 Eleanor, b. May I8, 1732; d. in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 5 '''Elisha''', b. June 22, 1734.
2 CONT
2 CONT 19 6 Eleanor, b. Sept. 24, 1737; m. Capt. Oliver Lyman, of Vt. Ch.6th Gen.:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Erastus, b. Feb. 9, 1761, who m. Abigail Bracket.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Mary, b., 1765; m. Lynde Lord, of Litchfield, Ct., Jan. 30, 1786.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Joseph, b. Oct. 22, 1767.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliographic information:
2 CONT
2 CONT *     Title Genealogy of the Lyman Family in Great Britain & America: The Ancestors & Descendants of Richard Lyman, from High Ongar in England, 1631
2 CONT *     Author Lyman Coleman
2 CONT *     Publisher J. Munsell, 1872
2 CONT *     Original from the University of Wisconsin - Madison
2 CONT *     Digitized Jun 13, 2007
2 CONT *     Length 533 pages
2 CONT *     Page 392
2 CONT *     https://books.google.com/books?id=IR43AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA392&lpg=PA392&dq=Mercy+Lyman+1729&source=bl&ots=TISL-d_C2K&sig=cUrx4VhrC5cDTJAOYJMxkE4gndU&hl=en&sa=X&ei=IxrOVLasF5XgoATMooHwBw&ved=0CD4Q6AEwBw#v=onepage&q=Mercy%20Lyman%20
2 CONC 1729&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 '''Elisha Lyman''', son of Joseph, and grandson of Benjamin, the ancestor of this branch, was b. June 22, 1734,  m. Abigail Janes ; d. Aug. 13, 1798. Northampton, Mass. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, Sixth Generation. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 96 1 Elisha, b. April 25, 1765, d. early. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 97 2 Micah Jones, b. Oct. 17, 1767, at Northampton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 98 3 Elisha, b. Jan. 26, 1770, Champlain, N.Y. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 99 4 Lewis, b. June 8, 1772 ; m. Mary Parrot Paine, b. at Troy, Aug. 9, 1815. He d. March 20, 1852, leaving no  children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 101 5 Theodore, b. Nov. 3, 1784. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 102 6 Henry, b. July 23, 1788 ; d. Sept. 20, 1809, at Burlington, Vt., though a resident of Montreal, unmarried. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 103 7 Lydia, b. Jan. 7, 1775; m. Samuel Hedge; d. in Montreal, in 185... ., . 
2 CONT
2 CONT 104 8 Susannah, b. Feb. 10, 1780 ; m. Roswell Corse, resides in Montreal; d. in 1852, leaving two daughters, viz:  ''Ch. 7th Gen''. : 1 Susan, m. Dr. Arthur Fisher. 2 Mary, m. Henry Lyman, son of Elisha of the 6th Gen., all of Mon
2 CONC treal. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 107 9 Abigail, b. Dec. 30, 1782; d. Oct. 25, 1806. 
2 CONT
