1 NAME Penelope /Thrall/
2 GIVN Penelope
2 SURN Thrall
2 _MARNM Welch
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1695
2 PLAC Rehoboth, Bristol, Massachusetts, United States
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 JUL 1756
2 ADDR
3 CITY Colchester
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He had one wife: Mary Kingsbury and two children: Mary and James.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Welch Surname: Welch Given Name: James Sex: M Birth: 27 Jul 1692 in Rehoboth, Bristol, Massachusetts Death: 6 Jul 1756 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Gordon Alan Morris & Thomas J. & Dixie Prittle, (1994) "The Descendants of William Sabin of Rehoboth, Massachusetts" pp. 26-27
2 CONT
2 CONT Harriet W. Hodge (1991) "Mayflower Families Through Five Generations" Vol. 5, pp. 100-101 James Welch m. late in life, ca. 1740, Mary Kingsbury who died while living at Bolton. The distribution of her father's estate 3 Jun 1777 in
2 CONC cluded a share to dau. Mary, without surname. On 2 Sep. 1768 James Welch and wife Mary of Bolton, CT quit claimed to her brother Ebenezer Kingsbury of Plainfield for her share of her brother Nathaniel Kingbury's estate. James Welc
2 CONC h, mason, of Voluntown, "with wife Mary releasing her dower, sold 100 acres, being for #8 laid out to the said James Welch in the north end of Voluntown. On 4 Jul 1744 James Welch "of Plainfield" (evidently a temporary residence) 
2 CONC bought 64 acres with "mansion house" in Bolton, and continued to acquire land after moving there. James was named in the will of his brother Ebenezer 25 Jan 1759. Administration of the estate of James Welch of Bolton, CT was grant
2 CONC ed 21 Nov 1770 to the widow Mary, with James Thrall, her son-in-law, as surety. Distribution of the estate was made 26 Mar 1783: a double share to James Welch the eldest and only son, a single share to Mary Thrall the only daughte
2 CONC r, with dower or "thirds" to the widow Mary. Note: The will of Ebenezer Welch proves that James Welch s/o March (Sabin) Welch, was living in 1759. The Mayflower Society formerly accepted, as a son, a different James Welch who died
2 CONC  at Colchester in 1756. That identification has been disproved and the Society closed the line, but two published genealogies continue to mislead researchers. Change Date: 11 Dec 2011 at 13:34:35
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: James Welch b: ABT 1655 Mother: Mercy Sabin b: 8 Mar 1666/1667 in Rehoboth, Bristol, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Mary Kingsbury b: 29 Feb 1719/20 in Plainfield, Windham, Connecticut Married: ABT 1740 Children Has No Children Mary Welch b: ABT 1743 Has No Children James Welch b: ABT 1745
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=richardsoni&id=I1904
2 CONT
