1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Captain Ezekiel Humphrey''' served in the 10th Company of the First Regiment of the Connecticut Militia during the French Indian War.  That war (1754–1763) was the North American theater of the worldwide Seven Y
2 CONC ears' War. The war was fought between the colonies of British America and New France, with both sides supported by military units from their parent countries of Great Britain and France, as well as Native American allies.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Humphrey&GSfn=Ezekiel&GSiman=1&GSob=n&GRid=36016806&df=all& Ezekiel Humphrey @ find a grave]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Captain Ezekial was member of the General Assembly from Simsbury, 1777. He died in 1795 at the age of 75. He was 6 feet, 4 inches, and all his sons were at least 6 feet 2 inches. Known for physical & mental stamina & strength, he 
2 CONC moved to West Simsbury, now called Canton, and owned most of the land in what is now known as Collinsville. His son George was executor of his large estate.
