1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Resided in Whortleberry Hill section of Northington Society until c1789 when he built what is considered the oldest house in Collinsville section of Canton.  In 1792, he and his brother, George, erected an iron for
2 CONC ge on the east branch of the Farmington River, severely damaged by the "Jefferson" flood of 1801, and then swept away by the great flood of 1804.  A grist and sawmill was erected afterward until being removed in 1827 for the build
2 CONC ing of the Collins Company manufacturing facilities.
