1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bio
2 CONT Seriah Stratton's name appears on the Payroll for Capt. Michael Bowyer's Company of the 12th Virginia Command by Col. James Wood, Esq. Commencing from 6th March 1777 and terminating the 30th of June. He was a sergeant and discharg
2 CONC ed April 20, 1777.
2 CONT
2 CONT His revolutionary war application matches his birth record born in Simsbury and died 1819.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Serajah Stratton (1740 - abt. 1819) 
2 CONT Son of Seraiah Stratton and Eunice (Case) Stratton
2 CONT Brother of Martin Stratton
2 CONT [spouse%28s%29 unknown]
2 CONT Father of Eunice (Stratton) Fisher
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT From ''A Book of Strattons : being a collection of Stratton records from England and Scotland, and a genea …'' Page 232.  < [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/61157/images/46155_b289774-00276 AncestryImage] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children - births recorded in Simsbury 
2 CONT 4 Martin3, b. 1730
2 CONT 5 Eunice3, b. July 27, 1733; m. 1st, Dudley Higley, who died in 1771; 2d, Nathaniel Messenger.
2 CONT 6 Serajah3, b. July 7, 1740; … (Further information concerning him is much desired.) Named his daughter after his mom.
2 CONT
