2 CONT *SPENCER -  Four brothers named Spencer were living in New England in 1648, namely - Michael, Jared, Thomas and '''William'''. They were legatees of Sir Richard Spencer, of London, England, evidently their uncle. Michael settled f
2 CONC irst in Cambridge, then in Lynn, and owned land also on the Connecticut river. '''William settled in Cambridge and then went to Hartford, Connecticut'''. Thomas lived in Cambridge and Hartford.
2 CONT *(I) Ensign Jared Spencer, son of Gerrard or Jerrard Spencer, was born in Stotfold, England, and baptized April 28, 1614. He came to New England in 1632 and was made a freeman of the Massachusetts Bay Colony,    . . . . .   He die
2 CONC d in 1685. His will was dated September 17, 1683, and proved in 1685. He married Hannah ___, Children: John, born at Lynn in 1638; Hannah, 1640; Alice, 1641; Mehitable, 1642; Thomas, about 1650,; Samuel, mentioned below; William; 
2 CONC Nathaniel; Rebecca, married (first) John Kennard, and (second) John Tanner; Ruth, married Joseph Clark; Timothy.
2 CONT *____________________
