1 OCCU Farmer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.holcombegenealogy.com/g0/p41.htm#i2041
2 CONT
2 CONT John Case was born on 22 August 1694 at Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT.4,5,6 He was the son of John Case and Sarah Holcombe. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Case married Abigail Humphrey, daughter of Lt. Samuel Humphrey and Mary Mills, on 24 January 1716/17 at Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT.7 John Case died on 2 December 1752 at Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT, at age 58. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >(Charles Case) "After his marriage, John, following in the footsteps of his father and grandfather, engaged in farming his land throughout his life. Like them, he performed his civic duties, but he did not seek positions in publi
2 CONC c life, preferring to devote himself tohis family and his farm."
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Case and Abigail Humphrey
2 CONT # Capt. John Case+ b. 19 Feb 1718, d. 24 May 1776
2 CONT # Noah Case+ b. 4 Oct 1720, d. 17 Dec 1797
2 CONT # Capt. Charles Case+ b. 1 Jul 1723, d. 17 Oct 1808
2 CONT # Abigail Case b. 10 Sep 1725, d. 28 Aug 1779
2 CONT # Mary Case+ b. 29 Dec 1727, d. Sep 1784
2 CONT # Lucy Case+ b. 17 Oct 1732, d. 1805
2 CONT # Martha Case+ b. 31 Jul 1735, d. 29 Mar 1809
2 CONT # Capt. Job Case+ b. 3 Jun 1737, d. 6 May 1798
2 CONT # Lydia Case+ b. 1 Sep 1741, d. 25 Aug 1796
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Case, IV married Abagail Humphrey on 24 January 1716/17 at Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut.  
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Abigail had nine children who were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Noah who married Miriam Holcomb, John who married Sarah Barber, Charles who married Phebe ?, Abigail who married Jonathan Case (who was her cousin - the son of Jonathan and Mary Beman), Mary (don't know much about her), Lucy who m
2 CONC arried William Wilcox, Martha who married Thomas Barber, Job who married Joanna Wilcox and Lydia who married Jonathan Pinney.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Case was buried in the Simsbury Cemetery (also known as Hopmeadow Cemetery), Simsbury, Hartford County, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tombstone Inscription:
2 CONT In Memory I’d
2 CONT Mr. John Case Who
2 CONT Died the 2nd of De
2 CONT cember 1752
2 CONT Aetage 58 years 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Epitaph)
2 CONT
