1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *[https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/49039903/joseph-case '''Joseph Case, Jr - Find A Grave''' - MEMORIAL ID] - 49039903
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Case, Jr., s. of Joseph Case and Anna Eno, b. Feb. 2, 1699/700 at Simsbury, Conn. He d. at Simsbury Mar. 12, 1782, Æ 83.
2 CONT
2 CONT In circa 1722, Joseph m. Hannah Humphrey, dau. of Dea. John Humphrey and Sarah Pettibone, b. Mar. 17, 1699/700 at Simsbury. She d. there Feb. 10, 1787, Æ 87. They had nine children b. of record at Simsbury, their third child being
2 CONC :
2 CONT
2 CONT • iii. Anne Case, b. Jan. 28, 1727/8, d. at Wintonbury Parish, now Bloomfield, Conn. Mar. 28, 1811, Æ 84; m. 1) Sept. 26, 1759 at Simsbury as his 2nd wife, Sgt. William Webster, Jr., s. of Ens. William Webster & Sarah Nichols, b. 
2 CONC Sept. 3, 1703 at Hartford, Conn. (bapt. Sept. 5, 2nd Chh.). He d. at Wintonbury Parish, now Bloomfield, Conn., Mar. 21, 1779, Æ 76. Five children of the marriage. The widow Anne (Case) Webster m. 2) after Aug. 23, 1790 as his 2nd 
2 CONC wife, her cousin Dea. Abraham Case of Simsbury, s. of Bartholomew Case and Mary Humphrey, who. d. Mar. 13, 1800. There were no children of this second marriage.
2 CONT --------------------
