1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Pending verification on SAR registration numbers on National and State. There was an application for Amos Phelps with SAR by Major James Dudley Dewell on 16 May 1939. Being researched by: Kenneth Joseph Bagg-Neder.
2 CONT
2 CONT Where did this DAR # come from?
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A090023  DAR Ancestor # A090023]  
2 CONT
2 CONT Red Flagged:  "FUTURE APPLICANTS MUST PROVE CORRECT SERVICE".
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription on Amos' grave marker:  "Death is a debt to nature due which I have paid and so must you. Our time on earth is short we see Oh then prepare to follow me."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Amos Phelps was mentioned in Joseph Phelps 1749 Will.  Amos was shown with an unlikely  birth date of 1708 in “The Phelps Family Of America” (page 107) so he shown here as born before 1704, son of Joseph Phelps and his second wife
2 CONC , Sarah Case.  “Genealogies of Connecticut Families” (page 294)  explains that Amos married in Simsbury on 1 July 1753, Sarah Pettebone, which would be his age 15.  “Moreover, the births of the first five children were all entered
2 CONC  together, probably in 1703, and when Amos was born the father neglected to enter his birth.”
