0 @I6000000000484631640@ INDI
1 NAME Samuel /Marshall/ of Windsor
2 GIVN Samuel
2 SURN Marshall
2 NSFX of Windsor
2 _MARNM Marshall
1 NAME Capt. Samuel Marshall
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 7 MAY 1630
2 ADDR
3 CITY Alford
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 16 DEC 1675
2 ADDR
3 CITY Fort Narragansett
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 BURI
2 DATE 19 DEC 1675
2 PLAC Smith's Castle Mass Gravesite
2 ADDR
3 CITY Wickford
3 STAE Rhode Island
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Military, Captain, Shoemaker
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Killed in swamp fight in King Phillips War
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in England - possibly Dorchester around 1615.  Second son of Thomas Marshall arrived in Boston, MA with his father.  Believed by historians that he moved soon afterwards to Windsor, CT with the earliest settlers because he he
2 CONC ld valuable property in Palizado by 1637.  He was actively engaged in military service during King Philip's War: a corporal in 1672, a quartermaster in 1673, an ensign in 1675 in Major Treat's army and then was "one of the five Co
2 CONC nnecticut captains who led the Colony's forces to the attack on Fort Narragansett, December 19, 1675 where he fell at the head of his troops."
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/23098554/samuel-marshall
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of THOMAS MARSHALL, he was brought to Boston by his widowed father as a child. He married MARY WILTON of Northampton, Mass. and they lived in Windsor, Hartford Co., Conn.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served as a juror, deputy, and was licensed to sell liquor from his home. In 1657/8 Corp. Samuel Marshall was a trooper from Windsor.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Dec. 19, 1675, Capt. Samuel Marshall, while serving in the First Company under Major Robert Treat was killed outright during the Great Swamp Fight at South Kingston, Washington County, Rhode Island during the Narragansett or Ki
2 CONC ng Philip's War. His body was taken along with many others to Smith's Castle in Wickford, Rhode Island and buried in a mass grave.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Samuel & Mary (Wilton) Marshall were:
2 CONT *Samuel, LYDIA (MARSHALL) HAWLEY (my ancestor), 
2 CONT *David, 
2 CONT *Thomas, 
2 CONT *Eliakim, 
2 CONT *John, and 
2 CONT *Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ordinary Keeper Avon CT 
2 CONT
