2 CONT * Elizabeth 1674
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes From "Smith-Kyllo Family" by Kenneth Smith WorldConnect at Rootsweb.com
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY OF THOMAS MARSHALL OF BOSTON
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Marshall was born in Alford, Lincolnshire, England in 1587. He was baptised on November 12, the son of William Marshall and Elizabeth Rogers. He married Lydia Angrom in Alford on August 17, 1627. They had three or possibly 
2 CONC four children in Alford and in 1634, left England, bound for Boston, in Massachusetts Colony. Their family numbered five, so if they had a fourth child, it must have died in Alford. They traveled in a large party led by Reverend J
2 CONC ohn Cotton, who had been the minister at Boston, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas' wife Lydia and their two daughters died during the journey to New England.
2 CONT
