1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The daughter and only child of DAVID & KATHERINE (HOSKINS) WILTON, the exact year or place of her birth is not known. "The Great Migration Begins" speculates that it is 1632. She married SAMUEL MARSHALL on May 6, 1
2 CONC 652 in Windsor, Hartford, Conn. Capt. Marshall died in the Great Swamp Fight of King Philip's War in 1674. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Samuel & Mary (Wilton) Marshall were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel, LYDIA (MARSHALL) HAWLEY,  David, Thomas, Eliakim, John, and Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==biographical notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=28475529 Find A Grave Memorial# 28475529]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary died intestate, so the Court ordered distribution of her estate to the children as follows: to the eldest son, a double portion, & to the six others equal portions, and that the younger children be secure until they come of a
2 CONC ge.
2 CONT
2 CONT The History and Genealogies of Ancent Windsor Connecticut: including
2 CONT East Windsor, South Windsor, Bloomfield, Windsor Lockes, and Ellington. 1635-1891. Volume II. Genealogies and Biographies. By Henry R. Stiles Page 465-466.
2 CONT
2 CONT A biography of Capt. Samuel Marshall is given and a list of children with his wife Mary (dau. Lieut. David) Wilton who he married on 6 May 1652.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Samuel, b. 27 May 1653; Bap. 7 Feb, 1657
2 CONT * 2. Lydia, b. 18 Feb. 1655
2 CONT * 3. Lydia, b. 3 Feb 1657; Bap. 7 Feb 1657. Married Joseph Hawley.
2 CONT * 4. Thomas, b 23 Apr. 1659; died before 1674.
2 CONT * 5. David, b. 24 July 1661; Married Abigail Phelps, 9 Dec. 1686.
2 CONT * 6. Thomas, b. 18 Feb 1663; Married Mary Drake on 3 March 1685/6 (my ancestor)
2 CONT * 7. Mary, b. 8 May 1667;
2 CONT * 8. Eliakim, B. 10 July, 1669; Married Sarah Leet of Guilford, 23 Aug. 1704
2 CONT * 9. John, b. 10 April, 1672; Married Abigail ________.
2 CONT * 10. Elizabeth, b. 27 Sept. 1674
2 CONT
2 CONT History of Torrington, Connecticut, From Its First Settlement in 1737, with Biographies and Genealogies. By Rev. Samuel Orcutt. 1878. Gives a similar list of children omitting 3. Lydia.
