1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ~MY ANCESTOR~ The daughter of CAPT. SAMUEL & MARY (WILTON) MARSHALL, she married CAPT. JOSEPH HAWLEY  on September 24, 1676 in Northampton, Mass.  They were the parents of at least seven children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia's father was killed at The Great Swamp Fight in Rhode Island in 1675 when she was about 20 yrs. of age.  Her grandfather, [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Wilton&GSfn=David&GSbyrel=in&GSdyrel=in&GSob=n&
2 CONC GRid=28480295& LIET. DAVID WILTON], in his will, bequeathed land next to his home lot to Joseph & Lydia providing that they build on it and live there for four years. Inscription: LIDIA THE WIFE OF IOSEP HAWLEY ESQ  WHO Dyd Oct 28
2 CONC th 1732 in ye 76 yr oF Her Age.
