2 CONC en02gris/page/16 (Steven Ferry, February 8, 2019.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Phelps b. a. 1623, England. m. Sarah Griswold, 10 Nov. 1650, Windsor, dau. of Edward Griswold (emigrant) of Kenilworth. England. She m. (2) Nathaniel Pinney. 1670 (Pinney 2). Samuel d. 15 May 1669, Windsor
2 CONT
2 CONT * Parents:  William Phelps b 1599 Tewksbury & Elizabeth _____(1) (Phelps and Servin p. 95)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Phelps 6 Sarah Griswold (Phelps and Servin p. 89) 
2 CONT # Lt. Samuel Phelps Jr. b. 5 Sept. 1652, Windsor. m. Abigail Williams, 21 June 1675 (b. 1658) dau. of John Williams & Mary Burley. Samuel d. 21 Oct. 1741, No children.
2 CONT # Sarah Phelps b. 16 Mar, 1653, Windsor m. Andrew Moore of Simsbury, 15 Feb. 1671. Moved to Poquonock. Phelps Gen. p. 98 & Windsor, p. 506 agree an the children (1672-1698), but Windsor p. 465 says she m. (2) John Mansfield, 13 De
2 CONC c, 1683 and had four children (1684-1689). The following assumes the Mansfield marriage is wrong because her later children were named Moore. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * The Phelps Family of America and Their English Ancestors, Compiled by Judge Oliver Seymour Phelps and Andrew T. Servin, Eagle Publishing Company of Pittsburgh, Massachusetts, 1899, pp. 88-9, states:
2 CONT
2 CONT "21. SAMUEL PHELPS, b. England, about 1625, emigrated to New England with his father, in ship Mary and John, settling with his father in Dorchester, removing from there to settling of Windsor, Ct., in 1635-6, where he m. Sarah Gri
2 CONC swold, 10th Nov., 1650. She was daughter of Edward Griswold, and b. Kenilworth, England, and came to New England with her father in 1639. After the death of Mr. Phelps, she m. 2nd Nathaniel Pinney, 21st July, 1670, and had Nathani
2 CONC el Pinney b. 11th May, 1671, and Sarah Pinney b. 11th Oct., 1673. Mrs. Pinney died 6th Nov., 1715.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Phelps bought 1st Oct., 1657, Thomas Orton's house and land south of road separating it from his father's homestead, and brother William's: the house stood on the rear of the lot just opposite his father's house. This lot was 
2 CONC of triangular shape, 4 rods on the rivulet, 60 rods on east and west road, 40 rods on Mill road, and 47 rods on the southeast line. The rear of this lot and house he sold to his brother Nathaniel, and removed to Poquonock, where h
2 CONC e had received a grant of land, and where he also bought John Bartlett's place east of Stony Creek, and north of Thomas Holcomb's, and running east of the rivulet. Here he died 15th May, 1669. He witnessed a deed of land to his fa
2 CONC ther by the Indians in 1666.
2 CONT
2 CONT January 8th, 1660, he paid rates for short slips, 7 shillings, highest amount assessed that year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Town Records--24th May, 1669, "There was a day of training; by reason of the death of Samuel Phelps, voted that Benjamin Holcomb supply his place as Way Warden."
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ====Probate: Samuel Phelps
2 CONT * '''Location''': Windsor
2 CONT * '''Date of Will [Probate]:''' 29 Jun 1669
2 CONT * Page: 65
2 CONT * '''Invt.''' £773-15-00. 
2 CONT * '''Taken 29 June, 1669,''' by John Moore, Matthew Grant, Sergt. Benedict Alvord, William Thrall. 
2 CONT * '''The legatees:''' Sarah the Widow, Samuel age 17 years, Sarah 15, Timothy 13, Mary 11, William 9, John 7, Ephraim 6, Abigail 3, Josiah 2 December next.
2 CONT * '''Court Record''', Page 89--2 September, 1669: Invt. exhibited. 
2 CONT * '''Adms. to the Relict. See File:''' Order to Distribute to the Relict œ78 to dispose of as she shall see cause, and one third of the use of Land during life also the improvement of the whole Estate until the children come of ag
2 CONC e. 
2 CONT ** To the eldest son £108 
2 CONT ** to the 2d, £80 
2 CONT ** to the 3d, £73 
2 CONT ** to the 4th, 5th & 6th, to each £73 
2 CONT ** to the three daughters, to each, £48-06-08. 
2 CONT * William Phelps and George Griswold to be Overseers.
2 CONT * '''Page 98--3 March, 1669-70:''' The Widow Phelps desires the Court to appoint Timothy Phelps to assist William Phelps and George Griswold as Joynt Overseers.
2 CONT * '''Source:''' Manwaring, Charles William, ed. 1902. ''A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records: Hartford District, 1635-1700''. Vol. 1. Hartford, Connecticut, USA: R. S. Peck & Company. Available at: [https://www.google
2 CONC .com/books/edition/A_Digest_of_the_Early_Connecticut_Probat/T9MLAAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=%22Samuel%20Phelps%22 Google Books], p. 225.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The first mention, yet discovered, of Andrew Moore, /\ of Poquonnock, Conn., is the record of his marriage, which is as follows: "Andrew Moore & fara Phelpes yt was Dafter of Samuel Phelpes ware married by capten Newberry, februar
2 CONC y. 15, 1671."' Samuel Phelps was the son of William, the immigrant, who came to Dorchester, Mass., in 1630, and thence to Windsor, Conn., in 1636. He married Sarah (dau. of Edward) Griswold Nov. 10, 1650, and "Sarah Phelps was bor
2 CONC n in March, the latter end of 1653." (JV/ndsor Tcnun Record.') The Phelps family came from Tewkesbury, England, on the ship Mary and John. Sarah Griswold, b. Kenilworth, England, in 1628, came to America with her father in 1639. T
2 CONC he)' settled in Windsor, Conn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * [http://www.phelpsfamilyhistory.com/research/william/descendants-phelps-tewkesbury.asp Identity and Family of William Phelps of Tewkesbury, England]
2 CONT * http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~steeles/Steele/d126.htm#P5848
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Samuel Phelps went to New England in 1630 on the ship "Mary & John", with his father William Phelps and stepmother Ann Dover and their family. They settled first at Dorchester, Massachusetts, moving to the new settlement of Windso
2 CONC r, Connecticut on the Connecticut River with Rev. Warham's church in 1635.
2 CONT
2 CONT He met Sarah Griswold in Windsor and they were married there on 10 Nov 1650.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 1 Oct 1657 he purchased a house in Windsor from Thomas Orton, which included land sourth of the road separating it from the homes of his father and brother William. Later he sold this property to his brother Nathaniel and moved
2 CONC  to Poquonock, where he had received a grant of land and also had bought John Bartlett's place east of Stony Creek and north of Thomas Holcomb's.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 8 Jan 1660 he paid rates (taxes) for short slips of 7 shillings, the highest amount assessed that year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel died 15 May 1669. The town record have an entry on 24 May 1669, "There was a day of training; by reason of the dath of Samuel Phelps, voted that Benjamin Holcomb supply his place as Way Warden."
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT * Article by Myrtle Stevens Hyde, "The English Origin of William Phelps of Dorchester, Mass. and Windsor, Conn., with Notes on His Marriages," The American Genealogist, Vol. 65, Jul 1990, p. 161
2 CONT
2 CONT * "The Phelps Family of America and their English Ancestors," by Oliver Seymour Phelps and Andrew T. Servin (Eagle Publishing, Pittsfield, Massachusetts, 1899), p. 88-89 (this book erroneously cites Tewkesbury, Gloucestershire, En
2 CONC gland as the area of this family's origin)
2 CONT
2 CONT * "The Great Migration: Immigration to New England 1620 - 1633," by Robert Charles Anderson, New England Historic Genealogy Society, Boston, Massachusetts, 1995, Vol. 3, p. 1444-1446
2 CONT
2 CONT Compiled and edited by Allen Alger, Alger Family Historian - e-mail: alger@alum.mit.edu [1]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Samuel Phelps b. o/a 1630 England d. 15 May 1669 at Poquonock, CT, married to Sarah Griswold b. 29 Jan 1631 England. No record of her parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue: Abigail Phelps Marshall
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy Phelps, b. Windsor, Ct , 26th Oct., 1656, soon removed with his father to Poquonock, m. 1st  Sarah Gaylord, 18th Nov , 1686, daughter of Walter and Sarah (Rockwell) Gaylord. Walter Ga}dord was son of William, a first settl
2 CONC er of Windsor, and Sarah Rockwell was dau. of William Rockwell, also a first settler. Sarah Gaylord, b. 13th April, 1665, d. 10 Nov., 1685. She had three children, 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 2nd, 13th Nov.. 1690, Sarah Pratt, b. Hartford, Ct., 1662, d. 18th Feb. , 1758, aged 96 years, daughter of Daniel Pratt. Her grave stone may be seen in the ancient burying ground, Centre Church, at Hartford, the only Phelps 
2 CONC stone in the yard. The inscription reads : — " Here lies interred ye body-  of Mrs. Sarah Phelps, ye relict of Mr. Tim Phelps, who died Feb. ye 18th, 1758, in ye 96th year of her age." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Phelps first settled in Simsbury, Ct. removing to Hartford about the time of his 2nd marriage in 1690, where he d. in 1714. His will dated 28th. March, 1712, probated 5th May, 1 7 14. At this time letters of administration gra
2 CONC nted to Sarah Phelps, relict of Tim. Phelps. No reference is made to his children except that he had seven daughters, and one son. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by 1st. wife: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 74. I. Stephen, b. Simsbury, Ct., 20 Jany., 1686, unm., d. young. Not mentioned in father's will. 
2 CONT
2 CONT + 75. II. Sarah, b. Simsbury, Ct., 20 Dec, 1687, m. David Marshall. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 76. III. Timotlvy, b. Simsbury, Ct., 22 Jany., 1689, d 28 Sept., 16S9. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by 2nd. wife: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 77. IV. Mary, b. Hartford, Ct., bapt. 21 Aug., 1692.
2 CONT
2 CONT + 78. V. Hannah, b. Hartford, Ct., 10 Sept., 1694, m. Timothy Eoomis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 79. VI. Mabel, b. Hartford, Ct., 28 Sept., 1696. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 80. VII. Elizabeth, b. Hartford, Ct., 4, Sept., bapt. 22 Oct., 1699. 
2 CONT
2 CONT > +81. VIII. Timothy, b. Hartford, Ct., 24, bapt. 31 May, 1702, m. Sarah Brown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT + 82. IX. Esther, b. Hartford, Ct., 29 Oct., 1703, m. William Hooker. .
2 CONT
2 CONT + 83. X. Abigail, b. Hartford, Ct., m. William Hooker. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The last named child, Abigail, we find in record of 1st Church, Hartford, as owning Covenant 29 Aug., 1730, full Covenant 8 Apr., 1733. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/phelpsfamilyofam01phel/phelpsfamilyofam01phel_djvu.txt
2 CONT
