1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT Nothing is known about the beginnings of Anthony Dorchester.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 1683: 28 Aug Death of Anthony Dorchester. Anthony was survived by his wife, Elizabeth, to whom he had been married about twenty years or more; his sons, John Dorchester and James Dorchester; and his daughters, Mary Dorchester Harm
2 CONC on and Sarah Dorchester Stebbins; and a step-daughter, Martha Kritchwell Wright. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by two wives: Sarah, who died in 1649; Martha, who died in 1662; and three children: Benjamin, who died in 1675; Hester, who died in 1662; and a step-son, Samuel Kritchwell, who died in 1651.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://archive.org/details/dorchesterfamily00swan The Dorchester family chronicles]  by Swanson, Earle S. (Earle Swen), 1928-; Swanson, Patricia (Patricia Maskrey), 1928-
2 CONT
2 CONT "Anthony Dorchester, employed by Parsons, had a one-fourth interest in a 
2 CONT cow which when killed was divided, his employer owning another one-fourth.  Both wanted the tongue of the animal, but it fell to Dorchester, and  subsequently when cooking it , it mysteriously disappeared from the pot. It  was the
2 CONC  work of a witch of course." 
2 CONT
2 CONT After a series of unexplainable incidents, the Parsons were charged with  witchcraft and tried by a jury in Boston. Mrs. Parsons, (who was apparently  mentally deranged by this time) pleaded guilty to the murder of their child.  T
2 CONC he jury found her guilty of murder but innocent of witchcraft. The General  Court confirmed the verdict and she was sentenced to be hanged. However, by  this time she was in poor health and died of natural causes before the  sente
2 CONC nce could be carried out. The witchcraft trial of Hugh Parsons ended in  conviction but the General Court refused to confirm the verdict so he escaped  execution. Following his trial, Hugh Parsons left Boston and probably  Massach
2 CONC usetts, and was never seen in Springfield again. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/112538506/anthony-dorchester
2 CONT
2 CONT Anthony arrived Springfield 1649, resided in Springfield 34 years until he died 1683.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Born 1619 Dorchester, Dorset, England
2 CONT * Died 1682/3 Aug 28 Springfield, MA
2 CONT * Father Anthony Dorcester 1562-1602
2 CONT * Mother Sarah 1580-1649
2 CONT
2 CONT Anthony Dorchester and his wife, Sarah, came here from Windsor and brought three children John, James and Mary.
2 CONT
