1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=29817433]
2 CONT
2 CONT A Patriot of the American Revolution for MASSACHUSETTS with the rank of Private.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A071490  DAR Ancestor # A071490]
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 1. Loomis Genealogy; 
2 CONT * Commanded a company of minute men at the Lexington Alarm
2 CONT * 8 Children are recorded in Loomis Genealogy-pg: 155
2 CONT
2 CONT =Burial=
2 CONT * Tombstone upper inscription: "Capt. Noah Loomis Died August 9 1808 Aged 84 years."  [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=29817433 Find A Grave Memorial# 29817433] Age at death: 84
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT # Rhoda Loomis (1/13/1749-1821) of Deerfield, Franklin, MA d. 3/13/1821
2 CONT # Mercy Loomis (1748-1780) of Deerfield, Franklin, MA burial 12/10/1888?
2 CONT # Tirzah Stiles (Loomis) (2/20/1752-1784) Westfield, Hampden, MA
2 CONT # Noah Loomis (4/11/1754-7/3/1819) b. in Westfield, Hampden, Massachusetts. d. in Southwick, MA  Married (1) Mary Dewey on Nov 1775, daughter of Joseph Dewey and Beulah Sackett; (2) Eunice Noble on 8/07/1814
2 CONT # Shem Loomis (9/13/1756-1757) b. in Westfield, Hampden, Massachusetts d. 8/15/1841
2 CONT # Ham Loomis (11/28/1758-1759) b. in Westfield, Hampden, Massachusetts 
2 CONT # Japhet Loomis (7/14/1761-1777) b. in Westfield, Hampden, Massachusetts  d. 7/31/1777
2 CONT # Grace Loomis (11/5/1763-1785)  b. in Westfield, Hampden, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT =Notes=
2 CONT Noah and Rhoda are usually credited with being the second settlers of the village of Southwick, MA. Noah served the community in several capacities over the course of his long life; selectman, committee of safety, and minute man.
2 CONT
2 CONT Noah served in his local militia as a private, later a corporal and a captain as his unit was absorbed into the regiment of Colonel Timothy Danielson.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is possible Noah profited in two ways by risking life and limb for the new nation; his village offered 30 shillings for men to enlist in the militia, and later increased the bounty to 15 pounds and later to 30 pounds when enlis
2 CONC tments were harder to come by. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sons of the American Revolution (SAR)=
2 CONT Application # 29049 (Jonas Crane) was approved on 1/8/1909
2 CONT # Noah Loomis and Rhoda Clark
2 CONT # Ham Loomis and Elizabeth Allen
2 CONT # Winthrop Laflin and Fanny Loomis
2 CONT # Zenas Marshall Crane and Caroline Laflin
2 CONT # Jonas Crane b. 12/6/1840
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT * "Encyclopedia of Massachusetts, biographical and genealogical", Vol. 4, edited by William Richard Cutter, American Historical Society. Pg. 165.  
2 CONT * Lineage Book, Vol. 10, by Daughters of the American Revolution. Pg. 3. 
2 CONT * Putnam's Monthly Historical magazine, Vol. 1, pub. by Eden Putnam. 1893, pg. 118.  
2 CONT * "Westfield and its Historic Influences, 1669-1919: the life of an early town, with a survey of events in New England and bordering regions to which it was related in colonial and revolutionary times" by John  Hoyt Lockwood. Pg. 
2 CONC 113. Printed and sold by the author, 1922. 
