2 CONT Jacob Ordway (1690 - bef. 1730)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Ordway
2 CONT Born 14 Jan 1690 in Newbury, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colonymap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Son of Edward Ordway and Mary (Wood) Ordway
2 CONT Brother of Anna Ordway, Rachel (Ordway) Johnson, Joanna Ordway, Isaiah Ordway, Daniel Ordway, Sarah Ordway [half], Edward Ordway II [half] and Joseph Ordway I [half]
2 CONT Husband of Rebecca (Wright) Ordway — married about 1711 in Lebanon, Connecticutmap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Father of Mary (Ordway) Gillett, Rebecca (Ordway) Hunt, Jemima (Ordway) Smalley, Rachel (Ordway) McCall, Daniel Ordway, Sarah Ordway and John Ordway
2 CONT Died before 1730 before age 39 [location unknown]
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile managers: Albertus Robert Casimir Jung private message [send private message] and Shirley Becker private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 23 Dec 2022 | Created 23 Aug 2011
2 CONT This page has been accessed 598 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Ordway was born 14 January 1689/90 at Newbury, Essex County, Massachusetts Bay Colony.[1][2] His parents were Edward Ordway and Mary Wood.[2] [3] [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob was married to Rebecca Wright. To this marriage were born:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Ordway, b. 16 Aug 1712; [5]
2 CONT Rebecca Ordway, b. 16 Jan 1713; [6]
2 CONT Jemima Ordway, b. 11 Dec 1715; [7]
2 CONT Rachel Ordway, b. 28 Nov 1717; [8]
2 CONT Daniel Ordway, b. 3 Jun 1719; [9]
2 CONT Sarah Ordway, b. 5 Nov 1723 - Windham; [10]
2 CONT John Ordway, b. 7 Dec 1725. [11] [12]
2 CONT Jacob Ordway died sometime between March 1725, when son John was conceived, and 1729 or 1730, when his widow Rachel married Isaac Lyman.
2 CONT
