2 CONT When Issac Lyman was born on 16 February 1681, in Northampton, Hampshire, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America, his father, Richard Lyman III, was 33 and his mother, Elizabeth Cowles, was 36. He married Abigail Pomer
2 CONC oy in 1700, in Hampden, Hampden, Penobscot, Massachusetts, United States. They were the parents of at least 1 son and 1 daughter. He lived in Northampton, Hampshire, Massachusetts, United States in 1682. He died on 22 May 1758, in
2 CONC  Lebanon, New London, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America, at the age of 77, and was buried in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America.
