1 NOTE Ebenezer emigrated to Canada as a United Empire Loyalist.
2 CONT He lived in Mansfield, Conneticutt until 1759-60, when he moved to
2 CONT New Fairfield, Conneticutt. Shortly after he moved to Newon, Sussex County.
2 CONT About 1765 he took up residence at Shaftsbury, Vermont. He and three of his
2 CONT sons refused to sign the Declaration of Independence and fled to Canada and
2 CONT settled in Cornwall Ontario. He was married for 50 years, 2 months, 2 days
