1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Hannah Hitchcock Chapin=
2 CONT * BIRTH 27 Nov 1702 Springfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 12 Apr 1778 (aged 75) Springfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Springfield Cemetery, Springfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 23124287 Photos by Helen (Auton) & Joe Presz
2 CONT
2 CONT Be Thou my Vision, O Lord of my heart;
2 CONT Naught be all else to me, save that Thou art.
2 CONT Thou my best Thought, by day or by night,
2 CONT Waking or sleeping, Thy presence my light.
2 CONT
2 CONT Be Thou my Wisdom, and Thou my true Word;
2 CONT I ever with Thee and Thou with me, Lord;
2 CONT Thou my great Father, I Thy true son;
2 CONT Thou in me dwelling, and I with Thee one.
2 CONT
2 CONT Be Thou my battle Shield, Sword for the fight;
2 CONT Be Thou my Dignity, Thou my Delight;
2 CONT Thou my soul's Shelter, Thou my high Tower:
2 CONT Raise Thou me heavenward, O Power of my power.
2 CONT
2 CONT Riches I heed not, nor man's empty praise,
2 CONT Thou mine Inheritance, now and always:
2 CONT Thou and Thou only, first in my heart,
2 CONT High King of Heaven, my Treasure Thou art.
2 CONT
2 CONT High King of Heaven, my victory won,
2 CONT May I reach Heaven's joys, O bright Heaven's Sun!
2 CONT Heart of my own heart, whatever befall,
2 CONT Still be my Vision, O Ruler of all.
2 CONT
2 CONT Words: At­trib­ut­ed to Dal­lan For­gaill, 8th Cen­tu­ry (Rob tu mo bhoile, a Com­di cri­de); trans­lat­ed from an­cient Ir­ish to Eng­lish by Ma­ry E. Byrne, in "Eriú," Jour­nal of the School of Ir­ish Learn­ing, 1905, and versed
2 CONC  by El­ea­nor H. Hull, 1912, alt.
2 CONT
