1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Married Elizabeth Bliss February 10, 1757
2 CONT ∼He served as a private, in the 4th Connecticut Provincial Regiment. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He relocated to Royalton, Vermont in 1783 from Canterbury, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married on February 10, 1757, at Lebanon, Connecticut, Elizabeth Bliss.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Lyman Genealogy: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ezekiel, eldest son of Jabez, Samuel, Richard, Richard, Richard, b. 1733; m. Feb. 10, 1757, Elizabeth Bliss, of Lebanon; resided in Canterbury; removed to Royalton, Vermont, about 1782, where he died at a great age.
2 CONT
2 CONT The History of Royalton, Vermont with Family Genealogies 1769-1911 by Evelyn M. Wood Lovejoy, Published by the Town and The Royalton Woman's Club 1911 also suggests that he was buried on the Skinner Farm.* Reference: [https://www.
