1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Elizabeth Tilley
2 CONT * Gender: 	Female
2 CONT *Birth: 	circa 1631 - England or, Dorchester, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America
2 CONT * Death: 	August 21, 1684 (48-57) Springfield, Hampshire County, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America
2 CONT *Daughter of John Tilley, of Dorchester & Saybrook and Edith (Moorecock) (Tilley) Camp
2 CONT * Wife of Thomas Merrick - m. 14 October 1653, Springfield, Massachusetts Bay Colony to Thomas Merrick as his second wife.  He was Sarah Stebbins widower.  Thomas Merrick was a boatman and carter for the Pynchon family in Springfi
2 CONC eld.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Merrick-10#Marriages_and_Children
2 CONT
2 CONT After Sarah Stebbin's death, Thomas Merrick married second, Elizabeth Tilley on 21 October 1653 at Springfield, Massachusetts.[8] She is believed to be the daughter of John Tilley and Edith Moorecock.[9] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Tilley and Thomas Merick had 8 children:[7][10][11] 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Comments: Stott (2022) only lists 5 but mentions there were 8:
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Elizabeth Merrick (1654-1659), born August 26 [or October 26], 1654;[12] died January 11, 1659. 
2 CONT #     Miriam Merrick (1656-1684), born May 1, 1655 [or 1656];[13] died October 11 [or 4], 1684. 
2 CONT #     John Merrick (1658-1748), born November 9, 1658,[14] married Mary Day, 11 Feb 1687; married 2nd Mrs. Rebekah Stebbins (widow), 14 Jan 1725; died 10 April 1748. 
2 CONT #     Elizabeth (Merrick) Day (1661-1743), born July 4, 1661;[14] married Thomas Day, of Springfield in 1685. 
2 CONT #     Thomas Merrick (1664-1743), born January 2, 1664 [or 1663],[15] married Hannah Dumbleton. 
2 CONT #     Tilley Merrick (1667-1736), born October 20, 1667,[16] married Sarah Cooley.[17] 
2 CONT #     James Merrick (1669-1765), born March 2, 1669/70[18][19], married Sarah Hitchcock; died September 8, 1765.[20] 
2 CONT #     Abigail (Merrick) Ferry (1673-1753), born September 1 [or 7], 1673;[21] married Gershom Ferry, 5 May 1702.[22][23]  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT From her father's info on this site:
2 CONT Father: John Tilley (d. 1636)
2 CONT Mother: Edith. Birth: abt 1611 England Death: before July 1652 - of Milford, New Haven, Connecticut
2 CONT Spouses: John Tilley Jr., Nicholas Camp (2nd wife)
2 CONT Children: Elizabeth Merrick (born Tilley)
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Tilley, master of a bark, was cruelly maimed by the Indians on the Connecticut River, near Saybrook, in October, 1636, and died three days later. He had a homelot assigned to him in Windsor, which Thomas Dewey "lawful att’y t
2 CONC o Nich. Camp of M. and his wife Eady, formerly Eady Tilley" sold in 1646. [Winthrop’s "History of New England, "1853, p. 238; Stiles’s "History of Windsor," 1: 67, 167.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Below has been discounted by the article in NEHGR Winter 2022 that states Elizabeth was the dau. of John and Edith.
2 CONT
2 CONT Possible information regarding Elizabeth's parentage from Descendants of John Porter, p. 49:
2 CONT
2 CONT >Thomas Merrick... married (second wife) 1653, Elizabeth Tilley, daughter of William Tilley (abt.1607-aft.1668), [who came] from England in the ship "Abigail," in 1635, with his wife Alice (Frost) Tilley (1594-aft.1668).[9] Willia
2 CONC m Tilley's profile does not mention a daughter Elizabeth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ——
2 CONT
2 CONT Comments John Tilley of the Mayflower died in the winter of 1621, along with his wife Joan. He left one daughter, Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edith Tilley is NOT a spouse of that John Tilley.
2 CONT
2 CONT set adrift 10 Jun 2011, Janet Palo-jackson, curator
2 CONT
2 CONT Apparently her dad came over in 1635, but not sure whether Elizabeth was born yet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Tilley1 d. 21 August 1684
2 CONT
2 CONT Her ancestry has not been found but she was definitely not the woman of this name who crossed on the Mayflower and maried John Howland. Elizabeth Tilley married Thomas Merrick on 21 August 1653. Elizabeth Tilley died on 21 August 
2 CONC 1684. Child of Elizabeth Tilley and Thomas Merrick Capt. John Merrick+ b. 9 Nov 1658, d. 10 Apr 1748  Citations [S61] George E. McCracken, "President Hayes." 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/g2g/138437/john-tilley-john-tilley-mayflower-have-daughter-elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT OK was Elizabeth's Tilley's grandfather on the '''MAYFLOWER'''?????  John Tilley on Mayflower married to Joan Hurst  see following from site
2 CONT
2 CONT FATHER - John TIlley (Mayflower) + Joan Hurst married 1596 > 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Rose Tilley 1597-1602 SON - John Tilley 1599-1636 Robert Tilley 1604-1687 Elizabeth Tilley  1607-1687 (Younger John's Sister Elizabeth) SON - John Tilley + Edith (? maiden name) married 1636  > Children Edmund Tilley  1630-1685 El
2 CONC izabeth Tilley 1632 -1684  (Younger John's Daughter Elizabeth) Younger John Tilley's DAUGHTER Elizabeth Tilley married Thomas Merrick (1620-1704) (Son of Rev. Jon Meyrick) in 1653. She was his 2nd marriage. They had 7 children tog
2 CONC ether> Miriam Merrick  1656-1684
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain John Merrick  1658-1743 (There are 3 daughters named Elizabeth Merrick listed as 1654-1660 / 1661 / 1655-1743 So it is thought they may have consecutively had one die at 6 yrs old, one stillborn, and one who lived 88 years
2 CONC  - each named Elizabeth because they really wanted to use the name for a living child.) Thomas Merrick Jr. 1664- Tilley Merrick 1667-1736 James Merrick 1669-1765 Abigail Merrick 1673-1753 So, simplified, John Tilley the younger ha
2 CONC d both a sister and a daughter named Elizabeth Tilley. (By the way - His son Edmond married an Elizabeth and both John's paternal Grandmother as well as his maternal Great Great grandmother were also named Elizabeth.) commented Fe
2 CONC b 16 by L Davenport G2G Rookie
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
