1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from  "The First Century of the History of Springfield: The Official Records from 1636 to 1736, with an Historical Review and Biographical Mention of the Founders" By Springfield (Mass.), Henry Martyn Burt Publishe
2 CONC d by H.M. Burt, 1899  :
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN MERRICK.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Merrick, son of Thomas and Elizabeth, married Mary Day, daughter of Thomas and Sarah, February 9, 1687. He was known as Captain John Merrick. His wife, Mary, died April 29, 1723, and he married Widow Rebecca Stebbins, widow o
2 CONC f Joseph, January 14, 1725. She died July 14, 1747, and he died April 10, 1748, in his 90th year. His children, all by his first wife, were:—
2 CONT
2 CONT #  John, b. February 29, Leap Year, 1688, d. March 26, 1689.  
2 CONT #  Thomas, b. June 9, 1690, drowned September 19, 1699.  
2 CONT #  John, b. September 27, 1692, m. Sarah Parsons.   
2 CONT #  Mary, b. July 24, 1694, m. William Colton.  
2 CONT #  Samuell, b. March 21, 1696, m. Isabelle Ingersoll.  
2 CONT #  Elizabeth, b. November i, 1698, m. Joseph Barnard, and second, Joseph Woodbridge.  
2 CONT #  Abigail, b. June 4, 1699, d. July 30, 1699.  
2 CONT #  Jonathan, b. August 13, 1700, m. Jerusha Miner.  
2 CONT #  Abigail (our line), b. April 5, 1702, m. Timothy Phelps.  
2 CONT #  Thomas, b. January 13, 1704, m. Eunice Stebbins.  
2 CONT #  Margaret, b. August 30, 1705, m. Nathaniel Warriner.  
2 CONT #  Benjamin, b. November 6, 1707, m. Mercy Hoar.  
2 CONT #  Deborah, b. February —, 1710, d. March 8, 1710. 
