1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James MERRICK, son of Thomas and Elizabeth, married Sarah HITCHCOCK, daughter of Luke and Sarah, July 30, 1696. She died February 5, 1734. He married Mrs. Abigail MOSELEY of Westfield, January 21, 1735. He died Sep
2 CONC tember 8, 1765, in his 95th year.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Merrick-368  by Jackie Merrick
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography James Merrick, the son of Thomas Merrick and Elizabeth Tilley, was born March 2, 1670. He married Sarah Hitchcock.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT James Merrick married Sarah Hitchcock on July 30, 1696. After Sarah died he married Abigail Root. He died September 8, 1765 and is buried at Old Meadow Cem, West Springfield, Hampden, MA.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT James was a selectman in 1715 and 1719, also constable, tithingman and fence viewer.(citation needed)
2 CONT
2 CONT See also Find A Grave Memorial #5811
2 CONT
2 CONT See also Find A Grave Memorial #58118800 for James with his surname spelled Mirick. The #115682524 profile has been merged into the #58118800 profile on Find A Grave.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources ↑ The Settlers of the Beekman Patent, V.1-8 (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2013), (Orig. Pub. by Frank J. Doherty, Pleasant Valley, NY. Frank J. Doherty, The Settlers of
2 CONC  the Beekman Patent, Dutchess County, New York: An Historical and Genealogical Study of All the 18th Century Settlers in the Patent, ten volumes. 1990–2003), page 741. ↑ Find A Grave Memorial# 115682524. Dexter, Franklin Bowditch.
2 CONC  Biographical Sketches of the Graduates of Yale College (Holt, 1885) Vol. 1, Page 431 Doherty, Frank J. The Settlers of the Beekman Patent (1990)
