2 CONT ▼References
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 1. John1 Dumbleton , in Jacobus, Donald Lines, and Edgar Francis Waterman. Hale, House and Related Families, Mainly of the Connecticut River Valley. (Hartford: The Connecticut Historical Society, 1952)
2 CONT 523.
2 CONT "Nathaniel (Dumbleton), b. 10 June 1664; d. at Springfield, 13 Feb. 1736/7; m. at Northampton, 29 Dec. 1696, Hannah3 Allen … , b. at Northampton, Mass., abt. 1675, d. abt. 1745, dau. of John1 and Mary (Hannum) Allen. Administratio
2 CONC n on the estate of Nathaniel Dumbleton was granted to John and Samuel Dumbleton, 8 Mar. 1736/7. Samuel Dumbleton was appointed guardian, 14 May 1739, to Mary Dumbleton, one of the heirs, who is non compos mentis. The total estate 
2 CONC amounted to £1665.15.2 in real estate and £213.8.5 in personal estate. The widow, Hannah Dumbleton, was to have a third forever. Sums had been advanced to the daughters Elizabeth Walker and Hannah wife of Lamberton Cooper. The fin
2 CONC al settlement was a double share to the eldest son John, single shares to the son Samuel and to Mary Dumbleton, and Lamberton Cooper, Jr., was to have £156.3. of his uncle, John Dumbleton."
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Savage, James. A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England: Showing Three Generations of Those Who Came Before May, 1692, on the Basis of Farmer's Register. (Boston: Little, Brown, and Co, 1860-1862)
2 CONT 2:79.
2 CONT "JOHN, Springfield 1649, came in the serv. of William Whiting of Hartford, had John, b. 1658; and Nathaniel, 1664; beside six ds. wh. all m. Sarah m. 19 Dec. 1678, Josiah Leonard. JOHN, S. of the preced. m. 18 Mar. 1675, Lydia, d.
2 CONC  of John Leonard, and had a d. but in Philip's war was k. by the Ind. at Westfield 27 Oct. 1675. NATHANIEL, Springfield, br. of the preced. had six ch. Sprague, Hist. Disc. 24."
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 3.0 3.1 Book 1, Births, Marriages, Deaths, 1638-1728; Book 2, Deaths, 1728-1844; Hampshire Records, in Stott, Clifford L. Vital Records of Springfield, Massachusetts to 1850. (Boston, Massachusetts: New England Historic Genealog
2 CONC ical Society, 2002)
2 CONT 1:18; 1:497; 2:1666.
2 CONT "Nathaniell Dumbleton son off John Dumbleton borne the 10th off June 1664"
2 CONT "Nathal. Dumbleton of Springfield Dyed the 13th day of Februry Anno: Dom: 1736:7."
2 CONT "Nathaneel Dumbleton Son of John Dumbleton born June 10. 1664"
