0 @N6000000000337394168@ NOTE Source: Richardson, Ruth Ellsworth. Samuel Richardson and Josiah Ellsworth. Privately Published. 1974. 
1 CONT
1 CONT  Jonathon Ellsworth (Capt) b June 28, 1669 in Windsor, Conn.; 
1 CONT        d there September 13, 1749; m October 26, 1693 Sarah Gra
1 CONT        1675-1755 the dau of Tahan & Hannah (Palmer) Grant. They liv
1 CONT        in Windsor where Jonathon kept a tavern and a small sto
1 CONT        West Indian goods. He was a man of sterling good sense a
1 CONT        of such wit and humor that he bore the name of "Hector Ellsworth
1 CONT        In person he was tall and strong. His death was caus
1 CONT        being thrown from his horse. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Source #2:  Henry R. Stiles, "The History and Genealogies of Ancient Windsor, Connecticut 1635-1891" (Rockport, ME:  Picton Press, Feb 2000 reprint of 1893 original) Vol II, p. 210-211.
