0 @N6000000006165954863@ NOTE Moved to America in 1630 with sons James, Samuel and John(?).
1 CONT
1 CONT Some researchers list his 2nd wife as Mary Wall, daughter of Moses Wall and Ann Skinner. But Mary it appears that Mary was married to Robert Aylett during the time Bygod and his wife were having children. Some list her as being ma
1 CONC rried to Bygod first (in 1627) then to Aylett (in 1632) but she would have been having children with Bygod in 1632 and after - so she couldn't have been married to Aylett at the same time.
1 CONT
1 CONT It has also been suggested that Bygod married for a 3rd time to Sarah Talcott, Mary Wall's half sister (they had the same mother but different fathers). But according the the will of John Talcott and Ann Skinner Talcott, Sarah was
1 CONC  married to William Wadsworth - who outlived her - so he was her only husband.
0 @N6000000000140951175@ NOTE
1 CONT Name possibly Begot.
1 CONT
1 CONT Not sure which wife was the mother of which children.
1 CONT
1 CONT Begott Eggleston came to Dorchester, Massachusetts in 1630 in the “John and Mary.” He removed with Rev. John Warham in 1635 to Windsor, Connecticut.
1 CONT
1 CONT About 1635, he moved to Widsor, Hartford, Connecticut, which Bygod and his son James were admitted as freemen of the Lot gr. on Backer Rox, 14-1/2 r. wide from the Palisado Road.
1 CONT
1 CONT “Will of Bygatt Egllstone
1 CONT “I, Begat Egllstone of Windsor, Conn. in ye county of Hartford being aged an dweake, doe make this my last will and testament as follows; I comit my could in ye hands of God and my body to be buryed in seemly manner by my briends.
1 CONC  My estate which is but small, this is my will. My house and land after my decease I give to my son, Benjamin, he being ye staff of my age and condition, that he shall maintain his mother during her life and pay my debts. And in c
1 CONC ase that my son Joseph shall come and demand a portion his brother shall pay him 40 shillings as he is able with convenience. Also to my son, James and my son Samuel, son, thomas and to my daughters, Mary Sarah an dAbigail, to eye
1 CONC ther of these 3 shillings apiece. All the rest of my estate I give to my son, Benjamin and do make him my executor.
1 CONT “Begat Egleston”
