0 @N6000000003688550188@ NOTE John Owen1,2,3 was born on 25 Dec 1624 in Surrey, England or Mathavarn, Wales.  He emigrated in 1642 from To New Haven, CT, during or before 1642.  He Moved after 1650 in Windsor, CT.  He died on 1 Feb 1698/99 in Windsor, Hartford
1 CONC  Co., CT.  He signed a will on 5 Apr 1698 in Proved Court record page 22-25.  He was buried in 1699 in Congregational Church Cemetery, Windsor, CT.   A DIGEST OF THE EARLY CONNECTICUT PROBATE RECORDS.  1695 to 1700. Page 55
1 CONT
1 CONT Will of John Owen  b. Dec. 25, 1624  d. Feb. 18, 1697-98  m. Rebecca Wade
1 CONT Owen, John Sen, Died 18 February, 1698,  Invt. ¹29-01-00. Taken 5 April 1698 by Lt. Hayden and Benajah Holcomb.  Court record page 22-5, April 1698:  Inventory exhibited being only personal estate, and that given to the widow to b
1 CONC e at her dispose, the children consenting. Inventory inclkuded four coats and four pairs of britches, a powdering barrell, books and bottles, pewter platter, dishes, spoons and ladle, brass cast skillet and brass kettle, table clo
1 CONC ths and a dozen napkins.
1 CONT                 A DIGEST OF THE EARLY CONNECTICUT PROBATE RECORDS.  1695 to 1700. Page 55   Name: John Owen, Sen.   Location:   Died 18 February, 1698. Invt. 29-01-00. Taken 5 April, 1698, by Lt. Hayden & Benajah Holcomb.  Court R
1 CONC ecord, Page 22--5 April, 1698: Invt. exhibited, being only personal estate, and that given to the Widow to be at her dispose, the children consenting
1 CONT John OWEN (1295), born 25 Dec 1624 at , , Wales, died 1 Feb 1699 at Windsor, Hartford, CT.  Married 3 Oct 1650 at Windsor, Rebecca WADE (1296), born 1624 at Hartford, Hartford, CT, died 3 Dec 1711 at Windsor, Hartford, CT.
