0 @N6000000003017297342@ NOTE Will of Samuel Case
1 CONT I, Samuel Case, Sener, being visited with sudden sickness, do make this my last will and testament; I give to Elizabeth my wife the use and improvement of my dwelling house and homestead, with half the orchard thereon, during her 
1 CONC natural life. Item. I give to my son Samuel Case the land lying on Walnut Hill which was quitclaimed to me from the Town, to be reckoned to him at inventory price, and 10 more that the rest of the brethren abd sisters; also a piec
1 CONC e of swamp land bounded southerly ob Caldwell's land and easterly on land that goes to Hartford, he paying that money that he promised (about 8) to Nathaniel Goodwin, and the what it amounts to at inventory price to be reckoned to
1 CONC  him in part of his portion, not exceeding 8 more. Item. I give to the rest of my children the rest of my estate to be equally divided amongst them, only my son Nathaniel to have 5 acres of land joyning on his brother Samuel Case'
1 CONC s swamp before mentioned, which he hath made some improvement on already, and also excepting my daughter Irenia.  I give her an equall share excepting 15 which I already gave her. I appoint my sons Samuel Case Nathaniel Case and J
1 CONC onah Case my executors.
1 CONT Witnesses-Samuel Humphries, John Moses and Timothy Moses.
1 CONT Court record show 2 Nov 1725Caleb Case, a minor, 14 yrs old, chose his brother Samuel Case of Simsbury to be his guardian. Arriam Case, a minor, 17 yrs old, and Benjamin Case 15 yrs old, chose their brother Samuel Case to be their
1 CONC  guardian.
