0 @N6000000000337364646@ NOTE SERGEANT DANIEL LOOMIS, b. Farmington, June 16, 1657; m. 1st, Dec. 2
1 CONT       1680, Mary, b. May 7, 1660, dau. of Sergt. Josiah and Elizabeth (Holcomb) Ellsworth; 
1 CONT       m. 2nd, July 9, 1713, widow Hannah Drake. (The Ellsworth homestead has 
1 CONT       become the home and Chapter House of the Abigail Wolcott Chapter of the Conn. 
1 CONT       Dan. of the Am. Revolution). He d. June 25, 1740. He made his will Feb. 26, 1731- 
1 CONT       2, which was proven Aug. 5, 1740. See "A Digest of the Early Conn. Probate Records," 
1 CONT       by Chas. Wm. Manwaring. (First 15 Vols. of Original Records), Vol. III, p. 
1 CONT       302. Windsor. 9 children:
1 CONT
1 CONT 123.  DANIEL, b. Nov. 15, 1682.+ 
1 CONT 124.  JOSIAH, b. Nov. 28, 1684.+ 
1 CONT 125.  JOB, b. Jan. 21, 1686-7.+ 
1 CONT 126.  JOHN, b. Oct. 11, 1688.+ 
1 CONT 127.  MARY, b. Jan. 15, 1690-1; m. (???) 
1 CONT       Barbour. She was living, 1740. 
1 CONT 128.  ISAAC, b. Aug. 23, 1694.+ 
1 CONT 129.  ABRAHAM, b. Dec. 13, 1696.+ 
1 CONT 130.  BENJAMIN, b. Feb. 7, 1698-9.+ 
1 CONT 131.  BEMAJAN, b. Jan. 20, 1701-2, d. May 
1 CONT       6, 1702. 
