1 CONT Sarah Grant (125) b. Windsor, Sep. 19, 1675; d. Nov. 9, 1755, "‘ 82 yrs."; m. W., Oct. 26, 1693, Lieut. Jonathan Ellsworth [b. W., June 28 (22, 23), 1669; d. Sep. 13, 1749; s. of Sergt. Josias Ellsworth and Elizabeth Holcomb]; res
1 CONC . W.; kept tavern and a small store of West India goods, etc.; engaged in many business ventures; a man of sterling good sense, and of such wit and humor that he bore the name of "Heetor Ellsworth"; perhaps capt.+ 
1 CONT
