0 @N6000000000155664570@ NOTE BIOGRAPHY: September 12,1757 a seat assigned in meeting house Brimfield,Mass. Aug.4, 1766.  He was warned to get out of Sturbridge About 1800 moved to Woodbury, Vt. Was Elder of the Free Will Baptist Ch. Just before his death he h
1 CONC ad his family and friends called in and preached his own funeral sermon from the text Rev xiv:13 and as soon as the Amen was said he immediately expired.
1 CONT Another source claims; Quoting from the book entitled The Family of John Witham of Vermont by Minnie Flora Witham, published April 1991: "Florence (Georgianna) Ainsworth was a great, great granddaughter of Elder Ephraim Ainsworth 
1 CONC who was one of the founders of Woodbury, Vt.  The Woodbury History states that when Elder Ephraim was dying 'he called family and friends around him and preached his own funeral sermon from Revelation 21, and immediately expired.'
1 CONC "
