0 @N6000000006348624661@ NOTE Robert Charles Anderson has this to say about Benjamin in his article on Walter:
1 CONT
1 CONT      vi   BENJAMIN, b. say 1656; m. (1) by about 1680 Deborah _____ ("Deborah the wife [and] Elizabeth [and] Deborah the children of Beniamin Woddward" were bp. at Scituate on 16 July 1682 [NEHGR 57:319]); m. (2) by 1691 Hannah __
1 CONC ___ (on 24 June 1691 "Benjamin Woodworth and Hannah Woodworth his wife" acknowledged a deed in which Benjamin sold the land he had inherited from his father [PLR 3:11]).
1 CONT
1 CONT Will of Benjamin Woodworth
1 CONT
1 CONT Beniamin's Will: "In the name of God amen ye 21st day of January 1726/7. I, Benjamin Woodworth of Lebanon in ye County of Wendham and Colony of Connecticut in New England being very sick and weake in body but of perfect mind and m
1 CONC emory thanks be given unto God therefore calling to mind ye mortality of my body and knowing that it is appinted for all men once to dey, do make and ordain this my last will and testament. That is to say princeaply and first of a
1 CONC ll I give and recomend my soul in to ye hands of God that gave it and my body I recomend to ye earth to be beuried in decent Christian Beuril at ye discretion of my executor - nothing doubting but that at ye generall resurrection 
1 CONC I shall receve ye same again by ye mighty power of God - and as touching such worldly estate where with it had pleased God to bless me - with in this life I give demise and dispose of ye same in ye following maner and form: Imp - 
1 CONC I give and bequeath to my well beloved and eldest son Benjamin Woodworth twenty acres of my common right that is laid out joyning to his land that I gave formerly given to him to be first laide out to him begining at ye highway ye
1 CONC  wholl wedth as it is laide out and bounded on record and run so far by and ajoyning to his former land so far as to make twenty acres -
1 CONT
1 CONT Item: I give and bequeath unto my sons Benjamin, Ichabod and Ebenezer Woodworths all ye remaining part of my common right of land that is laide out ajoyning to that twenty acres above sd given to Benjamin - to be equaly devided to
1 CONC  my three sons Benjamin, Ichabod and Ebenezer they paying so much to my daughters as ye sd land shall be aprised at to be paide with in five years after my decease -and in case that my three sons Benjamin Ichabod and Ebenezer do n
1 CONC ot so cause to take ye sd lands and pay so much: to be devided amongst my daughters heare after named that ye ad lands shall be equaly devided amongst them my daughter.
1 CONT
1 CONT Item: I give and bequeath unto my son Amos Woodworth 33 acres and two 3ds of an acre of land ajoyning to that lot of land on Chusnut Hill that I have formarly given to him he paying twenty pounds to my daughters with in five years
1 CONC  after my deceas and in case he shall refuse to pay ye twenty pounds within the five years as afore sd that then ye sd 33 acres and two 3ds of an acre of land to be equaly devided amongst them -
1 CONT
1 CONT Item: I give and bequeath unto my sons Ezekiell and Caleb Woodworths all thos two tracts or persals of land that I purchased of Capt. Joseph Marsh ajoyning to ye farm where my now dweling hows now stands to be equaly devided betwe
1 CONC en them they paying all my just debts and in case they shall refuse to pay all my debts that then ye sd persels of land shall be sold to pay my just debts.
1 CONT
1 CONT Item: I give and bequeath unto my beloved daughters heare named to wit Debrough Sprauge and Hanah Walar and Ruth Owen and Judeth Newcomb and Margret Owen and Precillah Fuller all my moveable estate that I shall dye seizd of except
1 CONC  chains
1 CONT cart irons plough irons that my sons now have and one great chain that I use to take up ye mill that I give to my sons Ezekiel and Caleb. With ye mill and my Iron Harrow, I give to be used amongst all my sons so long as it shall l
1 CONC ast - all my moveables estate both within doars and without as ye stock and ye priece of my common lands laide out and not laide out and ye 20 that my son Amos is to pay that is to say all but only what I have heare except to be e
1 CONC qually devided amongst my above sd daughters only I give to ye children of Elezebeth Southard Deced - and ye children of Mary Sprauge Decd - ye heirs of thare own bodyes begoten amongst them half so much as to each of my daughtars
1 CONC  above named -
1 CONT
1 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my children both sons and daughters heare named in this my last will and testament all my right of land or aney estate that of right dos belong to me at or within the bounds of Seconet in ye provence o
1 CONC f Masachuse Bay and County of Bristoll they all being at equal charge in recovering ye same other wise ye charge to be payde out of ye part in proportion: and I do heareby likewise make and ordain my son Benjamin Woodworth my sole
1 CONC  executor of this my last will and testament - heareby I do utterly disalow revoack and disanull all and every other and former testaments wills legasies and bequests and executors by me in any ways before named willed and bequeat
1 CONC hed ratiefieing and confirmeng this and no other to be my last will and testament. In witness whereof I have heare unto set my hand and seall the day and year first above mentioned."
1 CONT
1 CONT Benjamin Woodworth (Seall)
1 CONT
1 CONT Signed sealled published pronounced and declared by ye sd Benjamin Woodworth as his last Will and Testement in presents of us ye subscribars: Thomas Root, Nathaniel Dewey and John Woodward.
0 @N6000000001503966216@ NOTE #
1 CONT # Note:
1 CONT
1 CONT     On the 23rd day of June 1692, Benjamin sold his land at Scituate, his second wife Hannah signing the deed with him, and he removed to Little Compton, Bristol Co., Mass. Bay, where his brother Isaac had preceded him.
1 CONT
1 CONT     In 1703, Benjamin removed again to Lebanon and bought a large tract of land from Phillip Smith on 25 February 1703, and was admitted as inhabitant of the town on 22 December 1704. His farm was situated in the northeast part of
1 CONC  the town, and on account of its remoteness from the church, he with others, petitioned in 1714 for a new church. In 1716 this new church was formed called Lebanon North Parish; later the town of Columbia.
1 CONT
1 CONT     In Lebanon land records [2:469] we find: "Moses Woodworth of Norwich sold to
1 CONT     Benjamin Woodworth of Lebanon five acres in Little Compton, Bristol Co., Colony of Mass. Bay, land being one-third of a 15 acre tract which was originally Walter Woodworth's.
1 CONT
1 CONT     Benjamin deeded land to his eldest son Benjamin in December 1712; to sons Ichabod and Ebenezer 13 February 1717/8; to son Amos 6 May 1720; to son Ezekiel who was "to care for his honored father and mother" 6 May 1723; to young
1 CONC est son Caleb 21 January 1726/7.
1 CONT
1 CONT     On 4 November 1714, Benjamin is said to have received land for service rendered in King Phillip's War. It is believed this account may have become confused with a Benjamin Woodward who was killed in that war.
1 CONT
1 CONT     Children mentioned in Benjamin’s Will, but not recorded in Lebanon or Little Compton [Genealogical & Family History of the State-of Connecticut, 1911, p. 885].
1 CONT
1 CONT     Beniamin's Will: "In the name of God amen ye 21st day of January 1726/7. I, Benjamin Woodworth of Lebanon in ye County of Wendham and Colony of Connecticut in New England being very sick and weake in body but of perfect mind a
1 CONC nd memory thanks be given unto God therefore calling to mind ye mortality of my body and knowing that it is appinted for all men once to dey, do make and ordain this my last will and testament. That is to say princeaply and first 
1 CONC of all I give and recomend my soul in to ye hands of God that gave it and
1 CONT     my body I recomend to ye earth to be beuried in decent Christian Beuril at ye discretion of my executor - nothing doubting but that at ye generall resurrection I shall receve ye same again by ye mighty power of God - and as to
1 CONC uching such worldly estate where with it had pleased God to bless me - with in this life I give demise and dispose of ye same in ye following maner and form: Imp - I give and bequeath to my well beloved and eldest son Benjamin Woo
1 CONC dworth twenty acres of my common right that is laid out joyning to his land that I gave formerly given
1 CONT     to him to be first laide out to him begining at ye highway ye wholl wedth as it is laide out and bounded on record and run so far by and ajoyning to his former
1 CONT     land so far as to make twenty acres -
1 CONT
1 CONT     Item: I give and bequeath unto my sons Benjamin, Ichabod and Ebenezer Woodworths all ye remaining part of my common right of land that is laide out ajoyning to that twenty acres above sd given to Benjamin - to be equaly devide
1 CONC d to my three sons Benjamin, Ichabod and Ebenezer they paying so much to my daughters as ye sd land shall be aprised at to be paide with in five years after my decease -and in case that my three sons Benjamin Ichabod and Ebenezer 
1 CONC do not so cause to take ye sd lands and pay so much: to be devided amongst my
1 CONT     daughters heare after named that ye ad lands shall be equaly devided amongst them my daughter.
1 CONT
1 CONT     Item: I give and bequeath unto my son Amos Woodworth 33 acres and two 3ds of an acre of land ajoyning to that lot of land on Chusnut Hill that I have formarly given to him he paying twenty pounds to my daughters with in five y
1 CONC ears after my deceas and in case he shall refuse to pay ye twenty pounds within the five years as afore sd that then ye sd 33 acres and two 3ds of an acre of land to be equaly devided amongst them -
1 CONT
1 CONT     Item: I give and bequeath unto my sons Ezekiell and Caleb Woodworths all thos two tracts or persals of land that I purchased of Capt. Joseph Marsh ajoyning to ye farm where my now dweling hows now stands to be equaly devided b
1 CONC etween them they paying all my just debts and in case they shall refuse to pay all my debts that then ye sd persels of land shall be sold to pay my just debts.
1 CONT
1 CONT     Item: I give and bequeath unto my beloved daughters heare named to wit Debrough Sprauge and Hanah Walar and Ruth Owen and Judeth Newcomb and Margret Owen and Precillah Fuller all my moveable estate that I shall dye seizd of ex
1 CONC cept chains art irons plough irons that my sons now have and one great chain that I use to take up ye mill that I give to my sons Ezekiel and Caleb. With ye mill and my Iron Harrow, I give to be used amongst all my sons so long as
1 CONC  it shall last - all my moveables estate both within doars and without as ye stock and ye priece of my common lands laide out and not laide out and ye 20 that my son Amos is to pay that is to say all but only what I have heare exc
1 CONC ept to be equally devided amongst my above sd daughters only I give to ye children of Elezebeth Southard Deced - and ye children of Mary Sprauge Decd - ye heirs of thare own bodyes begoten amongst them half so much as to each of m
1 CONC y daughtars above named -
1 CONT
1 CONT     Item: I give and bequeath to my children both sons and daughters heare named in this my last will and testament all my right of land or aney estate that of right dos belong to me at or within the bounds of Seconet in ye proven
1 CONC ce of Masachuse Bay and County of Bristoll they all being at equal charge in recovering ye same other wise ye charge to be payde out of ye part in proportion: and I do heareby likewise make and ordain my son Benjamin
1 CONT     Woodworth my sole executor of this my last will and testament - heareby I do utterly disalow revoack and disanull all and every other and former testaments wills legasies and bequests and executors by me in any ways before nam
1 CONC ed willed and bequeathed ratiefieing and confirmeng this and no other to be my last will and testament. In witness whereof I have heare unto set my hand and seall the day and year first above mentioned."
