1 CONT     Guilford, New Haven County, Connecticut for the free
1 CONT     exercise of religious and perhaps political opinions. He
1 CONT     had returned to England and died there.
0 @N6000000006348338756@ NOTE Babson's History of Gloucester, p. 107, says: "Thomas Jones was born in 1598. He was in Gloucester as early as 1642, and owned a house and land near the burying place. He was admitted Freeman in 1653; and died in 1671, leaving an 
1 CONC estate of œ 147: 15s. His wife was Mary, daughter of Richard, and Ursula North. She died in 1681."
1 CONT
1 CONT By court records,--see Mass. General Archives, office of Secretary of State, at the State House, Boston, Vol. 16, pp. 9, 10,--it appears that this record is incorrect in this: Ursula was the second wife of Richard North, and mothe
1 CONC r to none of his children, who probably were all born in England, before he emigrated to America.
