0 @N6000000003795996451@ NOTE Rootsweb
1 CONT URL:  http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~silversmiths/53/32811.htm
1 CONT Mrs Katharine Gibbs
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Born: 1604, Exeter Devonshire England
1 CONT     * Married: 13 Apr 1629, Saint Sidwell Exeter Devon England
1 CONT     * Died: 24 Oct 1660, Windsor Hartford CT
1 CONT
1 CONT     Katharine married Giles Gibbs on 13 Apr 1629 in Saint Sidwell Exeter Devon England. (Giles Gibbs was born in 1595 in St Sidwell Exeter Devon England, christened in St Sidwell's Devon England, died on 21 May 1641 in Windsor Har
1 CONC tford CT and was buried on 21 May 1641 in Windsor Hartford CT.)
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT ===================================================
1 CONT
1 CONT THE GREAT MIGRATION BEGINS 1620-1633
1 CONT ANCESTRY.COM CDROM
1 CONT
1 CONT GILES GIBBS
1 CONT
1 CONT ORIGIN:  St. Sidwell, Exeter, Devonshire
1 CONT MIGRATION:  1632
1 CONT FIRST RESIDENCE:  Dorchester
1 CONT REMOVES:  Windsor 1636
1 CONT
1 CONT CHURCH MEMBERSHIP:  Admission to Dorchester church prior to 4 March 1632/3 implied by freemanship.
1 CONT FREEMAN:  4 March 1632/3 [MBCR 1:367].
1 CONT EDUCATION:  The widow's inventory included 12s. in books.
1 CONT OFFICES:  Committee to make Dorchester rate, 3 November 1633 [DTR 4]; chosen Dorchester selectman (as "Go[odman] Gibbes"), 28 October 1634 [DTR 7].
1 CONT ESTATE:  Ordered to build twenty feet of fence, for one cow, 3 April 1633 [DTR 2]; granted three acres of land, 22 November 1634 [DTR 9]; granted two acres of meadow, and lot formerly Simon Hoyt's to be divided between Giles Gibbs
1 CONC  and Mr. Roger Williams, 17 April 1635 [DTR 11]; granted ten acres of land, 1 February 1635/6 [DTR 15]; received Lot #31, four acres, in meadow beyond Naponset [DTR 321].
1 CONT In the Windsor land inventory of 28 February 1640/1, Giles Gibbs had been granted four parcels, and had purchased one: seven acre homelot; ten and a half acres at the Great Meade; a parcel over the Great River, thirty rods in brea
1 CONC dth by three miles in length; forty-seven acres of upland above Rocky Hill; and (purchased of George Hull) "half an acre of the west end of his homelot."  This was annotated to show that Gregory Gibbs had received by bequest from 
1 CONC Giles Gibbs the lot over the great river thirty rods in breadth and in length three miles and that Katherine Gibbs had purchased this lot from Gregory Gibbs.  Two other purchases had been made (perhaps by the widow Gibbs): four ac
1 CONC res from Thomas Stayres and half an acre from Steven Terry [WiLR 1:94].
1 CONT In his will, dated 18 May 1641 (but date of probate not known), "Gyles Gibbs, of Wyndsor, on Connecticutt, yeoman, being weak in body" ordered "my son Gregory" to be apprenticed to "some godly man for the space of five years" and 
1 CONC if he stay out his time he is to have my lot over the great river, also if "my overseers have any encouragement to judge him worthy ... œ5 at age twenty-one years"; and bequeathed to "my two sons Samuel & Benjamin" œ20 each; to "m
1 CONC y daughter Sarah" œ20 at age twenty-one; to "Jacob, my son, ... my house and lots, meadows, home lot and great lot and lots whatsoever on this side the great river after his mother's life"; to "my wife" all my lots, houses, househ
1 CONC old goods, cattle, chattels, discharge of my debts; "provided that in case my said overseers have no good encouragement concerning the disposition of my son Gregory, but do judge him unworth a father's blessing under their hands, 
1 CONC my will is that my executor shall have the said lot toward the education of my children until my son Jacob shall attain the age of twenty-one years, and then my will is that my son Jacob shall have it"; "Katharine my wife" executr
1 CONC ix; the deacons of the church of Windsor overseers.  In a postscript he bequeathed to "Elizaphatt Gregory ten bushels of corn"; and to "Richard Wellar" 40s. [Manwaring 1:14-15; CCCR 1:504-05].
1 CONT In her will, dated 12 September 1660 and proved 6 December 1660, "Catharine Gibbs of Windsor" bequeathed to "my eldest son Jacob my dwelling house, barn & orchard, with the land whereon they stand, & all the land adjoining thereun
1 CONC to, which is my proper right by purchase," but if he dies without an heir living to the age of twenty-one then this land to go to "my second son Samuell"; to "my son Benjamin ... my lot on the other side the Great River, the which
1 CONC  I purchased of Gregory Gibbs my son-in-law [i.e., stepson]"; her moveables to "my son Jacob ... & to my daughter-in-law his wife," to "my son Benjamin," to "my son Jacob's daughter Mary," and to "my youngest son and executor Benj
1 CONC amin"; the residue to be divided among "my three youngest children," with specific reference to "my son Samuel's part" and "my daughter Sarah's part" [Hartford PD Case #2148; Manwaring 1:116-18].
1 CONT The inventory of the estate "left by the widdoe Gibbs Deceased" was taken 21 November 1660 and totalled œ220 7s., including real estate valued at œ160: "one home lot, seven acres," œ30; "one meadow lot, ten acres," œ50; "one lot o
1 CONC f upland, forty-eight acres," œ20; "the dwelling house with barn & land added to the homelot by the said widow's purchase," œ30; and "one lot over the great River," œ30 [Hartford PD Case #2148].
1 CONT Considerable mention appears in the Suffolk deeds regarding the estate of Katherine Gibbs in Windsor and Wethersfield, particularly as it related to her son, Benjamin, who died in Boston [SLR 11:192, 197, 252, 369].
1 CONT
1 CONT BIRTH:  By about 1600 based on estimated date of first marriage.
1 CONT DEATH:  Buried Windsor 21 May 1641 [WiVR].
1 CONT MARRIAGE:  (1) By about 1625 _____ _____; she died by 1629.
1 CONT (2) St. Sidwell, Exeter, 13 April 1629 Katherine Carwithe [TAG 61:33]; she died Windsor 24 October 1660 [TAG 61:32].
1 CONT CHILDREN:
1 CONT With first wife
1 CONT iGREGORY, b. say 1625 (to be apprenticed five years in 1641; certainly adult in 1649 [RPCC 71]); m. after 1676 Joyce (Smith) Osborn, widow of James [evidence not seen, but so stated in Windsor Hist 2:287].
1 CONT With second wife
1 CONT iiJACOB, bp. St. Sidwell, Exeter, 28 March 1629/30 [TAG 61:33]; m. Windsor 4 December 1657 Elizabeth Androus [Grant 43].
1 CONT iiiSARAH, bp. St. Sidwell, Exeter, 5 June 1631 [TAG 61:33]; m. Windsor 5 December 1661 John Share [Grant 71].  (On 5 February 1665/6 John Winthrop Jr. treated "Shire Sarah wife of John Shire a Cornish man, she was formerly Sarah G
1 CONC ibs" [WMJ 622].)
1 CONT ivSAMUEL, b. say 1633; m. Windsor 15 April 1664 Hepzibah Dibble [Grant 44].
1 CONT vBENJAMIN, b. say 1635 (adult in 1660 [RPCC 215]); m. by 1676 Lydia Scottow [SLR 11:192], daughter of Joshua Scottow.
1 CONT
1 CONT COMMENTS:  In 1986 James A. Rasmussen published the marriage record and the two baptisms from St. Sidwell, Exeter, Devonshire, which settle much of the chronology of the Gibbs family [TAG 61:32-34].  These three records show that 
1 CONC Giles Gibbs and his family could not have come on the Mary & John, and, in conjunction with the will of the widow Katherine Gibbs, determine unequivocally the birth order of all five children.
1 CONT As Rasmussen notes, the minister at St. Sidwell, Exeter, when the Gibbs family appeared there was Rev. JOHN WARHAM, and it may be that Gibbs was attracted to that minister, and followed him to New England in 1632.
1 CONT On 4 August 1635 Massachusetts Bay court ordered "Will[ia]m Wills to pay to Gyles Gibbs the sum of 16s., for felony by him committed" [MBCR 1:153].
1 CONT In the years after Giles Gibbs died, the family was often in court for unacceptable behavior.  In one court on 7 March 1650/1 Jacob Gibbs was complained of for several misdemeanors and fined 40s., Samuel Gibbs was "to be corrected
1 CONC  by his master" and Sarah Gibbs "the daughter of the widow Gibbs hath carried herself very sinfully and disorderly the court judges it necessary that she should be put to service, and therefore if her mother does not provide her a
1 CONC  good service ... Sarah Gibbs is to appear at the court ... and from thence be sent to the house of correction" [RPCC 97].  She was still in trouble in 1660 [RPCC 217].
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT THE MARY AND JOHN; A STORY OF THE FOUNDING OF DORCHESTER,MASSACHUSETTS 1630
1 CONT P32:
1 CONT Giles Gibbs removed to Windsor,Conn., where he became a member of the First Congregational Church. The records of that church, kept by Mattew Grant, give the date of his burial as May 21,1641. His will, dated May 18,1641 shows tha
1 CONC t all his children were minors at the time. The will of Katherine, his widow, written in 1660, shows that Gregory was not her son, Katherine being Giles' second wife.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT GIBBS Descent Email from Jackie Towner dated May 15,1999:
1 CONT Katherine Gibbs will:
1 CONT In the name of God , Amen. I, Catherine Gibbs, of Windsor, being sick &
1 CONT weak off boddy But of perfect memory, doe ffor Dyverse Considerations
1 CONT Make & Ordayne this my last will and Testament In Manner as following: 
1 CONT Imprimis: I bequeathe my sowle unto God yt gave itt, hopeing with  him
1 CONT to Inioy Eternall Rest & pece; & secondly, my boddy to Convenyent
1 CONT Cristyen Bewryall; & whereas, itt hath Plesed God to Bestow on Mee some
1 CONT part off this worlds Goods, my Will concerning yt Itt be disposed off in
1 CONT Manner as followeth, Namely: Ett ye end off halfe yeare affter my decese
1 CONT to enter Possession; I give & bequeath unto my eldest sonne Jacobb my
1 CONT Dwelling Howse, Barne & Orchard, with ye Land Whereon they stand, & all
1 CONT ye land Adioyneing thereunto, Wich is my proper right by Purchas, with
1 CONT all umoveables thereunto belonging, wth ffence & ffences, viz., to him &
1 CONT his heares ffor ever. Provided he has an heir off his owne body Begotten
1 CONT yt lives to ye Age of twenty & one yearses, then the sd. Aeyre to Inioy
1 CONT ye sume affter the ffather's decese: Butt in case he want such an heire,
1 CONT then affter his decese I give & Bequeath All the aforesd. unmovables
1 CONT with ffences or Lick Apertyneces unto my second sonne Samuell, & to his
1 CONT Owner Propper yowce; & unto my sonne Beniamin I give & Grant & Sett over
1 CONT my lott on ye other syde ye Great River, the which I purchased off
1 CONT Gregory Gibbs my son In Law ffor sattisffacktion of ye twenty pounds
1 CONT which his ffather gave att his Deeces, viz., to his Owne propper yowce &
1 CONT Acct, only in Case he doth Ethere By ye yeare of ffor Terme off yeare
1 CONT Lett ye sd. Land or yt he sett ye sd Land to Sale, then my Will is that
1 CONT my son Samuell have the first tender & Refuse off ye same; & my will
1 CONT ffurther is That in ye ffirst place all just debts Be Payde & Sattisfyed
1 CONT according to ye Spesya, & yt being Performed I dispose off my moveables
1 CONT as ffoll: viz., I give & bequeath unto my sonne Jacob my Greate Chest: &
1 CONT to my daffter in Law his wife my hatts; & unto my sonne Beniamin I Give
1 CONT &  Bequeath the twoe Gilt Lether Cosyens yt are in ye Abovesd Chest &
1 CONT whatt Else he hath bestowed on Mee as ffore Gifft; & unto My sonne
1 CONT Jacob's Daffter Mary I give twenty Shill to be Improved ffor hir
1 CONT Advantage att ye Discreasyen of my Exeeckters & to be payde hir att ye
1 CONT Day of her meryadge or att ye Age off one & Twenty yeares In Case she
1 CONT Marry nott Before; But in case she live nott to yt Age, then I Give &
1 CONT Bequeath ye same unto my yongest sone & Xseckter Beniamin; & Concerning
1 CONT ye rest of my Estate my Will is that Affter Inventory is taken &
1 CONT everything vallewed as equally as may Bee, thatt itt Bee equally dyvided
1 CONT Between my thre yongest Children, only my will is yt my sone Samuell's
1 CONT Part Bee in ye Plow & Cart Instruments unless he Refuseitt, & my daffter
1 CONT Sarah's Part Bee in or yt ffore her Part she have ye Refuse off my
1 CONT Aperell & part off howsehold stuff: & ffor ye Exsecktors off this My
1 CONT Last Will & Testament I Mack Coice off, ordayne & Appoynt my twoe sons
1 CONT Samuell & Beniamin, home the Lord dyreckt to ackt ye up sd. (Amen)
1 CONT Katherine Gibbs Ls.
1 CONT Witness: John Moore
1 CONT Phillip X (Drake?)
