0 @N6000000003795996580@ NOTE Henry R. Stiles, THE HISTORY OF ANCIENT WINDSOR, VOL II,  (New Hampshire Publishing Co., 1976*), P287:
1 CONT
1 CONT Pt. Ct.,  1651, Misdemeanors
1 CONT Daughter of William Gibbs, hath carried herself very sinfully. She is adjudged to be put out to service. If her mother does not do it to the satisfaction of Magistrates of Windsor before the court meet May next, she is to be sent 
1 CONC to house of correction if she does not give satifaction by three witnesses that she hath reformed from her evil practices.
1 CONT
1 CONT Part. Ct. Rec.
1 CONT She was again condemned, 1654, for several misdemeanors, to 6 days imprisonment, and the Widow Gibbs failing to appear on her bond was fined £, to be paid into the public treasury.4
