1 CONC  in his will, as well as  daughter Mary who married Jacob Drake, and Joyce who married Samuel Pinney. John Moore was supervisor of the will. He was the father of Nathaniel`s wife, Mindwell. Married in England.
0 @N6000000004066710903@ NOTE
1 CONT Believed to have been of Huguenot origin and to have fled with the numbers who left France after the slaughter of St. Bartholomew’s Day and to have taken an English name to cover his nationality.  According to family tradition he 
1 CONC came from Plymouth England to Dorchester Mass. and was among the colony that reached Windsor Conn. in the autumn of 1635.  In consequence of the severe loss of cattle that winter he was in the spring dispatched to England for a su
1 CONC pply and returned with 19 cows and a bull, receiving therefor in addition to his apportionment of land the ferry across the Connecticut river for his services.  According to Farmer he came from England with Rev Ephrai Hewitt in 16
1 CONC 39 directly to Windsor, and that he was a member fo  his church in England.  His name appears on the Windsor church record under date of May 3, 1640 and is second on the list of church members left by Rev. Rowland.  He died a tthe
1 CONC  residence of his son Nathaniel on the east side of the River.  His wife died in Windsor in May 21, 1641.  A 2nd wife died March 29, 1665.
