0 @N6000000000337364674@ NOTE Source #1:  Elias Loomis "Descendants of Joseph Loomis in America" Update of 1875 edition published by Elisha S. Loomis, Berea, Ohio,1908.  NOTE--Dr. Elias Loomis died before the Supplement was published. But this third (1908) edi
1 CONC tion contains all new materials which he had collected, along with all new data collected and obtainable since his death. 
1 CONT
1 CONT DEACON JOHN LOOMIS, b. Co. Essex, England, 1622; m. Feb. 3, 1648-9. Elizabeth, 
1 CONT      b. 1625, d. May 7, 1696, dau. of Thomas and Ann Scott, who sailed from Ipswich, 
1 CONT      England, April, 1634, to Ipswich, Mass., [Stiles says in the "Elizabeth" ) and had with them dau.      Elizabeth, aged 9 ( - see Beckler's note in Thomas Scott notes, this may have been another family! - )
1 CONT      years, and removed to Hartford, Conn. (See land records in office of Sec'y of Conn., 
1 CONT      Vol. II, p. 123, and Manwaring's Digest, I, pp. 32-35). He was admitted to the Windsor. 
1 CONT      Church Oct. 11, 1640. On May 3, 1643, he had granted him from the Plantation 40 
1 CONT      acres of land. He resided in Farmington from 1652 to 1660, when he returned to 
1 CONT      Windsor, and was Deacon of the church. He was deputy to the General Ct. in 1666 
1 CONT      and '7, also from 1675 to 1687. He died Sept. 1, 1688, ‘. 66, and his monument is still 
1 CONT      preserved in the Windsor burying ground. His will is preserved in the Probate office 
1 CONT      at Hartford, and his name is signed John Loomys.--See copy of same below. 13 children 
1 CONT      --all b. Windsor, except 3rd, 4th, 5th and 6th, b. Farmington. 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT 21.  JOHN, b. Nov. 9, 1649.+ 
1 CONT 22.  JOSEPH, b. Nov. 7, 1651.+ 
1 CONT 23.  THOMAS, b. Dec. 3, 1653.+ 
1 CONT 24.  SAMUEL, b. June 29, 1655, d. young. 
1 CONT 25.  DANIEL, b. June 16, 1657.+ 
1 CONT 26.  JAMES, b. Sept. 19, 1659, d. Dec. 14, 
1 CONT      1669. 
1 CONT 27.  TIMOTHY, b. July 27, 1661.+ 
1 CONT 28.  NATHANIEL, b. July 8, 1663.+ 
1 CONT 29.  DAVID, b. May 30, 1665, d. June 24, 
1 CONT      1665. 
1 CONT 30.  SAMUEL, b. Aug. 12, 1666.+ 
1 CONT 31.  ISAAC, b. Aug. 31, 1668, d. Dec. 12, 
1 CONT      1668. 
1 CONT 32.  ELIZABETH, b. May 8, 1671; m. Windsor, 
1 CONT      Feb. 4, 1691-2, John, b. Jan. 8, 
1 CONT      1668, d. Feb. 4, 1728, son of Peter and 
1 CONT      Mary (Gillett) Brown, who was the 
1 CONT      son of Peter Brown, who came to 
1 CONT      Plymouth in the Mayflower in 1620. 
1 CONT      She d. Dec. 11, 1723. Children: 1. 
1 CONT      Elizabeth, 2. Mary, 3. Ann, 4. Hannah, 
1 CONT      5. John, ancestor of Capt., John4 
1 CONT      Brown (Owen,3 Capt. John,2 John1) b. 
1 CONT      May 9, 1800, of Harper's Ferry, 1859, 
1 CONT      whose "soul goes marching on"; also 
1 CONT      of Rev. Dr. Heman4 Humphrey 
1 CONT      (Hannah3 [Brown], Capt. John,2 
1 CONT      John1) b. Mch. 26, 1779, Pres. Amherst 
1 CONT      Coll. 1823-45; and also of many 
1 CONT      other noted ones, some of whom are-- 
1 CONT      Rev. Charles F. Hudson, author of 
1 CONT      several books; Rev. Dr. Edw. P. 
1 CONT      Humphrey, Prof. Danville Th. Sem.; 
1 CONT      Hon. James Humphrey, memb. Cong.; 
1 CONT      Rev. John Humphrey, Prof. Mor. 
1 CONT      Phil., Hamilton Coll.; Rev. Dr. Zephaniah 
1 CONT      M. Humphrey, Prof. Lane Theol. 
1 CONT      Sem., Cincinnati, O., etc. 6. Ann, 7. 
1 CONT      Sarah, 8. Isaac, 9. Daniel, 10. Margaret, 
1 CONT      11. Esther. (See Whitney Gen. 
1 CONT      p. 1274, for many descendants). 
1 CONT 33.  MARY, b. Aug. 7, 1673, d. May 14, 
1 CONT      1675. 
1 CONT
1 CONT WILL OF JOHN LOOMIS, WINDSOR
1 CONT Will dated 27 Aug., 1688. Exhibited 4 Dec. 1688. Will on file. No Court Records found. 
1 CONT
1 CONT John Loomiss senior doe beinge of a competent understandinge and memory ordayne and appoynt this my Last will and Testament. 
1 CONT
1 CONT In primis my will is that my eldest son John shall have a double portion of my estate in Land yt to bee accounted for part that he have already beene possessed of and by this I give liberty to bee assured of 
1 CONT
1 CONT my will is that all my land on both sides ye River shall be equally devided between all my children now livinge I leave itt in charg in my will yt there bee indeavered of all a ready complyance to agree in ye devission itt beinge 
1 CONC so small devissions I know not how to pleas myself nor them My will is yt my daughter Elizabeth shall have equall portion with my sons excepting John of ye moveable estate my will is yt my wife shall have ye product of ye thirds o
1 CONC f all my land as longe as she lives and that ye house homested & Barne Remayne to my wife as longe as she lives and ye free dispose of itt amongst my children when she dies & thatt ye 3rd prt of my moveable estate of what she shal
1 CONC l chuse to bee to her free dispose amongst my children 
1 CONT
1 CONT my will is yt my son Thomas's two sons shall have ten pound a pees of my moveable estate I apoynt my wife and son John Executors of this my will always provided yt my Just debt shall bee payd out of my moveable estate and if itt w
1 CONC ill not reach every one proportionable shall abete 
1 CONT
1 CONT my will is that               (illegible) 
1 CONT by my wife at her death 
1 CONT                                                 I subscrib my hand 
1 CONT Wittness:                                                       John Loomys Sr 
1 CONT  Abigail Aling 
1 CONT  Nathanale Porter 
1 CONT
1 CONT
0 @N6000000008308001679@ NOTE Savage
1 CONT ==============
1 CONT JOHN, Windsor, s. of the first Joseph, b. in Eng. m. 3 or 6 Feb. 1649, Elizabeth d. of Thomas Scott of Hartford, had John, b. 9 Nov. 1649; Joseph, 7 Nov. 1651; Thomas, 3 Dec. 1653; Samuel, 29 June 1655, d. young; Daniel, 16 June 1
1 CONC 657; James, 19 Sept. 1659, d. young; Timothy, 27 July 1661; Nathaniel, 8 July 1663; David, 30 May 1665, d. young; Samuel, again, 12 Aug. 1666; Isaac, 31 Aug. 1668, d. at 20 yrs. soon aft. his f.; Elizabeth 8 May 1671; and Mary, 7 
1 CONC Aug. 1673, d. in few mos.; was rep. 1666 and 7, 75-7, liv. some time a. 1652 at Farmington, but went back; was deac. and d. 2 Sept. 1688. Nine of the ch. outliv. him and Elizabeth  m. 4 Feb. 1692, John Brown. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Loomis Family Genealogy    http://www.aritek.com/hartgen/htm/loomis.htm
1 CONT ==========================
1 CONT Deacon John Loomis - was born about 1622 in Braintree, Essex, England and died on 2 Sep 1688 in Windsor, CT and was buried in Windsor Burying Ground . He was the son of Joseph Loomis and Mary White. Deacon John married Elizabeth S
1 CONC cott on 3 Feb 1648/1649. Elizabeth was born about 1625. She was the daughter of Thomas Scott. She died on 7 May 1696 in Windsor, CT . 
1 CONT
1 CONT Deacon John - was accepted in the Windsor Church 11 Oct. 1640. Granted forty acres of land from the Plantation on 3 May 1643, lived in Farmington, Conn. 1652 to 1660, returned to Windsor, Conn., was Deacon of the Church. His monum
1 CONC ent still stands in Windsor Burying Ground, will is in the Probate office at Hartford, Conn. name is signed "John Loomys." 
