1 CONT The National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution Volume 106
1 CONT page 165
1 CONT Mrs. Lucretia Greenman Resick.
1 CONT DAR ID Number: 105516 
1 CONT Born in Union City, Ind. 
1 CONT Wife of Carl H. Resick. 
1 CONT Descendant of Aaron Harrison, Capt. Zacheus Gillett and Alexander Wolcott, as follows: 
1 CONT 1. Almon Greenman (b. 1826) m. 1852 Emily Witter (1833-92). 
1 CONT 2. Alfred Witter (1800-92) m. 1827 Lucretia Gillett (1809-81). 
1 CONT 3. Nathan Gillett, Jr. (1781-1841) m. 1803 Abigail Wolcott (1785-1830). 
1 CONT 4. Nathan Gillett (b. 1755) m. 1779 Lucy Harrison (b. 1762); Guy Wolcott (1760-1823) m. 1781 Abigail Allyn (b. 1765). 
1 CONT 5. Zacheus Gillett m. 1743 Ruth Phelps; Aaron Harrison m. 1748 Jerusha Warner (d. 1819); Alexander Wolcott m. 3rd Mary Richards. 
1 CONT Aaron Harrison (1726-1819) was a member of the Committee of Inspection and an active patriot during the Revolution. He was born in East Haven; died in Wolcott, Conn. 
1 CONT Also No. 68446. 
1 CONT Zacheus Gillett (1724-93) responded to the Lexington Alarm as captain and, 1776, served in the militia. He died in Granby, Conn. 
1 CONT Also No. 41767. 
1 CONT Alexander Wolcott (1712-95) was a representative to the General Assembly and served on the Committee of Inspection. He was born in East Windsor; died in Windsor, Conn. 
1 CONT Also No. 77305. 
1 CONT View full context
1 CONT
1 CONT The National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution Volume 110
1 CONT page 246
1 CONT Miss Emily Amanda Greenman.
1 CONT DAR ID Number: 109792 
1 CONT Born in Fort Wayne, Ind. 
1 CONT Descendant of John Greenman, Capt. Zacheus Gillett, Aaron Harrison, Alexander Wolcott and Stephen Dunwell, as follows: 
1 CONT 1. Rev. Almon Greenman (1826-1914) m. 1852 Emily Amanda Witter (1833-92
1 CONT 2. Anson Greenman (1805-47) m. 1825 Olive Cunningham (1809-46); Alfred Witter, Jr. (1800-92), m. 1827 Lucretia Gillett (1809-81). 
1 CONT 3. Silas Greenman (1782-1870) m. Electa Hardy (d. 1834); Nathan Gillett (1781-1841) m. 1803 Abigail Wolcott (1785-1830); Alfred Witter (1779-1864) m. 1799 Deborah Dunwell (1784-1851). 
1 CONT 4. John Greenman m. Rachel Grover; Nathan Gillett (b. 1755) m. 1779 Lucy Harrison (b. 1762); Guy Wolcott (1760-1823) m. 1781 Abigail Allyn (b. 1765). 
1 CONT 5. Zacheus Gillett m. 1st 1743 Ruth Phelps; Aaron Harrison m. 1748 Jerusha Warner (1727-1819); Alexander Wolcott m. 3rd 1745 Mary Richards. 
1 CONT John Greenman (1762-1840) received a pension on claim executed [p.246] 1832, for service as private, Massachusetts Line. He was born in Westerly, R. I.; died in New York. 
1 CONT Aaron Harrison (1726-1819) was a member of the Committee of Inspection and an active patriot during the Revolution. He was born in East Haven; died in Wolcott, Conn. 
1 CONT Zacheus Gillett (1724-93) responded to the Lexington Alarm as captain and 1776 served in the militia. He died in Granby, Conn. 
1 CONT Alexander Wolcott (1712-95) was a representative to the General Assembly and served on the Committee of Inspection. He was born in East Windsor; died in Windsor, Conn. 
1 CONT Also No. 105516. 
1 CONT Stephen Dunwell (1762-1840) enlisted as private, 1777, under Capt. Willard Converse, Col. Heman Swift's regiment, Connecticut troops. In 1818, he applied for a pension, which was allowed. He died in Solon, Ohio. 
1 CONT Also No. 90675. 
1 CONT
0 @N6000000006165923465@ NOTE Amos MOORE (Andrew) was born 19 Oct 1698 in Simsbury, Hartford, Connecticut. He died 20 Feb 1785 in Simsbury, Hartford, Conecticut and was buried in East Grandby, Hartford, Connecticut. Amos married (1) Martha OWEN, daughter of Ob
1 CONC adiah OWEN and Christiana WINCHELL, on 21 May 1720 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut. Martha was born 31 Aug 1698 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut. She died 20 May 1780 in Simsbury, Hartford, Connecticut. They had the following c
1 CONC hildren:
0 @N6000000003221218830@ NOTE 06-Feb-2009:
1 CONT
1 CONT from http://kinnexions.com/ancestries/smithh.htm#ECSmith
1 CONT
1 CONT Ebenezer and Christiana (Owen) Smith
1 CONT
1 CONT Ebenezer SMITH - b. Apr. 4, 1699, Suffield, CT. Son of Ebenzer SMITH and Sarah HUXLEY. Ebenezer was granted land at Suffield in 1709, 1713, 1716 and 1717. He served the town in a number of offices between 1700 and 1741, being sele
1 CONC ctman four times, constable three times, moderator of the town meeting four times, and surveyor of highways once. Admitted to the Suffield church on Feb. 27, 1725. Married at Suffiled, CT in Nov. 1725.
1 CONT
1 CONT Christiana OWEN - b. Jan. 10, 1702/3, Windsor, CT. Daughter of Obadiah OWEN and Christiana WINCHELL.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children of Ebenezer and Christiana Smith
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Jedediah - b. Jan. 31, 1727, Suffield, Hartford Co., CT; bap. there Feb. 5, 1726/7; d. Sep. 2, 1776, Natchez, MS. Graduated from Yale (AB 1750, AM 1754), and became minister at Granville, MA Dec. 1, 1756. His being a Loyalis
1 CONC t at the beginning of the Revolution was no doubt a prime motivation for leaving the ministry Apr. 16, 1776 and departing for for Spanish West Florida (now Mississippi state) with his wife, 10 of his 11 surviving children, and his
1 CONC  brother Elnathan's wife and 2 daughters, his brother having moved to West Florida two years prior. Upon arrival at Natchez, he heard of his brother's death, and died 7 days later of a fever aggravated by stress, grief and climate
1 CONC . Additional narrative about the journey appears in Stile's Genealogies... of Ancient Wetherfield. Married at Granville, MA Sarah COOK. The eldest child remained in MA. Children of Jedediah and Sarah SMITH: Judge Jedediah, Jr. mar
1 CONC ried Rhoda HUBBARD; Ebenezer died young; William married Mrs. NETTLES; Sarah married Joshua ALEXANDER; Josephus married Patience COBB (who married second John BAKER; daughter of Arthur and Susanna COBB); Richard Philetus married M
1 CONC s. THOMPSON; Israel married first Sarah 'Sallie' COBB (daughter of Arthur and Susanna COBB), and second Jane LORENZO DOAN; Philander married first Esther BRASHIER, and second Susan MILLER SCOTT; Philomela married David MITCHELL; C
1 CONC alvin married Priscilla COBB (daughter of Arthur and Susanna COBB); Luther L. married first Martha Elizabeth 'Patsey' BAKER (sister of John BAKER), and second Anna Eliza DAVIS (sister of CSA Pres. Jefferson DAVIS); and Courtland m
1 CONC arried first Catherine COOPER (daughter Aurelia's first husband was Dr. Ben DAVIS, youngest brother of CSA Pres. Jefferson DAVIS), second Narcissa BOONE, and third Jane BOONE (sister of Narcissa).
1 CONT    2. Asa - b. Apr. 20, 1729, Suffield, Hartford Co., CT; bap. there May 4, 1729; d. Sep. 27, 1798, Hartland, CT; bur Second Congregational Church Cemetery, Hartland CT. His grave marker includes the title of "Dr." Asa was probabl
1 CONC y living at Granville, MA until about 1770 to 1774, and then moved to Hartland, CT. A history of Hartland indicates he was a private in the Revolution, and one of the original members of the Second Congregational Church when it wa
1 CONC s created in 1780. Asa was married at Westfield, MA to Experience DEWEY, with two dates appearing in the records. It is likely that the first date, Mar. 30, 1760, was the date the marriage intentions was published and the second d
1 CONC ate, Apr. 17, 1760, was the actual marriage date. Children of Asa and Experience SMITH: Abigail; Thodosia; Asenath; Asa married; and likely other children.
1 CONT    3. Christiana - b. Aug. 21, 1731, Suffield, CT; d. there Sep. 19, 1732.
1 CONT    4. Ebenezer - b. Mar. 1, 1733, Suffield, CT. Married on Feb. 12, 1767 at Granville, MA to Abigail ROSE. Ebenezer served as a corporal of Capt. Lebbeus BALL's Company, answering the Lexington alarm on Apr. 29, 1775. Children of 
1 CONC Ebenezer and Abigail SMITH: Ebenezer; and Zebulon.
1 CONT    5. Christian - b. Oct. 3, 1734, Suffield, CT; d. Mar. 9, 1757/8.
1 CONT    6. Eliakim - b. Jan. 25, 1736, Suffield, Hartford Co., CT; d. Aug. 27, 1775, Watertown, Middlesex Co., MA. Married first on Jun. 17, 1760 to Mehitable SMITH (b. Mar. 24, 1740; d. Apr. 16, 1770), daughter of Jonathan SMITH and M
1 CONC ehitable COOK, and second on Nov. 14, 1771 to Jerusha KELLOGG (b. about 1739; d. Sep. 22, 1823), daughter of James KELLOGG and Experience SMITH. Children of Eliakim and Mehitable SMITH: Rebecca died young; Eliakim probably married
1 CONC  Submit (DICKINSON) GAYLORD; and Rebecca married Rev. Timothy HOPKINS.
1 CONT    7. Elnathan - b. Jul. 9, 1737, Suffield, CT; bap. there Jul. 16, 1737; d. 1776, MS. Removed to Spanish West Florida (now Mississippi) about 1774, his letters encouraging his brother Jedidiah to join him there. Married on May 23
1 CONC , 1764 at Granville, MA to Hannah BATES. His wife and daughters remained at Granville, MA when he moved south, and he died before they could join him. Children of Elnathan and Hannah SMITH: Elphalet perhaps died young; Eada (daugh
1 CONC ter); and Eunice.
1 CONT    8. Zebulon - b. Dec. 16, 1739. Died as an infant on the 16th day of a month in 1738 or 1739 (perhaps on date of birth), probably at Suffield, CT.
1 CONT    9. Elijah - b. Sep. 6, 1741, Suffield, CT.
1 CONT   10. Dorcas - b. Jul. 3, 1743, Suffield, CT; d. Jun. 8, 1833, Nassau, NY. Married Josiah HOLCOMB. 
