0 @N6000000000337352581@ NOTE Source #1:  Goodwin, Nathaniel. Genealogical Notes of Connecticut and Massachusetts. F.A.Brown. Hartford. 1856. 
1 CONT
1 CONT ELIZABETH CLARK was twice married. 1. To Moses Cooke, of Warronoke, [Westfield,] Mass., son of Captain Aaron Cooke, one of the first settlers of Windsor, Conn., afterwards of Northampton, Mass., November 25, 1669. He was slain by 
1 CONC the Indians at Westfield, aged --. 2. To Lieut. Job Drake, of Windsor, son of Job Drake, of that town, September 13, 1677. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Lieut. Job Drake died December 19, 1711, in the 60th year of his age. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Mrs. Elizabeth Drake, alias Cook, died December 22, 1729, aged 78. 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Children,--by her first husband.
1 CONT 12 Elizabeth,     born August  25, 1673, in Westfield. Married to Benjamin Griswold, 
1 CONT                                               of Windsor, Conn., by wh
1 CONT                                               she had a numerous family of children, 
1 CONT                                               among them, Moses, born July 
1 CONT                                               10, 1714, and married Mary Nichols, 
1 CONT                                               daughter of Cyprian Nichols, of 
1 CONT                                               Hartford. 
1 CONT 13 Moses,         born April   17, 1675, in Windsor. 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Children,--by her second husband.
1 CONT 14 Job,           born               1678.  Died unmarried, October 15, 1712. 
1 CONT 15 Mary,          born April     29, 1680.  Married to John Porter, of Windsor, 
1 CONT                                               September 23, 1697. Children,--John, 
1 CONT                                               born March 7, 1699. Mar
1 CONT                                               born July 10, 1703. Anna, born 
1 CONT                                               April 2, 1706. Catharine, born September 
1 CONT                                               14, 1707. Lydia, born M
1 CONT                                               4, 1711. Ann, born October 13, 
1 CONT                                               1714. 
1 CONT 16 Jacob,         born January   29, 1683.  Dwelt in Wintonbury Parish, Wind 
1 CONT                                               sor. He died January 29, 1762, 
1 CONT                                               aged 80 nearly. Had 5 chldren, 
1 CONT                                               among them, Job, his 4th child, born 
1 CONT                                               November 6, 1714, in whose line 
1 CONT                                               descended Richard G. Drake, Esq., 
1 CONT                                               of the city of Hartford, attorney at 
1 CONT                                               law. 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT 17 Sarah,         born May       10, 1686.  Married December 3, 1702, to Hon. 
1 CONT                                               Roger Wolcott, of Windsor, Conn. 
1 CONT                                               He became Major General and second 
1 CONT                                               in command at the taki
1 CONT                                               Louisburg, in 1745, and was Lieut. 
1 CONT                                               Governor of the Colony of Connecticut, 
1 CONT                                               from 1741 to 1750, and Governor 
1 CONT                                               from 1750 to 1754. He di
1 CONT                                               May 17, 1767, aged 89. They had 
1 CONT                                               11 children.(*) 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT (*) Oliver, the youngest of the eleven, was born in 1723, and filled many State offices; was a 
1 CONT Brigadier General during the war of the Revolution; member of the Continental Congress, 
1 CONT and Signer of the Declaration of Independence; Lieut. Governor from 1786 to 1796, and 
1 CONT Governor, 1797. He married Laura Collins, of Guilford, Conn., by whom he had four children, 
1 CONT two sons and two daughters. He died December 1, 1797, aged 71. Oliver, one of the 
1 CONT sons, was born January 11, 1760; Yale College, 1778; admitted to the Bar in 1781: was appointed 
1 CONT one of the Committee of Pay-table at Hartford, January, 1782; Joint Commissioner 
1 CONT to settle Accounts with the United States, May, 1784; Sole Commissioner, May, 1787; 
1 CONT Comptroller of Public Accounts of the State, May, 1788; Auditor of the Treasury of the 
1 CONT United States, September 12, 1789; Comptroller of the same, June 17, 1791, and Secretary 
1 CONT of U. S. Treasury, February 2, 1795, which office he resigned in 1800; a Judge of the Second 
1 CONT Circuit of the United States, February 20, 1801; Governor of Connecticut from 1817 to 1827. 
1 CONT Died June 1, 1833. Gov. Wolcott was married in 1785, to Elizabeth Stoughton, only daughter 
1 CONT of John Stoughton, of Windsor, Conn., by whom he had several children. 
