1 CONT William Spencer, brother of Thomas and Jared, had been at Cambridge, in 1631, and was a representative in 1634-5.  He was one of the first settlers of Hartford, Conn. and in 1639, a selectman of that town.  Mr. Spencer was one of 
1 CONC the deputies in the General Court in 1639, and appointed with Mr. Wyllis and Mr. Webster to prepare the first revisal of laws in that year.
1 CONT
1 CONT Source #3:  Douglas Richardson, "The English Origin of Agnes Harris, of Hartford, Conn., Wife of William Spencer and William Edwards." in "The American Genealogist," [TAG Vol. 63], January, 1988: pp. 33-44.
